window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6401,"title":"Chapter 6401: Chapter 6399: Master’s Legacy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6399: Master’s Legacy","Bai Yunqing’s eyes shot open in astonishment. He suddenly noticed countless figures reminiscent of celestial soldiers in the sky, but the person who truly caught his attention was Chu Feng.","“Big brother Chu Feng, is it you?” Bai Yunqing stood up, and he looked like he would flit over right away.","“Stop! You aren’t done inheriting the legacy. Do you not want to live anymore?” Chu Feng roared.","“Big brother Chu Feng, the legacy is too much for me to bear. I should never have gotten overconfident and activated it. It looks like I’m going to die here today. I’m glad I’m able to meet you one last time before I die,” Bai Yunqing said with a sigh.","“Cut the crap. You won’t die with me around.” Chu Feng waved his sleeves and conjured a formation blueprint.","“Lord Chu Feng, you...”","The Spirit God Clansmen were astounded by the formation blueprint, including Shen Hui.","Chu Feng had merely revised Bai Yunqing’s formation, but the modifications he made brought the formation up to another level. But the most shocking thing of all was that despite the complexity of the formation blueprint, Chu Feng relayed it in an easily comprehensible manner.","“Lord Chu Feng’s grasp of formations far surpasses mine. I finally understand why even someone of Lord Xue Ji’s character is willing to befriend Lord Chu Feng,” Shen Hui murmured.","Bai Yunqing also understood the ingenuity of Chu Feng’s formation. With tears of gratitude streaming down his face, he said, “Brother Chu Feng, how can I ever thank you for this? Should I change my gender and betroth myself to you?”","The formation would not only save his life but also help him obtain the powerful legacy. He might have given up earlier, but if given a choice, he would much rather live on.","“Stop rambling nonsense. Quickly modify your formation and continue accepting the legacy,” Chu Feng urged.","“All right.” Bai Yunqing hurriedly did as he was told.","This was an individual trial, so outsiders couldn’t interfere. Chu Feng could offer pointers, but Bai Yunqing had to do the work himself. Fortunately, the formation blueprint was simplified to be comprehensible, and Bai Yunqing was a talented world spiritist, not to mention a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist now.","Otherwise, he couldn’t have succeeded in activating the tombstone legacy.","After Bai Yunqing completed the modifications, the formation suddenly flared with greater energy than before. Bai Yunqing continued receiving the legacy, but this time, he was more confident than ever.","“Big brother Chu Feng, your formation is incredible! As expected of my big brother.”","It was to the point where Bai Yunqing could receive the legacy while chatting with Chu Feng.","“Focus on receiving the legacy lest something go wrong. We’re counting on you,” Chu Feng said.","“Counting on me?” Bai Yunqing was confused.","Chu Feng explained their current plight to Bai Yunqing, including the Seven Stars Orbs. Much to his surprise, Bai Yunqing didn’t look worried in the least. If anything, he was enthused.","“Big brother Chu Feng, I’ll be of help to you this time!” Bai Yunqing declared proudly.","“If you know what’s at stake, you should focus on receiving the legacy,” Chu Feng said.","“Big brother, you must not know how powerful your formation is. The legacy is pretty much in my grasp right now; it’s just a matter of how long it takes,” Bai Yunqing replied.","It went without saying that Chu Feng knew that; he was the one who modified the formation, after all. He had already seen through the legacy, and he knew his formation was more than enough for Bai Yunqing to complete the legacy inheritance.","“Big brother Chu Feng, you’re growing too fast. You’re already at rank two Heavenly Dragon!” Bai Yunqing exclaimed.","“I’m merely borrowing someone else’s spirit power. My true strength is far beneath yours.”","Those words made Bai Yunqing’s face darken.","“Big brother Chu Feng, I didn’t obtain my power through cultivation. My master passed it down to me,” Bai Yunqing said.","Those from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion were startled.","“Passed it down? You can pass down spirit power?” someone exclaimed in bewilderment.","“It is possible to pass down one’s spirit power, but it needs to be done via a special procedure, and it is highly risky. A misstep can spell the end of the inheritor,” Shen Hui explained.","“Cultivation is an arduous journey. All of us went through a great deal of hardship to reach our current levels. Even if such a special procedure existed, who would be willing to pass down their spirit power to someone else? Unless... Unless that person cultivated with the intent of passing down his spirit power to nurture someone else right from the start,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Huangfu Zhantian added, “It’s also possible that the person has reached his limit.”","He noticed the melancholic look on Bai Yunqing’s face.","“Elder Ouyang is no longer around?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes. My master was already terminally ill when he first met us. He took me in because he was in a rush to pass down the divine physician’s legacy. It was using the divine physician’s method that he passed his spirit power down to me, but I wasn’t able to fully assimilate it due to the limitations of my talent,” Bai Yunqing explained.","Chu Feng was not surprised to hear that. He had already guessed as much when he sensed Ouyang Kongyu’s aura in Bai Yunqing’s spirit power.","When he last bade farewell to Ouyang Kongyu, the latter looked a little down, and it felt like he had something to say, though he held his tongue. Thinking back, he had probably wanted to tell Chu Feng that his days were numbered, just that he didn’t want to add to Chu Feng’s burden.","Though Ouyang Kongyu did say things like he could put his mind at ease knowing Bai Yunqing had a brother like Chu Feng.","“Death is a natural rite of life. Don’t feel burdened by it. You’re fulfilling his will by living on with his legacy,” Chu Feng said.","Hu!","A bizarre tornado carrying a black aura suddenly appeared from nowhere, emanating a terrifying aura. They formed a massive spiral reminiscent of a world spiritist gate.","“Lord Chu Feng, it’s a teleportation gate. Something is trying to come here,” Shen Hui said.","The Spirit God Clansmen channeled their spirit power, and golden chains descended from the sky to bind the teleportation gate. However, the golden chains shattered before they could reach the teleportation gate.","A destructive aura emanated from the black aura.","“This is bad.”","Even experts of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief’s caliber felt unnerved. The pressure coming from the black aura drove them into despair."]},{"number":6402,"title":"Chapter 6402: Chapter 6400: Inheritor of the Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6400: Inheritor of the Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor","The black aura manifested into a teleportation gate, and an ancient voice echoed from within, “You little rats d-d-don’t know your place! Do you think the Immemorial Cemetery is a p-p-place you can come and go as you like?!”","The crowd turned grim, not knowing how to respond to this situation. They knew the person inside the teleportation gate was not someone they could trifle with. Some of them considered kneeling and begging for mercy, but they held in the urge and instead turned to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng mentioned earlier that he had met someone who appeared to be the Immemorial Cemetery’s master and had grasped some of its secrets. It would be safer to let Chu Feng deal with this mysterious entity.","In contrast to the crowd, Chu Feng wasn’t nervous at all. Instead, he replied with a chuckle, “Aren’t you here too? Your ass isn’t big enough to block the entrance for the rest of us.”","Chu Feng’s words shocked the crowd. He was courting death by saying those words!","The voice inside the teleportation gate roared in anger, “You brat! How d-d-dare you speak to me like that? Do you know w-w-who I am?”","“Who else can you be other than Wang Qiang?” Chu Feng scoffed.","“Wang Qiang?”","The crowd was stunned. Most of them knew about Chu Feng’s relationship with Wang Qiang, and some Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen had even met him in person. Wang Qiang was even a member of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.","“What the hell! H-h-how did you know?”","A figure leaped out of the teleportation gate.","The crowd couldn’t believe their eyes, especially those from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion. It was Wang Qiang!","The black aura teleportation gate dissipated after Wang Qiang jumped out from within. The terrifying aura also vanished as if it had never appeared.","“Brother, how did you know it’s me?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Did you forget you’re carrying my location talisman?” Chu Feng asked.","“Shit! I-I-I forgot about it.” Wang Qiang turned to the crowd from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion and grinned. “Paying respect to Lord Mansion Master.”","“Wang Qiang! How did you come out of there?”","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion had yet to recover from his shock. He was still shaken up by the teleportation formation’s terrifying aura.","“Mansion Master, I was just j-j-joking around. That gate is useless d-d-despite its terrifying aura. It’s a new ability I picked up!” Wang Qiang replied merrily.","He proceeded to share what he had been through.","It turned out he had activated a tombstone and obtained its legacy. At the same time, he acquired the ability to open teleportation gates within the Immemorial Cemetery and swiftly travel to wherever he wanted.","He could even teleport specifically to an individual. He had thought about Chu Feng when he opened this teleportation gate, which was why he was transported here.","“That’s wonderful! It’ll be much easier to travel within the Immemorial Cemetery now that we have your ability,” Huangfu Shengyu said.","“Easier my a-a-ass! You don’t know how much e-e-energy it takes to open a teleportation gate, and there’s a s-s-short cooldown period after I successfully open one,” Wang Qiang replied.","“What kind of legacy did you obtain? It must be from a formidable figure, right?” Huangfu Shengyu asked.","“The owner of the legacy doesn’t seem t-t-to be a good person. His name is Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor,” Wang Qiang replied.","“Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor?” Chu Feng was taken aback.","Wang Qiang rolled up his sleeves to reveal a black, lustrous imprint. “The tombstone realm ignited with black flames after I o-o-obtained the legacy. It looked s-s-so sinister! And this weird thing suddenly appeared on my a-a-arm.”","“This...”","The crowd was taken aback. Everyone turned to look at Chu Feng.","Even though the imprint was much smaller and the light it emanated was different, it still bore some resemblance to the rune imprint on Yuwen Yanri’s chest.","Chu Feng’s face lit up in delight.","“W-w-why are you smiling, brother? Is this something g-g-good?” Wang Qiang asked.","“So, you’re the one who obtained the legacy of the second star!” Chu Feng exclaimed.","“What’s the s-s-second star?” Wang Qiang was baffled.","Chu Feng told Wang Qiang about the Seven Stars Orbs.","“Damn! So, t-t-this is actually a good thing?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Of course it’s a good thing!” Chu Feng replied. “Your ability to teleport within the Immemorial Cemetery should be unrelated to the legacy you received. The Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor sounds like a formidable figure. What did you get from his legacy?”","“I’m still assimilating it. It’ll likely advance my cultivation, t-t-though not by much. The biggest benefit is still the rise in my fighting p-p-prowess. I suspect it’ll amplify the prowess of my Four Fiends Divine Body,” Wang Qiang said.","“Sounds like a fruitful trip,” Chu Feng remarked.","“I think s-s-so too. I was worried the imprint was a c-c-curse, but it looks like my worry was unfounded. I’m glad it’s s-s-something good. Brother, have you r-r-received any legacies yet? Speaking of which, what brings you b-b-back here? Actually, I made a m-m-mistake. I just so happened to think about you and ended up opening a t-t-teleportation gate here. I thought it w-w-would lead me out of the Immemorial Cemetery. I didn’t expect to see you h-h-here,” Wang Qiang voiced his confusion.","Chu Feng told Wang Qiang about his encounter with his grandmother.","“D-d-don’t worry, brother. Your grandmother will be fine,” Wang Qiang said.","...","Meanwhile, Jie Mubai continued to wander in the Immemorial Cemetery. He wasn’t disheartened despite having suffered two setbacks to Chu Feng. He was confident that, with his talent, he would get something good from the Immemorial Cemetery.","Soon, his eyes lit up. He set his eyes on a tombstone realm.","This tombstone realm was not particularly big, but it emanated an intimidating aura. Even the tombstone looked special.","Most tombstone realms only had a tombstone, but this one had two. They resembled sharp swords piercing into space. Even though the tombstones were empty, they emanated bizarre purple auras as if some terrifying monstrous beasts were hiding within them.","Anyone else would have circumvented the tombstone realm, but Jie Mubai looked as if he had stumbled upon gold.","“I found yet another good place,” Jie Mubai remarked as he flew into the tombstone realm.","The inside of the tombstone realm was equally bizarre, too. Other tombstone realms merely had peculiar terrains, but this one was covered in holes as if there had been an intense fight.","The ground was littered with white bones that seemed to go further back than the Ancient Era. Their origin energies had long dissipated, making it impossible to gauge their cultivation when they were still alive.","It was evident from the mountainlike bones that these weren’t just corpses of humans but monstrous beasts, too.","Jie Mubai had seen enough not to be intimidated by such sights. He quickly identified the formation’s location and rushed over. Soon, he arrived before two massive tombstones.","Unlike other tombstone realms, these two tombstones resembled buildings.","One of them had a massive gate in it, but the gate was closed, and an eight-meter-tall humanlike figure was guarding it. He wasn’t wearing clothes, for his skin was naturally cloaked with a layer of black armor.","This black armor looked imposing and nigh indestructible."]},{"number":6403,"title":"Chapter 6403: Chapter 6401: Sea Conqueror Saint Exalted’s Tomb","paragraphs":["Chapter 6401: Sea Conqueror Saint Exalted’s Tomb","“A monstrous beast?” Jie Mubai frowned.","He could tell that the guard in black armor was not a human but a monstrous beast.","Just then, the guard suddenly turned to look at him despite his concealment, causing his heart to clench up. Then, the guard revealed his cultivation—rank one Heavenly God!","“Hah...” Jie Mubai sneered in disdain as he revealed himself.","He was a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist who had the means to outrun even rank three Heavenly Gods. Needless to say, he didn’t fear a mere rank one Heavenly God.","The guard’s eyes and black armor suddenly turned golden, and his cultivation surged to rank three Heavenly God level.","“There’s no need for that. We can work together,” Jie Mubai said.","He opened his palm, and a sliver of spirit power the size of a snake flew into the sky.","Boom!","The sliver of spirit power abruptly morphed into a humongous formation that was even larger than the two tombstones. The aura of a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist could be felt from the formation.","Jie Mubai’s display of power worked.","The armored guard narrowed his eyes and asked, “Who are you?”","“It doesn’t matter who I am. The important thing is that we can claim the legacy if we join forces,” Jie Mubai said.","“Why should I work with you when I can monopolize everything?” the armored guard asked.","“You ought to set your sights further. This legacy might be formidable, but there are far greater treasures we can go after here,” Jie Mubai said.","“Far greater treasures?”","“You’ll be interested in it.”","“Tell me about it.”","“Chu Feng,” Jie Mubai replied.","“Chu Feng?” The armored guard frowned.","“You should have heard about him. He possesses not just the Ruler’s Bloodline but the legendary Genesis Bloodline as well. I bet he has other treasures, too. Putting all things aside, just the Genesis Bloodline could be worth more than the entire Immemorial Cemetery. He is the true treasure here,” Jie Mubai said.","“And you know where Chu Feng is?” the armored guard asked.","“Mm. If we work together...”","Shoosh!","Before Jie Mubai could finish his words, the armored guard flitted up to him and pierced his dantian with his sharp claw.","“You...” Jie Mubai stared at the armored guard in disbelief as he blurted, “What the hell is wrong with you?”","But the armored guard didn’t respond. He plunged his other claw into Jie Mubai’s dantian and ripped him into two. Seconds later, his face suddenly turned cold.","Much to his astonishment, Jie Mubai’s ripped body dissipated as spirit power.","Jie Mubai’s voice echoed from the sky, “Bloody hell! Are you another one of Chu Feng’s acquaintances?!”","The armored guard traced the voice out of the tombstone realm and into space, but the voice was from a formation. The real Jie Mubai had escaped. Infuriated, the armored guard smashed the formation into bits with his overwhelming martial power.","Then, he sneered, “Pray that I don’t find you.”","With that, the armored guard returned to the tombstone realm.","In truth, Jie Mubai was still inside the tombstone realm. He clutched onto a burning Ancient Era’s talisman paper, which enveloped him in a powerful layer of spirit power. He was currently escaping from the tombstone realm.","“What’s with that monstrous beast? He has sharp eyes! He might have found it if I hadn’t activated this talisman paper. But why did he suddenly make a move on me? Is he acquainted with Chu Feng, or is he just reluctant to work with me? I must be thinking too much. He can’t be acquainted with Chu Feng as well. How can Chu Feng know so many powerful figures?”","Jie Mubai murmured under his breath as he fled in a fluster. Regardless of the truth, he had to concede that his luck was the worst.","...","Soon, Bai Yunqing was at the final phase of his legacy inheritance.","Just then, the Spirit God Clan’s Shen Hui turned to Chu Feng and reported, “Lord Chu Feng, a young woman is approaching us.”","She handed a formation compass to Chu Feng.","While waiting for Bai Yunqing to complete the legacy inheritance, the Spirit God Clan had constructed a formation in the vicinity. The formation could detect approaching individuals and even eliminate them if necessary.","“Oh? That woman is beautiful. She must have quite the background to dare wander the Immemorial Cemetery alone.” Huangfu Zhantian leaned over and peeked at the woman reflected in the formation compass.","The woman was riding on a copper sparrow.","The copper sparrow was a non-living being, spanning only around ten meters wide. It was extremely small compared to their warships, but its incredible speed made it no secret that it was an invaluable treasure.","“It’s my friend,” Chu Feng replied.","There was no way he wouldn’t recognize Song Yun.","Shen Hui deactivated their offensive formations to let Song Yun through. Song Yun must have locked onto Chu Feng, for she was heading straight for him.","“Wow, it’s crowded here,” Song Yun exclaimed with an exaggerated expression when she saw how many people were gathered in the tombstone realm, though she wasn’t afraid in the least.","“Your location talisman is amazing. I didn’t expect you to find me here.”","Chu Feng took out the location talisman he had received from Song Yun. Location talismans became less potent the further away one was, so it shouldn’t have been easy for her to find him in a place as vast as the Immemorial Cemetery.","Even the location talisman he had given Wang Qiang only worked when they were in proximity.","He had once given Little Fishy a pendant embedded with a location formation before she was taken away by a God Clansman. He could track her from a far distance away because he had devoted precious treasures to it and sacrificed its effective duration.","That pendant’s location formation was no longer working now.","Song Yun’s location formation was even stronger than the one Chu Feng had given Little Fishy, and its effective duration was incredible.","“Of course. The location formation was worth a fortune. I’d only give it to big brother Chu Feng,” Song Yun said with a grin.","“How’s your body doing?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’m fine now. Don’t worry, big brother Chu Feng,” Song Yun replied.","Chu Feng first introduced the crowd to Song Yun before explaining their current situation to her.","“No wonder the entrance closed right after I entered. Is the Immemorial Cemetery planning to kill us off here? But there’s no need to worry since I’m here, big brother Chu Feng. I’ll settle one of the Seven Stars Orbs for you,” Song Yun declared confidently.","Huangfu Zhantian scoffed, “Lass, you must not know how difficult it is to secure a Seven Stars Orbs’ legacy.”","Song Yun ignored Huangfu Zhantian and flashed a mischievous smile at Chu Feng. “Big brother Chu Feng, you trust me, right?”","“Of course. Go ahead and take a legacy if it’s suited for you.” Chu Feng harbored no doubts about Song Yun’s capability.","Bai Yunqing finally obtained the legacy, and the rune imprint appeared on his body. At the same time, the tombstone realm emanated a brilliant light.","Chu Feng sensed the location of the fourth star and urged the group to immediately set off.","“Shen Hui, we must move fast. Someone is inheriting the fourth legacy,” Chu Feng said.","“I understand.”","The group traveled even faster than before.","Through a formation, they could see the tombstone realm from a far distance away. This tombstone realm was even larger than the ones Yuwen Yanri and Bai Yunqing had obtained their legacies.","Words had also appeared on the tombstone— Sea Conqueror Saint Exalted’s Tomb.","All of a sudden, the tombstone realm emanated a brilliant light. A blue aura enveloped the tombstone realm, transforming it into a blue planet. This was a sign that the legacy inheritance was complete.","“Acceleration talismans!” Shen Hui ordered.","The Spirit God Clansmen took out a talisman each and ignited it. There was a burst of spirit power, and all the warships further accelerated.","They had to quickly find the legacy inheritor. It would be troublesome if they left.","The group finally arrived at the tombstone realm, and everyone except for the Spirit God Clan breathed a sigh of relief. Once they were inside the tombstone realm, they could see what was going on via the Spirit God Clan’s formation.","Reflected in the formation were familiar faces—the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen. Two people had inherited the legacy—Xianhai Shaoyu and Xianhai Yu’er.","“Chu Feng, why are they all your friends? Is it a coincidence?” Eggy blurted out."]},{"number":6404,"title":"Chapter 6404: Chapter 6402: Song Yun’s Taunt","paragraphs":["Chapter 6402: Song Yun’s Taunt","“I don’t think it’s a coincidence.”","Chu Feng had chatted with Bai Yunqing along the way.","After receiving Ouyang Kongyu’s legacy and burying him, Bai Yunqing went into closed-door training to assimilate the legacy. But from the aura he emanated, he hadn’t accomplished that yet.","He came to the Immemorial Cemetery because he had a weird feeling reminiscent of a summon. The closer he came to the Immemorial Cemetery, the stronger the summon became. The summon was coming from the Profound Acupuncture Physician Saint’s tombstone.","It was one thing if Bai Yunqing was the only one who experienced that, but Yuwen Yanri and Wang Qiang experienced something similar, too. Their experiences were slightly different and less intense than what Bai Yunqing went through, but there was no question that they were drawn here as well.","“Chu Feng, is the Immemorial Cemetery after you?” Eggy asked.","The Seven Stars Orbs were all related to Chu Feng’s friends, and it felt like Chu Feng was here to ensure their success. It felt like it had all been planned out.","“I’m already here, The Immemorial Cemetery’s master can do whatever he likes to me. There’s no need for him to go in circles.” Chu Feng didn’t think things were as simple as that.","“Could it be that the Immemorial Cemetery’s master has a high opinion of you and wants to pass down a formidable legacy to you, but he wants you to overcome his trial first? He could have lured your friends here to test your character,” Eggy asked.","“I hope that’s the case,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","That would mean that the Immemorial Cemetery was a blessing and not a boon. But the dangerous and sinister aura shrouding the Immemorial Cemetery made him think that things couldn’t have been that simple.","...","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan mainly comprised Little Fishy’s parents, grandfather, and their strongest elders.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu had successfully obtained the legacy, and rune imprints appeared on their bodies, namely on Little Fishy’s right wrist and Xianhai Shaoyu’s left wrist. They didn’t know what the rune imprints represented and were worried.","Before they could study the rune imprints, a blinding light suddenly appeared in the distance, and a massive army came into view. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s war flags could be spotted among the massive army, and that made the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s elders tense up.","“Big brother?”","A moment later, Little Fishy suddenly flew into the sky with an excited grin and flitted toward the massive army. Xianhai Shaoyu did the same.","Little Fishy’s parents and the others breathed sighs of relief as they followed suit. They had also noticed not just Chu Feng but Wang Qiang, Yuwen Yanri, and several other familiar faces.","“Big brother, what brings you here?” Little Fishy’s face erupted in joy.","It hadn’t been long since they last parted ways, but it looked as if they were reuniting after a long farewell.","Before Chu Feng could reply, Song Yun stepped forward and said, “Xianhai Yu’er, we finally meet.”","“You... know me?” Little Fishy eyed Song Yun in confusion.","“I am Song Yun. This is our first time meeting, but I have long heard about you. My big brother Chu Feng cherishes you a lot and is willing to put his life on the line for you. You probably don’t know how many women are jealous of you. You are indeed beautiful. I can see why big brother Chu Feng likes you.”","Song Yun’s words were spoken with a smile, but her words were barbed with thorns.","The crowd plunged into silence.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan was displeased, but the others watched the situation in amusement. All eyes were focused on the two beautiful ladies, Song Yun and Little Fishy, to the point where they even overlooked Chu Feng.","The crowd sensed the peculiarity of the situation.","Huangfu Zhantian took out a bunch of melon seeds and began snacking on them. Wang Qiang reached over to grab some melon seeds, too.","“G-g-give me some.”","The generous Huangfu Zhantian tossed a Cosmos Sack filled with melon seeds over.","Little Fishy’s excitement at seeing Chu Feng was greatly cooled by Song Yun’s words, but she still politely asked, “I’m afraid I don’t understand what you’re saying.”","“You don’t understand? I was from the Netherworld Sect,” Song Yun replied.","“Netherworld Sect?” Little Fishy’s eyes flared up with enmity.","Song Yun added, “But that’s a thing of the past. I’m no longer a Netherworld Sectmember, and neither am I your enemy. I told big brother Chu Feng where you were when you were captured by them. In that regard, you are indebted to me, but I don’t need you to repay the favor. I’m just jealous at how big brother Chu Feng is willing to throw away his life for you.”","Song Yun turned to Chu Feng and continued with a smile, “Big brother Chu Feng, has big sister Zi Ling met our beautiful and adorable little sister Yu’er yet? I wonder if big sister Zi Ling will be jealous, given how much you dote on little sister Yu’er.”","“You don’t need to worry. Your big sister Zi Ling isn’t that narrow-minded,” Chu Feng replied before turning to Little Fishy. “Song Yun is my little sister, too. She likes to joke around, so don’t pay her any mind.”","“It’s true you dote on me though,” Little Fishy replied with a ravishing grin. It felt like she could forget about all her troubles just by looking at Chu Feng. Still, she asked out of curiosity, “Big brother, how did you find this place?”","“Yeah, Brother Chu Feng. I thought you had left the Immemorial Cemetery. What brings you here? And you even have such a huge army with you!” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","“It’s a long story.”","Chu Feng told the Immortal Sea Fish Clan about the circumstances that had led him here, what he had experienced after arriving at the Immemorial Cemetery, and that they were now trapped here and needed to obtain the Seven Stars Orbs to overcome this crisis.","But instead of being worried about their situation, Xianhai Shaoyu looked at the Spirit God Clansmen and exclaimed, “Damn, you have so many Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists aiding you?”","“I’m lucky,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Big brother, are you able to sense the fifth star’s location?” Little Fishy asked.","“Yes, I can sense it.”","“When are we making a move?”","“Right now.”","The group got moving right away.","Along the way, Chu Feng learned that Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu had made significant advancements after returning to their ancestral land, but they later felt something peculiar that prompted them to make their way to the Immemorial Cemetery.","In other words, they were summoned by the Sea Conqueror Saint Exalted’s tomb."]},{"number":6405,"title":"Chapter 6405: Chapter 6403: Another Familiar Face?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6403: Another Familiar Face?","The group made their way to the fifth star.","This time, Chu Feng instructed the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to drive the warship instead of the Spirit God Clan. He had another mission for the Spirit God Clan—construct a reliable and powerful teleportation formation that could transport everyone to a fixed location when activated.","Chu Feng didn’t just sense the location of the fifth star, but he also sensed that the fifth star was different from the first four. The first four only posed a danger if the legacy inheritance failed, but the fifth star’s environment was inherently dangerous.","Worst of all, Chu Feng could sense the danger even from a far distance away, but he couldn’t determine what kind of danger it was.","“Chu Feng, does the legacy inheritance get increasingly harder?” Huangfu Shengyu asked worriedly.","“That seems to be the case, and the danger posed by the fifth star isn’t limited to the legacy. However, risk and reward come hand in hand. The greater the risk, the higher the rewards,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","That only deepened Huangfu Shengyu’s frown.","“Don’t feel pressured, Brother Shengyu. We can leave this legacy to Song Yun,” Chu Feng said.","“Song Yun?” Huangfu Shengyu turned to Song Yun. “You’re... letting this miss decipher the fifth star?”","Even though Song Yun said she was going to do her part earlier, Huangfu Shengyu didn’t take her seriously. He had never heard of Song Yun, and due to the latter concealing her cultivation, he thought that she was far weaker than him.","That was why he thought he would have to bear the responsibility of inheriting the next legacy and was so nervous. He had seen how potent the other legacies were and wasn’t confident.","“Rest assured, she’s very strong.” Chu Feng turned to Song Yun. “Isn’t that so?”","“I’m not that strong, but I’ll accomplish anything big brother Chu Feng entrusts to me,” Song Yun replied with a smile.","Chu Feng suddenly narrowed his eyes.","“What’s wrong, big brother?” Little Fishy asked.","The others also looked at Chu Feng with tense faces, knowing he must have sensed something.","“Someone has begun deciphering the fifth star,” Chu Feng said.","“Ah?”","The crowd was astounded.","“Young friend Chu Feng, should we speed up? I can channel my bloodline power into the warship,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“There’s no need for that. The fifth star’s legacy isn’t that easy. He won’t be able to decipher it before we arrive. We can make it in time with our current speed.”","Chu Feng knew the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief would have to pay a price by using his bloodline power, and there was no need for them to resort to that yet.","Eggy asked, “Chu Feng, which familiar face do you think we’ll meet this time?”","She wasn’t nervous in the least. Instead, she looked forward to learning who was the one deciphering the fifth star.","“Why are you so certain it’s a familiar face? It could be a coincidence,” Chu Feng replied.","“Give it a guess. Could it be Xian Miaomiao? The legacies aren’t limited by age, but the ones drawn to them are all juniors. Most talented juniors you know are already here; the only one left is Xian Miaomiao,” Eggy said.","“That seems to be the case, but I don’t think it would be that coincidental.”","Even though the circumstances suggested it wasn’t a coincidence, Chu Feng somehow felt like it could truly just be a coincidence.","“Chu Feng, why do you think it won’t be that coincidental? Tell me what you’re thinking,” Eggy asked.","“I just think both possibilities are equally likely. The Immemorial Cemetery may be targeting me by choosing seven individuals related to me to decipher the seven stars, but there is also a chance that the Immemorial Cemetery is just seeking the most suitable inheritor for the legacies lying in its countless tombstones.","“The Immemorial Cemetery’s master wields great power, and the world of cultivation is now imposed with many restrictions. It would make sense for him to search for suitable inheritors for these deceased ancestors. It just so happens that I’m acquainted with other talented juniors who are suited for the legacies,” Chu Feng voiced his analysis.","“Hmmm...” Eggy pondered over those words. “That makes sense.”","...","It was a long journey, but the fifth star finally came into sight.","The fifth star looked sinister, emanating a dangerous vibe even when observing it from afar. Most tombstone realms, no matter how they looked inside, appeared as massive tombstones outside, but this tombstone realm comprised two tombstones.","“Lord Chu Feng, we have completed our teleportation formation, but we’ll have to pay a price to channel it. In the meantime, we won’t be able to construct the formation to lend you our powers. However, if we encounter an enemy, we can still fight,” Shen Hui said.","“I’ll leave it to your discretion. If you sense something amiss, don’t hesitate to activate the teleportation formation and bring everyone to somewhere safe,” Chu Feng instructed.","“Understood.” Shen Hui nodded.","The warships rushed ahead, passing through the formation to enter the tombstone realm.","The tombstone realm was covered in white bones, which made it feel even more eerie. However, the crowd was more concerned about who was inheriting the legacy rather than the scenery.","The Spirit God Clan used their observation means to lock onto the target.","Someone was deciphering the formation, but that person wasn’t a human. He was eight meters tall and wore armor that seemed to be his skin. He was a monstrous beast.","“It’s him?” Chu Feng was surprised.","Eggy was right. It was a familiar face."]},{"number":6406,"title":"Chapter 6406: Chapter 6404: The New King","paragraphs":["Chapter 6404: The New King","This was the tombstone realm Jie Mubai had been to, and the armored monstrous beast was the one who attacked him.","Shoosh!","While Chu Feng and the others were observing the armored monstrous beast via the observation formation, the latter, who was about to activate the legacy, suddenly turned to look at them.","Shen Hui frowned. She turned to Chu Feng and said, “Lord Chu Feng, that monstrous beast appears to have noticed us.”","The armored monstrous beast began flitting toward Chu Feng and the others, but what arrived before him was his oppressive might. He was a rank three Heavenly God level cultivator!","Startled, Shen Hui and her clansmen hurriedly constructed a protective formation on par with rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. Huangfu Zhantian raised his cultivation to rank three Heavenly God level, while the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief whipped out his God Armament.","Everyone was tense.","But Chu Feng suddenly spoke up, “Elders, let’s refrain from making a move until he does.”","“Understood,” the crowd replied.","They thought this was Chu Feng’s style of handling matters—he wouldn’t cross others unless they crossed him.","In truth, Chu Feng already recognized the other party—he was the new king!","Back then, Xia Xingchen took him and Huahua to one of the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s forbidden grounds to steal their resources. Upon arriving at the location, Chu Feng quickly noticed something amiss about the place.","The protective formation was already tattered, but he still struggled to get in. It would have been impossible for him to breach the formation at all if the protective formation had been intact. The person who constructed the formation was far stronger than he could have imagined.","And residing in the protective formation was the King Ant Tribe.","Despite the formidable protective formation and the King Ant Tribe’s fearsome appearances, they were actually extremely weak. By the time Chu Feng and the others entered the formation, the King Ant Tribe had already been enslaved by the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect for many years.","Within the King Ant Tribe was a peculiar boy who looked unassuming but wielded influence surpassing the King Ant Tribe’s chieftain. What was even more shocking was his strength.","He noticed the meticulously concealed Chu Feng and led them to the remaining resources, but in exchange, he demanded Chu Feng to rescue all of his tribesmen.","It was no easy feat for Chu Feng and the others to rescue the King Ant Tribe from the well-guarded forbidden ground, but they still pulled it off in the end.","Before parting ways, the boy said that while the deal was an exchange, he owed Chu Feng a favor as the latter erased the imprints on them despite not being obliged to do so.","And the boy was known as the new king. He was much taller than before, but Chu Feng still recognized him at a glance.","Chu Feng didn’t expect the new king to grow so fast. The latter needed to be rescued the last time they met, but in the blink of an eye, he now wielded the strength of a rank three Heavenly God level cultivator.","While the new king had raised his cultivation using his bloodline power, it was also proof of his tremendous talent. So far, of all Heavenly Gods Chu Feng had met, Huangfu Zhantian was the only one who could raise his cultivation by two ranks.","Soon, the armored monstrous beast was close enough for Chu Feng to see him without the aid of the observation formation. He stopped a distance away and called out, “Chu Feng, we meet again.”","This confirmed that he was the new king.","Chu Feng wasn’t surprised, but the others looked at Chu Feng in astonishment.","“T-t-the heck! Brother, y-y-you know this fellow?” Wang Qiang asked.","“I know him,” Chu Feng replied.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you’re frighteningly well-connected!” Huangfu Zhantian exclaimed.","The others didn’t say a word, but their shocked expressions were more than enough to relay their thoughts.","Chu Feng looked at the new king with a tight frown. “New king, how did you become...”","“How did I become so powerful?” the new king completed the sentence. “I ate all my tribesmen.”","“What?” Chu Feng was taken aback. “Your joke isn’t funny.”","“He isn’t joking,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief interjected. He turned to the new king and asked, “If I’m not mistaken, you’re from the King Ant Tribe, right?”","“Have you heard of my tribe?” the new king asked with a lofty tone devoid of respect for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief was irked, but he replied with a chuckle, “You’re indeed from the King Ant Tribe.”","He then turned to Chu Feng and said, “Chu Feng, there is a bizarre tribe in the Ancient Era whose tribesmen believe in sacrificing themselves to strengthen their tribe. It came to a point where there’s only a single person left in the King Ant Tribe, and he proclaimed himself king.","“The king was extremely powerful, so much that he posed a threat to the world of cultivation. Many major powers had to join forces to eradicate him. To think that the King Ant Tribe survived to this day! Chu Feng, are you friends with him?”","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Chu Feng, I know you’re kind, but not everyone can be a friend. The King Ant Tribe devours their kin and friends for power. You can’t befriend someone like that! Now that the new king has gathered the entire tribe’s bloodline, he’ll swiftly grow. We have to eliminate him before he grows too powerful.”","Chu Feng turned to the new king and raised his doubt, “New king, are you the one behind the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s destruction?”","The Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect suffered a tragic fate. Chu Feng deduced that they had offended an Ancient Era’s race, though he had no idea which race it was. Seeing how powerful the new king was now, he had an answer in mind.","“Yes, it’s me. Too bad I don’t know where the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s sectmaster is hiding, or else I’d make him suffer a fate worse than death,” the new king replied with a regretful tone. “Now that you know what kind of entity my King Ant Tribe is, do you intend to listen to that old man’s suggestion?”","“I don’t believe in rumors. I only believe in what I see. It’s none of my business whether your tribesmen are willing to sacrifice themselves to pass their power to you or not. I believe that you aren’t a bad person,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is that so?”","The new king’s gaze suddenly turned cold.","Boom!","Oppressive might gushed over like a wave.","The Spirit God Clansmen’s barrier immediately cracked.","The new king charged up to the barrier and shattered it with a punch.","“My apologies, but you have made the wrong call.”"]},{"number":6407,"title":"Chapter 6407: Chapter 6405: I Want This Legacy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6405: I Want This Legacy","The new king suddenly attacked.","The experts on Chu Feng’s side retaliated. The first one to make a move was the Spirit God Clan.","Whoosh!","Space shook as countless formation chains whizzed forth amid sonic booms to strike the new king. This was the second layer of the Spirit God Clan’s protective formation.","Lightning and waves enveloped the sky as they crashed down upon the new king. Four rank three Heavenly Gods’ auras could be felt from these devastating forces—the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, Huangfu Zhantian, and Little Fishy’s parents.","The latter three were able to raise their cultivation level to rank three Heavenly God by activating their bloodline powers, which showed how exceptionally talented they were.","The new king didn’t sit still as they launched their attacks. The space around him shook, and red light spots and a black aura gushed forth from him like an erupting volcano and clashed with the formation chains, lightning, and waves.","Countless piercing screams echoed from the black aura; it turned out that the red light spots were eyes. The black aura comprised countless ants. These ants were made out of incorporeal aura, but they were powerful enough to suppress the combined prowess of four Heavenly Gods.","Meanwhile, the crowd hurriedly retreated to the warship under the Spirit God Clan’s cover.","The shockwaves arising from clashing Heavenly Gods were too strong for other cultivators to bear. The tombstone realm was still shaken up despite Huangfu Zhantian and the others trying their best to suppress the shockwaves. If not for the Spirit God Clan’s protective formation, there would have been great casualties by now.","“Bad news, Lord Chu Feng.” Shen Hui nervously looked at Chu Feng.","Little Fishy’s parents were highly talented to be able to raise their cultivation by two ranks as Heavenly Gods, so there was no question about their fighting prowess.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and Huangfu Zhantian were strengthened by the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen’s bloodline power, making them slightly more powerful than the former two.","These four were considered strong even among Heavenly Gods. Yet, despite them cooperating with the Spirit God Clan’s formation, they were still being suppressed by the new king.","The battle might have just begun, but the four Heavenly Gods had already gone all out, whereas the new king remained calm, a sign that he still had more aces up his sleeves.","This suggested that the odds weren’t in their favor. At this rate, they might lose the battle.","“Should we escape?” Shen Hui took out a talisman paper. This talisman paper could be used to activate the teleportation formation.","Shen Hui had placed an imprint on everyone before they entered the tombstone realm. By activating the talisman paper, she could immediately transport everyone out of here.","“Shen Hui, you can decide based on how it goes,” Chu Feng said.","“I understand.” Shen Hui nodded.","Shoosh!","The entire sky suddenly darkened. The new king released a black aura that swiftly spread outward while manifesting humongous spikes. These spikes harnessed immense destructive prowess that pierced through even space itself.","The four Heavenly Gods couldn’t stop it. Even the Spirit God Clan’s formation chains and protective formation shattered in its face.","That black aura was not a martial skill or a secret skill; it resembled a bloodline power. It was a unique move to the new king!","“Lord Chu Feng, we have to leave now!” Shen Hui said as she ignited the talisman paper.","“You don’t have to waste that means,” the new king said as he retracted his black aura and oppressive might.","Shen Hui hesitated, not knowing what the new king meant by that, though those words were clearly directed toward her. To be safe, she clutched the talisman paper tightly in her hands.","“Little ant, why are you stopping now?” Huangfu Zhantian roared in indignation. He would have continued the fight if not for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief stopping him.","He was angry that he couldn’t get the better of the new king despite giving it his all, and he thought this was a stain on his reputation as a prodigy. On top of that, he was irked by the new king’s arrogant attitude.","The new king ignored Huangfu Zhantian and looked at Chu Feng, speaking with an earnest tone, “I was joking earlier. If you think of me as a friend, I’ll recognize you as one, too.”","Chu Feng smiled. “I knew you can be trusted.”","“What makes you say that?” the new king asked.","“We could have simply parted ways when our partnership ended, but you said you owed me a favor. From that, I know you are someone who can be befriended,” Chu Feng replied.","“What makes you think it isn’t mere pleasantries?” the new king asked.","“You aren’t the type to speak pleasantries.”","“You’re awfully confident of my character when we have only known each other for a short time.”","“You don’t judge a person’s character based on how long you know them, but whether they can be relied on when things happen. We have put our lives on the line on our previous partnership. I’d say that’s already a good gauge of our characters.”","“That’s reasonable.” The new king revealed a rare smile.","“Are we continuing the fight?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","The new king finally looked at Huangfu Zhantian. “You wouldn’t stand a chance if I get serious.”","“What a joke. How’d you know if I was serious.” Huangfu Zhantian refused to give in.","The new king turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Are you here for this legacy? I can give it to you, but it won’t be easy to activate the legacy.”","“Are you confident of activating it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Me? Of course I am,” the new king replied.","“That’s good enough for me.” Chu Feng told the new king about the Seven Stars Orbs.","“All right, I’ll help you on that. However, that can’t be considered as repaying your favor. It’s a trivial matter compared to you saving my life,” the new king replied.","Chu Feng smiled.","Just then, Song Yun suddenly spoke up, “I want this legacy.”"]},{"number":6408,"title":"Chapter 6408: Chapter 6406: Demon Heavenly Exalted’s Tombstone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6406: Demon Heavenly Exalted’s Tombstone","The crowd turned their eyes to Song Yun, including the new king. In particular, Huangfu Shengyu and the others were bewildered by her maneuver.","They could tell how dangerous the legacy was, and they would have avoided it wherever possible. It was a blessing that the new king wanted to activate and take the legacy, so why was Song Yun coveting it?","The new king eyed Song Yun before turning to Chu Feng. “Who is this person?”","“She’s a friend,” Chu Feng replied.","The new king finally turned to Song Yun and asked, “Are you afraid of death?”","“Who isn’t afraid of death?” Song Yun replied.","“This legacy can be shared, but most people can’t withstand it. They’ll die if they fail to do so,” the new king replied.","“I’ll just have to withstand it then,” Song Yun smiled.","“You’re very confident in yourself.”","The new king was surprised. He realized from Song Yun’s smile that she was much more than what she appeared. Anyone with eyes could tell the legacy wouldn’t be easy to inherit, and most people wouldn’t even dare step into this tombstone realm.","But Song Yun was unfazed. Her calmness didn’t appear to be feigned.","“I plan to stand at the top of the world of cultivation with big brother Chu Feng. I should at least have the confidence to inherit a mere legacy,” Song Yun replied.","“A mere legacy? Don’t get ahead of yourself. This legacy isn’t as simple as you think,” the new king said.","Just then, Chu Feng interjected, “Can the two of you not compete for this legacy? I trust your capabilities, but there are two more stars after this, and their legacies will be harder to activate and inherit. There’s no need to compete over this one. Our goal is to decipher all seven stars. I can take a star, but there’ll be no one to take the last one if you two share this legacy.”","“Chu Feng, this legacy is highly compatible with me. If you want it, I can give you all of it. However, if you’re planning to give it to your friend instead, the most I can do is to share it with her on your account. I’ll be frank with you. Something has been summoning me ever since I step foot into the Immemorial Cemetery, and it led me here. This legacy was prepared for me,” the new king said.","Chu Feng turned to Song Yun. Since the new king was summoned here, he would rather she take the next star.","Song Yun replied with a smile, “Big brother Chu Feng, I was summoned here as well. I merely took a detour to look for you first.”","“You were summoned here, too?” The new king was baffled.","“Why else would I compete with you over this legacy?” Song Yun replied. “Big brother Chu Feng, I understand we have to activate the seven stars, but I can tell from the summon that I have to obtain this legacy, or else I’ll regret it for life.”","“Miss, can’t you prioritize the bigger picture? We’re all going to die here if we can’t overcome this crisis. It will be meaningless even if you obtain the legacy,” Huangfu Zhantian said.","“Big brother Chu Feng will find a solution, right?” Song Yun said with a smile.","“I wouldn’t be advising you against it if I had a solution.” Chu Feng sighed.","“My apologies, big brother Chu Feng, but I’m not giving up on this legacy.” Song Yun refused to budge despite looking apologetic.","Chu Feng turned to the new king and asked, “Are you certain you two can inherit the legacy together without hurting each other?”","“Yes, we can inherit the legacy together. The legacy itself is dangerous, but she should be able to withstand it if she isn’t lying about being summoned here.”","The new king eyed Song Yun. He hoped she would activate the legacy with him, mainly because he thought she was lying and wanted her to pay the price for it.","“All right. You can activate the legacy together,” Chu Feng said.","Even though he hoped one of them could take on the next star, he couldn’t guarantee their success there. What if they failed? Besides, he didn’t like to force others to act against their will. Even if there was no one to take on the sixth star, they could only take a step at a time.","Thus, the crowd made their way to the two tombstones.","The two tombstones resembled buildings. They weren’t linked, but they were close, and there was a door in one of them. What they needed to open first was not the legacy but the door.","“The activation of the legacy can be divided into two stages. The first stage can be done with either of us—we just need to decipher the tombstone. I have already completed that step and can open the door right away.”","The new king placed his hand on the door, and the world shook. Peculiar energy was pulsating from the door. Moments later, countless runes appeared on the door.","The door opened, revealing a dark corridor.","At the same time, a light pillar gushed out from the underground into the sky, and words appeared on the previously empty tombstones.","The tombstone with the door wrote: Demon Heavenly Exalted’s Tombstone.","The other tombstone wrote: Nine Pupils Demon Aura’s Tombstone .","“Are these two tombstones?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","The new king ignored Huangfu Zhantian’s question and looked at Chu Feng. “This tombstone contains the Demon Heavenly Exalted’s legacy. I didn’t receive any information about the Nine Pupils Demon Aura, but it could be the Demon Heavenly Exalted’s pet or companion. They might have been buried together because of that.”","After meticulously explaining the situation to Chu Feng, the new king turned to Song Yun. “We’re in the second stage now. We have to enter the door, but there will be no turning back. Failure means death. It’s not too late to give up now if you’re afraid.”","Song Yun flashed a brilliant smile at Chu Feng. “Wait for me here, big brother Chu Feng.”","With her hands behind her, she leisurely skipped her way toward the dark corridor, looking relaxed even in this critical moment.","The new king laughed under his breath before following her."]},{"number":6409,"title":"Chapter 6409: Chapter 6407: The Immemorial Monstrous Beast Emerges","paragraphs":["Chapter 6407: The Immemorial Monstrous Beast Emerges","“Don’t worry, Chu Feng. I’m sure they’ll pull it off. Since there are people summoned for the five stars we have encountered so far, there should be people summoned for the last two stars, too. We don’t have to worry about there being no one to activate and inherit the legacy... though it’s weird that you haven’t felt the summoning,” Eggy remarked.","“Yeah, I haven’t felt the summoning. I hope everything goes well.”","Chu Feng was confident of activating a star, but there was no one suitable for the other one within their current group. However, he wasn’t too worried as Eggy’s words made perfect sense. The Immemorial Cemetery should have picked someone suitable for the last two legacies.","Thus, he sat down and began his cultivation.","He wasn’t the one who activated the legacy here, so he didn’t know much about it. It would be entirely up to the new king and Song Yun whether they succeeded or not.","The others also went to cultivate, especially for Yuwen Yanri, Wang Qiang, Bai Yunqing, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu. They had acquired a legacy each but hadn’t fully assimilated them yet. So, they were working on it whenever they had time.","Some time later, everyone abruptly opened their eyes and floated into the sky to look at the second tombstone. The ground shook intensely, and cracks appeared. It looked like the earth was going to implode at this rate.","And this phenomenon came from the tombstone inscribed with the words Nine Pupils Demon Aura’s Tombstone. It was shaking so lightly that mortals could hardly perceive it, yet it was this light shaking that threatened to collapse the ground.","“Could that tombstone be a sealing formation?” Chu Feng frowned. He turned to Shen Hui and instructed, “Shen Hui, construct a sealing formation.”","Shen Hui, as a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, came to the same conclusion as Chu Feng. The moment Chu Feng gave the instruction, the Spirit God Clan began constructing a formation.","In a few moments, a towering formation enveloped the tombstone, coiling around it layer after layer.","However, the tombstone continued to shake, to the point where cracks appeared on its surface. A powerful energy suddenly poured out of the tombstone. With its indomitable might, it crashed through the Spirit God Clan’s sealing formation in an instant.","Boom!","The world was enveloped by the eerie purple energy, making it look as if they had plummeted from the mortal world into hell.","“Oh no.”","Even the usually calm Chu Feng frowned. The crowd was bound in place, incapable of moving. Eggy tried to open the gate to head out and protect Chu Feng, but she was unable to do so.","“Chu Feng, why can’t I open the gate?” Confused, Eggy thought Chu Feng was behind this.","“It’s a skill that prevents one from utilizing any means, unless one is stronger than the other party. Not even the World Spirit Gate can be opened,” Chu Feng replied.","“What happened? Is there something alive inside the tombstone?” Eggy was feeling uneasy. If she couldn’t even leave the World Spirit Gate, she wouldn’t be able to use any of her means.","“Looks like there is indeed something terrifying sealed inside that tombstone.” Chu Feng could move his eyes despite being unable to move.","Everyone’s eyes were focused on the tombstone. Dark purple energy was seeping out from the tombstone’s cracks; it was even darker than the purple energy enveloping the sky, though they had the same aura.","The crack on the tombstone grew increasingly bigger. Something terrifying was about to emerge, but they couldn’t do anything about it. Even fleeing was not an option for them.","Grar!","Boom!","A loud roar shook the world as the tombstone shattered into pieces. Smoke puffed into the sky. A behemoth of over ten thousand meters tall stood amid the smoke.","As the smoke scattered, the crowd saw a ferocious aura beast that didn’t have a tangible body. It was shaped like a lion, with four strong limbs and a tail.","What was most eye-catching about it was its eye. It only had one eye, but it was humongous, spanning half of its head. In that massive eye was nine irises, making it look eerie, disgusting, and unnerving.","It was likely the Nine Pupils Demon Aura stated on the tombstone.","The Nine Pupils Demon Aura looked at Chu Feng and the others.","Chu Feng and the others couldn’t even utter a word. Naturally, the Spirit God Clan couldn’t utilize the teleportation formation they had constructed beforehand, too. They were all lambs waiting to be slaughtered.","Finally, the Nine Pupils Demon Aura set its gaze on five individuals—Bai Yunqing, Wang Qiang, Yuwen Yanri, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh shoosh shoosh!","Five auras resembling needles shot out from the Nine Pupils Demon Aura, and they pierced through the bodies of the five individuals. These auras harnessed unthinkable energy, and the damage they dealt was more than what it appeared.","Little Fishy and the others screamed in pain.","“Damn it!” Chu Feng frowned. His eyes hardened in determination.","Just then, a voice echoed in the sky, “A monstrous beast abandoned in the old era dares to wreak havoc?”","At the same time, the crowd realized they had regained control of their bodies. They raised their heads to look in the direction where the voice was coming from.","The Nine Pupils Demon Aura did the same, too. It decisively severed the auras torturing Little Fishy and the others, unfurled its massive claws, and sprinted toward the voice.","Boom!","The world shook. The purple energy enveloping the world was severed into two.","A twirling axe fell from the sky, flying toward the Nine Pupils Demon Aura. The axe was normal-sized, but it harnessed a tremendous aura. It felt strong enough to destroy even the entire tombstone realm!","The Nine Pupils Demon Aura halted its footsteps. It unleashed a piercing roar, and its body swiftly expanded to over tens of thousands of meters tall. Then, it shot out countless purple auras in the form of arrows toward the axe.","No, it wasn’t an attack.","The purple auras, after flying some distance away from the Nine Pupils Demon Aura, interweaved to form a protective net. Even the Nine Pupils Demon Aura knew it couldn’t rival the axe, so it quickly put up a defensive barrier.","But the axe suddenly disappeared. A cold glint flashed across the sky. Before the crowd could react, the Nine Pupils Demon Aura was already sliced into two.","The axe continued to twirl downward after hacking through the Nine Pupils Demon Aura.","This made the crowd worried. If the axe landed on the ground, the tombstone realm might be severed into two. Just as the axe was about to land on the ground, a hand shot out and held it.","It was an unassuming middle-aged man. He was accompanied by a young lady with yellow hair, blue eyes, and sharp ears."]},{"number":6410,"title":"Chapter 6410: Chapter 6408: True Danger","paragraphs":["Chapter 6408: True Danger","“Miaomiao! Elder Song!” Chu Feng was overjoyed to see the two of them.","The ones who had just arrived were Xian Miaomiao and her master, Song Changsheng.","Chu Feng knew that Song Changsheng was extremely powerful, a true hidden expert in the world of cultivation. It could be seen as much from how he had made quick work of the Nine Pupils Demon Aura.","But Chu Feng didn’t head over to greet them right away.","Instead, he went up to Little Fishy and the others to check their conditions. They weren’t in a good state, but fortunately, their lives weren’t in danger. It would take time, but they would make a full recovery.","Bai Yunqing took out a few pills and handed them around. Then, he constructed a recovery formation.","Both his pills and formation were potent, such that Chu Feng didn’t have to make a move.","“It’s him? They do know each other!”","Huangfu Zhantian was taken aback. He had already met Song Changsheng at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith and lost to him. He knew Song Changsheng was unfathomably powerful, and it was due to his warning that he dared not harm Chu Feng.","Chu Feng flashed a smile at Xian Miaomiao, the latter responded with a beaming smile, too. This was enough for them to relay their sentiments to each other.","Chu Feng headed to them and first bowed to Song Changsheng. “Paying respect to elder.”","The latter was not just Xian Miaomiao’s master but his master’s friend, too.","“We meet again, young friend Chu Feng,” Song Changsheng said with a smile.","Chu Feng was overjoyed to meet Song Changsheng, for he had been wanting to ask the latter about the Darkness Monstrous God’s soul. He had learned that the little girl was the Darkness Monstrous God’s soul, and Song Changsheng had taken her away.","The realm suddenly began stirring.","“They have succeeded,” Chu Feng remarked as if he had expected as much.","The tombstone’s door opened, and the new king and Song Yun walked out. Their foreheads carried a rune imprint. Both of them simultaneously glanced at the other tombstone, which had crumbled after the Nine Pupils Demon Aura was defeated.","Song Yun walked up to Chu Feng and asked, “I’m glad you’re fine, big brother. Did that elder deal with that monstrous beast?”","“You know about the monstrous beast’s unsealing?” Chu Feng asked.","Before Song Yun could reply, the new king stepped forward and said, “It’s my fault. That monstrous beast is the Nine Pupils Demon Aura. It’s an immemorial monstrous beast created by the Demon Heavenly Exalted.","“The legacy is divided into two phases. The first phase involves obtaining the Demon Heavenly Exalted’s legacy. If the first phase is cleared, the challenger can choose to challenge the second phase and attempt to establish control over the Nine Pupils Demon Aura.","“I was greedy. I ignored this lady’s advice and insisted on challenging the second phase, but I failed. That resulted in the Nine Pupils Demon Aura getting unsealed and running rampant. I’m glad that you’re fine.”","The new king sounded conscience-stricken.","Chu Feng and the others finally understood why the Nine Pupils Demon Aura suddenly appeared without any warning.","“You bastard! You nearly had us all killed! Do you know what monster you have unleashed on us? Do you see their conditions? This was all done by the Nine Pupils Demon Aura! If not for this elder stepping in to save us, we would have died a dog’s death!” Huangfu Zhantian pointed at pale-faced Bai Yunqing and the others as he bellowed.","“My apologies.” In a rare show of apology, the new king lowered his head to Huangfu Zhantian. He also understood how huge his mistake was.","“Forget it. We’re fine anyway,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","He was feeling better after some recuperation, so he stood up with Little Fishy and walked up to Song Changsheng.","Yuwen Yanri and Bai Yunqing caught his drift and followed suit.","They walked up to Song Changsheng and bowed in unison. “Elder, thank you for saving our lives.”","“It was nothing,” Song Changsheng replied with a faint smile.","He wasn’t planning to reveal himself at the start, since he could have dealt with this situation while remaining hidden. But this time, he wanted to show himself.","“T-t-the heck! Miaomiao, is this your master? I didn’t k-k-know your master is so overpowered!” Wang Qiang exclaimed. He respectfully bowed to Song Changsheng as well and said, “Junior W-W-Wang Qiang pays respect to elder!”","Song Changsheng nodded with a smile.","“Why are all of you gathered together?” Xian Miaomiao asked.","“It’s a coincidence.” Chu Feng told Song Changsheng and Xian Miaomiao about the Seven Stars Orb.","“That would mean you have been chosen. As expected, there’s more to the Immemorial Cemetery than I thought,” Song Changsheng remarked.","“Elder, what brings you and Miaomiao here? Were you summoned here?” Chu Feng asked.","“It wasn’t because of a summon. I felt great danger lurking here, and it felt like everyone might die if it wasn’t promptly resolved,” Song Changsheng replied.","“H-h-heavens! Elder, did you sense the N-N-Nine Pupils Demon Aura?” Wang Qiang asked.","“No, encountering that being was a coincidence. The danger is still present,” Song Changsheng replied.","“The danger is still present?”","The crowd tensed up. Song Changsheng’s words implied that there was something more dangerous than the Nine Pupils Demon Aura here.","Chu Feng activated his Heaven’s Eye to survey the surroundings, but he couldn’t find anything. Thus, he switched to the Three Realms Divine Eyes. What he saw horrified him.","A bizarre aura that could only be seen through the Three Realms Divine Eyes was coiling behind the tombstone.","“It’s there.”","As soon as Chu Feng uttered those words, the bizarre aura erupted like a volcano, and a door several times taller than the tombstone rose from the ground.","Everyone lost their composure.","The door resembled a pitch-black tombstone, and it emanated overwhelming pressure. Contained inside the door was an aura far more terrifying than the Nine Pupils Demon Aura’s."]},{"number":6411,"title":"Chapter 6411: Chapter 6409: Top-notch Expert","paragraphs":["Chapter 6409: Top-notch Expert","“What’s that?”","The sight of the door made the crowd feel uneasy.","“Lord Chu Feng.” Shen Hui took out the talisman paper to activate the teleportation formation.","Even the Nine Pupils Demon Aura was beyond them. They wouldn’t stand any chance against what was lurking inside the door. Their only option was to escape right now.","Sensing Shen Hui’s intention, Song Changsheng said, “We’re trapped here. Escaping won’t solve the problem. Miaomiao, you stay with Chu Feng. Chu Feng, get your friends to retreat from the door.”","With that, Song Changsheng marched toward the door with his axe.","The crowd knew what Song Changsheng was going to do, and they hurriedly retreated on their own accord.","Boom!","As if sensing a challenger, the door slowly opened.","The crowd stiffened up out of nervousness. They couldn’t imagine what was behind the door.","But much to their surprise, the immense pressure vanished after the door opened. What appeared in the door was not a cavern nor a palace, but compressed space. Inside the space were many humongous tombstones.","It was the Immemorial Cemetery.","The door seemed to take them out of the tombstone realm back into the Immemorial Cemetery.","“What’s that place? Why does it l-l-look like the Immemorial Cemetery?” Wang Qiang asked.","“That could be the Immemorial Cemetery as well, but a deeper area,” Chu Feng replied.","Shoosh!","The immense pressure reappeared. It was coming from a person within the door.","That person was muscular and stood at two meters tall. He wore black armor and carried a black saber on his shoulder. Both his armor and his saber emitted black auras. His face was obscured by his armor, revealing only a pair of blood-colored eyes filled with bloodthirst.","He felt even more terrifying than a ferocious beast.","Boom!","A powerful aura rippled from the door. It was so overwhelming that Chu Feng and the others felt as if their breath would stop at any moment.","The world split into two.","The half where Chu Feng and the others stood remained intact, but the other half cracked and its land disintegrated into nothing. It was due to that person’s oppressive might!","“This...”","Even the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master, Shen Hui, and the others were appalled.","All of them would have been dead if not for Song Changsheng blocking the oppressive might.","“Interesting,” a hoarse but resonating voice echoed from the person.","He began walking over with his saber. He moved at a casual pace, yet every step he took covered a colossal distance. With just a few steps, he arrived at the door and stepped out.","Then, he froze in place. His crimson eyes widened in shock.","“You...” he murmured in disbelief.","Song Changsheng suddenly appeared before him like a specter, hacking his axe into his head. That person barely managed to get a word out before disintegrating.","“How arrogant,” voices echoed from within the door.","Thousands of people appeared on the other side of the door.","“There are so many of them?”","The crowd was astounded.","These people wore the same armor, but they had different physiques and wielded different weapons. They weren’t mere clones. There was an army of these powerful beings, and what they were seeing might not be all.","“H-how can we win against this?” Huangfu Zhantian blurted out, feeling helpless and despair.","Little needed to be said about how the others were feeling when even the Heavenly Gods were already in despair.","Shoosh shoosh!","A cold gleam flashed.","Before the crowd could register what had happened, Song Changsheng’s axe twirled out of the door and returned to his hand.","The thousand powerful people inside the door disintegrated.","Song Changsheng killed all of them in an instant!","“This!”","The crowd stared at Song Changsheng in disbelief.","“To think there is someone like that in the present world of cultivation!”","The stronger those people were, the more formidable Song Changsheng appeared. The immense security they felt from him washed away their feelings of helplessness and despair. The strength he had displayed far surpassed their understanding.","How could someone this strong exist in the present world of cultivation?","“This is tricky.” Song Changsheng sighed. He turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Are you confident of dealing with the Seven Stars Orb?”","He didn’t wait for Chu Feng’s answer before continuing, “You’ll have to resolve it even if you aren’t confident. This could be a sealed region of the Immemorial Cemetery, and this door is their way out. There is only one door now, but it will be a catastrophe if more spawns elsewhere. I’ll have to march into their nest and vanquish them all.”","“Be careful, elder. We can settle things on this side,” Chu Feng replied.","“You take care as well,” Song Changsheng replied before stepping through the door.","Once he was inside, he tossed out a martial power token, which expanded into a shield that sealed off the door. Nothing could slip out from the door anymore.","The crowd remained shaken. They were relieved Song Changsheng appeared at the right time, or else they wouldn’t even have had the chance to escape.","Having witnessed Song Changsheng’s overwhelming strength, the crowd turned to Xian Miaomiao. Even the usually proud powerhouses carried deference in their eyes, knowing she was Song Changsheng’s disciple."]},{"number":6412,"title":"Chapter 6412: Chapter 6410: The New Taking Over the Old","paragraphs":["Chapter 6410: The New Taking Over the Old","“What is that place? Why are there so many terrifying people there? It’s a relief they are trapped in there. It’ll be a calamity if they escape!” Huangfu Zhantian cursed, but more than that, he was feeling unnerved.","“It’s a good thing with that this miss’ master,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said as he walked up to Xian Miaomiao. “You are Miss Xian, right? I am the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief. I know there is a misunderstanding between you and Huangfu Shengyu at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith.”","He glared at Huangfu Shengyu and roared, “Shengyu, come and apologize!”","Huangfu Shengyu obediently rushed over, looking nothing like the arrogant man they had met at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith.","“You don’t need to apologize. Reconciling with Chu Feng is the same as reconciling with me,” Xian Miaomiao said.","Xian Miaomiao had been secretly communicating with Chu Feng, and she had already been updated about Chu Feng and the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s current relationship.","“I’m surprised you’re alive,” Xian Miaomiao said teasingly.","“I have to thank Chu Feng for showing me mercy for that,” Huangfu Shengyu replied with an awkward smile. He didn’t expect the woman whom he looked down on would have such strong backing.","“I am the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master. Miss, thank you for taking care of our Yanri at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith,” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master stepped forth to greet Xian Miaomiao.","“You’re being too polite. We were looking out for one another, and Yanri is strong enough to not require anyone’s help,” Xian Miaomiao replied.","She knew these important figures were only being friendly to her because of her master. The world of cultivation was pragmatic, showing little regard for the weak and fawning on the strong.","On this aspect, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion were already quite good, in the sense where they were polite but not to the extent of subservience.","After trading pleasantries, Xian Miaomiao turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Chu Feng, you already know the location of the sixth star, right?”","Their priority was to complete the Seven Stars Orbs. This place was too dangerous. They needed to leave this place as soon as possible.","“I do. Surprisingly, the sixth star is located at the entrance of the Immemorial Cemetery,” Chu Feng said with a smile.","“At the entrance?”","The crowd was surprised. All of them entered via the entrance, and they had been closely examining all the tombstone realms along the way, be it using their means or with the help of treasures. Yet, none of them noticed any special tombstone realms at the entrance.","The difficulty and reward from the legacies should increase as they advanced down the Seven Stars Orbs. In other words, all of them had overlooked a potent tombstone realm.","The group quickly set off.","“Miaomiao, what’s your current cultivation level?” Wang Qiang asked out of curiosity.","“Rank nine True God level,” Xian Miaomiao replied as she revealed her aura.","“T-t-the heck! Are you sure this is y-y-your base cultivation, and that you didn’t secretly r-r-raise your cultivation? You still needed me to p-p-protect you in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith, but it looks like I’ll be under your p-p-protection now. Little sister Miaomiao, you’re g-g-growing too fast!”","Wang Qiang was awed. The others were stunned as well, including those from the older generation.","At rank nine True God level, Xian Miaomiao was just a step away from reaching Heavenly God. Such a feat would have been unthinkable for a junior in the past.","“Chu Feng was the one protecting me in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith.” Xian Miaomiao rolled her eyes before explaining with a smile, “It’s all thanks to my master. He took the time and effort to find many valuable resources, and that gave rise to the current me.”","She secretly sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng, “I’ve gained a stronger grasp of the Soul Fog with my master’s help. That’s the reason my cultivation grew so quickly.”","At the same time, she asked, “It looks like you still haven’t grasped control of the Genesis Bloodline yet, right?”","She was well aware of Chu Feng’s talent. The Genesis Bloodline and the Soul Fog were top-notch powers nurtured within their respective galaxies, and they were deemed to be of the same level.","But Song Changsheng, unable to awaken the Genesis Bloodline, suspected that the Genesis Bloodline was superior to the Soul Fog. If Chu Feng were to grasp the Genesis Bloodline, his cultivation would surely grow by leaps and bounds.","“Yes, I haven’t grasped control of it. I can sense its presence, but I’m unable to tap into it. Perhaps the time isn’t ripe yet,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“It must be. If even you can’t conquer the Genesis Bloodline, no one else can.” Xian Miaomiao had the utmost confidence in Chu Feng. Her cultivation was above Chu Feng not because she was more talented than him, but because of her master’s means.","Chu Feng had been doing everything himself all along.","“Is that new king a junior?” Xian Miaomiao asked. Her instinct told her that the new king was a junior.","“New king, are you a junior?” Chu Feng asked the new king.","The others pricked up their ears out of curiosity. As powerful as Xian Miaomiao was, the new king was even stronger. It would be insane if the new king was a junior as well.","“I am a junior if you start counting from my birth year, but I have existed for a very, very long time now,” the new king replied.","“H-h-how long?” Wang Qiang asked.","The new king ignored Wang Qiang and instead looked at Chu Feng, as if to say that he would only answer the question if Chu Feng wanted to know the answer, too.","“I’m curious as well,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“I don’t have memories of that time, but I think I was already being nurtured even in the Ancient Era,” the new king replied.","“Did your m-m-mum carry you for so long?” Wang Qiang blurted out in astonishment.","“Brother Wang Qiang, you should speak less if you don’t know how to speak. If not for Chu Feng, I wouldn’t have been surprised if he had slapped you to death. You know he’s a Heavenly God, right?” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","The new king couldn’t be deemed as a normal junior, considering the long nurturing period before his birth. However, his level of strength wouldn’t have been surprising even if he was a normal junior. The King Ant Tribe had been extremely powerful back in the Ancient Era.","“It’s God’s Era indeed,” the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master remarked.","He knew it was only a matter of time before the younger generation took over, but he didn’t expect this day to arrive so quickly. Only the new king had overtaken him thus far, but he did not doubt that it wouldn’t take long for Chu Feng and the others to surpass him, too.","Older folks like him were doomed to lag in this race."]},{"number":6413,"title":"Chapter 6413: Chapter 6411: Xiahou Jue","paragraphs":["Chapter 6411: Xiahou Jue","Many powers were gathered at the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance. They had come to watch the commotion, only to be sucked into the Immemorial Cemetery right before it closed.","They dared not to venture in, so they continued to linger at the entrance. They were hoping that the entrance would open soon so that they could leave this place.","Little did they know that a humble tombstone realm nearby was drawing a huge army over, and this tombstone realm was none other than the sixth star.","“T-t-the heck! Is this it?” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","The group had already inspected the tombstone even when they were still a distance away. They found nothing special about it, but they thought they were just too far away, and that they should notice something peculiar when they observed it close up.","They were close to the tombstone realm now, but they still failed to find anything special about it. It still looked as normal as it was before. It felt like an average tombstone realm with nothing good inside, so much so that they wouldn’t have been surprised if it was empty.","“Yes, this is it. There’s no mistake,” Chu Feng replied confidently. He turned to Shen Hui, who controlled their escape teleportation formation, and said, “The sixth star will be more difficult to deal with. It could be different from the other tombstone realms we have been to. We need to be more vigilant than before.”","“Don’t worry, Lord Chu Feng,” Shen Hui replied.","The crowd dared not to let their guard down. They faced no trouble passing through the formation layer, but the moment they entered the formation realm, Chu Feng felt an ominous premonition.","Before they could examine the tombstone realm, the sky suddenly turned blood-red. Thick, crimson smoke resembling fresh blood had enveloped the sky, and it harnessed tremendous energy.","“It’s a sealing formation. Lord Chu Feng, the teleportation formation has been sealed off,” Shen Hui said apologetically. She could still invoke the talisman paper, but the teleportation formation they had prepared wouldn’t work.","Huangfu Zhantian also noticed something was amiss and raised his cultivation. He whipped out his God Armament spear and thrust it toward the crimson aura.","Boom!","The crimson aura rippled, but it remained unfazed.","“What’s going on? Is it a trap?” Huangfu Zhantian murmured with a tight frown.","The crimson aura was formidable, but it wasn’t native to the tombstone realm, evident from how it was at odds with the tombstone realm’s aura.","“Over there.”","The area where Chu Feng looked at distorted, and a figure appeared out of thin air. He was dressed in a red cloak, a red, veiled bamboo hat, and a red cape. Written on the cape were the words ‘Netherworld Marshall’.","“It’s someone from the Netherworld Sect?”","The crowd was surprised. Why would someone from the Netherworld Realm be here? Could he be the culprit behind the terrifying crimson aura?","“Song Yun?”","Before Chu Feng could say anything, the Netherworld Marshall cast his eyes on Song Yun. His voice resembled that of a middle-aged man.","But with the exception of Huangfu Zhantian, Chu Feng, Song Yun, and the others was still hiding inside a concealment formation. The Netherworld Marshall’s ability to see through their concealment, as well as the crimson aura sealing off the tombstone realm, made it clear that he was extremely powerful.","“Lord Xiahou? What are you doing here?” Song Yun asked in surprise.","At the same time, she sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng and the other key figures of the group. “He is Xiahou Jue, a Netherworld Marshall belonging to the new faction. He and the others in the Netherworld Sect’s upper echelons went into closed-door training at the same time, and they were at Heavenly God level before then.","“I don’t know whether their closed-door training succeeded or not, but if it succeeded, they would have grasped the power of the Netherworld Embryo. If so, it’d be tough for me to estimate how much stronger he is now.”","Xiahou Jue took off his veiled bamboo hat, revealing a ghastly-pale, emaciated face. His eyes were emanating the same crimson aura that enveloped the tombstone realm. He likely noticed them due to the crimson aura.","This crimson aura was also at odds with his own aura; it was likely from an external treasure.","“The Netherworld Sect has been around since the nascent years of the present era, and it has many formidable treasures in its grasp. However, these treasures can only be channeled with a sufficiently powerful Netherworld Embryo. He must have succeeded in his closed-door training, granting him further control over the Netherworld Embryo to channel those treasures,” Song Yun warned.","“I chanced upon the Immemorial Cemetery right after I emerged from my closed-door training, so I came to join the commotion. It’s a huge coincidence. The Immemorial Cemetery closed the moment I came in here. I wouldn’t have been able to get in here if I was any slower.","“Perhaps I was lucky, but I received a directive from the Immemorial Cemetery to kill everyone who steps into this tombstone realm. If I succeed, I’ll receive a huge benefit. I didn’t expect so many people to come here. It must be a truly huge benefit,” Xiahou Jue spoke with a smile.","He looked at Chu Feng and the others as if they were sheep in the slaughterhouse.","“So, h-h-he’s here to ambush us. But how does he know w-w-we’ll be here? Is he the one planning to s-s-stop us from forming the Seven Stars Orbs?” Wang Qiang asked.","Chu Feng didn’t say a word. Something felt amiss. Someone was keeping track of their movements, but he couldn’t tell if this was someone’s scheme or the directive of the Immemorial Cemetery’s directive.","“Lord Xiahou, could this be a misunderstanding?” Song Yun asked.","“Misunderstanding? How so? I was promised a benefit if I killed you. Would you give up on this opportunity if you were in my shoes?” Xiahou Jue asked.","“Lord Xiahou, my friends are here as well. Can you spare them on my account? We have grasped the initiative in the Immemorial Cemetery, and there are fortuitous encounters to be found all around. We’ll compensate you severalfold,” Song Yun replied.","“Spare them on your account? Song Yun, you’re a Netherworld Sectmember, but you aren’t wearing your uniform and are instead hanging out with these people. You must have betrayed our sect, haven’t you?” Xiahou Jue asked.","“Lord Xiahou, that joke isn’t funny. The Netherworld Sect has treated me well. I’d never betray the sect! I’m under the Netherworld Sect’s orders to explore the Immemorial Cemetery. I’m only with my friends to better accomplish the mission,” Song Yun replied.","Song Yun knew Xiahou Jue rarely intervened with sect affairs, and he had only just emerged from his closed-door training. There was a chance he hadn’t received news about her leaving the Netherworld Sect yet, so she thought she could pretend that she was still a Netherworld Sectmember to convince him to spare them.","“Hah... You’re a resourceful one to have made so many friends. But Song Yun, humans are inherently greedy. I’d receive a huge fortuitous encounter by killing you. Even if you are here under the Netherworld Sect’s order, you’re still doomed to die here today. Only I, Xiahou Jue, will leave this place alive today,” Xiahou Jue declared confidently.","“Damn it! That bastard wants to kill us all. Why are we wasting words on him? Let’s screw him over already!”","Unable to tolerate it anymore, Huangfu Zhantian brandished his spear to slice Xiahou Jue into half, but the strike dissipated before it could reach. Xiahou Jue casually unleashed a sliver of his oppressive might.","That was enough to plunge the crowd into despair.","Xiahou Jue was a rank four Heavenly God!"]},{"number":6414,"title":"Chapter 6414: Chapter 6412: Promise of Ten Days","paragraphs":["Chapter 6412: Promise of Ten Days","A searing aura suddenly assaulted the crowd from all directions. It only took an instant for everyone to be sweating profusely. The heat was unbearable.","To deal with the incoming heat, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief unleashed his martial power, and Shen Hui hurriedly constructed a formation. Even so, the heat remained unbearable for most people.","“Damn it! W-w-what is this? Are we in a c-c-cauldron?” Wang Qiang exclaimed in a fluster.","Flames were raging all around them, both in the sky and on earth. It felt like the world had transformed into a pill cauldron.","“He isn’t the one behind the flames,” Chu Feng said with a frown.","While Xiahou Jue was a powerful rank four Heavenly God antagonistic to them, the flames around them didn’t contain his aura. The flames felt like the Immemorial Cemetery’s tribute formation.","He looked at Xiahou Jue and saw that the latter was unfazed by the flames.","“It’s true. It looks like the Immemorial Cemetery intends to assimilate you.”","Xiahou Jue smirked in glee. With a wave of his sleeves, the crimson aura morphed into countless arrows that shot toward Chu Feng and the others.","However, the arrows shattered as if they had crashed into an invisible wall.","A black aura containing countless blood-red eyes had manifested out of nowhere and enveloped the surroundings. It was this black aura that blocked those crimson aura arrows.","“New king?”","The crowd turned to the new king. The black aura was from the new king, but who could have thought he could raise his cultivation level from rank one Heavenly God to rank four Heavenly God?","“You’re able to raise your cultivation by three ranks as a Heavenly God?!”","Xiahou Jue wasn’t the only shocked one. Even the experts on Chu Feng’s side were flabbergasted as well. That explained why the new king had been so confident. His limit was not rank three but rank four Heavenly God!","“Who are you?” Xiahou Jue asked.","He did notice the new king, but he thought the other party was just another Ancient Era’s monstrous beast and was nothing noteworthy. But things were different now. The other party was displaying strength and talent that he had to take seriously.","“You’re not worthy of knowing who I am,” the new king said.","He straightened his right arm and opened his palm. A black thorn emerged from his palm.","The black thorn was long, resembling a spear, but it was no ordinary weapon. It felt more like the new king’s body part.","The new king placed the black thorn next to him.","Boom!","More black aura flared from the new king as he grew several times stronger.","“You miserable creature. Are you certain you want to make an enemy out of me?”","The new king looked at Xiahou Jue in disdain. His gaze sent shivers down Xiahou Jue’s spine.","“Y-you are a junior?” Xiahou Jue asked.","This was important. Xiahou Jue was a prodigy as well, but he had only reached this level by tapping into the Netherworld Sect’s vast resources, obtaining many fortuitous encounters, and cultivating for countless years.","If the new king were a junior, he couldn’t begin to imagine the humongous chasm that would arise between them in the near future.","“Scram right now, and I’ll spare your life,” the new king said.","“Lord Xiahou, this entity’s ancestors used to be a powerhouse in the Ancient Era. He isn’t an entity we can deal with. There might still be hope if you back off now, or else our Netherworld Sect will be destroyed because of your actions today,” Song Yun said.","She understood Xiahou Jue. The latter wasn’t intimidated that easily. She had to stoke his fears further to force him to retreat.","“Is he that formidable?” Xiahou Jue first remarked, then burst into laughter. “Hahaha...”","He laughed manically as if he had lost his mind. Then, he reined in his smile and flared his killing intent. “More reason not to let you off. The strong prey on the weak. I might kill you if I go all out today, but if I let you leave, I’ll definitely die in your hands in the future.”","Xiahou Jue clasped his hands, and a golden God Armament truncheon emerged from each hand. Crimson aura gushed from his body and enveloped the God Armaments, greatly raising his fighting prowess.","He crossed the two God Armaments before swinging them.","The world shook. A humongous blood gorge hissed as it charged toward Chu Feng and the others.","The new king waved his sleeves and sent his black aura at the blood gorge.","The world shook yet again when the red and black auras clashed. Were it not for the new king’s intervention, that single move could have killed all of them.","“Incredible!”","The crowd was awed by the strength of the rank four Heavenly Gods.","“Chu Feng, can I trust you?” the new king sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng.","“What’s wrong?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’ll give you ten days. You have to save me within ten days,” the new king said.","He formed a hand seal and vanished. The next moment, he reappeared behind Xiahou Jue.","“An ambush? Hmph, I’ve been expecting you.”","Xiahou Jue was prepared for it. As soon as the new king appeared, he twisted his God Armaments to slash at him.","The strike landed, but Xiahou Jue stiffened up. The area where he struck the new king at emanated thick puffs of black aura that coiled around his weapons.","“Ant Tribe’s Secret Skill: Mutual Imprisonment!”","A dense black aura poured out from the new king’s body to form a massive sphere that enveloped him and Xiahou Jue. Xiahou Jue thrashed around with all his might, but he was helpless against the sphere prison.","Just then, the new king’s black thorn shot toward the sky.","It struck the crimson aura sealing off the tombstone realm, forming ripples of crimson and black that swiftly brewed into a massive vortex. Moments later, the black thorn finally pierced through the crimson aura, thus unraveling the seal.","“The n-n-new king is sacrificing himself to rescue us! Is he no m-m-match for Xiahou Jue?” Wang Qiang asked in bewilderment.","The new king boasted tremendous fighting prowess. With both him and Xiahou Jue at rank four Heavenly God level, he should have been able to easily subdue Xiahou Jue.","“His aura changed,” Chu Feng replied.","“Ah? It did!”","The crowd realized that even though the black aura imprisoning the new king and Xiahou Jue remained at rank four Heavenly God level, the new king’s cultivation had regressed to rank one Heavenly God level.","They finally understood what was going on.","The new king must have resorted to an unorthodox means to raise his cultivation to rank four Heavenly God level. This increment couldn’t be sustained for long, and his fighting prowess also wouldn’t have been as strong as it was when he was at rank three Heavenly God level.","He was doing this just to save Chu Feng and the others.","Shen Hui and the others quickly transported Chu Feng and the others out of the tombstone realm.","As they flew out, Chu Feng noticed the black thorn. It had been a majestic spear moments ago, but as if having expended all its energy, it was only the size of a carrot now, and it was devoid of energy.","Chu Feng grabbed the black thorn and looked back at where the new king was. “Hold on tight, new king. I’ll rescue you within ten days.”"]},{"number":6415,"title":"Chapter 6415: Chapter 6413: Calling Reinforcement","paragraphs":["Chapter 6413: Calling Reinforcement","After leaving the tombstone realm, Shen Hui quickly ordered the Spirit God Clansmen to cooperate with her in constructing a formation. “Lord Chu Feng, we’ll be able to escape via the teleportation formation now, even if he chases us.”","“Shen Hui, can you do me a favor?”","“Feel free to speak, Lord Chu Feng.”","“I’d like you to construct the largest communication formation within your means,” Chu Feng said. He turned to the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and asked, “Otherwise, does any of the elders have the means to relay information as widely as possible?”","“We have something like that,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief replied at the same time, each taking out a scroll.","Their scrolls were different, but they emanated the Ancient Era’s aura.","“Use mine. My clan has more of such treasures,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said as he handed the scroll to Chu Feng.","“Chu Feng, are you calling for reinforcement?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","“I can only try putting my name out and see if I can find anyone to help us out. We can’t leave the new king to the lurch.”","Chu Feng took the scroll and wrote a line of words— I, Chu Feng, am seeking help from a rank four Heavenly God.","He formed a hand seal, and the scroll shot a burst of light into the sky. Shortly after, the words he had written on the scroll appeared in the sky and swiftly enlarged. It reached a point where each word was larger than a realm, glowing brightly to draw attention.","At the same time, the scroll swiftly diffused Chu Feng’s aura into the surroundings.","“Chu Feng?”","The first ones to notice those words were the powers stationed at the entrance.","“He seems to be quite near to us.”","“Is Chu Feng here, too?”","“He’s looking for a rank four Heavenly God?”","“Are there rank four Heavenly Gods in this world?”","While the crowd was still speculating among themselves, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, and the other powers came out of concealment and revealed themselves.","“My gosh! It’s the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion!”","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan? Isn’t that the Ancient Era power that intervened at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith? They look formidable.”","“Even the Immortal Sea Fish Clan is here as well!”","“Wait a minute, aren’t those people looking for Chu Feng? Why are they standing with him? Are they actually his friends?”","“Am I daydreaming? Their auras... They are all Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists! 1111 Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists?”","Those waiting at the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance were shocked by the lineup of Chu Feng’s allies, especially the Spirit God Clan. Despite only comprising 1111 people, the Spirit God Clansmen were all Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","This was beyond shocking.","Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists were still legends before the Nine Heavens’ Zenith; even the strongest world spiritist in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, Jie Tianran, was only at pinnacle True Dragon then.","Every Heavenly God and Heavenly Dragon felt no different from a god to ordinary cultivators, entities whom they couldn’t hope to catch up with in their lifetime. It was naturally shocking to see so many Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists appearing in a single location.","“These people appear to be Chu Feng’s friends.”","“It boggles me to fathom that there’s a problem these experts can’t resolve. What in the world is going on?”","“Could it be related to the Immemorial Cemetery?”","The smarter ones connected the dots and realized that their situation was worse than expected. They hadn’t wanted to enter the Immemorial Cemetery in the first place, knowing that it was fraught with dangers, but they were forcefully dragged in.","Some naively thought the entrance would eventually open for them, but the majority of the people had already realized that they would likely perish here. Even if they escaped from here, it would be with the aid of a powerful cultivator.","The appearance of Chu Feng and the others felt like a beacon of hope.","The knowledge that this unbelievably powerful group of experts was facing a quandary as well made them sink deeper into despair.","Meanwhile, the Zhao Immortal Clan was secretly cruising through the Immemorial Cemetery’s depths. It had been some time since they arrived at the Immemorial Cemetery, but they hadn’t reaped any gains due to their vigilance.","However, a tombstone realm had caught their eye, and they were making their way over.","Gathered inside the main ship’s palace were Eighth Zhao, his two daughters, Zhao Zhuyin and Zhao Tingxue, and other elders like Zhao Daobin. But there was also a person there who wasn’t from the Zhao Clan—Jie Mubai.","Jie Mubai had taken off his cloak to reveal his true face. There was no need for him to disguise himself, as he had already voluntarily revealed his identity to them as a token of sincerity for their partnership. He had done the same for the Netherworld Sect, too.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen had turned their attention away from their destination to look at an observation formation, which showed a conspicuous line of words.","I, Chu Feng, am seeking help from a rank four Heavenly God.","“Father.” Zhao Zhuyin looked at Eighth Zhao nervously.","Chu Feng wasn’t the type to ask for favors easily. He must be in a difficult position to be publicly asking for help. However, her father had told her that the Zhao Immortal Clan’s fate couldn’t fall on Chu Feng’s shoulders.","“Is Chu Feng in trouble?”","Zhao Tingxue’s tone was gloating. She was not inclined to help Chu Feng at all.","Zhao Daobin looked nervous. He wanted the clan chief to help Chu Feng if possible, but the Zhao Immortal Clan’s fate was at stake here. A reckless move here, in the treacherous Immemorial Cemetery, could spell a calamity for their Zhao Immortal Clan.","Jie Mubai appeared nonchalant, but he was more worked up than anyone else. No one wanted Chu Feng’s death more than him, but he wanted Chu Feng to die in his hands so that he could acquire his treasures.","But if he had to weigh his options, Chu Feng’s death took precedence over everything.","Eighth Zhao soon made up his mind and announced, “Turn the ship around. We’ll head to where Chu Feng is!”"]},{"number":6416,"title":"Chapter 6416: Chapter 6414: The Man Who Calls Himself Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6414: The Man Who Calls Himself Emperor","Eighth Zhao’s order was quickly relayed.","Jie Mubai quickly interjected, “Lord Clan Chief, this is a rare opportunity. It isn’t easy for us to find this tombstone realm. I beseech you to think twice.”","“Master, our clan is acquainted with Chu Feng. I cannot avert my eyes when he needs help. If you aren’t in a rush, you're welcome to come with us. We’ll visit the remnant after we resolve Chu Feng’s quandary. Otherwise, I’m afraid we’ll have to part ways here. If fate allows, we’ll work together another day,” Eighth Zhao said.","“How regrettable.” Jie Mubai waved his sleeves and left.","Zhao Daobin called out, “Master, there is no need for us to rush. Not everyone wields means like yours to discover potential tombstones, and the Immemorial Cemetery is huge enough that it’ll be hard for others to come across this specific tombstone.”","“You’re right, Elder Zhao, but I chose to work with the Zhao Immortal Clan because of your strength and decisiveness. I thought you’d grasp every opportunity that comes your way. I’m surprised that the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief would give up on this opportunity for Chu Feng. Perhaps our expectations do not align,” Jie Mubai said with a coercive tone.","He was issuing an ultimatum to the Zhao Immortal Clan—if they left now, he would never work with them ever again.","Eighth Zhao understood Jie Mubai’s threat, and he smiled. “Master, I understand your intention. Feel free to leave.”","Zhao Daobin decided to say no more. He had to respect their clan chief’s decision.","Jie Mubai harrumphed as he walked out of the palace and left the warship.","“Father, is it worth giving up on this opportunity for Chu Feng?” Zhao Tingxue asked.","“Opportunity? How big an opportunity can it be? If you ask me, Chu Feng is the biggest opportunity in the Immemorial Cemetery! There’s no point latching onto him like leeches when he doesn’t need us, but he must be in great trouble now that he’s actively seeking help. This is the perfect opportunity to sell him a favor. It’d be the equivalent of delivering charcoal to him in the dead of winter. Chu Feng will remember this favor,” Eighth Zhao said.","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen soon disappeared in the darkness.","Jie Mubai traveled alone toward the tombstone realm, but his complexion looked terrible.","“What kind of spell has Chu Feng cast on these people? All of them are going all out for him as if they are out of their minds!”","This didn’t make sense to him. Eighth Zhao should have been the kind of person who would prioritize his clan’s interests over all things else, yet he was choosing an outsider over his clan’s fortuitous encounter.","The more he thought about it, the angrier he felt.","Jie Mubai would have never reached out to the Zhao Immortal Clan if he were capable of claiming the fortuitous encounter alone. In any other circumstances, he would give in and go along with the Zhao Immortal Clan, but he couldn’t take losing to Chu Feng yet again.","Even though he was the one who chose to part ways with the Zhao Immortal Clan, he wasn’t confident of deciphering the tombstone realm by himself. It made him feel regret, and the more he regretted, the angrier he felt. However, his anger was not directed at himself but at Chu Feng.","“What’s the point of throwing a tantrum?” a voice suddenly echoed ahead of him.","Jie Mubai was taken aback.","It was a masculine voice. It didn’t sound old, but the accent didn’t sound like someone from the present era. The voice carried no oppressive might or energy, but it made Jie Mubai’s hair stand on end, and even his soul quivered in fear.","“Who are you?” Jie Mubai asked deferentially.","He realized the other party could be a formidable existence.","A divine, golden light that was at odds with the eerie Immemorial Cemetery suddenly appeared before him. It wasn’t particularly brilliant, but it filled one with hope. It was only the size of a bead at the very start, but as it revolved, it began to expand until it manifested into a gate.","A black talisman covered with a red, humanlike pattern floated out from the gate. It looked terrifying. Jie Mubai could tell just by looking at it that it was a powerful talisman.","“You’re an ambitious man, but your talent is limited. You won’t be able to reach the pinnacle of cultivation alone. You’d only be devoured by your ambitions. But if you submit to this emperor, your path will be smooth sailing. I am not fond of forcing others into submission. The choice is in your hands,” the man’s voice echoed from the golden light.","“Milord, may I know your name?” Jie Mubai hurriedly asked.","Not only was there no answer, but the golden light dissipated as well. However, the black talisman in his hand made it clear what had just happened wasn’t his imagination.","“He calls himself ‘emperor’?” Jie Mubai looked conflicted.","He understood the weight of this title. Had it been anyone else, he would have shrugged it off as an empty title. But the person’s voice itself was worthy of the title.","This could be an immensely fortuitous encounter, and the black talisman was the crux of it.","But he was conflicted.","As a world spiritist, he could sense the peculiarity of the talisman paper. Activating the talisman paper would awaken the powerful entity inside, but he would have to offer his soul in exchange. This was not a decision he could make in the spur of the moment.","He looked at the boundless darkness and the bizarre tombstones around him and murmured, “Just what kind of place is the Immemorial Cemetery?”","He had known the Immemorial Cemetery was not as simple as it looked, but the earlier encounter made him realize that he was still underestimating this place. This could be the most unfathomable place he had set foot on in his entire life."]},{"number":6417,"title":"Chapter 6417: Chapter 6415: The Immortal Clans’ Aid","paragraphs":["Chapter 6415: The Immortal Clans’ Aid","Chu Feng’s army was still stationed outside the tombstone realm.","Chu Feng, Xian Miaomiao, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, Huangfu Zhantian, Shen Hui, and the others stood on the warship’s deck.","Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, Yuwen Yanri, and the others were absent because they sensed a change in their inherited power after they escaped from the tombstone realm. To stabilize their legacies, they decided to go into closed-door training.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master, and the others looked uneasy. They were waiting for reinforcements, but would there really be reinforcements?","They had directed this question to Chu Feng, but not even he was certain about it. He was trying his luck.","Broadcasting their location was dangerous.","But since Chu Feng had made up his mind, there was nothing more they could say. Despite being stronger than him, they had to follow Chu Feng’s directives here.","“Lord Chu Feng, a huge army is swiftly approaching us,” Shen Hui suddenly said.","Huangfu Zhantian and the others quickly raised their cultivation to the highest level and prepared for battle.","“Calm down, young friend Chu Feng. It’s me,” a voice echoed.","The huge army suddenly appeared out of nowhere. The flags they flew under shocked everyone.","It was the Zhao Immortal Clan!","“The Zhao Immortal Clan is a powerful clan that has recently emerged. Are they Chu Feng’s reinforcement?”","“Surely not. The Ancient Era’s races have always looked down on the present-era cultivators, especially the powerful ones. I heard the Zhao Immortal Clan is strong enough to unify the world of cultivation, so why would they help Chu Feng?”","“What’s there to be surprised about? Isn’t the Huangfu Heavenly Clan standing with Chu Feng now?”","Discussions buzzed among the powers standing at the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance.","The more cowardly ones even fled at the sight of the Zhao Immortal Clan, afraid that the latter would make a move against the present-era cultivators.","Even the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked, “Chu Feng, are they an ally?”","The others turned to look at Chu Feng. They had heard about the Zhao Immortal Clan and knew how powerful they were.","“I think so,” Chu Feng said. He couldn’t confirm it since Eighth Zhao hadn’t given a clear stance, though he already had an answer in mind.","The Zhao Immortal Clan stopped a distance away. Eighth Zhao brought Zhao Zhuyin, Zhao Tingxue, Zhao Daobin, and other key personnel of the Zhao Immortal Clan over.","“Young friend Chu Feng, we meet again. I sensed your aura and saw your message, so I rushed over to take a look. Did you meet with trouble?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“Elder, you should know by now we’re trapped in the Immemorial Cemetery. If we don’t escape in time, we’ll all die here,” Chu Feng said.","“Does this relate to what you require help for?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“That’s right.”","Chu Feng filled Eighth Zhao in about the Seven Stars Orbs. He told the latter that the tombstone realm before them was the sixth star, but someone from the Netherworld Sect had gotten to it ahead of them and was obstructing them.","“I didn’t expect the Netherworld Sect to be so powerful as to have a rank four Heavenly God. Miss, is that Xiahou Jue fellow the strongest cultivator in the Netherworld Sect?” Eighth Zhao asked Song Yun.","He had learned about Song Yun’s relationship with the Netherworld Sect from Chu Feng, so he decided to probe for more information.","“As strong as Xiahou Jue is, he isn’t the strongest cultivator in the Netherworld Sect. There’s a gap even among the Netherworld Marshalls in the Netherworld Sect. Xiahou Jue belongs to the new faction, and the most influential person in the new faction is Baili Zilin’s father, Baili Xukong,” Song Yun replied.","“I guess the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion isn’t the only formidable present-era power. The Netherworld Sect is also quite the force to be reckoned with,” Eighth Zhao said with a frown.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and the others sensed that things might be going awry. Eighth Zhao appeared to be intimidated by the Netherworld Sect, and no one could blame him for prioritizing the Zhao Immortal Clan’s safety here.","“Elder, I am speaking the truth. What’s happening in the Immemorial Cemetery concerns everyone’s safety. I, Chu Feng, will not forget this favor if you help us,” Chu Feng said.","Surprisingly, Eighth Zhao suddenly revealed a bright smile.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you’re being too distant. Our Zhao Immortal Clan knew nothing about the Seven Stars Orbs while we were making our way here. We came with the sole purpose of backing you up. Even if not for the Seven Stars Orbs, I’d have still helped you deal with Xiahou Jue. Your enemy is our Zhao Immortal Clan’s enemy. If we’re going to make a move, we’ll have to be thorough lest it lead to endless trouble,” Eighth Zhao said.","“Elder, if it’s convenient, please take me with you when you’re making a move. I can unravel his protective formation if he has one,” Chu Feng said.","“That’d be great!” Eighth Zhao said.","“What a crowd!” a voice boomed from the horizon.","The voice came from so far away that the crowd couldn’t see who spoke. Shen Hui brought up an observation formation, through which they saw a warship swiftly approaching them.","There was only one warship, but it was humongous and shrouded in a golden light. It looked as if a brilliant sun was rushing at them.","“Who’s that?”","The crowd was horrified, for the warship was moving at a frightening speed.","Those with Chu Feng were more shaken up as they could see the warship clearly via the observation formation. Even Zhao Daobin and the others were frowning. The warship was flying flags with the words: Ye Immortal Clan .","“Clan Chief?” Zhao Daobin glanced at Eighth Zhao with worried eyes.","Unlike other powers, they had a better understanding of the Ye Immortal Clan. The Ye Immortal Clan had been sealed all this while, and it was only in recent days that they were released. They had never met each other in person, but they did communicate via special means.","The Ye Immortal Clan was extremely arrogant, such that the Zhao Immortal Clan viewed them as a rival power.","“Let’s see what their intentions are first. We have nothing to fear even if they choose to make a move,” Eighth Zhao said.","As the Ye Immortal Clan approached, a resonant voice echoed from their warship, “Chu Feng, I’m here to help you!!!”","The crowd turned to Chu Feng.","Even Eighth Zhao was baffled. “You’re acquainted with the Ye Immortal Clan as well?”","—","Translator Note:","The Ye Immortal Clan is the clan where Chu Feng reunited with Song Yun. Their clan chief (Ye Xiancheng) is a junior who has inherited their ancestors’ cultivation and has reached rank nine True God level despite being a junior.","(Chapter 6357)"]},{"number":6418,"title":"Chapter 6418: Chapter 6416: The Immortal Clans vs. the Netherworld Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6416: The Immortal Clans vs. the Netherworld Sect","“We met a while back,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Soon, the Ye Immortal Clan’s warship arrived.","All the Ye Immortal Clansmen greeted loudly, “Paying respect to Lord Chu Feng.”","The distant spectators were baffled.","“What’s going on? Are these people all Chu Feng’s helpers?”","The voices carried deep respect, but it was bewildering why such a formidable power would be so deferential to Chu Feng? Could there be more to the story?","While the crowd was trying to make sense of the situation, Ye Xiancheng alighted from the warship with his parents and made their way to Chu Feng’s side. As if to flaunt their strength, Ye Xiancheng’s parents unleashed their cultivation.","The weaker ones felt greatly intimidated. The stronger ones could tell that the couple had reached rank four Heavenly God level.","“Gosh, what incredible auras.”","“Chu Feng has such strong backing?”","“No wonder he doesn’t fear the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion!”","The crowd was shocked.","Even Ye Xiancheng’s parents also greeted Chu Feng warmly, though Ye Xiancheng was far more enthusiastic. Not only did he greet Chu Feng and Xian Yun, but he could also hardly tear his eyes away from Xian Miaomiao. In the end, he asked, “Chu Feng, who is this miss?”","“She’s Xian Miaomiao, a friend I have known for many years. Miaomiao, this is Ye Xiancheng. He’s the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, but he’s a junior like us,” Chu Feng introduced the two of them to each other.","“It’s my pleasure to meet you,” Xian Miaomiao replied with a polite smile.","Ye Xiancheng warmly said, “Xian Miaomiao—what a wonderful name.”","“Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, we have stumbled upon a problem and will require your help. Will it be convenient?” Chu Feng got straight to the point, not wanting to dawdle since the new king was still trapped inside the tombstone realm.","“Chu Feng, can’t you tell that we rushed here to help you? Tell me what happened. I’ll settle it on your behalf. Otherwise, my parents can help you, too,” Ye Xiancheng thumped out his chest and said.","Ye Xiancheng’s parents acknowledged those words with a smile. They had already agreed before entering the Immemorial Cemetery—they would do their best to fawn on Chu Feng if they met him in here. This was also the reason behind all the fanfare.","They wanted to make it clear that the Ye Immortal Clan was on Chu Feng’s side.","Chu Feng quickly filled Ye Xiancheng and the others in on the situation.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you can leave this to our Ye Immortal Clan! Construct the formation!” Ye Xiancheng’s parents issued the order.","Tremendous formation energy was imbued into Ye Xiancheng’s parents, greatly raising their fighting prowess. With that, the two of them dove into the tombstone realm.","“The rest of you wait here,” Eighth Zhao said as he entered the tombstone realm with Chu Feng.","The three rank four Heavenly Gods gathered before the black sphere created by the new king.","Ye Xiancheng’s parents looked at Chu Feng with troubled eyes. “Young friend Chu Feng, can you see the situation inside? I’m worried we’ll accidentally hurt your friend if we make a wrong move.”","They were capable of breaking open the black sphere, but for some reason, they couldn’t peer into the black sphere to see inside it.","Kacha!","Cracks suddenly appeared on the black sphere’s surface and swiftly spread. By the time Chu Feng and the others realized something was amiss, the black sphere had already shattered with a loud explosion.","Terrifying oppressive might enveloped the area.","“Brat, you’re a loyal one to dare return. That makes things easier for me,” Xiahou Jue sneered.","The new king emerged from the black sphere as well, but he was bound by Xiahou Jue’s energy.","“Chu Feng, are your helpers reliable? If not, you should flee right away. He could have broken free from my restraints earlier, but he knew it would be futile to chase you, so he was waiting for you to return! This fellow is not to be underestimated. He hasn’t revealed all his means yet!” the new king warned.","A figure suddenly flitted behind Xiahou Jue and hurled a fist at him. The ground gave way, and Xiahou Jue was smashed deep underground like a falling comet, forming a deep pit.","It was Eighth Zhao.","“Brat, do I look reliable to you?”","He released the new king’s restraints and tossed him to Chu Feng’s side. The new king smiled.","“You’ll die here for daring to make an enemy out of young friend Chu Feng.”","A golden light lit up the sky, and countless golden beams shot into the deep pit. Ye Xiancheng’s parents had unleashed their God Taboo Martial Skill!","But it didn’t take long for Ye Xiancheng’s parents to widen their eyes in astonishment. They had unleashed this move with the intention to end Xiahou Jue’s life, but to their disbelief, Xiahou Jue was unharmed!","Terrifying oppressive might gushed forth from the pit. Ye Xiancheng’s parents were immediately forced into a kneeling position as blood gushed from their mouths and nostrils.","A gigantic red silhouette resembled a sinister embryo emerged from the pit. It swiftly expanded, looking as if it would fill up the entire realm.","It was the Netherworld Embryo!","The Netherworld Embryo transformed into a humanoid form. Blood-red armor manifested around it, and it resembled a war god from hell. It dove back into the pit where Xiahou Jue was.","Shortly after, Xiahou Jue emerged from the pit.","His eyes were blood-red, and a blood-red aura was flowing ceaselessly from his body. While his appearance remained the same, he was now wearing the blood-red armor that the gigantic Netherworld Embryo was wearing earlier.","His cultivation rose from rank four Heavenly God to rank five Heavenly God.","“I didn’t expect this simple task to turn out so troublesome. I was even forced to unleash the power of the Netherworld Armament. But it all comes to an end now.”","The world was devoured by the blood-red aura. Chu Feng felt the threat of death.","Yet, everyone remained safe.","“Oh?” Xiahou Jue looked at Eighth Zhao in astonishment.","“You are actually...” Ye Xiancheng’s parents also looked at Eighth Zhao in shock.","A golden light shrouded Eighth Zhao, making him look divine. At the same time, his cultivation rose to rank five Heavenly God level.","“Why are you being so arrogant? Do you think you’re the only Heavenly God who can raise his cultivation?” Eighth Zhao sneered.","“Oh?” Xiahou Jue smiled, but his eyes looked incredibly cold.","A red aura rose from the ground. Eighth Zhao bravely charged at the red aura in response.","The red aura and the golden light clashed, causing cracks to appear in the spatial fabric and in the ground. A clash between two rank five Heavenly Gods was devastating.","But soon, the golden light plummeted from the sky.","Eighth Zhao profusely spewed blood, and there was a gaping hole in his chest.","“What about now?” Xiahou Jue stood unharmed in midair as he gazed upon Eighth Zhao in disdain."]},{"number":6419,"title":"Chapter 6419: Chapter 6417: Heaven’s Will?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6417: Heaven’s Will?","Faced with Xiahou Jue’s look of disdain, the injured Eighth Zhao laughed.","“Brother, there’s no need to go this far. There isn’t a grudge between us in the first place. I attacked you because I’m acquainted with Chu Feng and wanted to lend him a helping hand, but I don’t plan on throwing my life away for that.","“Our Zhao Immortal Clan has been around for a long time, and we know many secret places in the world of cultivation. I dare say the remnants we know about number no less than what you see in the Immemorial Cemetery. Since the Netherworld Sect is this powerful, why don’t we join forces to acquire those fortuitous encounters?” Eighth Zhao proposed.","“You’re begging me to let you all off?” Xiahou Jue narrowed his eyes.","He was surprised that Eighth Zhao would resort to this.","“No, I’m just asking you to let me off. You can deal with Chu Feng however you want,” Eighth Zhao said.","“I was tasked to kill anyone who steps into this land. You have brought many of your clansmen here; I cannot spare all of them. If you’re interested in surviving and working with me, you’ll have to give up on some of them.","“Our Netherworld Sect is stronger than you can imagine. Losing those burdens may be a good thing for you. I’ll recommend you to Lord Xukong, so that you can become a subsidiary of our Netherworld Sect,” Xiahou Jue said.","He knew better than to underestimate Eighth Zhao despite the latter being weaker. The long history of Ancient Era’s clans allowed them to accumulate countless years of intelligence and wealth, such that they were bound to be an asset to the Netherworld Sect.","Not to mention Eighth Zhao could raise his cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level. Recruiting someone this strong into the Netherworld Sect was bound to be a huge merit for him.","“Just sparing the elites is enough,” Eighth Zhao said.","“I can allow twenty people at most,” Xiahou Jue replied.","“I don’t need twenty people. Ten is enough.”","Xiahou Jue laughed. “Good.”","Eighth Zhao suddenly morphed into a streak of light and appeared behind Xiahou Jue.","“Good your head!”","He hacked his God Armament down on Xiahou Jue’s head. His golden aura was blazing with incredible fervor, and it translated into a massive boost in his fighting prowess.","Xiahou Jue activated his secret skill to dodge the attack right away, but blood still splattered. Eighth Zhao had hacked off his arm.","“How dare you deceive me!” Xiahou Jue quickly distanced himself from Eighth Zhao while roaring in anger.","“Yes, I deceived you. What about it?” Eighth Zhao scoffed as he unleashed several golden blades at Xiahou Jue, not giving the latter a chance to catch a breather. At the same time, he shouted to Chu Feng, “Young friend Chu Feng, leave this man from the Netherworld Sect to me. Please take care of Zhuyin if I fail to survive this ordeal.”","Eighth Zhao’s golden aura blazed with greater fury, and his attacks became more aggressive.","Chu Feng and the others only saw golden ripples everywhere as the world shook around them.","“Elder, there’s no need to put your life on the line here,” Chu Feng exclaimed. He could tell Eighth Zhao had ignited his bloodline to gain a temporary boost in fighting prowess.","“Hahaha! Humans are bound to die one day. Rather than be trapped in the Immemorial Cemetery and die a dog’s death, I’d rather stake my life in exchange for my clansmen’s safety. Even if I die, I’ll die a hero!” Eighth Zhao laughed heartily, showing no fear of death.","“You want to save your Zhao Immortal Clan? You’ll have to kill me first! Otherwise, I’ll make your Zhao Immortal Clan suffer a fate worse than death!”","Xiahou Jue’s killing intent flared as he unleashed a series of killing blows against Eighth Zhao.","Red and golden auras suffused the tombstone realm. Even space itself was being devastated by their clashes, let alone the ground. It was fortunate the tombstone realm was sturdy enough to withstand their might, or else it would have long collapsed.","“He’s igniting his life force,” the new king told Chu Feng.","Chu Feng was nowhere strong enough to watch the battle; he could only feel the shockwaves. His eyes brimmed with hesitation.","Eighth Zhao was still holding his ground for the time being, but he would lose his life at this rate. He had to end this battle quickly.","But Xiahou Jue was extremely powerful. Despite Eighth Zhao’s relentless attacks, he couldn’t claim the upper hand in the battle. They were equally matched.","Xiahou Jue was also using a secret skill that was likely to burden his body, but it was not so severe as to cost him his life.","In a battle of attrition, Eighth Zhao would die.","Weng!","The red and golden auras were suddenly severed.","A humongous sword descended from the sky and pierced into the bubbling lava below. Even so, the other half of the sword still towered above them.","A resonant, feminine voice echoed from the sky, “The Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief is noble indeed, but as long as our Heavensword Sacred Palace is here, there’s no need to fear a mere Netherworld Sect!”","Countless figures floated in the sky as if celestial soldiers. They were all from the Heavensword Sacred Palace.","Aside from Tianjian Canhua, Chu Feng also spotted a dark-skinned man and a white-haired, blindfolded man—Tuoba Yijian and Tuoba Tianxue.","But Chu Feng’s attention was quickly drawn to the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s formation. Their clansmen were divided into two groups.","The group behind had formed hand seals, and their bodies were emanating a faint, divine light. The light gave off the same aura as the humongous sword that had descended from the sky.","The group in front consisted of nineteen old women. Eighteen of them were at rank four Heavenly God level, and their leader even exuded an aura on par with Eighth Zhao and Xiahou Jue—rank five Heavenly God level.","She was the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master, as well as the person who had spoken earlier.","“The Heavensword Sacred Palace? What a timely arrival! Heaven must have decreed that I’m not fated to meet my end here!” Eighth Zhao laughed heartily as he sat in mid-air.","His golden aura receded, and his cultivation returned to rank four Heavenly God level.","But that was not all.","His black hair turned white, and his muscular body visibly slimmed down as it was no longer able to fill up his shirt. Wrinkles also appeared on his face. He had aged years in just an instant.","No one was surprised, as Eighth Zhao had ignited his life force earlier to fight Xiahou Jue.","“Don’t thank heaven. Thank Chu Feng instead. We rushed here because Chu Feng needed help,” the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master replied as she flashed an amicable smile to Chu Feng.","All of a sudden, she flitted in front of Eighth Zhao.","Xiahou Jue had launched an abrupt attack on Eighth Zhao.","She swung her silver God Armament sword to deflect Xiahou Jue’s attack. The two weapons clashed. Xiahou Jue was forced back several steps, but she had to retreat tens of thousands of meters.","Fortunately, the Palace Master pulled Eighth Zhao back with her and tossed him into the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s formation.","“That’s all you have despite your big talk? I’ll massacre your Heavensword Sacred Palace along with everyone else!” Xiahou Jue sneered.","The Palace Master smiled. “Construct the formation!”","All the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members changed their hand seals, and the light they emanated intensified.","Clang!","Another light sword descended from the sky.","The Palace Master charged forth once more, thrusting her God Armament sword straight at Xiahou Jue’s face.","Xiahou Jue harrumphed. Without taking a step, he raised his God Armament to block the attack.","Clang!","A loud reverberation echoed.","Xiahou Jue was horrified.","This time, the Palace Master remained still, but Xiahou Jue was sent flying a long distance before he finally regained his balance. His hand bled from the sheer impact of the clash and trembled nonstop.","“This is our Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Heavensword Sacred Formation. We can manifest nineteen Heavenswords.” The Palace Master pointed her weapon at Xiahou Jue. “How many can you take?”"]},{"number":6420,"title":"Chapter 6420: Chapter 6418: Peach Blossom Luck","paragraphs":["Chapter 6418: Peach Blossom Luck","Xiahou Jue looked at his bleeding palm and suddenly burst into laughter. It started as a chuckle, but it quickly grew unnervingly louder and manic.","Everyone from the Heavensword Sacred Palace stood at attention, ready to launch follow-up attacks.","But the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master quickly realized something was amiss. The red aura looked threatening, but Xiahou Jue’s presence had vanished. Only his laughter continued to echo in the tombstone realm.","“The Heavensword Sacred Palace? I’ll remember you.”","The red aura dissipated with the wind, and Xiahou Jue’s silhouette vanished into thin air.","“Huh? Is it a feint? Is he just putting on an act to slip away?” Eighth Zhao asked.","It was clear to everyone that Xiahou Jue had escaped. Those from the Heavensword Sacred Palace weren’t surprised, as they knew how strong their Heavensword Sacred Formation was.","“That’s all the Netherworld Sect amounts to!”","The Palace Master waved her sleeves, and their formation and the two humongous light swords dissipated.","Chu Feng rushed to Eighth Zhao’s side to inspect his injuries. Eighth Zhao had stopped in time to preserve his life and his cultivation, but his body would never be the same as before.","News about the battle’s conclusion quickly spread. The Zhao Heavenly Clansmen, the Ye Heavenly Clansmen, and the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s members quickly entered the tombstone realm.","“What’s wrong, father?” Zhao Zhuyin and the others were concerned.","“I’m fine.” Eighth Zhao grinned. Despite his aged appearance, he was still as carefree and vibrant as before.","“My apologies for arriving late, young friend Chu Feng.” The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master went up to Chu Feng with her elites.","“Don’t say that, elder. We would have struggled to deal with Xiahou Jue if you weren’t here.” Chu Feng stood up and bowed.","“Young friend Chu Feng, we’re only doing what we must. This was Lord Qingyuan’s instruction, after all,” the Palace Master said.","Eighth Zhao, Zhao Daobin, and the others were taken aback.","“Lord Qingyuan? Which Lord Qingyuan?”","Even Ye Xiancheng’s parents, who were recuperating some distance away, cast their gazes over. The word ‘Qingyuan’ was too striking for them to overlook.","The Ancient Era races had records of the events that transpired in the Ancient Era.","Faced with the curious gazes of the two immortal clans’ experts, the Palace Master replied, “Your question suggests that you have records of Lord Qingyuan. Yes, the Lord Qingyuan I speak of is the renowned prodigy of our Heavensword Sacred Palace back in the Ancient Era, Tianjian Qingyuan.”","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen and the Ye Immortal Clansmen were flabbergasted.","“Tianjian Qingyuan has survived to the present era?”","Tianjian Qingyuan was still a junior when she first rose to prominence. Her astounding talent was the reason her name appeared in the records of countless clans.","Not much was known about her afterward, but with her level of talent, her cultivation must have risen to an unimaginable level if she had survived from the Ancient Era to the present era.","With Tianjian Qingyuan’s backing, no power within the eight galaxies would dare challenge the Heavensword Sacred Palace.","While reeling in shock, some Zhao Immortal Clansmen and Ye Immortal Clansmen subconsciously glanced at Chu Feng. This would explain why the lofty Heavensword Sacred Palace had rushed to Chu Feng’s aid and was so amicable to him.","It turned out Chu Feng had ties with Tianjian Qingyuan.","This filled them with relief. They were glad that they had chosen to befriend Chu Feng.","“Chu Feng, are you injured?” Tianjian Canhua stepped forward and asked out of concern.","“I’m fine,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s good to hear.” Tianjian Canhua smiled. Her friendly attitude made it seem as if there had been no conflict between them.","Chu Feng turned to Tuoba Yijian and Tuoba Tianxue. “Brothers, we meet again.”","Tuoba Yijian and Tuoba Tianxue greeted Chu Feng with a smile, but they didn’t speak much. They had been relaxed and confident the last time they met Chu Feng, but now, they appeared reserved.","From where they stood, Chu Feng could tell that they were indeed prodigies in the Heavensword Sacred Palace, but they were nowhere near on par with Tianjian Canhua.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace had two clan names—Tianjian and Tuoba. Those from the Tuoba lineage were beneath those from the Tianjian lineage.","Chu Feng first traded some pleasantries with the Heavensword Sacred Palace before informing them about the Seven Stars Orbs.","“To think such dangers lurked within the Immemorial Cemetery.” The Palace Master was surprised, but she decisively chose her stance, “Young friend Chu Feng, feel free to command our Heavensword Sacred Palace.”","“I’m sure we’ll overcome this crisis with the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s aid,” Chu Feng replied with a confident smile.","“Are you certain the sixth star is here? I have looked around the realm, but I don’t see a tombstone anywhere,” the Palace Master said.","“The tombstone is hidden, but I know the method to make it appear,” Chu Feng said.","This method could be used by cultivators and world spiritists. The higher one’s cultivation was, the greater the ease in making the tombstone appear.","The Palace Master was overjoyed. “It would have been much more difficult to overcome this crisis if not for young friend Chu Feng.”","Chu Feng responded with a smile as he shared the method with the Palace Master.","“Chu Feng,” a voice suddenly echoed. It was Ye Xiancheng.","He had first checked on his parents as they were injured, and only after confirming his parents were fine did he head over to Chu Feng’s side.","“Who is this lady?” Ye Xiancheng’s attention was immediately drawn to Tianjian Canhua.","“Tianjian Canhua,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“What a graceful name! I am Ye Xiancheng, the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief,” Ye Xiancheng first introduced himself before bowing to the Palace Master. “Paying respect to the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master.”","“You’re too polite, Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief. It’s incredible someone as young as you is already taking on such a heavy burden,” the Palace Master replied.","After trading some pleasantries, the Palace Master took her leave to make the tombstone appear. Tianjian Canhua followed her.","Ye Xiancheng’s gaze followed Tianjian Canhua.","“Have you fallen in love?” Chu Feng asked.","“Nay, I have decided to seal off my heart after what happened with Song Yun. I’ll devote myself to my career,” Ye Xiancheng replied.","“Then why do you keep looking at her?” Chu Feng was skeptical.","“Just because I’m not in love doesn’t mean I can’t appreciate beauty.” Ye Xiancheng leaned closer to Chu Feng and whispered, “I think Miss Miaomiao is prettier. Haven’t you realized that Miss Miaomiao and Tianjian Canhua look at you with peculiar eyes? You are truly blessed with peach blossom luck.”","Ye Xiancheng’s eyes brimmed with envy.","Before Chu Feng could reply, Ye Xiancheng suddenly directed his gaze elsewhere. His eyes lit up as he blurted out a curse, “Holy shit.”","Little Fishy and the others were making their way over."]},{"number":6421,"title":"Chapter 6421: Chapter 6419: Top-tier Peach Blossom","paragraphs":["Chapter 6419: Top-tier Peach Blossom","Ye Xiancheng’s eyes were fixed on Little Fishy even though Wang Qiang and the others had come with her. He could even be heard swallowing his saliva as he said, “Am I dreaming? How can there be such a beautiful lady in the world?”","Little Fishy looked in Ye Xiancheng’s direction and beamed a brilliant smile.","Ye Xiancheng was stupefied. His saliva trickled down his lips.","“Chu Feng, Chu Feng, did you... see that? That woman is...”","Before he could finish his sentence, Little Fishy came over and called out, “Big brother!”","She marched up with Chu Feng with a smile so wide that it felt as if it were a long-awaited reunion. But they had been together all this while, and she had only briefly gone into closed-door training to assimilate the legacy.","That was how she was like. There was no room for anyone else in her starry eyes whenever she looked at Chu Feng.","“Did it go well?” Chu Feng asked.","“It went smoothly. I didn’t fully assimilate the legacy, but I assimilated a part of it,” Little Fishy replied.","“That’s good to hear.”","The legacies in the Immemorial Cemetery were extraordinary, and this was even more so for the legacies Little Fishy and the others obtained. Obtaining the legacies was tough, but assimilating them was no easy feat either. They wouldn’t be able to accomplish it anytime soon.","“Brother Chu Feng, is this lady your little sister?” Ye Xiancheng asked.","Little Fishy had long noticed Ye Xiancheng, but she had only spared him a glance before turning her undevoted attention to Chu Feng.","“Allow me to introduce the two of you. This is the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, Ye Xiancheng.”","Then, Chu Feng introduced Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and the others to Ye Xiancheng as well. Little Fishy and the others were polite to Ye Xiancheng, having learned that the latter had come here to help Chu Feng.","That said, Little Fishy only smiled faintly at Ye Xiancheng, not bothering to speak a word.","Ye Xiancheng was the most interested in Little Fishy, but he had enough common sense to tell that Little Fishy was interested in Chu Feng. Her parents, grandfather, and brother were around, but there was one person in her eyes.","So, he sent an envious voice transmission to Chu Feng, “Brother Chu Feng, you must have been a peach blossom tree in your previous life.”","“Ah?” Chu Feng was taken aback by the remark.","It quickly occurred to him that Ye Xiancheng had said something similar when he first met Eggy, though he had only asked if Chu Feng was a peach blossom in his previous life. It looked like he had ‘upgraded’ by a peach blossom to a peach blossom tree.","“Isn’t your peach blossom luck too good? How can you have so many top-tier peach blossoms around you?” Ye Xiancheng exclaimed via voice transmission.","“What do you mean by top-tier peach blossoms?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’m talking about your love interests! How can they all be so beautiful? And their feelings for you are all pure!","“I am a good catch too. I, Ye Xiancheng, do not lack strength, background, and looks. By no exaggeration, if I declare that I’m looking for a wife, there will be a queue the length of a little starfield at my footstep!","“But I couldn’t capture Song Yun’s heart no matter how I fawned on her. Xianhai Yu’er is also completely uninterested in me. I’m not different from air to her. She only has you in her eyes.”","Ye Xiancheng was overflowing with jealousy, though there was a tinge of respect, too.","“Hahaha! This Ye Xiancheng is an interesting one.” Eggy adored such commotions.","Ye Xiancheng suddenly added, “More importantly, you have such a beautiful world spirit. My gosh! I’ve never seen anyone that beautiful. I’m about to die from jealousy. Brother, if I could have such a beautiful world spirit, I’d devote my life to her and never marry a second woman!”","Eggy’s laughter disappeared, and her face grew stern. “Is this Ye Xiancheng sick in the head? Chu Feng, pay no attention to him!”","Chu Feng laughed. “I thought you had devoted yourself to your career?”","“And you believe my words? Why do you think I’m working on my career? It’s all so I can marry a good wife,” Ye Xiancheng scoffed.","Chu Feng was rendered speechless.","The lava beneath them suddenly bubbled, and a humongous tombstone emerged. Evidently, the Heavensword Sacred Palace had successfully deciphered the formation.","The tombstone was as massive as the other tombstones, but its jade color and texture, as well as its fluorescence, made it seem more like a treasure instead. However, the words inscribed on its surface said otherwise.","Tombstone of the Spectral Fairy.","“The master of the tombstone must be a woman,” Eggy said.","“The name has surfaced. Does this mean we can claim the legacy right away?” someone else asked.","In previous tombstone realms, the name of the tombstones’ masters only appeared after the tombstone had been deciphered, and the legacy was ready to be claimed.","“Not yet. We have not activated the formation,” Chu Feng replied.","“Chu Feng, I’ll give it a try,” Tianjian Canhua said.","She knew about the Seven Stars Orbs, and she was aware that the legacies in each of these seven tombstone realms were extraordinary. She didn’t want to miss this opportunity. On top of that, she was confident in pulling it off.","Weng!","An emerald light suddenly shot out from the tombstone and fell on Xian Miaomiao. This happened faster than anyone could react.","“Miaomiao!” Chu Feng rushed over, but he was much too slow.","In an instant, Xian Miaomiao had already been dragged into the tombstone. Mysterious runes surfaced on the tombstone right after.","“This is... an auxiliary formation?” Shen Hui and Chu Feng murmured.","The others widened their eyes in astonishment.","The purpose of the auxiliary formation was clear—it was to support the person deciphering the formation. But Chu Feng and the others were still outside. Who was going to decipher the formation then?","Only one person came to mind.","“Xian Miaomiao has been chosen?”","That was the most likely answer.","Tianjian Canhua frowned in displeasure."]},{"number":6422,"title":"Chapter 6422: Chapter 6420: Shocking Transformation. The Sealed Entrance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6420: Shocking Transformation. The Sealed Entrance","The tombstone soon emitted a red light.","The crowd was startled.","It was a warning.","The person deciphering the formation was struggling, and someone had to channel the auxiliary formation to help her.","At the same time, the red light was also warning about the dangers of the auxiliary formation. Those who channeled it would be taking on the risks involved in the deciphering as well.","But Chu Feng didn’t hesitate to channel his spirit power into the auxiliary formation.","Seeing that, Shen Hui and the other Spirit God Clansmen made a move, too.","As spirit power flowed into the auxiliary formation, the red light faded.","However, Chu Feng and the others dared not let their guard down. They could already sense the high difficulty in controlling the auxiliary formation.","“This auxiliary formation can only be channeled by world spiritists. I’ll work with the Spirit God Clansmen on this. I ask the rest of you not to make a move,” Chu Feng said.","The more people involved in the auxiliary formation, the more chaotic the situation became. Those who lacked proficiency in world spiritist techniques would only be causing a mess for themselves.","The Spirit God Clan comprised 1111 Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, but Shen Hui was the one channeling all their spirit power, so they were as good as one entity.","It would be easier for Chu Feng to control the formation if he simply worked with Shen Hui on it.","“Lord Chu Feng, shall I transfer our spirit power to you?” Shen Hui asked. She thought that this formation was more suited for one person to take charge.","“All right.” Chu Feng accepted the offer.","The auxiliary formation was challenging, and the slightest misstep could cause a backlash. If they failed to control it properly, not only would they be of no help to Xian Miaomiao, but it would also increase the difficulty of her obtaining the legacy.","And if Xian Miaomiao failed to obtain the legacy, the only outcome awaiting her was death.","While Chu Feng was focused on the auxiliary formation, a major event happened in the world of cultivation.","All the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders and the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief were gathered around an observation formation.","Their auras were stronger than before. Jie Tianran’s return from the God’s Era had brought great benefits to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, pushing their strength to a greater height. However, their faces looked grim and even slightly pale, as if something huge had happened.","They were shaken up.","Jie Tianran finally arrived, landing at the center of the observation formation. When he saw the image projected by the observation formation, he frowned.","A faint, black fog had appeared at the outer perimeter of the Ninth Galaxy, causing the previously brightest galaxy to turn into the dimmest one instead.","This was no ordinary black fog. It harnessed some kind of power.","“Lord Mansion Master, can you tell what it is?” the elders asked.","Jie Tianran had been in closed-door training. He had made it clear beforehand that he was not to be disturbed unless something major happened.","Under normal circumstances, they shouldn’t have disturbed the training Jie Tianran for an external development. But, as Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, they could tell that the black fog shrouding the Ninth Galaxy was a huge deal.","It concerned the world of cultivation’s safety.","“You’re world spiritists from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. How can you not tell what it is just because it’s further away?” Jie Tianran frowned in displeasure.","“Lord Mansion Master, is it a sealing power?” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","They had a conjecture, but they weren’t sure if they were right.","What they were seeing was not the true Ninth Galaxy but just its entrance, but even so, the Ninth Galaxy was still the largest galaxy in the present world of cultivation. It was unbelievable that any power could seal it off, so they doubted their guess.","That was why they called Jie Tianran out.","“It is a sealing power, and it is seeping out from the Immemorial Cemetery,” Jie Tianran said.","“The Immemorial Cemetery wields the power to seal off the Ninth Galaxy? But why does it seek to seal off the Ninth Galaxy? Is it related to the Ninth Galaxy?”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the other Saint-tier elders were perplexed.","Jie Tianran suddenly frowned. He quickly turned to look at God’s Era.","Confused, the others did the same. What they saw made them turn pale. This was the second shock they had suffered today.","God’s Era was dimming.","Why would God’s Era dim when the Ninth Galaxy was being sealed off? Was there a connection between the two?","“Even God’s Era is affected,” Jie Tianran said. “Looks like I’ve underestimated the Immemorial Cemetery.”","His words confirmed that the Immemorial Cemetery was behind the sealing of the Ninth Galaxy’s entrance.","Jie Tianran had ordered the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion not to venture into the Immemorial Cemetery, thinking that the power it wielded was bound to be inferior to God’s Era.","He assumed that he could plunder whatever fortuitous encounter others claimed from the Immemorial Cemetery once he grasped God’s Era’s power.","But it had become clear the Immemorial Cemetery was no weaker than God’s Era. If anything, the Immemorial Cemetery appeared to be the stronger one now.","Having entered God’s Era himself, Jie Tianran knew that God’s Era had yet to reveal its true power, and he still held on to the belief that the power inside God’s Era was unparalleled. That said, he acknowledged that the Immemorial Cemetery was not to be underestimated.","A brief moment later, Jie Tianran burst into laughter.","“The world of cultivation sure is interesting.”","There were so many mysteries in the world of cultivation waiting to be uncovered, and that excited him. Then, he said, “We’ll deal with it when it comes our way. Do whatever you should in the meantime.”","He disappeared after leaving those words behind.","Despite Jie Tianran’s words, the other elders remained worried.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had risen to the top through the ranks by clearing remnants that others couldn’t. But God’s Era emerged, and now the Immemorial Cemetery was proving to be more formidable than they had expected as well.","It felt like they were confronting powers far beyond their means to deal with, and control was swiftly slipping from their hands. This made them feel insignificant and uneasy.","The voice in Jie Tianran’s body asked, “You’ll have to venture into the Ninth Galaxy in the future. You won’t be able to step in there if that power seals off the Ninth Galaxy’s entrance. Aren’t you worried?”","Jie Tianran smirked. “I don’t know what lurks in the Immemorial Cemetery, nor do I know its intent for sealing off the Ninth Galaxy. But one thing I know is that it shan’t get in my way once I have made up my mind to enter the Ninth Galaxy.”"]},{"number":6423,"title":"Chapter 6423: Chapter 6421: The First Heaven Gate","paragraphs":["Chapter 6421: The First Heaven Gate","Song Changsheng was inside the Immemorial Cemetery, but the area he was in was different from the area Chu Feng and the others were at.","This area was packed with powerful black aura monsters and ferocious beasts. These beasts were bloodthirsty and lacked sentience. An encounter with these beasts would lead to certain death if one were incapable of slaying them.","Surprisingly, Song Changsheng could view the situation outside the Immemorial Cemetery in this space. His eyes were locked on the Ninth Galaxy. Due to the proximity, he could clearly see the billowing black fog.","“They are cornering us.”","Others might not know why the black fog was sealing off the Ninth Galaxy, but Song Changsheng, being inside the Immemorial Galaxy, could fathom a guess.","The monsters inside the Immemorial Cemetery were extremely powerful. They were beyond the means of the present-era cultivators to deal with, and they were countless. Should they escape from the Immemorial Cemetery, given their bloodthirsty nature, it would be a massacre.","The only way out was to escape to the Ninth Galaxy.","But with the Ninth Galaxy sealed, there was nowhere to escape to. What awaited all living beings in the world of cultivation was to be torn into shreds.","Song Changsheng’s eyes turned cold.","The only way to avoid such an ending was for him to slay all the monsters in the Immemorial Cemetery. He had already found the monsters’ nest—it was located in a tombstone realm.","His eyes widened in surprise when he stepped into that eerie realm.","There were carcasses piled up wherever he looked. It were the carcasses of the ferocious beasts.","Unlike the black aura monster that attempted to escape from the gate, these ferocious beasts didn’t dissipate upon death, though they didn’t possess origin energies either. Judging from the bodies, they had only just been killed.","Song Changsheng suddenly sensed an aura. He took a step forward, and the scenery swiftly flew past him. In an instant, he arrived at somewhere completely different.","A white-robed lady stood in front of him—Tianjian Qingyuan.","Song Changsheng had already met Tianjian Qingyuan some time ago while he was exploring the Immemorial Cemetery. The latter had tried to stop him from venturing any further back then. Due to that, he knew that she was extremely powerful.","“I was wondering who could kill all those ferocious beasts,” Song Changsheng said.","That doubt was immediately answered when he saw Tianjian Qingyuan.","“I knew you’d come.”","“Are you here to stop me again?”","“It looks like we’ll have to join hands, or else a calamity might befall the world of cultivation.”","Tianjian Qingyuan glanced at a stone gate not too far away.","The stone gate was open, and it was inscribed with the portrait of an armored ferocious beast wielding a weapon. It felt like a hybrid between the black aura monster and the ferocious beasts here.","Whatever the being inscribed on the stone gate was, it looked much stronger than the black aura monsters and the ferocious beasts Song Changsheng had encountered along the way.","“The water here runs deeper than I thought.” Song Changsheng sighed.","“Mm.” Tianjian Qingyuan nodded.","“Have you entered yet?”","“Not yet.”","“I’m guessing that monster lurks in there?” Song Changsheng was referring to the portrait inscribed on the stone gate.","“If that’s all, we won’t have anything to fear. But I don’t think it’ll be that simple. I fear there may be stronger entities inside,” Tianjian Qingyuan replied.","“Indeed. We’ll be in trouble if there are immemorial beings in there,” Song Changsheng said.","He was rarely pessimistic, but it was important to remain grounded here. He was confident in his strength, but only against present-era experts. He was still lacking compared to top experts in the Ancient Era, let alone beings from the Immemorial Era.","“We might not need to enter. I have a treasure to seal this gate off,” Song Changsheng said.","“I have to enter,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","“To sever the problem at its root?”","“I’m not the one who opened this gate. It's the person I am looking for, and she has entered the gate.”","“Who is it?” Song Changsheng was intrigued.","Someone capable of reaching this place was bound to be extraordinary, and he was curious to know who else in the present world of cultivation was capable of such a feat.","“Have you heard of Chu Feng?” Tianjian Qingyuan asked.","“Mm,” Song Changsheng replied.","“It’s Chu Feng’s grandmother. I have promised Chu Feng to help him find his grandmother,” Tianjian Qingyuan replied as she stepped into the stone gate.","Song Changsheng followed suit.","He had come here to resolve this problem, and there was less reason to hesitate now that he knew Chu Feng’s grandmother had entered the stone gate.","Beyond the stone gate was a pitch-black space that was devoid of anything but a path. The path was wide and stretched into the horizon. Dangers lurked in this space, but opportunities were waiting to be uncovered as well.","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan flitted down the path.","Moments later, they sensed searing heat. Taking a closer look, they spotted a charred carcass lying on the path ahead of them. From the carcass’ outline, they recognized it to be the ferocious beast inscribed on the stone gate.","Tianjian Qingyuan seemed to have sensed something, prompting her to accelerate forth.","Song Changsheng followed suit.","There were countless charred carcasses along the way, but neither of them paid them any heed. They sensed something much more important ahead.","Finally, a gate appeared in their sights.","It stood in the middle of the path, spanning a hundred meters wide but over ten thousand meters tall. Beyond the gate was a brilliant world filled with countless stars, an amazing sight that could no longer be seen in the present world of cultivation.","Concentrated natural energies seeped out from the gate. It felt like the world on the other side of the gate existed as well.","Chu Feng’s grandmother could be seen on the other side of the gate.","“That should be the real Ninth Galaxy. Could this be the Heaven Gate Chu Feng mentioned?” Song Changsheng murmured.","“Heaven Gate?” Tianjian Qingyuan was confused.","Song Changsheng quickly explained about Heaven Gate.","In the meantime, the two of them flitted up to the gate.","Tianjian Qingyuan stretched her hand forth to drag Chu Feng’s grandmother out from within.","By now, she had already learned that passing through the Heaven Gate was an amazing fortuitous encounter, but she had been tasked to bring Chu Feng’s grandmother back. However, she realized that her hand couldn’t pass through the gate at all.","It occurred to her that she was going to break her promise."]},{"number":6424,"title":"Chapter 6424: Chapter 6422: Formation Failed","paragraphs":["Chapter 6422: Formation Failed","Tianjian Qingyuan thought of an idea and shouted, “Are you going to abandon Chu Feng?”","Chu Feng’s grandmother, despite having ventured some distance across the Heaven Gate, suddenly halted her footsteps. She was briefly stunned before she abruptly turned around and walked back.","Boom!","Space jolted and distorted when she made her very first step. A formidable power was preventing her from turning back. However, Chu Feng’s grandmother’s turbid eyes hardened with resolution.","“Feng’er!”","She had to return no matter what it took for Chu Feng.","Thus, she unleashed terrifying flames that swiftly fanned outward like waves. Her aura also flared, revealing strength capable of destroying several realms with a snap of the finger.","Even Tianjian Qingyuan was astounded by this sight. “Her cultivation!”","Song Changsheng was surprised as well, but he soon laughed in realization. No wonder Chu Xuanyuan is so strong. Even his mother is a figure to be reckoned with as well.","But the force stopping Chu Feng’s grandmother was far stronger, almost like a heavenly law. Every step she took was incredibly strenuous, causing lacerations to appear all over her body. Despite her strength, she couldn’t overcome this force.","“There’s no way to return after entering Heaven Gate. You’re only harming her by calling her back,” Song Changsheng said.","“But I promised Chu Feng to bring his grandmother back,” Tianjian Qingyuan replied.","“Do you intend to bring a corpse back?” Song Changsheng replied.","Tianjian Qingyuan was stunned.","“Chu Feng engaged your help because he thought the Immemorial Cemetery was too dangerous, and he was worried that a mishap might befall his grandmother. It goes without saying that he wishes his grandmother to be safe.","“And don’t you think he would want his grandmother to benefit from the Heaven Gate if she has managed to open it? You shouldn’t ruin her over a promise,” Song Changsheng said.","He turned to Chu Feng’s grandmother and shouted, “Elder, don’t force yourself. Chu Feng and Chu Xuanyuan will be heartbroken if something happens to you. Your safety is more important than anything.","“Chu Feng is safe here, so you can venture into the Ninth Galaxy with ease of mind. Chu Xuanyuan is also in the Ninth Galaxy now. Don’t you want to meet him? You should head there and find a way to treat your body, so that you can meet your family members in your best state.","“It’s only a matter of time before Chu Feng enters the Ninth Galaxy as well. Make sure to look for Chu Feng when the time comes. Don’t let him continue shouldering everything alone like an orphan, without anyone to protect him.”","Song Changsheng’s words struck some sense into Chu Feng’s grandmother, and tears brimmed in her determined eyes.","Without saying a word, she reined in her flames.","Just then, a trail of light appeared beneath her feet. The light expanded, enveloping her and forming an entire path. Then, the path of light disintegrated from the tail end till it vanished from sight.","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan knew the path would lead Chu Feng’s grandmother toward the special region prepared by the Heaven Gate.","The Heaven Gate closed, but the path before them continued into the horizon.","Tianjian Qingyuan’s eyes lingered on the area where Chu Feng’s grandmother disappeared.","“Don’t worry, I’ll back your words,” Song Changsheng said.","Tianjian Qingyuan nearly ruined Chu Feng’s grandmother over the promise she made, but it was an unintentional mistake. She didn’t know that it was impossible to turn back once one had entered the Heaven Gate, and turning back would result in a backlash.","She didn’t stop Song Changsheng from dissuading Chu Feng’s grandmother, which showed that she wished for the safety of Chu Feng’s grandmother, too.","Tianjian Qingyuan smiled. “I still owe Chu Feng one.”","She continued venturing down the path, and Song Changsheng followed her.","Bringing back Chu Feng’s grandmother was a side mission. They had to continue with the more important task they had on hand.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng was busy channeling the auxiliary formation. They had reached a critical point. His undivided attention was required, for a lapse in focus could unravel all they had done thus far.","All of a sudden, his eyes widened.","His grandmother’s aura had vanished. He could no longer sense his grandmother’s location, as if she had disappeared from the face of the world.","This resulted in a lapse in his attention.","The auxiliary formation immediately turned blood red. Blood pillars shot toward Chu Feng and the Spirit God Clansmen.","It happened so fast that Chu Feng and the Spirit God Clansmen were enveloped by the red light before the crowd could react.","“Chu Feng!!!”","Little Fishy, Song Yun, Wang Qiang, and the others rushed over, but they couldn’t do anything about the red light shrouding Chu Feng.","Chu Feng and the others stopped moving as if they were frozen in time. Not even their eyes were blinking.","“Don’t make a reckless move. You might harm them instead,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Little Fishy and the others knew he was right and held themselves back despite being worried.","Meanwhile, Shen Hui and her Spirit God Clansmen’s consciousness were transported into another space. They found themselves standing on a stone pavement, before a majestic hall.","There were no other buildings in the vicinity, and the sky was shrouded in a white light.","“Lord Shen Hui, have we lost?”","The Spirit God Clansmen looked at Shen Hui.","Before Shen Hui could reply, a middle-aged woman’s voice echoed, “You’re world spiritists. You should have known there is a price to pay for failing the auxiliary formation.”","The voice was pleasant. It was authoritative yet not severe.","“What’s the price?” Shen Hui asked.","“You entrusted your spirit power to that lad because you trusted him. I’ll give you two choices. One, give up on him and let him shoulder the punishment all alone. You’ll still be punished, but your lives will be spared. Two, trust him and shoulder the punishment with him. However, the chances are that you won’t walk out of here alive.”","The Spirit God Clansmen turned to Chu Feng. They didn’t utter a word, but their panic was evident on their faces. Even Shen Hui couldn’t make a choice.","They had come here to aid Chu Feng, but it was to repay their debt to Xue Ji. They had no ties with him beforehand. To decide whether they should put their lives on the line for Chu Feng was too much of a decision for them to make in the spur of the moment.","To be fair, their hesitation already revealed the goodwill they harbored toward Chu Feng. Anyone else in their position wouldn’t hesitate to abandon him."]},{"number":6425,"title":"Chapter 6425: Chapter 6423: The Spirit God Clan’s Honor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6423: The Spirit God Clan’s Honor","“Are there any other choices?” Shen Hui asked.","“There are none,” the voice replied.","More than a thousand red needles appeared in the majestic hall. They corresponded to the number of Spirit God Clansmen.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","The red needles shot forth and pierced the Spirit God Clansmen.","A brief silence later, piercing screams rang. The Spirit God Clansmen were in so much pain that they couldn’t even stand stably. They dropped to their knees and bums, with some even lying on the floor, clutching where they were impaled while convulsing nonstop.","Shen Hui was the one who coped the best in her clan. She didn’t wail, but she gritted her teeth and sweat trickled down her pale face.","A red light flickered in the majestic hall, and countless more red needles appeared. There had to be at least a million of them.","“A thousand needles for each person. That’s the price you have to pay. But if you give up on Chu Feng now, you’ll only have to endure nine needles,” the woman said.","“Lord Shen Hui!”","Many looked at Shen Hui with pleading eyes. A single needle was already unbearable; enduring a thousand of them was unimaginable. Their minds would be crushed even if they survived this ordeal!","But Shen Hui continued to hesitate.","“Lord Shen Hui, it’s one thing if we do this for Lord Xue Ji, but is it worth undergoing this for Chu Feng, too? We don’t owe him anything! He’s not the one who broke the formation trapping us!” a clansman said.","Many agreed with her.","“Don’t forget the mission of our Spirit God Clan. This is Lord Xue Ji’s order,” Shen Hui replied.","But her words failed to convince her clansmen.","“But he isn’t the one who rescued us! I’m not afraid of death. I would willingly lay down my life for Lord Xue Ji. But Lord Xue Ji is not here, and I don’t think it’s worthwhile for me to die for Chu Feng. Lord Shen Hui, I beseech you to reconsider your decision. Our lives mean something as well!” a Spirit God Clansman exclaimed.","This placed tremendous pressure on Shen Hui. It wouldn’t make sense for their clansmen to lay down their lives for Chu Feng.","In the first place, the Spirit God Clan was different from mortals; they were worthy of being deemed gods just by virtue of their bloodline.","“There is a price for hesitation. You don’t get to choose anymore,” the woman said.","A formation suddenly descended from the sky.","Spirit power converged to form a window, and within the window was another palace that resembled theirs. There was only one person inside that palace—Chu Feng.","Chu Feng had a knee on the floor and was gasping for air. He was drenched as if he had been caught in a torrential rain. Sweat droplets rained down from him. Even his eyes were bloodshot.","“Lord Chu Feng?”","The Spirit God Clansmen’s hearts clenched up. They had even forgotten about the pain they were in. They noticed countless red needles scattered on the ground behind Chu Feng—there were a thousand of them.","Chu Feng didn’t collapse or even let out a howl despite having taken a thousand needles?","The Spirit God Clansmen were taken aback.","A spirit formation gate appeared behind Chu Feng.","“What’s this?” Chu Feng asked.","The woman replied, “You have overcome the trial of a thousand needles. You may leave now.”","The Spirit God Clansmen paled in despair. They realized that they didn’t have the option to offset the punishment to Chu Feng anymore and that they had to withstand the punishment of a thousand needles, too.","But Chu Feng didn’t leave via the spirit formation gate. “Where are my companions?”","“They have to suffer the same punishment as you,” the woman said.","“I’ll take it on their behalf,” Chu Feng said.","The Spirit God Clansmen, including Shen Hui, couldn’t believe what they had heard. Even the woman was startled, and she only asked after a momentary pause, “Are you saying that you’ll take the thousand needles for them?”","“That’s right,” Chu Feng replied without hesitation.","“How many of them will you take the punishment for?”","“All of them.”","“All of them? You should think it through. They have to withstand a thousand needles each. Do you know how many needles you have to take if you wish to take all their punishments?”","“I know.”","“Are you tired of living?” The woman’s voice was tinged in disbelief.","“I’ll survive. And so will they,” Chu Feng declared.","Shen Hui was dumbstruck.","The Spirit God Clansmen had conflicted feelings, especially those who had urged Shen Hui to give up on Chu Feng earlier. They hadn’t known Chu Feng for long, and there were no deep ties between them.","It would have been reasonable for Chu Feng to give up on them, just like how they had given up on Chu Feng.","“No wonder Lord Xue Ji says we’re more suited to follow Lord Chu Feng. I see it now,” Shen Hui said with a smile.","The Spirit God Clansmen didn’t speak a word, but determination gleamed in their eyes.","“You are a tenacious one, but you don’t get to choose. The final call lies on them,” the woman said.","The two windows aligned, allowing Chu Feng to see the Spirit God Clansmen as well.","Shen Hui said, “I’ll take on my share of the thousand needles.”","The other Spirit God Clansmen voiced her words, “We’ll take on our share of the thousand needles, too.”","Chu Feng looked at their pale faces, as well as the single needle behind them, and hurriedly interjected, “Shen Hui, you won’t be able to withstand it. Let me take it on your behalf. I was the one who got careless and made a mistake. I ought to take responsibility for this.”","Shen Hui shook her head. “No.”","She stood up and led the Spirit God Clansmen toward the window.","Chu Feng was intrigued. He sensed a subtle change in the gazes of Shen Hui and the Spirit God Clansmen.","“Lord Chu Feng, there is something I have not told you.","“Our Spirit God Clansmen’s ‘Shen (God)’ surname was bestowed upon us by our first master. Since our master left, we have been scattered over the world of cultivation. Our master has left a formation with each of our lines, and if someone succeeds in deciphering that formation, we’ll have to pledge our loyalty to that person.","“Lord Xue Ji has not only saved us but also deciphered that formation, but she refuses to be our master and instead recommended Lord Chu Feng. That’s the true reason we sought you out. We had our reservations regarding this, as Lord Chu Feng wasn’t the one who deciphered the formation, and we couldn’t make up our mind whether to view you as our master.","“But now, we have made up our minds.”","Shen Hui kneeled. The other Spirit God Clansmen followed her. All of them kowtowed to Chu Feng at the same time.","“Paying respect to master!”","Before Chu Feng could respond, the Spirit God Clansmen stood up. Shen Hui said, “We’ll take our share of the thousand needles. Please begin.”","“You’ll die!” Chu Feng exclaimed.","“Even if we die here, we’ll make sure you survive,” Shen Hui replied.","“If you truly acknowledge me as your master, you ought to listen to me. I’ll survive even if I take your share of the punishment. I order you right now to heed my order,” Chu Feng said.","He believed this was his responsibility, and he didn’t want anyone to suffer for his mistake.","But Shen Hui replied, “Lord Chu Feng, you are the first master we have acknowledged since the Ancient Era. There has been a teaching passed down within our line.","“If our master’s life is not compromised, we will prioritize our master’s orders.","“If our master’s life is compromised, we will prioritize our master’s safety.","“It’s our greatest honor to lay down our lives for our master.","“And it’ll be our greatest shame should we cause the death of our master.”"]},{"number":6426,"title":"Chapter 6426: Chapter 6424: The Final Star","paragraphs":["Chapter 6424: The Final Star","After saying those words, Shen Hui turned to the red needles and said, “You may begin.”","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","The red needles flew toward the Spirit God Clansmen.","The Spirit God Clansmen might have hardened their resolve, but seeing the red needles whiz toward them still filled them with so much fear that they closed their eyes.","Seconds passed. They opened their eyes in bewilderment and confusion. The pain they had been waiting for never came. So, they raised their heads, only to see that the red needles had vanished.","Even the red needles that had pierced through their bodies and fallen on the ground had disappeared.","The formation window expanded, linking the two palaces where the Spirit God Clansmen and Chu Feng were together. They were finally in the same place.","Shen Hui quickly flitted over to Chu Feng’s side with the Spirit God Clansmen to protect him. The red needles might have vanished, but that didn’t mean they were out of danger yet.","“The Spirit God Clansmen are very alert.” Eggy nodded in approval.","These 1111 Spirit God Clansmen were Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists; they would have been revered as gods no matter where they went. Yet, they lowered their posture before Chu Feng as if they were his servants, and they were willing to lay down their lives for Chu Feng.","Eggy liked to see strong people lowering themselves to Chu Feng.","Boom!","The ground suddenly shook vigorously, and a giant appeared in the hall. The hall was, by no means, small, but the appearance of the giant made the hall feel cramped. Before this giant, Chu Feng and the others felt like tiny ants.","Taking a closer look, it was a green monstrous beast resembling a dragon. It had six feet, and it lay curled on the ground. It exuded a natural air of malevolence even though it didn’t release its aura. It was immediately apparent to Chu Feng and all the Spirit God Clansmen that this dragon could kill them in a heartbeat.","But Chu Feng and the others were more focused on the monstrous beast’s head.","The monstrous beast wore a crown, but upon closer examination, one would realize that the crown was a chair. Atop the chair sat a woman.","The woman wore a green skirt with open seams that revealed hints of her snowy thighs. Her emerald eyes glistened like jewels. But her most striking trait was still her powerful disposition, which made it clear that she was unbelievably strong.","No wonder the monstrous beast could only serve as her chair leg.","She held a red needle in her hand—it was identical to the ones that had pierced through Chu Feng and the others, but the one she held was the real one.","“Trust is the most precious thing in the world, and I see it in all of you,” the woman said. It was the same voice that had addressed them earlier.","“Elder, are you the Spectral Fairy?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s right,” the woman replied.","“Chu Feng, is she the main body, a soul fragment, or a formation? Is she from the Ancient Era or the Immemorial Era?” Eggy was burning with curiosity.","“I can’t tell, but she’s terrifyingly strong even if it’s just a soul fragment,” Chu Feng replied.","“She’s formidable. I can’t even begin to gauge her limits. I doubt I’d stand a chance against her even if I pit my life against her. Chu Feng, make sure you speak to her politely. Don’t anger her,” Eggy reminded.","Chu Feng could tell as much, so he quickly greeted with a bow, “Junior pays respect to the Spectral Fairy.”","Shen Hui and the Spirit God Clansmen followed suit.","Having acknowledged Chu Feng as their master, they would mirror Chu Feng’s stance. If Chu Feng didn’t pay respect to the Spectral Fairy, they wouldn’t do it either, despite knowing she was not to be trifled with. If Chu Feng wanted her dead, they would cooperate with him even if it spelled death.","“You may stand on ceremony. I’m satisfied with all of you. I shall pass on the power of the auxiliary formation to Xian Miaomiao, though it’s still up to her whether she can claim my legacy or not.”","The Spectral Fairy set her eyes on Chu Feng and smiled faintly. “You, in particular, are very commendable, but unfortunately, my legacy doesn’t suit you.”","The space around Chu Feng and the others warped once more. Before they knew it, their consciousness had returned to their bodies, and they were standing where they were before.","The red light shrouding them had returned to the auxiliary formation, and the auxiliary formation was finally pulling its weight, emanating incredible energy without anyone channeling it.","“Big brother.”","“C-C-Chu Feng.”","Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and the others stood around Chu Feng, looking at him with worried eyes. Sensing their concern, Chu Feng said, “Don’t worry, I’m fine.”","The crowd breathed a sigh of relief.","Even though Chu Feng and the others were shaken earlier from being struck by the red needles, they recovered after returning to their bodies. There were no injuries on their bodies or their souls.","Soon, the tombstone began to glow.","Chu Feng and the others were overjoyed. This phenomenon only appeared whenever someone successfully inherits a tombstone’s legacy.","“It’s so close?” Chu Feng could now sense the location of the seventh star, and he was surprised by what he felt. He turned to Shen Hui and pointed out a general direction for her. “Shen Hui, scout this location.”","Shen Hui quickly turned the observation formation over.","Their next destination was not too far away. A red light had appeared amid empty space, and it grew larger until it covered every corner. Tombstone realms that stood in its way were devoured and turned red.","The red light originated from a massive congregation of flames resembling the sun... but that was not the sun but a tombstone. Unlike other eerie tombstones, this one was covered in flames and lightning that interweaved without clashing with each other.","“W-what’s that?”","The spectators outside were initially drawn to the phenomenon from Xian Miaomiao inheriting the Spectral Fairy’s legacy, but their attention was quickly stolen by the humongous tombstone imbued with flames and lightning.","How huge was the tombstone?","It was a hundred times larger than other tombstones. The other tombstones looked underwhelming compared to it.","“Chu Feng, what is that?” Huangfu Zhantian and the others turned to Chu Feng.","They also saw the tombstone realm through Shen Hui’s formation.","“It’s the final star,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6427,"title":"Chapter 6427: Chapter 6425: I Wholeheartedly Agree","paragraphs":["Chapter 6425: I Wholeheartedly Agree","“The final star?”","The crowd felt immense pressure. The final star looked too terrifying. If such was its appearance, the difficulty level was bound to be extreme.","Chu Feng didn’t feel intimidated.","In contrast, Tianjian Canhua’s complexion looked awful. She wanted a Seven Stars Orbs’ legacy, and she had intended to challenge the sixth star, but the legacy chose Xian Miaomiao. Thus, she set her eyes on the final star.","She didn’t expect the final star to be this scary.","This sparked fear in her heart.","“Chu Feng.” Xian Miaomiao flew out from the tombstone.","“Did you obtain the legacy?” Chu Feng asked.","“Mm. The legacy is very compatible with me, though the trial wasn’t easy. I wouldn’t have succeeded if not for you and the other elders. Thank you.” Xian Miaomiao thanked Chu Feng before bowing to the Spirit God Clansmen.","She had already learned that the Spirit God Clansmen had aided Chu Feng in channeling the auxiliary formation. If not for the auxiliary formation, she might not have obtained the legacy.","“We’re just following our master’s orders,” Shen Hui replied.","“Master?”","The crowd directed curious looks over.","The Spirit God Clan’s background was an enigma to the crowd.","Their top-tier fighting prowess was lacking compared to the Zhao Immortal Clan, the Ye Immortal Clan, and the Heavensword Sacred Palace, but they were the strongest in terms of average strength, with their clan being filled with Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","On top of that, they wielded extraordinary means. Their power ceiling appeared to be high.","Who could the master of this clan possibly be?","“Our master is Lord Chu Feng,” Shen Hui replied.","“Huh? Chu Feng has become your master?”","That baffled the crowd, including Tianjian Canhua. There was a difference between calling someone ‘lord’ and ‘master’. Lord could have been a respectful term to refer to a person of higher stature, but master outright pointed to a subservient relationship.","Why would the powerful Spirit God Clan acknowledge Chu Feng as their master? Despite Chu Feng’s great potential, he was still far weaker than them right now.","“It’s a long story. It’s my honor to have won the Spirit God Clan’s approval.” Chu Feng smiled.","Shen Hui quickly corrected him, “No, master. It is our honor to serve you.”","“Lord Shen Hui is right. It is the honor of our Spirit God Clan to serve you, master.”","Even the reticent Spirit God Clansmen also nodded in agreement.","This left the crowd flabbergasted.","Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, Xian Miaomiao, and the others smiled in delight. They were overjoyed that Chu Feng had won over the Spirit God Clan.","Xian Miaomiao relayed a voice transmission to Chu Feng, “You have to decipher the final star. It’ll grant you not just the legacy but the power to open the Heaven Gate, too. I have obtained the power myself, and I can open it to enter the Ninth Galaxy right away if I wish to.”","Chu Feng replied via voice transmission, “Congratulations, Miaomiao.”","“It’s all thanks to you! Chu Feng, you’re also planning on entering the Ninth Galaxy, right? If so, you should decipher the final star yourself. Don’t leave it to anyone else. Our lives are at stake, so you mustn’t mess up. I feel more confident entrusting my life to you,” Xian Miaomiao said.","She glanced at Tianjian Canhua while saying those words.","She could tell that Tianjian Canhua coveted the legacy. Knowing Chu Feng, she was worried Chu Feng could give this opportunity away to Tianjian Canhua.","“Yes, I’ll do it myself,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission.","Chu Feng led the group to the final star.","As they approached the star, they were suddenly bound by a powerful force and transported into a spatial passageway. At the other end of the spatial passageway was the star realm.","The realm was as big as it appeared on the outside, but it was shrouded in a thick fog that limited their visibility. They were located on a clearing, and at the center of the clearing was a huge tombstone shaped like a beautiful sword.","The tombstone itself was a treasure. It was made not out of stone but a fiery-red material.","However, the crowd’s attention was drawn to the clearing itself.","The clearing was not only large, but the ground was also embedded with what resembled little cobblestones. These ‘cobblestones’ exerted energy that caused their blood to gush, as if their bloodlines were telling them that the ‘cobblestones’ were highly beneficial to them.","“As expected of the final star. It’s different from the ones before. Little Chu Feng, can we use these treasures if we awaken them?”","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master, Ye Xiancheng’s parents, and the others asked Chu Feng. Even the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master looked over as well.","“I’m not sure, but all of us played a part in this. I’ll share the rewards if it’s possible to do so,” Chu Feng said.","The crowd smiled. Those gathered here could all be considered as Chu Feng’s allies.","“Chu Feng, why share the rewards with them? Judging from their expressions, those things are formidable, right? Why not keep them for ourselves?” Eggy was not very happy about it.","In her view, Chu Feng was the only one who could decipher the final star. No one should be able to complain if he took all the rewards for himself.","“Those stones reinforce a person’s cultivation foundation, such as their bloodline power or their Divine Body. Those from the older generations are excited because they sense that the energy inside those stones are highly beneficial to them, but I don’t feel anything. I suspect the stones won’t be of much use to us.”","By ‘us’, he was referring to the juniors.","The ones who were excited were those from the older generations.","Little Fishy’s parents and Huangfu Zhantian were excited by the stones as well, but they didn’t lose themselves.","As for Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and the others, they were as nonchalant as Chu Feng. Their talent was derived from their bloodlines, and their bloodlines were already strong enough. Due to that, the stones held little appeal to them.","“Brother, this place makes me u-u-uncomfortable. You should quickly obtain the l-l-legacy,” Wang Qiang urged.","“Big brother, you should get it over and done with,” Little Fishy also urged with a smile.","Tianjian Canhua suddenly interjected, “Chu Feng, please allow me to challenge this legacy.”","Those words displeased not just those who were close to Chu Feng, but even Yuwen Yanri and the new king as well. They might have obtained the Seven Stars Orbs, but they understood that the person who had done the most was Chu Feng.","There had been an implicit understanding that the final star would go to Chu Feng. It was not just about the difficulty level, but also so that Chu Feng could claim the biggest share of the reward given his contribution thus far.","But Tianjian Canhua wanted to snatch that away. Anyone with a sense of shame wouldn’t have done that.","Wang Qiang sneered, “Hmph. Shouldn’t y-y-you have some awareness? It’s not a f-f-food testing. You can’t just t-t-try it out just because you want to. This is the last star; our lives are all a-a-at stake here! You can die if you w-w-want too, but don’t drag us down with you!”","Wang Qiang’s words angered not just Tianjian Canhua but many others from the Heavensword Sacred Palace.","Someone even berated Wang Qiang, “Audacious! How dare you offend Miss Canhua?”","They saw Wang Qiang’s words as not just an affront to Tianjian Canhua but to the entire Heavensword Sacred Palace.","“Wang Qiang, what are you saying?” Song Yun interjected. She walked up to Tianjian Canhua and explained with a smile, “Miss, Wang Qiang isn’t good with words. I’m worried that you might misunderstand his intention, so let me explain on his behalf.","“He doesn’t think you’re worthy of this legacy, and I wholeheartedly agree.”"]},{"number":6428,"title":"Chapter 6428: Chapter 6426: The Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor","paragraphs":["“Audacious!”","Many swords were immediately pointed at Song Yun, but she stood brazen and fearless, her eyes gleaming with coldness.","“Stop!” the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master roared with visible displeasure.","The members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace hurriedly sheathed their swords.","“It’s normal for youngsters to bicker. It’s an argument, not a fight. Don’t you think it’s too much for the elders to get involved?” The Palace Master glared at the elders.","The members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace didn’t reply, but they lowered their heads out of deference for the Palace Master.","“Wang Qiang, Song Yun, we’re all friends. You shouldn’t say such words,” Chu Feng berated Wang Qiang and Song Yun.","Wang Qiang smiled without saying a word.","Song Yun remarked, “It was a joke. I’m sure that miss doesn’t mind.”","“Are we close enough for you to joke with me? I don’t like it when others joke about me,” Tianjian Canhua scoffed coldly.","Song Yun replied, “How unfortunate. I happen to like to joke around.”","Sensing the atmosphere going awry, Chu Feng quickly interjected, “Miss Canhua, I have observed the legacy here, and it’s possible for us to awaken it together. Do you want to come with me?”","“I’d like to give it a try.” Tianjian Canhua was much more polite when speaking to Chu Feng.","“Let’s go then.”","Chu Feng made his way toward the swordlike tombstone.","Tianjian Canhua followed him, though she trailed at a distance behind. She was already intending to give up on the legacy, but after entering the realm, the circumstances didn’t feel as dire, so she thought of giving it a try.","That said, she was still not confident about it.","She could tell that the trial would be triggered once one was within a certain radius of the tombstone. She wasn’t sure how the trial would be like, so she decided to keep a distance and let Chu Feng test the water first.","Weng!","As Chu Feng approached the tombstone, runes resembling lightning bolts began appearing on the tombstone’s surface. He immediately halted his footsteps, formed a hand seal, and closed his eyes to prepare for the trial.","“Hoh. T-t-this final tombstone is indeed not the same as the ones before,” Wang Qiang said.","Even the airs emanated by the final star was already far stronger than the previous stars.","Tianjian Canhua paid close heed to Chu Feng’s expression. It was only after seeing the calm look on his face did she dare approach.","But as soon as she arrived beside Chu Feng, her face warped in horror. Energy swiftly gushed into her body, making her feel like her head and soul were going to burst. She was forced to turn around right away and retreat.","“Chu Feng, you’re more compatible with the legacy. I shan’t compete with you.”","Tianjian Canhua headed back to where the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members were gathered.","“Canhua, this legacy looks extraordinary. How can you give up just like that?” an elder asked.","The Palace Master placed her fingers on Tianjian Canhua’s pulse. The latter’s pulse was extremely unstable. Tianjian Canhua only appeared unfazed because of her remarkable self-control; anyone else in her place would be bleeding from their seven apertures by now.","“Is Chu Feng that formidable?”","The Palace Master took another look at Chu Feng, who appeared completely unfazed, and sighed.","Tianjian Canhua was the most outstanding prodigy in their lineage, yet she paled far in comparison to Chu Feng. This humongous gap sent shivers down her spine. Just what kind of monster was Chu Feng?","“The legacy might just be suited to him,” Tianjian Canhua replied, refusing to admit defeat.","“It could be the same situation as the sixth star. He could be the chosen successor of this legacy, just that it wasn’t made obvious,” the Palace Master replied.","She was inclined to believe Tianjian Canhua, since she didn’t think it could be possible for there to be such a huge gap between top-tier prodigies. It would make sense if the legacy had chosen Chu Feng and was rejecting anyone else who came close.","“Are you all right?” Song Yun asked Tianjian Canhua with a provocative smile. It was as if she had seen through Tianjian Canhua’s deception.","Tianjian Canhua ignored her. That only made Song Yun’s smile widen.","That irked Tianjian Canhua. She turned to the Palace Master and discreetly asked, “Palace Master, why do we have to cooperate with scums from the Netherworld Sect?”","“She is Chu Feng’s friend. We should show her some courtesy here. But that won’t matter once we’re out of here,” the Palace Master replied.","Tianjian Canhua’s complexion finally alleviated.","In gist, the Palace Master was saying that she was free to deal with Song Yun, Wang Qiang, and anyone else once they parted ways with Chu Feng.","Meanwhile, lightning began manifesting around Chu Feng as well.","Boom!","Flames suddenly ignited around Chu Feng and the tombstone. The flames and the lightning interweaved, forming a sight similar to that outside the tombstone realm.","The tombstone emitted a peerless aura reminiscent of a true sword. The little stones in the clearing that could enhance one’s bloodline power glowed with peculiar lights. Suddenly, the clearing resembled a holy land.","Words appeared on the tombstone—Tombstone of the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor!","Whoosh!","Metallic clangs could suddenly be heard from the surrounding fog.","Thick chains shot out from the fog and sealed off the clearing like a bird cage. Red runes surfaced on the chains, causing the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor’s tombstone and the clearing to dim.","The chains had sealed the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor’s legacy!","Whoosh!","One of the chains shattered, creating an opening in the cage.","Before the crowd could make sense of the situation, a hoarse voice echoed from the direction of the opening, “Are you trying to release the Seven Stars Orbs? You aren’t qualified!”"]},{"number":6429,"title":"Chapter 6429: Chapter 6427: Inside the Gate","paragraphs":["The crowd, including Chu Feng, felt their hearts clenching up.","They sensed an incredibly oppressive aura crushing down from the sky. It was not coming from this realm but further beyond, and it enveloped the entire Immemorial Cemetery.","Even Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan sensed it as well.","They were still on the path where they had found Chu Feng’s grandmother, just that they had ventured further in. The path had widened to the point where they couldn’t see where the sides ended anymore, but it was still apparent to them that it was a path.","Both of them were wielding weapons. There were beads of sweat on their faces.","The further they ventured into the path, the stronger the monsters they faced became. It would be a catastrophe if any of the monsters collapsed around them slip into the world of cultivation.","“That aura...” Tianjian Qingyuan frowned.","“We need to make haste, or else we’ll all die here.”","Song Changsheng immediately flitted forth. He was getting an ominous feeling, so he wanted to resolve the situation here as quickly as possible.","Tianjian Qingyuan followed him.","While journeying on this path, they realized that the deepest secrets of the Immemorial Cemetery could very well be hidden here. The Seven Stars Orbs might not be the only solution. If they uncovered the secret of this path, they might be able to save everyone.","Meanwhile, the other cultivators trapped in the Immemorial Cemetery panicked over the terrifying aura.","“Ugh! We’ll die at this rate. Let’s run!”","Some thought the pressure was triggered by Chu Feng entering the terrifying tombstone realm, so they wanted to flee as far as possible from it.","“It’s useless.”","The stronger and more knowledgeable cultivators shook their heads. They could tell the pressure extended throughout the Immemorial Cemetery. There was no escape for those trapped here.","“I knew the final star couldn’t have been that easy,” Chu Feng remarked with a sigh.","The pressure felt like a sharp sword pressed against their necks. If he couldn’t resolve this situation, everyone in the Immemorial Cemetery would be decapitated.","“Elder, how can I earn the qualification?” Chu Feng asked.","Despite there being many powerhouses present, none dared to speak after sensing the other party’s overwhelming aura because they feared losing their lives. Yet, Chu Feng dared speak to the other party with a normal voice that was neither arrogant nor subservient.","This courage transcended cultivation. Even Eighth Zhao was impressed, for he wouldn’t have dared to speak up.","“You’ll have to defeat me to earn the qualification,” the voice replied.","The fog receded to the sides, revealing a humongous spirit formation gate. An overwhelming aura seeped the spirit formation gate.","Rank five Heavenly God!","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master’s nervousness loosened up. The others breathed sighs of relief. A rank five Heavenly God level cultivator was indeed formidable, but they had rank five Heavenly God level cultivators on their side, too.","It was within their means to deal with.","So, the Palace Master turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Young friend Chu Feng, you can leave this to us.”","Chu Feng didn’t stand on ceremony. It was indeed beyond the means of juniors like them to deal with a rank five Heavenly God level cultivator.","“Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, will you remain here or come with us?” the Palace Master asked.","“I’m here to help out. I’ll go with you,” Eighth Zhao said.","“Members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace, get into formation and follow me!” the Palace Master ordered.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members formed hand seals, ready to activate the Heavensword Sacred Formation at any moment.","But the voice from the spirit formation gate echoed, “Are you going to challenge me? You only have two chances. Once you deplete both chances, all of you are going to die.”","The Palace Master and Eighth Zhao hesitated upon hearing those words. Those words were clearly a warning. They glanced around, but no one else was qualified to take on this challenge.","“Should we wait for my master to return?” Xian Miaomiao asked.","“Indeed. A rank five Heavenly God would be nothing to fear once Miss Miaomiao’s master returns.”","The others voiced their agreement.","On the fifth star, a terrifying gate had manifested out of nowhere, and a monster that was stronger than rank five Heavenly God level emerged from it. Yet, Song Changsheng subdued it with absolute ease. There was no question he could defeat a rank five Heavenly God as well.","Just then, an incense stick appeared on the formation.","“What does that mean?” someone asked out of confusion.","“W-w-what else can that mean? They aren’t giving us t-t-time to wait. We’ll die once time is u-u-up,” Wang Qiang scoffed.","The meaning behind the incense stick was not lost on anyone.","The Palace Master calmly looked at Eighth Zhao and asked, “Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief, do you still dare to step in?”","“What do I have to fear?” Eighth Zhao replied as he stepped forward.","The Palace Master also led the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members forth.","Eighth Zhao entered the spirit formation gate, but the Palace Master stopped right before the gate and ordered, “All juniors are to stay behind.”","“Palace Master, the prowess of the Heavensword Sacred Formation depends on our bloodline. We can contribute as well,” Tianjian Canhua and the others said.","“We don’t know the situation inside. Someone has to stay behind to carry the torch for our Heavensword Sacred Palace if a mishap happens in there. This is an order,” the Palace Master said.","Since it was an order, Tianjian Canhua and the others had no choice but to stay behind.","The Palace Master led the other members into the spirit formation gate.","The next moment, they froze in place. Their confidence shattered, and their faces paled in horror. Some even collapsed to the floor out of sheer fright."]},{"number":6430,"title":"Chapter 6430: Chapter 6428: An Opponent Who Cannot Be Defeated","paragraphs":["It was a boundless plain. A massive blood moon covered half of the sky, casting a blood-red glow over the realm. The ground was neither covered in grass nor barren; it was stacked with layer after layer of carcasses.","Mountains could be spotted here and there, but there were carcasses of gigantic monstrous beasts.","These carcasses must have been powerful cultivators or world spiritists when they were alive, evident from the traces of their cultivation that lingered even though they had been dead for a long time now.","Their combined lingering might was quite terrifying.","But what was more striking was the sinister air, so much so that even Eighth Zhao, who had never shied away from murder, felt chilled. The cause of it was not the carcass but a figure who stood in the distance.","Despite being far away, his presence commanded attention. He was three meters tall, and he appeared humanoid even though he was not a human. He wore no clothes, and there was no need for him to wear them as his body was covered in scales reminiscent of armor.","He kneeled on the floor like an unmoving statue, but he was no statue. Behind his head were countless strands of hair that flickered around like a living being.","He emanated the aura of a rank five Heavenly God, but the pressure he gave off was not just because of his cultivation. His gaze was arrogant and domineering. He was the culprit behind the massacre here.","He looked at the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members as if they were prey despite being outnumbered by them.","“Get in formation!” the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master roared, shattering the stifling atmosphere. She dared not let her guard down against such an entity, so she ordered her palace members to activate the Heavensword Sacred Formation right away.","Moments later, the palace members’ faces darkened. To their horror, they couldn’t form their formation.","“Hah...” the black monstrous beast scoffed. “You’ll have to count on yourselves here.”","The palace members’ faces paled. The voice had not come from afar but right in front of them. The black monstrous beast had flitted up to their Palace Master like a specter.","Clang!","The Palace Master drew her sword, only to stiffen up. Her sword had been unsheathed, but the black monstrous beast grabbed it with a single hand.","She formed a hand seal and infused her martial power into her God Armament, causing it to glow brilliantly. This was a Heavensword Sacred Palace’s martial skill. If she swung this blade, the sheer force could slice a smaller realm into halves.","Even if she couldn’t swing it, the sheer energy channeled into the sword would make it incomparably sharp and indestructible.","Yet, the black monstrous beast continued holding onto the God Armament with a single hand without any signs of taking damage.","Seeing this, Eighth Zhao drew his weapon to aid the Palace Master.","The black monstrous beast suddenly turned to look at Eighth Zhao.","No word had to be said. A mere gaze from the black monstrous beast was enough to make Eighth Zhao realize that even though they were both rank five Heavenly God level cultivators, he was no match for the black monstrous beast.","Thus, Eighth Zhao didn’t make a move.","Even the Palace Master stood still. No one dared to take a breath.","“You have one last chance. If you still can’t defeat me, everyone who stepped into the Immemorial Cemetery will die.”","The black monstrous beast released the Palace Master’s God Armament and vanished.","The crowd turned to where the black monstrous beast had first appeared. Indeed, he had returned to his original position, kneeling still like a statue, with his hair wriggling behind him.","“Milord, we are cultivators. It’s normal for cultivators to seek fortuitous encounters. It’s only normal for us to be drawn to the incredible opportunity that the Immemorial Cemetery has to offer. We don’t mean to cross you. Will you spare our lives?” Eighth Zhao tried to seek other methods to resolve this situation, but the black monstrous beast refused to reply.","The Palace Master sheathed her sword and left.","Eighth Zhao knew negotiation was futile, so he left as well.","Chu Feng and the others worriedly rushed up to the Palace Master and Eighth Zhao when they returned. They couldn’t help noticing their poor complexions. Fortunately, they were unharmed.","“Father, are you injured?” Zhao Zhuyin anxiously asked. She was worried as Eighth Zhao’s complexion looked terrible.","“I’m fine,” Eighth Zhao replied with a resigned smile. He looked like he had suffered a huge blow.","It was not just Eighth Zhao. Everyone from the Heavensword Sacred Palace, including their Palace Master, had the same expression. Their faces revealed their despair.","“Elder, it didn’t work out?” Chu Feng asked.","“Haa...” Eighth Zhao first let out a bitter smile. “At least the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master drew her sword and somewhat clashed with the other party, but I didn’t even have the courage to do so. We might both be rank five Heavenly God level cultivators, but the gap between us is as good as heaven and earth. We might be destined to die here.”","The Zhao Immortal Clansmen reacted the strongest to his words.","Their clan chief had always been fearless. The entity in there must have been truly fearsome for him to utter such words.","“What is the nature of the person in there? Is it a formation entity? Or a real living being?” Chu Feng asked.","The Palace Master replied, “He should be a real living being.”","She waved her sleeves and drew out the black monstrous beast.","Chu Feng’s heart clenched up.","Back when Yuwen Yanri obtained the legacy and received the imprint, Chu Feng attempted to analyze the imprint with his Three Realms Divine Eyes, only to be transported into a dark realm. There, he met a humongous being kneeling in the middle of space.","That being was the one who told him about the Seven Stars Orbs, which led him to suspect that the other party was the master of the Immemorial Cemetery. He might not have seen the other party’s face, but he did see a rough outline.","It was similar to the figure whom the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master drew."]},{"number":6431,"title":"Chapter 6431: Chapter 6429: The Spirit God Clan’s Secret Skill","paragraphs":["“Is that person the size of a realm?” Chu Feng asked.","“No, that is exactly how we saw him.” The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master gestured to the portrait she drew of the black monstrous beast.","“How does he sound? Does he have the same voice as the person we heard from within the gate?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, they sound the same,” the Palace Master replied.","“I see...” Chu Feng fell into deep thought.","“Young friend Chu Feng, why did you ask if that person is the size of a realm?” Eighth Zhao asked.","Chu Feng told them that the person in the portrait greatly resembled the person he had previously met, whom he suspected to be the master of the Immemorial Cemetery.","“The person we met is the master of the Immemorial Cemetery?”","That revelation made the crowd realize that their opponent was stronger than they had expected.","“But the voice and size are different. It could be a clone, or maybe they are only from the same clan,” Chu Feng revealed his analysis.","“Brother, t-t-that isn’t the main point. The main point is that we’re no m-m-match for him!” Wang Qiang replied.","Chu Feng eyed Eighth Zhao and the Palace Master. He could tell they had lost all fighting will.","“Let me give it a try,” Chu Feng said.","“You? H-h-how? How do you intend to beat a Heavenly God, not to mention a r-r-rank five Heavenly God? Isn’t this courting d-d-death? Calm down. There must be another w-w-way.” Wang Qiang panicked, knowing that Chu Feng would do as he said.","But how could Chu Feng defeat a rank five Heavenly God?","The crowd fell silent. The only ones who stood a chance against that person were the Zhao Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief and the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master, but both of them had fallen in defeat. An air of despondence shrouded the crowd.","“Big brother, I’ll accompany you.”","“Brother Chu Feng, I’ll go with you.”","“Chu Feng, take me with you.”","Three voices echoed. It was Little Fishy, Song Yun, and Xian Miaomiao.","“W-w-why are you all going, too? So that you can die together? We can’t do this by force. T-t-there must be another way. Let’s brainstorm. Maybe the key is n-n-not to defeat him?” Wang Qiang said, though he couldn’t think of a solution either.","“I have an idea,” Shen Hui suddenly spoke up.","Everyone turned to Shen Hui.","Shen Hui turned to Chu Feng and said, “Master, I have a conjecture.”","“What is it?” Chu Feng asked.","“The Seven Stars Orbs appear to be our ticket out of the Immemorial Cemetery, but they also confer benefits to those who have inherited their legacies. Perhaps, the goal of the Seven Stars Orbs is to find successors to their legacies, and this is a trial targeted at you. Maybe the ones who ought to challenge that person are the inheritors of the Seven Stars Orbs,” Shen Hui said.","“That doesn’t make sense. That person is a rank five Heavenly God level cultivator, whereas Chu Feng and the others are only juniors!” Zhao Zhuyin said.","“We have been underestimating the Immemorial Cemetery. We know next to nothing about it, but it knows everything about us. Our gathering here might not have been a coincidence. Our clan can do more than just bestow our spirit power to others; we can also transfer a person’s cultivation to others. We can borrow the Palace Master’s cultivation and simultaneously imbue it inside our master and the others,” Shen Hui said.","“You’re saying that you can simultaneously raise the cultivation of many people to rank five Heavenly God level?” Eighth Zhao asked.","“We can’t do it for too many people, but doing it for ten people should still be within our means,” Shen Hui replied.","“I don’t think it’ll work. The Palace Master and I have personally experienced that person’s strength. This is not a challenge that can be overcome with more people.” Eighth Zhao revealed his worry.","“The secret skill only uses the lender’s cultivation as a medium. Those borrowing the cultivation won’t be able to use any means to further raise their cultivation, but their fighting prowess will be retained, and they will be able to use their martial skills as well,” Shen Hui replied.","“That’s incredible!” Eighth Zhao’s eyes lit up with hope.","He knew that Chu Feng and the other juniors were top-notch prodigies whose talents surpassed earlier generations of experts, including legendary figures who dominated the Ancient Era. Their fighting prowess was bound to outclass older generations like theirs.","If they could raise their cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level while retaining their fighting prowess and means, they might stand a chance against the black monstrous beast.","“Why didn’t you mention it earlier?” Tianjian Canhua said coldly.","She felt like her palace members had unnecessarily risked their lives earlier, if such an option had been possible from the start. If Shen Hui had said it earlier, they could have just done this right away.","“Your Heavensword Sacred Formation boasts unrivaled strength among rank five Heavenly Gods. I didn’t think it would be impossible to construct formations in there,” Shen Hui replied.","Tianjian Canhua was rendered speechless.","Indeed, they had been planning to use the power of the Heavensword Sacred Formation, and they didn’t think it would be impossible to employ it.","“Won’t your formation be nullified in there, too?” the Palace Master asked.","“Our secret skill differs from traditional formations, and we can construct and activate it out here. It’s unlikely that it’ll be restricted,” Shen Hui replied.","“Are you certain? This is our final chance. All of us will die if it fails,” a Heavensword Sacred Palace’s elder said.","Shen Hui fell silent. She couldn’t give any guarantees, either.","Chu Feng turned to the elder and asked, “Do you have other ideas in mind? I’m all ears.”","“I... This...” The elder had no answer. She wouldn’t have been standing helplessly here if she had an idea to contribute.","“I believe the formation is going to be centered around our Palace Master, right? If so, we’ll need to know what the side effects are,” Tianjian Canhua said.","“I promise it won’t cause the slightest harm to the Palace Master,” Shen Hui said.","“Don’t worry about me. Our survival is at stake, and Lord Qingyuan has ordered us to offer unconditional support to young friend Chu Feng. You can be assured that our Heavensword Sacred Palace will offer unreserved support for this,” the Palace Master said.","“Shen Hui, what about you? The formation should place considerable burden on your clansmen, right?” Chu Feng asked.","He was a world spiritist as well, so he understood that it was no easy feat to transfer a third party’s cultivation into someone else. Such a formation was bound to put a heavy toll on the world spiritist.","“Don’t worry, master. It is one of our clan’s bloodline secret skills. We can withstand it,” Shen Hui replied.","Chu Feng nodded. He turned to the crowd and said, “Elders, I think Shen Hui’s idea is feasible. Please feel free to share your ideas if you have any. Otherwise, I’m inclined to give this a try.”","“Our Heavensword Sacred Palace approves this idea.” The Palace Master made her stance clear.","The others also voiced their agreement.","Shen Hui’s idea was the most feasible one thus far.","Having come to a decision, the Spirit God Clan began constructing a formation. It didn’t take long for them to complete it.","The crowd could sense the ingenuity of the formation. It precisely extracted the Palace Master’s cultivation.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, Bai Yunqing, Yuwen Yanri, Wang Qiang, Xian Miaomiao, Song Yun, and the new king waited outside the formation.","The next step was to transfer the cultivation. The Spirit God Clansmen sliced their wrists, allowing a huge amount of their blood mixed with their spirit power and bloodline power to flow into the formation.","Chu Feng frowned.","Shen Hui had clearly understated the toll that their secret skill would have on the Spirit God Clansmen. In just an instant, all the Spirit God Clansmen’s faces turned ghastly pale.","—","Translator Note:","In essence, fighting prowess refers to how strong one is within a cultivation rank. Think of it as sub-tiers within a cultivation (F to S)","In terms of fighting prowess, Chu Feng would probably be S-tier, whereas Eighth Zhao and the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master are at C-tier.","If Chu Feng retains his fighting prowess when his cultivation is raised to rank five Heavenly God level, by virtue of his superior fighting prowess, he would be stronger than Eighth Zhao and the Palace Master (S > C)."]},{"number":6432,"title":"Chapter 6432: Chapter 6430: Price","paragraphs":["“Shen Hui! You...”","Chu Feng was appalled when he saw the Spirit God Clansmen’s conditions.","“Master, please do not worry. This secret skill is bound to take a toll on us, but it will not impair our foundation. It is our clan’s secret skill, after all,” Shen Hui replied.","The Spirit God Clansmen changed their hand seal, and the extracted cultivation transformed into a light pillar and flowed into Chu Feng’s body. His cultivation immediately rose to rank five Heavenly God level.","Next, the light pillar flowed into the bodies of Yuwen Yanri, Wang Qiang, Bai Yunqing, Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, Song Yun, the new king, and Xian Miaomiao.","“Holy s-s-shit! I obtained the power of a rank five H-H-Heavenly God just like that? It doesn’t feel like a formation!” Wang Qiang was amazed by the power coursing through his body.","“It’s as if this cultivation belongs to me. Other than being unable to raise my cultivation, I can use my means without a hitch,” Xianhai Shaoyu said. He whipped out a God Armament sword and brandished it around to test his newfound strength.","“Interesting.”","Even the new king smiled in satisfaction as he clenched his fist. He was awed. The process was nowhere as complicated as he had imagined it to be.","“The Spirit God Clan is amazing! Young friend Chu Feng is indeed someone blessed with great fortune!”","Even Eighth Zhao and the others were amazed.","With such incredible means at their disposal, there was no question that the Spirit God Clan hadn’t reached their highest potential yet. It was incredible that such a powerful race was willing to submit to Chu Feng.","“Why is it that your cultivation remains at that level even when your link to the formation has been severed?” Eggy asked.","It looked as if Chu Feng and the others were no longer connected to the formation after they received the cultivation.","“The link hasn’t been severed. It just looks that way. The Spirit God Clan’s means are indeed amazing,” Chu Feng said.","“I see. Perhaps we’d be able to fool the entity inside,” Eggy said.","“There might be no need to fool him. As Shen Hui has said, this could be his intention. They could be trying to test the limit of our potential. There’s a good chance rank five Heavenly God level is not his limit; he’s merely matching our limit,” Chu Feng replied.","“In other words, this is a trial,” Eggy replied.","“I think so, but this won’t be a simple trial.” Chu Feng had already mentally prepared himself.","“Our formation has enough energy for one more person.” Shen Hui glanced at Tianjian Canhua.","“I’ll pass. I’m not an inheritor of the Seven Stars Orbs, so it’ll be meaningless for me to go in,” Tianjian Canhua turned down the offer.","“Y-y-you can give it to me instead,” Wang Qiang said.","“You have already obtained the energy. Even if we grant you more energy, it won’t raise your fighting prowess. On the contrary, it might burden you,” Shen Hui replied.","“Give it to me,” Zhao Zhuyin said.","Eighth Zhao immediately interjected, “No, Zhuyin. I’ll go on your behalf.”","“Father.”","Zhao Zhuyin wanted to argue against it, but Eighth Zhao was adamant about it. “It’s an order. This is not up for negotiation.”","Zhao Zhuyin understood her father’s feelings. She was the Zhao Immortal Clan’s future; he couldn’t allow her to take this risk.","“Father, I...” Huangfu Shengyu was tempted to give it a try, so he turned to his father to seek his opinion.","“Shengyu, you’re also our clan’s future,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Huangfu Shengyu didn’t insist on it after hearing that. It was not just because he was the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s future but because he was far weaker than Chu Feng and the others, too. He didn’t think he could contribute much even if he entered.","Now that the formation had been completed, Chu Feng looked at the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master sitting at the formation center. She looked relaxed, as if the formation hadn’t put any burden on her.","Chu Feng then turned to Shen Hui and the Spirit God Clansmen. To his relief, their complexions didn’t worsen over time. That put his heart at ease.","According to his calculations, a secret skill like this was bound to take a significant toll on the world spiritists. He was worried that Shen Hui and the others were paying a hefty price to help them. Fortunately, the situation didn’t appear to be that serious.","“Shen Hui, how long can our cultivation last?” Chu Feng asked.","“Master, it’ll last until the incense burns out,” Shen Hui replied.","“We have troubled you.”","Chu Feng, the juniors linked to the Seven Stars Orbs, and Eighth Zhao made their way toward the spirit formation gate together.","“Elder, you should stay behind,” Chu Feng paused in front of the gate and advised Eighth Zhao.","“Your current cultivation stems from a formation, whereas mine is the real deal. If a mishap happens, I might still be able to save all of you. The most important thing for us right now is to ensure your survival. If you die, it’ll spell the end of us all. Don’t worry, I’ll stay at the entrance and escape right away if things go awry. I won’t become a burden,” Eighth Zhao said.","Chu Feng knew Eighth Zhao was doing this out of goodwill, so he accepted the offer. So, the ten of them, including Eighth Zhao, stepped into the spirit formation gate.","Uwa!","As soon as Chu Feng and the others entered, the Spirit God Clansmen spurted blood. Some couldn’t maintain their balance and fell to their knees.","“What’s wrong?!”","The crowd was worried.","The Spirit God Clansmen were in a horrendous state, but whether it was those who were barely standing or had collapsed to the ground, they tenaciously held their hand seals.","“Please don’t tell my master. We can’t let this influence them right now,” Shen Hui said feebly.","The crowd realized Shen Hui and the others had been concealing their injuries. This secret skill took a huge toll on them, and it could inflict irreparable damage to their foundations at this rate.","Yet, no one tried to inform Chu Feng about it.","Chu Feng and the others were their hope right now. If Chu Feng gave up, it would spell the death of not just the Spirit God Clansmen but all of them.","...","The faces of Chu Feng and the others turned severe upon entering the spirit formation gate, though they didn’t display immense fright like the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members.","The environment was shocking, but it posed no threat to them. So, they turned their sights toward the kneeling figure in the distance. That was the person who had easily defeated the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master.","Chu Feng could tell at a glance that the other party wasn’t the one who had told him about the Seven Stars Orbs, but without a doubt, he was a fearsome adversary."]},{"number":6433,"title":"Chapter 6433: Chapter 6431: Clash","paragraphs":["Chu Feng was convinced of his conjecture that rank five Heavenly God level wasn’t the other party’s limit; it was the limit he had capped on himself to test them.","“Looks like you have made up your minds. Everyone has staked their lives on you juniors, but are you sure you’re up to par?” the black monstrous beast asked.","“Please guide us along, elder,” Chu Feng said with a bow.","The black monstrous beast smirked.","The ground around Chu Feng suddenly shattered. Chains gushed forth from the earth and enveloped Chu Feng like a bird cage. Spirit power seeped from the chains, sealing off even the space between the chains.","“Big brother!” Little Fishy whipped out her God Armament to slash the cage.","Clang!","Sparks flew. Little Fishy was forced back, but the chains remained undamaged.","Song Yun, Xian Miaomiao, Wang Qiang, and the others employed their means, but they were to no avail.","“Don’t worry about me.”","Chu Feng raised his hand, gesturing for Little Fishy and the others not to attack blindly. He noticed that the chain cage couldn’t be unraveled, even with their rank five Heavenly God level cultivation.","Little Fishy and the others also noticed the same. After confirming that Chu Feng was imprisoned but unharmed, they refrained from making any more reckless moves. It was even more so at times like this that they had to tread carefully in order to help Chu Feng.","So, they waited for the black monstrous beast to reveal his will.","They noticed the black monstrous beast was holding a normal incense stick. He planted it into the ground, lit it with a snap of his finger, and stood back up.","“Elder, what does that mean?” Chu Feng asked with a respectful tone.","“All of you will die if you don’t defeat me before the incense stick outside burns out. The incense stick in here only dictates his fate. If you aren’t able to defeat me before this incense stick burns out, he’ll die,” the black monstrous beast said while pointing to Chu Feng.","“What do you want?” Little Fishy asked with murderous eyes.","“Yes, that’s the kind of eyes I want to see. Show me how far you are willing to go for Chu Feng,” the black monstrous beast said.","“All of us are willing to lay down our lives for big brother Chu Feng,” Bai Yunqing said as he charged at the black monstrous beast.","Pu!","But he suddenly froze in mid-air and spurted blood.","It turned out that the black monstrous beast had thrust his palm forth to impale Bai Yunqing, but what was shocking was how fast the black monstrous beast was. None of them could follow his movements.","Little Fishy and the others were horrified.","What happened next further stoked their unease.","The black monstrous beast casually waved the hand that had impaled Bai Yunqing’s neck. Blood splattered. Bai Yunqing’s head dropped to the ground, and the black monstrous beast stepped on it.","“Is that all you have?” the black monstrous beast sneered.","He coldly raised his foot to stomp down on Bai Yunqing’s head, but before he could complete the motion, he suddenly got into a defensive posture. His reaction was timely as a kick flew at him right after.","The new king had made a move!","The new king’s kick was so powerful that it pushed the black monstrous beast several steps back. He didn’t continue the assault, opting instead to remain in position to protect Bai Yunqing. “You aren’t dead yet, right?”","Bai Yunqing formed a hand seal. His fallen head returned to his neck and sealed itself back in place, leaving not even an injury or scar behind. However, his complexion remained pale from sheer fright.","“I-I am fine,” Bai Yunqing replied with a quivering voice. His body was trembling as well.","He had lost his fighting will. That momentary clash was enough for him to conclude that the black monstrous beast was not an opponent he could hope to surmount.","“Stay back,” the new king said.","Right after saying those words, the new king hurriedly dodged.","The black monstrous beast has thrust his dagger-like palm at the new king’s neck. Despite the new king’s attempt to dodge, the black monstrous beast changed his attack trajectory, and the attack eventually still pierced the new king’s neck.","Dang!","There was no splatter of blood. On the contrary, a loud metallic clang echoed.","The new king was sent flying, but he wasn’t decapitated like Bai Yunqing. He was even able to flip in mid-air to adjust his position. When he finally landed on the ground, the sheer momentum sent him skidding a long distance before he regained his balance.","That said, he still escaped unscathed from the black monstrous beast’s assault despite being struck in the neck.","Taking a closer look, the new king was shrouded in a black aura and clothed in a newly-grown armor that covered his whole body, including his face. Only his eyes were exposed.","“You’re a sturdy one, but a hard shell won’t be enough to defeat me,” the black monstrous beast chuckled.","Boom!","A gigantic fireball resembling a comet descended from the sky, unleashing an inferno the moment it crashed onto the ground. The surroundings transformed into a sea of flames.","It was Yuwen Yanri’s martial skill.","But Yuwen Yanri’s face warped in astonishment. He couldn’t sense the black monstrous beast anywhere in the sea of flames. The latter had dodged the attack!","Shoosh!","The black monstrous beast suddenly appeared behind Yuwen Yanri.","“Ambushing me? You aren’t the only one capable of that,” the black monstrous beast sneered as his palm impaled Yuwen Yanri’s neck.","What happened next made the black monstrous beast narrow his eyes.","It was not fresh blood but flames that gushed out from Yuwen Yanri’s neck.","Whoosh!","Fire chains shot out from Yuwen Yanri’s body and bound the black monstrous beast. At the same time, flame circles also appeared beneath the black monstrous beast’s feet.","Yuwen Yanri’s voice echoed from the distance, “Rank three God Taboo Fire Prison Hell!”","Boom!","It was as if the ground beneath the black monstrous beast had transformed into a volcanic crater. Raging flames poured out from the ground, but instead of flowing out, they converged into a gigantic cage.","As the cage thickened, it started to feel impenetrable.","“N-n-not bad, Yanri. To think you’d master this martial skill!” Wang Qiang complimented.","As a fellow member of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, he understood the ingenuity of the rank three God Taboo Fire Prison Hell.","First and foremost, it was nigh impossible to distinguish the clone from the real entity, unless one possessed exceptional discernment. Should the enemy strike the clone, the clone would immediately unleash fire chains to bind them in place before manifesting the cage.","Anyone trapped in the cage was doomed to be burned to death.","Wang Qiang’s smile suddenly froze in place.","“You resort to an underhanded measure despite possessing the Blazing Sun Divine Body. You’re a disgrace,” the black monstrous beast spoke with a resonant voice from the fire cage as if unfazed by it."]},{"number":6434,"title":"Chapter 6434: Chapter 6432: Joining Forces","paragraphs":["Boom!","A black shadow suddenly darted out from the fire cage. The black monstrous beast had emerged unscathed from his prison and was charging at Yuwen Yanri. He was now wielding a three-meter-long black thorn that resembled a spear.","It was with this spear that he broke free of Yuwen Yanri’s Fire Prison Hell.","Yuwen Yanri was unfazed. With a flick of his wrist, he took out a golden bracelet.","As soon as the golden bracelet left his palm, it began expanding till it was over a meter in diameter. At the same time, the bracelet morphed into a shape resembling flames, and obscure runes appeared on its surface. It resembled the sun.","This was Yuwen Yanri’s God Armament.","Clang!","Sparks flew. Shockwaves rippled.","The black monstrous beast was wielding a single black thorn, but Yuwen Yanri felt like tens of thousands of black thorns were simultaneously assaulting him. Yuwen Yanri managed to block the attacks, but at the same time, he was forced to retreat again and again.","The black monstrous beast was too powerful.","Yuwen Yanri had never felt so pressured by an enemy before. He was still holding his ground for the time being, but at this rate, it was only a matter before he fell in defeat.","“A-a-arrogant bastard!” Wang Qiang cursed as he ambushed the black monstrous beast from behind.","His intervention greatly alleviated Yuwen Yanri’s pressure.","Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, Song Yun, and Xian Miaomiao also joined the battle with their God Armaments. They imbued their bodies with weapons with martial power as they unleashed their martial skills.","Under the effects of their martial skills, their speed and strength were greatly amplified.","From how the black monstrous beast was unfazed from Yuwen Yanri’s Fire Prison Hell, it was clear that ordinary martial skills couldn’t hope to breach the black monstrous beast’s incredible defenses. Thus, they decided to join hands to deal with the black monstrous beast.","“Everyone is so strong,” Bai Yunqing said with conflicted eyes.","He was happy for them, but he felt down because of the massive gap between him and the others. He couldn’t even follow their movements; he would only drag them down if he joined the battle.","“Brother, are you all right?” someone asked via voice transmission. It was Chu Feng.","“I-I’m fine.” Bai Yunqing rushed to Chu Feng’s side.","“You don’t need to feel inferior. You’re a world spiritist, not a cultivator. It’s only normal for you to be unaccustomed to how they fight.” Chu Feng saw through Bai Yunqing’s weakness.","“I... am useless. Perhaps I am unworthy of the legacy,” Bai Yunqing said with a lowered head.","“Brother, this isn’t the time for self-deprecation. We are carrying countless lives on our shoulders. You might not be able to fight like the others do, but you have your unique strengths as a world spiritist.","“Our opponent might have suppressed his cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level, but he remains a formidable opponent. There’s no guarantee we can take him down even if we join hands. Our only hope is to exploit his weakness.","“Unfortunately, this cage not only restrains me but also limits my observation. You will have to be the one to uncover his weakness,” Chu Feng said via voice transmission.","“Me? But I...” Bai Yunqing’s gloomy voice and dodgy eyes revealed a lack of confidence.","“Brother, you are a talented world spiritist. Yes, Little Fishy and the others are formidable, but it would be foolish to undermine yourself over others,” Chu Feng said as he looked at Bai Yunqing with a confident smile.","He trusted Bai Yunqing even though the latter had nearly lost his life to the black monstrous beast just a moment ago.","This brought some courage to Bai Yunqing. He still lacked confidence, but he didn’t want to let down Chu Feng’s expectations.","I would have died a long time ago if not for big brother. My life belongs to him. I can’t be doing nothing when big brother is in danger. Even if my efforts are futile, I should at least give it all I have got here.","“I understand, big brother Chu Feng.”","Bai Yunqing turned to the battlefield, closed his eyes, and formed hand seals.","Chu Feng noticed that those were no ordinary formation hand seals. They were so profound that even he struggled to make sense of them.","“Bai Yunqing’s hand seals are rather unique. Did he obtain them from the Profound Acupuncture Physician Saint’s legacy?” Eggy also noticed Bai Yunqing’s exceptional hand seals.","“Perhaps.” Chu Feng couldn’t say for sure.","Now that Bai Yunqing had gotten serious, Chu Feng turned his attention back to the battlefield.","The new king was not participating in the battle and was instead observing from a distance away, but the combined prowess of Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, Yuwen Yanri, and the others was formidable. The tide of the battle was immediately turned.","The black monstrous beast was being suppressed.","“Hahahaha! Things are finally getting interesting, but it won’t do if this is all you have. I’ll start counting to ten. If none of you can land a blow on me before then, I’ll stop holding back.”","But Little Fishy and the others had already gone all out. The black monstrous beast’s words made them flustered.","“One. Two. Three...” The black monstrous beast began counting.","Even though Little Fishy and the others appeared to be suppressing the black monstrous beast, none of their attacks landed properly on the latter.","In between attacks, Song Yun turned to the side and shouted, “New king, come and help out.”","But the new king remained rooted to the spot. He watched the battle as if it were a mere show, displaying no inclination to get involved.","“The new king is ignoring Song Yun and the others. Chu Feng, perhaps you should talk to him. He listens to you better,” Eggy said.","“The new king is not the kind to throw tantrums at critical moments. He likely has his considerations,” Chu Feng replied.","In the meantime, the black monstrous beast continued counting.","“Ten.”","As soon as he finished counting, the black monstrous beast’s scales flared, releasing sounds resembling cicada calls. At the same time, the surrounding space distorted.","Wang Qiang and the others felt sharp pain piercing their ears and filling their beings. This caused their movements to slow.","“It’s over,” the black monstrous beast sneered.","The whiskers behind the black monstrous beast suddenly bared their fangs and lurched at Wang Qiang and the others, biting all of them.","Wang Qiang and the others were knocked a far distance away, but surprisingly, they landed stably without sustaining any injuries. Upon closer examination, they were shrouded in black aura armor resembling the new king’s.","The new king changed his hand seal, and the black aura armor dissipated. He had just protected all of them."]},{"number":6435,"title":"Chapter 6435: Chapter 6433: Despair","paragraphs":["“Ah, I have wrongly blamed you,” Song Yun, who happened to land next to the new king, turned to him and said with a smile.","She had thought the new king was idling around, but in truth, the latter had merely opted to take on a supportive role to protect them during critical moments.","“I’m only doing this to rescue Chu Feng,” the new king replied.","The black monstrous beast turned to the new king. “It’s you again? I guess I’ll have to eliminate you first.”","The black beast sneered as he charged at the new king.","Unfazed, the new king prepared for battle. His strengths were not limited to defense.","But the black monstrous beast suddenly changed trajectory and charged at Bai Yunqing. This time, his attack was not aimed at Bai Yunqing’s neck but his head, and his killing intent could be clearly perceived by everyone.","Boom!","Bai Yunqing was slammed into a formation pillar, but he was unharmed because the new king’s black aura armor had manifested on him as well. The black aura armor could block fatal attacks while cushioning impacts, making it tough to deal with.","Wang Qiang and the others rushed to Bai Yunqing’s side to protect him.","Even if Bai Yunqing was clad in the black aura armor, they couldn’t let the black monstrous beast continue making his moves against him.","But once Wang Qiang and the others arrived at Bai Yunqing’s side, the black monstrous beast suddenly retreated into mid-air before turning to face the new king.","“That black aura armor is indeed a formidable means, but it’s more suited for personal use. You’re only straining yourself if you use it to protect others. You won’t last long at this rate.”","Only then did the crowd realize that the new king’s aura had weakened considerably.","That explained why the new king had only momentarily manifested the black armor to protect them before dispelling them right away. As the black monstrous beast had said, using the black aura armor on others took a toll on the new king.","“You can’t hope to match for me, not when a member of your group is dragging you down. How do you plan to deal with this situation? Are you going to abandon him, or will you continue in this manner until I crush all of you? Or will you dawdle around until the incense stick burns out and Chu Feng dies?” the monstrous beast asked.","He was explicitly labeling Bai Yunqing as dead weight.","“Someone your age shouldn’t be sowing discord. We won’t give up on our brother,” Xianhai Shaoyu said. He patted Bai Yunqing’s shoulder, not wanting the latter to feel burdened.","Despite not being close with Bai Yunqing, he trusted Chu Feng’s eye for people. That was enough reason for him to do everything he could to protect Chu Feng’s friends.","Bai Yunqing finally opened his eyes.","He didn’t look gloomy or down. Instead, he formed hand seals and conjured a series of translucent talisman papers carrying the word ‘Protection’. These talisman papers were conjured not from spirit power but martial power.","With a wave of his sleeves, the talisman papers flew toward Wang Qiang and the others before dissipating into a wisp that fused with their clothes.","Wang Qiang and the others sensed something.","Wang Qiang grinned. “Brother Bai, y-y-you’re better than I thought!”","“This is all I can do. I’m counting on you to rescue big brother Chu.”","Bai Yunqing changed his hand seal, and white auras swiftly shrouded Wang Qiang and the others. These white auras healed their injuries and restored their energies. Even the new king’s weakened aura was immediately restored to normal.","This was a powerful healing energy channeled by martial power.","On top of healing injuries, the healing energy also rejuvenated their spirits, putting them in their tip-top conditions. This was a powerful means indeed.","“Leave the rest to us,” Xianhai Shaoyu said as he brandished his God Armament and charged into the air.","The others, except for the new king and Bai Yunqing, followed suit. They simultaneously unleashed their rank three God Taboo Martial Skills. They had secretly discussed and agreed on this earlier.","It appeared to be an all-out assault, but in truth, it was another probing attempt. They needed to verify if martial skills worked on the black monstrous beast or not.","Faced with so many rank three God Taboo Martial Skills, the black monstrous beast was forced to take evasive maneuvers. Yet, when the shockwaves finally dissipated, it remained unharmed.","“Focus on the offense. Leave all defense to me,” the new king said.","“Got it,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","The new king descended to Bai Yunqing’s side and said, “Bai Yunqing, right? Can I trust you?”","“Of course,” Bai Yunqing replied confidently.","Using the black aura armor to protect the others took a toll on him, but Bai Yunqing’s healing energy could keep him in tip-top condition and alleviate the burden. With Bai Yunqing’s support, he could better protect the others, allowing them to make bolder moves.","Bai Yunqing didn’t disappoint the new king, and the new king didn’t disappoint Wang Qiang and the others.","Openings were bound to appear when a cultivator focused on offense, but each time the black monstrous beast discovered an opening and tried to exploit it, the new king’s black aura armor would appear in time to protect them.","This allowed Wang Qiang and the others to go further in their attacks.","Soon, Little Fishy discovered an opening in the black monstrous beast’s attacks and plunged her God Armament sword wrapped in a blue aura toward the latter’s dantian.","“Hmph!” The black monstrous beast harrumphed.","His scales flared once more, and the cicada calls echoed again.","But this time, the word ‘Protection’ appeared on the robes of Wang Qiang and the others, protecting them from the sonic attack. That was the true purpose of Bai Yunqing’s talisman paper!","That allowed Little Fishy to push through with her attack.","But what happened next caused the crowd’s faces to warp in horror.","Little Fishy had devoted ample strength to this attack, and for that reason, her blade shattered.","In contrast, the black monstrous beast was also sent flying backward. His armor had retracted in this critical moment to block Little Fishy’s fatal attack.","“Shit! How is he that h-h-hard? How are we going to defeat someone like t-t-that? Why don’t you just kill us straight!” Wang Qiang cursed.","Even imbuing martial skills in weapons to amplify the destructive prowess didn’t work.","The black monstrous beast was ridiculously sturdy. It felt nigh impossible to breach his defense. How were they supposed to defeat an enemy like that?","“You don’t have much time left. Are you going to give up?” the black monstrous beast sneered.","Little Fishy and the others tasted despair. They saw no way of defeating the black monstrous beast, given the little time they had left."]},{"number":6436,"title":"Chapter 6436: Chapter 6434: This Sword Is Named Lightning Flame","paragraphs":["Just then, the new king relayed a voice transmission to Little Fishy and the others, “His defense is not impenetrable. I have a conjecture...”","On top of his powerful defensive means, he also had a sharp eye, evident from how he had never failed to manifest the black aura armor in time to protect Wang Qiang and the others whenever they exposed an opening.","He informed Wang Qiang and the others what he had observed and deduced via voice transmission. Wang Qiang and the others also began secretly discussing it. Moments later, Xian Miaomiao and Wang Qiang’s eyes hardened in determination.","A green aura and a black aura gushed from their bodies into the sky, but the auras swiftly receded into them. Their presence intensified. Their fighting prowess grew, and their life force flared as well.","“Igniting your life force? Looks like you’re getting desperate,” the black monstrous beast sneered.","Wang Qiang and Xian Miaomiao charged at the black monstrous beast with their God Armaments. By igniting their life force, they grew strong enough to rival the black monstrous beast by themselves, as long as they focused on offense.","“Why aren’t you coming at me together? Are the others incapable of igniting their life force? Four Fiends Divine Body and Soul Fog—such incredible treasures. It’s a pity you’ll be dying here today,” the black monstrous beast scoffed.","His eyes suddenly narrowed as he noticed the ground beneath him billowing.","At the same time, Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu shouted, “Bloodline Secret Skill: Shackles of the Forbidden Sea!”","Whoosh!","Luminescent waves of towering heights gushed forth from the ground, instantly devouring the black monstrous beast, Wang Qiang, and Xian Miaomiao while transforming the surroundings into an ocean.","To the black monstrous beast’s surprise, neither Wang Qiang nor Xian Miaomiao was affected by the terrain change, but his own movements had gotten a lot slower.","“Uwa!” an infant’s cry suddenly echoed.","A terrifying embryo head suddenly appeared in front of the black monstrous beast. The moment the embryo opened its eyes, his heart quivered.","It was Song Yun’s means.","At the same time, two bundles of flames were imbued into Xian Miaomiao and Wang Qiang’s weapons.","“Blazing Sun Secret Skill: Fiery Weapon Enchantment.”","It was Yuwen Yanri. His secret skill amplified the prowess of Xian Miaomiao and Wang Qiang’s God Armaments so much that the sheer flames distorted space.","Wang Qiang and Xian Miaomiao charged at the black monstrous beast from different directions.","With his movements slowed and mind shaken, the black monstrous beast couldn’t hope to dodge the attack. He did manage to deflect Wang Qiang’s blade, but he was unable to do the same for the other attack.","Xian Miaomiao’s God Armament plunged into his body.","Boom!","Flames erupted from the black monstrous beast inside out, torching him alive. Xian Miaomiao didn’t hesitate to slice downward, cutting the black monstrous beast into half.","The black monstrous beast’s body fell to the ground, yet the edges of his lips curled into a smile. Then, he dissipated into thin air.","“Sharp observation, new king! You were right!” Xianhai Shaoyu cheered, only for his body to tilt sideward right after. He would have collapsed to the ground if not for Little Fishy holding him up.","Little Fishy was faring much better, but her beautiful face was slicked in cold sweat, and she was breathing rapidly. The bloodline secret skill posed a heavy burden on Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu despite them channeling it in unison.","Song Yun fell on her bum and stretched her hands wide open, forming a ‘大’ character on the ground. She didn’t have the energy to even consider whether her posture was beautiful or not.","Yuwen Yanri was also gasping for air.","All of them had used their strongest means for the earlier coordination, pushing themselves to their very limit to ensure the highest probability of success. It was an all-out gamble. Fortunately, they succeeded.","And the greatest contributor was none other than the new king.","The black monstrous beast’s armor was indeed formidable, capable of withstanding most attacks without the slightest scratch. However, it didn’t make sense for a God Armament imbued with a God Taboo Martial Skill to fail to penetrate his body and even be shattered by his armor.","If that was the black monstrous beast’s base defense level, there would have been no need for him to dodge any of their attacks. He could have charged into their ranks and rampaged instead of going through so much trouble.","Thus, the new king theorized that the black monstrous beast must have utilized some kind of secret skill that allowed him to focus all his defensive prowess at a single point in the moment the attack landed. That would explain why Little Fishy’s God Armament shattered.","The black monstrous beast might be capable of using this secret skill multiple times, but chances were that he could only focus his defense at a single area at any point in time.","Thus, when Xian Miaomiao and Wang Qiang attacked him at the same time, he could only choose to block one of their attacks, of which, he chose Wang Qiang’s attack. That, in turn, allowed Xian Miaomiao’s attack to go through.","“Hm?’","Chu Feng and the others suddenly sensed a change in the spirit formation gate and glanced over.","“Can the people outside see us now? What does this mean?”","Chu Feng and the others still couldn’t see what was happening outside, but they sensed gazes coming from the other side of the spirit formation gate. As they had guessed, the people outside could see what was happening inside the spirit formation gate now.","“That entity is no longer there. Did they succeed?”","“Why is Chu Feng trapped?”","The crowd outside were both surprised and overjoyed, but more than anything, they remained worried. Their attention was swiftly drawn to the square they stood on, for it had started glowing brightly.","The treasures in the square had been unsealed, so they could be used for cultivation now.","At the same time, the humongous tombstone shattered. Its smithereens fell and dissipated as auras when they struck the ground. Soon, there was only a single item left where the tombstone once stood.","It was a fiery-red sword shaped like the tombstone.","It was simple but domineering. The words ‘Lightning Flame’ was inscribed on its blade. It didn’t emanate any aura, but everyone’s eyes were drawn to it because of another character inscribed on it—’Heaven’. Around its ‘Heaven’ character was a circle of indecipherable runes.","It was clearly an extremely powerful God Armament.","The black monstrous beast’s dissipated aura reappeared and converged together.","“The Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor carries the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline, which was dubbed to be a mortal bloodline because it pales in comparison to other god-tier bloodlines. However, the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor, with his sheer talent, stood alongside cultivators possessing God-tier Bloodlines. The Lightning Flame Swordsmanship he created even had him crowned as one of the most aggressive experts in the Immemorial Era.","“The legacy left here by the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor is none other than his God Armament sword, Lightning Flame. This sword was forged with the Otherworldly Lightning and the Nine Revolutions Netherworld Flame,” the black monstrous beast announced.","By then, his body had already fully recovered.","Chu Feng and the others weren’t surprised. The black monstrous beast was merely testing them earlier; there was no way his true cultivation was only at rank five Heavenly God level.","“Clear this trial, and one of you will be permitted to take Lightning Flame with you.”","The cage around Chu Feng unraveled.","At the same time, cages manifested around everyone else in the spirit formation gate except for Chu Feng, trapping them in place.","The black monstrous beast pointed his black thorn at Chu Feng and declared, “Defeat me before the incense stick burns out, and all of you will be permitted to live. Fail to defeat me before the incense stick burns out, and all of you will die.”","The crowd looked at the incense stick. There was only a tenth of it left."]},{"number":6437,"title":"Chapter 6437: Chapter 6435: Lend Me Your Spear","paragraphs":["“Big brother.”","Little Fishy and the others were nervous, but there was nothing they could do since the cage was nigh indestructible to them. They couldn’t hope to break free of it with their strength.","“Oi, c-c-can’t you use another incense stick? That one is a-a-about to go out!” Wang Qiang shouted indignantly.","But the black monstrous beast paid no heed to him.","“Chu Feng, why don’t you let me give it a try?” Eggy offered her help, though she didn’t come out on her own accord. She respected Chu Feng’s decision.","“Eggy, I suspect this is a part of the trial, too. I’ll have to do it alone,” Chu Feng said. He turned to the spirit formation gate and shouted, “Brother Ye, come in!”","Ye Xiancheng pointed to himself in bewilderment. “Are you calling for me?”","Those outside could now hear the voices of those inside, too.","“He should be calling for you,” Ye Xiancheng’s parents said.","Ye Xiancheng entered the spirit formation gate, but he didn’t venture too far away from the entrance like Eighth Zhao. He knew he was nowhere strong enough to join the battle, and going too deep inside would expose him to great danger.","Despite understanding the risk, he still came in here because he trusted Chu Feng.","Chu Feng said, “Lend me your God Armament spear.”","“All right.” Ye Xiancheng accepted the offer. He took out the God Armament spear with a flick of his wrist and handed it to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng took the God Armament spear and inspected it, only to toss it back. He clarified with a sigh, “I’m referring to the golden spear embedded with jade. You used it back when you were sparring with me.”","“Ah? Are you talking about Lord Jade Immortal?” Ye Xiancheng was startled.","The Ye Immortal Clansmen were taken aback, too. They understood the significance of the spear named Jade Immortal.","“Yes, that one,” Chu Feng said.","Ye Xiancheng whipped out an exquisite God Armament spear that looked as beautiful as an artwork. The spear body was golden, but it was embedded with pieces of emerald jade. Its presence stirred the surrounding natural energies, making it known that it was different from other God Armaments.","“Chu Feng, Lord Jade Immortal is our Ye Immortal Clan’s hereditary treasure. I’m the only one in the Ye Immortal Clan who can control it. Outsiders can’t hope to...”","Chu Feng interjected, “Brother Ye, lend it to me.”","Ye Xiancheng was put in a spot. He would have never entertained the thought of lending the Jade Immortal to anyone else. This God Armament was of great significance to the Ye Immortal Clan, evident from how even he had to respectfully address it as Lord Jade Immortal.","That said, he understood the severity of the situation. If necessary, he was ready to lend Jade Immortal to Chu Feng.","But there was no use doing so if Chu Feng couldn’t earn Lord Jade Immortal’s acknowledgement. Forcefully wielding Lord Jade Immortal would only result in a backlash.","But since Chu Feng insisted on it, and knowing time was of essence, he tossed Jade Immortal over and said, “Be careful, Brother Chu Feng.","Chu Feng grabbed Lord Jade Immortal and brandished it. The world shook. An aura that was an amalgamation of golden and green flowed from the Jade Immortal into Chu Feng’s body.","“Surely not?” Ye Xiancheng was dumbstruck.","“How is that possible?”","Ye Xiancheng’s parents and the Ye Immortal Clansmen were flabbergasted. They wondered if they were seeing things.","Jade Immortal had a reputation of being difficult. Even Ye Xiancheng’s parents were unable to control it. Of the entire Ye Immortal Clan, Ye Xiancheng was the only one who could wield it, but even he only earned its acknowledgment after obtaining the Immortal Legacy.","Yet, an outsider like Chu Feng earned Jade Immortal’s acknowledgement so easily?","“Good spear.” Chu Feng looked at Jade Immortal with a satisfied smile.","“Brother, y-y-you need to be careful. That fellow is a c-c-cunning one!” Wang Qiang shouted. He knew Chu Feng was strong, but the black monstrous beast was no pushover either.","Chu Feng flashed a confident smile at Wang Qiang and the others and said, “Don’t worry. It’s thanks to you that I was freed from the cage. Leave the rest to me. I’ll bring you out here safe and sound.”","“Chu Feng, my fighting prowess might be weakened from the earlier battle, but are you certain you can handle me alone?” the black monstrous beast scoffed.","Despite being faced with the black monstrous beast’s provocation, Chu Feng clasped his fist at the black monstrous beast and said, “Please guide me, elder.”","Shoosh!","Holding his spear in a single hand, Chu Feng charged at the black monstrous beast. He had no intention of using any martial skills because he had understood the other party’s weakness. The only way to defeat him was through close-quarter combat.","The two approached.","Flashes of black and golden clashed to a loud explosion, unleashing sparks and shockwaves into the surroundings. Chu Feng and the black monstrous beast were clashing with each other.","“Chu Feng, you’re indeed strong.” The new king narrowed his eyes.","The black monstrous beast was indeed weaker than before, or rather, he had lowered his fighting prowess as he was only fighting with an individual now. Nevertheless, he was still a fearsome adversary.","Yet, Chu Feng was able to deal with the black monstrous beast with ease. This was testimony to his strength.","This tempted the new king to spar with Chu Feng.","Just then, Chu Feng suddenly spoke aloud, “Thank you for your help, Brother Ye. Please wait for me outside.”","He was merely worried that Ye Xiancheng would be in danger, but it also showed that Chu Feng had yet to go all out against the black monstrous beast, considering how he still had the energy to chat.","“All right.” Ye Xiancheng knew he would only be a baggage if he stayed behind, so he didn’t hesitate to turn around and leave.","As soon as Ye Xiancheng stepped out of the spirit formation gate, his parents rushed up to him and asked, “Xiancheng, how did that happen? Did you say something to Lord Jade Immortal?”","“I didn’t say anything. It’s not as if Lord Jade Immortal would listen to me anyway,” Ye Xiancheng replied with a sigh.","“Doesn’t that mean that Chu Feng has truly received Lord Jade Immortal’s acknowledgment?” Ye Xiancheng’s parents asked.","“That looks to be the case.” Ye Xiancheng turned around to look at Chu Feng.","At the same time, the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master observed the battle from the formation she was standing in. She had no idea what happened inside the spirit formation gate before it turned transparent, but she could fathom a guess.","So, she sent a voice transmission to Tianjian Canhua, saying, “Canhua, your talent might rival Lord Qingyuan, but there are many talented figures in this era. You have many rivals. It’s not just Chu Feng; none of those juniors are to be underestimated. You must keep your guard up and keep pace with them.”","Tianjian Canhua asked, “Lord Palace Master, is that monstrous beast that powerful?”","“He’s an entity I don’t stand a chance against,” the Palace Master replied.","Tianjian Canhua’s face turned grim."]},{"number":6438,"title":"Chapter 6438: Chapter 6436: The Black Monstrous Beast Regains His Fighting Prowess","paragraphs":["Inside the spirit formation gate, after a brief clash, the black monstrous beast scoffed, “Chu Feng, you can’t hope to beat me if that’s all you have.”","The black monstrous beast’s scales flared open, and the cicada calls echoed.","Chu Feng frowned. His face warped in pain, and his movements stiffened.","The black monstrous beast exploited this opening to thrust his black thorn into Chu Feng’s face.","Just as the black thorn was about to impale him, Chu Feng suddenly dodged. His spear suddenly moved at a much faster speed than before, surging forth like a bolt of lightning to strike the black monstrous beast.","The black monstrous beast hurriedly concentrated his defense, and only then did he barely block Chu Feng’s attack. Even so, he was sent flying a long distance as a result of the impact.","“How are you unfazed?”","The black monstrous beast quickly regained his balance and stared at Chu Feng in confusion.","It was apparent that Chu Feng had pretended to fall for his sonic boom to make him lower his guard. That trick worked, and the black monstrous beast was nearly skewered as a result. He would have fallen in defeat if not for his ability to concentrate his defense.","He couldn’t understand why his sonic boom didn’t work on Chu Feng.","“Elder, your earlier attack was a sonic boom, right? I can just cover my ears,” Chu Feng replied.","“Interesting.” The black monstrous beast laughed, knowing his sonic boom was nowhere that easy to deal with.","Chu Feng had indeed sealed off his ears, but not in a conventional sense of the term. Only someone with extremely precise control over their body, soul, and martial power could have pulled off a feat like that.","In other words, no one else could have replicated what Chu Feng had done.","“You’re more capable than I thought. There’s no reason for me to hold back then,” the black monstrous beast said with a smile as he continued his assault.","His fighting prowess recovered to the same level back when he was fighting against the new king and the others. He was indeed unharmed; he had merely lowered his fighting prowess to match Chu Feng.","The tables were immediately turned.","As they resumed trading blows, Chu Feng found himself struggling to fend against the black monstrous beast’s attacks. It was tough to even maintain his defense, let alone counterattack. The black monstrous beast was not only strong but fast as well.","“Elder, didn’t you say you’re weakened? You don’t seem weakened at all,” Chu Feng asked.","“I was weakened. But I recovered.”","But Chu Feng remained fearless.","He formed a hand seal, and a golden aura seeped from his finger and enveloped his body, shrouding him in the airs of an immortal. His fighting prowess surged.","“That...!”","Ye Xiancheng and his parents widened their eyes in shock. They could tell at a glance that was their Ye Immortal Clan’s hereditary martial skill—rank three God Taboo, Immortal Protection.","But that wasn’t all.","Another golden aura emerged from Chu Feng’s fingertip, but unlike the one before, it didn’t immediately form anything or shroud Chu Feng’s body. Instead, it morphed into divine runes that passed through Immortal Protection and seeped into Chu Feng’s legs.","Chu Feng’s movement speed increased, allowing him to deal with the black monstrous beast now despite the latter having reverted to his original fighting prowess.","“H-how is he able to...” Ye Xiancheng yelped with widened eyes.","That was also a Ye Immortal Clan’s hereditary martial skill—rank three God Taboo, Immortal Footwork.","“Could it have happened then?” Ye Xiancheng narrowed his eyes.","He suddenly recalled Chu Feng using a bizarre skill[1] that day that made him feel as if a part of his soul had been siphoned away. It felt terrible, but somehow, he emerged unscathed from it. He had asked Chu Feng about it back then, but the latter didn’t tell him anything.","As inconceivable as it was, Chu Feng must have stolen the martial skills he had painstakingly trained then.","“How does Chu Feng know our clan’s hereditary martial skills?” Ye Xiancheng’s parents remained confused, oblivious to the truth.","“Chu Feng has a powerful skill that can plunder other people’s martial skills,” Ye Xiancheng informed his parents via voice transmission, knowing it was one of Chu Feng’s hidden cards.","“What? He can plunder someone’s martial skill? How can there possibly be a skill like that?!”","Ye Xiancheng’s parents were appalled, but they had no choice to believe those words, given how impeccably Chu Feng was using their Ye Immortal Clan’s hereditary martial skills.","Chu Feng held Jade Immortal in his right hand to clash with the black monstrous beast while forming hand seals with his left.","A bead of golden light emerged from his fingertip and rose into the air, expanding to over tens of thousands of meters in diameter as it ascended. It didn’t take long for it to resemble a sun.","“Rank three God Taboo, Immortal Suppression.”","Ye Xiancheng and his parents recognized the martial skill right away. With this, Chu Feng had used all three of the hereditary martial skills Ye Xiancheng had employed that day.","Chu Feng harrumphed. “Rank three God Taboo, Immortal Suppression.”","The golden sphere suddenly exerted immense pressure. The black monstrous beast frowned, sensing that his fighting prowess had been suppressed.","The tables had turned. Chu Feng now held the upper hand.","“You’re simultaneously using three God Taboos? Interesting. But how long can you maintain them?” the black monstrous beast sneered.","He completely abandoned all offense and focused solely on defense.","Chu Feng, despite wielding the upper hand, was unable to breach his defense.","To make things worse, the incense stick was about to burn out.","“This isn’t good. That fellow is only defending now, and that’s obviously his speciality. He’s just buying time right now!” Ye Xiancheng was getting nervous.","Despite his low cultivation, he could still barely follow the battle with his parents’ help and the aid of the Ye Immortal Clan’s formation. He didn’t mind Chu Feng stealing his martial skill, for he only hoped for Chu Feng’s victory right now.","The outcome of this battle determined their life and death.","Even Ye Xiancheng’s parents, who were much more conservative in their mindsets, didn’t criticize Chu Feng for plundering their clan’s hereditary martial skills. On the contrary, they were worried and nervous as well.","“It’s a pity Chu Feng doesn’t know Formless Spearmanship, or else he could have breached that black monstrous beast’s defenses.” Ye Xiancheng sighed.","Both Immortal Protection and Immortal Footwork were built around Formless Spearmanship; they were the keys to bringing out Formless Spearmanship’s true prowess.","“Unlike martial skills, Formless Spearmanship requires the accumulation of experience to truly grasp its essence. It can’t be plundered so easily,” Ye Xiancheng’s parents said.","Sweat rained from Chu Feng. He kept glancing at the incense stick, which was on the verge of burning out, unable to maintain his earlier composure.","“Chu Feng, it looks like you won’t be bringing your friends out with you today,” the black monstrous beast scoffed.","1. Chapter 6364 - Chu Feng used Dark Plunder, the skill he incubated from the Immemorial Era’s Dao of Absolute Darkness. ☜"]},{"number":6439,"title":"Chapter 6439: Chapter 6437: Human Heart is Hard to Read","paragraphs":["“Elder, i-i-isn’t this a trial? Are we r-r-really going to die if we fail to defeat you?” Chu Feng said with a stutter, showing none of the composure he displayed earlier.","“The price of failing this trial is death. Weaklings have no place here,” the black monstrous beast sneered.","Chu Feng suddenly smirked. He changed his hand seal, and a pair of incomparably massive golden eyes appeared behind him.","“You brat...” The black monstrous beast’s face stiffened up.","The appearance of the golden eyes heightened the pressure on him, further suppressing his fighting prowess. That was Chu Feng’s means—rank three God Taboo Divine Might. He could only use it for an instant, but its suppression effect was superior to that of Immortal Suppression.","By stacking the two skills, the black monstrous beast was greatly weakened.","Without any hesitation, Chu Feng thrust his spear into the black monstrous beast’s face.","“You’re a cunning one, but it’s futile,” the black monstrous beast sneered.","He couldn’t dodge this attack, but he could concentrate his defense and block Chu Feng’s attack, just like how he had done earlier. At the same time, he launched a counterattack against Chu Feng.","Victory was his to claim.","His face suddenly warped in shock the next moment. The spear whizzing toward his face suddenly vanished, and blood spurted from his neck instead.","“This...”","The crowd was flabbergasted. They might not have been able to follow the battle, but the outcome of the battle was clear now that both Chu Feng and the black monstrous beast had stopped moving.","Chu Feng’s spear was lodged inside the black monstrous beast’s neck.","“Elder, you have lost,” Chu Feng said.","The black monstrous beast smiled bitterly. “Not only are you able to simultaneously use four God Taboo Martial Skills, but you also had such a trick hidden in your sleeves. You must have practised that spearmanship for a long time now?”","“Elder, you have sharp eyes. I have indeed practised that spearmanship for a long time,” Chu Feng replied.","“Rubbish! How did you grasp our Formless Spearmanship so quickly? You monster!” Ye Xiancheng exclaimed, though he wasn’t truly angry. There was a hint of excitement and delight in his voice.","The others were excited as well.","Chu Feng had won.","“Chu Feng, you’re qualified to claim the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor’s God Armament, but I ought to give you one last lesson—know a person but not their heart.”","Hu!","The black monstrous beast suddenly transformed into a swiftly expanding hurricane and enveloped Chu Feng. It generated powerful winds that hurtled Eighth Zhao out of the spirit formation gate.","“Big brother!”","“Chu Feng!”","Little Fishy and the others, imprisoned by the cage, were unfazed by the black hurricane, but they were worried about Chu Feng.","“Lord Chu Feng.”","Shen Hui quickly dispelled the formation, knowing the rank five Heavenly God level cultivation was no longer useful to Chu Feng. Worried for Chu Feng, she and her clansmen rushed to the spirit formation gate.","Many of the Spirit God Clansmen were so weakened that even standing up and walking was a trial to them. Some of them had to resort to crawling and rolling. Even so, all of them still rushed to the spirit formation gate like moths plunging into candlelight.","Uwa!","As soon as Shen Hui stepped into the spirit formation gate, she was hurtled out with a cry of agony. She was in a severely weakened state, not to mention she was nowhere as strong as Eighth Zhao in the first place, so there was no way she could stand a chance against the force of the black hurricane.","She could have lost her life if not for the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master catching her and neutralizing the immense momentum on her.","Yet, the Spirit God Clansmen still poured into the spirit formation gate.","Even after the Palace Master caught them, they still relentlessly crawled their way through the gate, hoping to aid Chu Feng.","“Enough! This is young friend Chu Feng’s trial. You should have more faith in him if you acknowledge him as your master. What makes you think he needs your saving?” the Palace Master roared.","That jolted some sense back into the Spirit God Clansmen. Indeed, this could be a trial. No, it has to be a trial!","“I know you are worried about your master, but you don’t have the means to help him. You’ll only bring him misery if he learns you have died such futile deaths,” the Palace Master added with a gentler tone.","Those words struck a chord with the Spirit God Clansmen. Indeed. Chu Feng would only blame himself if we die like that.","“Thank you for your reminder,” Shen Hui said. She ordered the Spirit God Clansmen to sit down and recuperate.","Having regained their composure, they knew they wouldn’t be of any help to Chu Feng even if they entered the spirit formation gate. But if Chu Feng cleared the trial and saw them in a horrid state, he would surely feel self-reproach.","Only by recuperating right now would they bring Chu Feng ease of mind.","The members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace walked up to their Palace Master and asked, “Lord Palace Master, are you fine?”","They were more worried about their Palace Master. It defied common sense for their Palace Master to be unharmed after lending her cultivation to so many people.","The Palace Master found it unbelievable as well, but she was indeed completely unharmed.","“The Spirit God Clan is formidable indeed. I have suffered no adverse effects from the formation.” The Palace Master even eyed Shen Hui with approving eyes.","“This feeling...”","The Palace Master’s face darkened.","...","Deep in the Immemorial Cemetery stood behemoths with bodies larger than the Great Chiliocosm Upper Realm. Even their eyes were several times larger than the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm. Just a stomp from them could destroy multiple realms.","Thousands of such beings stood in a circle as if surrounding something.","Normal cultivators would have died of shock if they had witnessed this sight. Should such entities appear in the world of cultivation, they would unleash devastation wherever they went. There would be no realms nor starfields.","With enough time, they could destroy the eight galaxies.","With their humongous bodies came tremendous strength.","Even their oppressive might could collapse realms, eradicating the beings residing in them before they could even understand what was going on.","Yet, wariness and unease were reflected in the massive eyes of these behemoths as they looked upon two insignificant beings who looked no more than dust specks in their presence.","It was these two beings who instilled fear in them, making them dare not make a move."]},{"number":6440,"title":"Chapter 6440: Chapter 6438: Betrayal","paragraphs":["A blinding light suddenly burst forth, and space tremored. A loud explosion followed.","Several gigantic swords of light whizzed across space at a ridiculously fast speed, so much so that the behemoths were impaled before they could even react. The sheer momentum behind the sword vaporized their souls.","It was Tianjian Qingyuan. She had a grim look on her face.","“Why did you suddenly make a move?” Song Changsheng asked in confusion.","The two of them were standing in a formation. They had refrained from making a move because they weren’t sure eliminating these behemoths was the best way to breach the formation.","But it worked. Their surroundings warped, transporting them back onto the path they were previously walking on. The path, however, had gotten wider.","“I sensed a threat earlier. I had to make a move,” Tianjian Qingyuan explained.","“It’s fine. It’s a good thing you made a move. That saved us some time.” Song Changsheng didn’t mind it, since returning to this path meant that they had breached the formation anyway. The ends justified the means.","“You didn’t sense anything?”","“The threat?”","“Mm.”","“I didn’t feel it.”","Tianjian Qingyuan fell into deep thought. The threat had been so vivid that she was certain she would die. She had never felt anything like that except from the top experts in the Ancient Era.","This was her first time sensing anything like that in this era.","“Something is off.” Tianjian Qingyuan suddenly thought about something.","She turned around, and her gaze changed. She gazed across vast space, peering through several realm barriers, to lay her eyes on the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor’s tombstone realm, on the square where the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members stood.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members were all looking at their Palace Master’s palm. Their faces were pale, and some of them even began weeping.","On their Palace Master’s palm was a life token—Tianjian Qingyuan’s life token.","“Did something happen to Lord Qingyuan?” Tianjian Canhua asked in disbelief. She couldn’t believe such a thing had happened.","She voiced out the crowd’s concern, though her question was extraneous. Life tokens were crafted to reflect a person’s condition, and Tianjian Qingyuan had personally handed this life token to the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master.","The life token’s shattering signified Tianjian Qingyuan’s death.","Tianjian Qingyuan was their Heavensword Sacred Palace’s greatest backing. With her death, the members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace suddenly found themselves not knowing what to do.","At the same time, they were chilled. To think someone of Tianjian Qingyuan’s caliber died here. Just what kind of entities were hiding inside the Immemorial Cemetery?","After a brief shock, some members began to weep. Tears were contagious, and it didn’t take long for more people to begin sobbing.","This naturally drew attention.","The experts from the Zhao Immortal Clan, the Ye Immortal Clan, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan looked over. They were concerned about Chu Feng’s safety, but it was hard to turn a blind eye when so many members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace were weeping at the same time.","Something huge must have happened.","Before they could ask any questions, the Palace Master stowed away Tianjian Qingyuan’s life token and sternly glared at her palace members. “Stop crying!”","Despite their anguish, the palace members closed their mouths and wiped away their tears.","“Canhua, try pulling out that sword.” The Palace Master looked at the Lightning Flame Sword, which stood at the center of the square.","“Lord Palace Master!” Tianjian Canhua looked conflicted.","“You don’t have the confidence to do so?” the Palace Master asked.","Startled, Tianjian Canhua looked at the Palace Master. The latter was serious about it.","“I’ll give it a try.”","Tianjian Canhua flitted over to the Lightning Flame Sword, but before she could reach it, several figures descended from the sky and blocked her path. It was Eighth Zhao and Xianhai Shaoyu’s parents and grandfather.","“Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master, what are you trying to do? This sword belongs to Chu Feng.” Eighth Zhao ignored Tianjian Canhua and directly addressed the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master.","He had overheard their conversation.","Boom!","Overwhelming oppressive might suddenly crushed down in the surrounding area, causing the earth to shake.","Eighth Zhao hurriedly raised his cultivation and unleashed his oppressive might to block the attack, but he was still forced down to one knee. The others fared worse, dropping straight to the floor like dead dogs.","The only ones unaffected were the members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace.","Even the flying warships in the sky, except the one belonging to the Heavensword Sacred Palace, plummeted to the ground.","The Palace Master walked up to Eighth Zhao and questioned, “You say the sword belongs to Chu Feng? I only see a sword without a master.”","Her demeanor remained the same, but her disposition changed. Her earlier warmth gave way to extreme coldness.","“I didn’t expect an orthodox sect like the Heavensword Sacred Palace to be this shameless. We all know who deciphered the legacy and defeated the entity inside the spirit formation gate. How can you face your ancestor?” Eighth Zhao asked.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master slowly drew her God Armament sword as she coldly replied, “That’s none of your business.”","Eighth Zhao quickly pieced the puzzles together and scoffed, “Something must have happened to Tianjian Qingyuan. That’s why you’re getting desperate. Panicking in the face of a crisis. You aren’t worthy of leading the Heavensword Sacred Palace...”","Pu!","A sword impaled Eighth Zhao’s head, pierced through his tongue, and pinned him to the ground. He wasn’t dead, but he couldn’t speak anymore. This sword had not only impaled his body but inflicted grievous damage to his soul, too.","“I am the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master. I have to prioritize our palace over everything else. It’s also for the future of our palace that Lord Qingyuan instructed us to protect Chu Feng. I have no regrets even if it means becoming a bad person. I am responsible not for the world but just the Heavensword Sacred Palace. I’m appalled that a clan chief like you don’t even understand such basic logic,” the Palace Master sneered.","With a wave of her sleeves, she sent everyone, including Ye Xiancheng’s parents, flying like scattered leaves. Only Eighth Zhao remained on the spot.","“Draw the sword,” the Palace Master commanded.","Tianjian Canhua marched up to the Lightning Flame Sword."]},{"number":6441,"title":"Chapter 6441: Chapter 6439: Deserving of Death","paragraphs":["“Those scoundrels,” Tianjian Qingyuan roared in anger.","She had seen everything that had just happened with her sharp eyes. She wanted to flit over to where the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members were.","But Song Changsheng suddenly called out, “Are you worried about Chu Feng?”","Tianjian Qingyuan turned to Song Changsheng and noticed the gleam in his eyes. Clearly, he must have seen what she saw as well.","“I won’t stop you from teaching your foolish descendants a lesson, but you don’t need to worry about Chu Feng. Nothing in these eight galaxies can threaten Chu Feng,” Song Changsheng said.","“Are you sure?” Tianjian Qingyuan asked.","“At least that’s true right now,” Song Changsheng replied. “But if you’re worried about your palace members, you ought to return right now.”","“This line deserves to be wiped out,” Tianjian Qingyuan sneered as she ventured deeper down the path.","“Well said,” a deep voice boomed from further down the path, causing their surroundings to tremor. It felt as if the entire realm was speaking to them, given the intense tremors generated from the voice.","An end suddenly appeared in their path, but at the same time, the tremors grew so intense that it felt like their surrounding space would collapse.","A golden light surfaced from the path’s end like a rising sun, vanquishing the darkness. However, the light wasn’t coming from a star but from chains so humongous that they spanned the size of an entire starfield.","These golden chains overlapped like a dumpling, seemingly binding something in place, but they were covered in cracks.","Whoosh!","The golden chains shattered, and their remnants dissipated as golden auras.","Lying inside the golden chains was a black door made out of stone. Two identical entities resembling the black monstrous beast Chu Feng fought were inscribed on both sides of the doors.","Crk!","The black door spanning the size of a starfield opened.","The tremors intensified, but for some reason, they followed a certain rhythm.","The truth was soon revealed.","A colossal being emerged from the door, with each step it took causing the surrounding space to shake. While the colossal being was smaller than the door, it was larger than the behemoths Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan had fought along the way.","The colossal being had traits identical to the black monstrous beast Chu Feng fought—a humanoid body covered in black scales reminiscent of armor. Whiskers resembling snakes wriggled on its head and behind its back, giving it an eerie appearance.","Due to its hulking size, it resembled the entity who informed Chu Feng about the Seven Stars Orbs, the entity whom he suspected to be the Immemorial Cemetery’s master.","“The two of you brought harm to the world by stepping into a place you shouldn’t have. Don’t the two of you deserve more to be wiped out then?” the colossal being asked.","“Hah...” Song Changsheng laughed in self-derision. He raised his head and asked, “You said we brought harm to the world. Is it because we released you?”","“What do you mean by that?” the colossal being asked with a glimmer of interest.","“That earlier formation was a trap, isn’t it? Or should I say that everything in here is a trap? There are indeed legacies and benefits to be claimed in the Immemorial Cemetery, but you used your power to alter certain elements to bait us into your trap, compelling us to do things for you.","“While we did obtain legacies and benefits along the way, everything we do also contributes toward the lifting of your seal. I reckon the whole thing about the Seven Stars Orbs is intended to lift your seal. You were making use of all of us,” Song Changsheng said.","The colossal being smiled. “The two of you harness great potential. I should have made you my subordinates, but you both possess things that interest me.”","The colossal being licked his lips as he stared at Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan as if they were food.","“You must be carrying some kind of treasure, or else you couldn’t have controlled so many elements by yourself to lure us into your trap. What is that treasure? Or should I ask what lies inside that door instead?” Song Changsheng asked.","It was all dark beyond the door, resembling an unfathomable abyss. He sensed an even greater power inside, but he couldn’t tell if it was an entity of a treasure.","His guess was that it was a treasure. The colossal being must have used the treasure’s power to distort their senses to lure them into this trap.","Unfortunately, a restriction placed on the door prevented Song Changsheng from seeing through it.","Tianjian Qingyuan was also observing the door, but she couldn’t see through it with her special eyes either.","Sensing Song Changsheng’s and Tianjian Qingyuan’s gazes, the colossal being said, “Those who are about to die need not know too much.”","Song Changsheng smiled. He looked at his axe as he said, “Someone is indeed going to die, but it won’t be us.”","His axe suddenly vanished.","The colossal being hurriedly raised his head to look upward.","A glowing axe spanning the size of a realm had suddenly appeared above its head and was hacking down on him. At the center of the glowing axe was Song Changsheng’s vanished axe.","Boom!","The impact hacked a gorge into the boundless path.","But the colossal being vanished.","Grar!","A massive mouth suddenly appeared behind Song Changsheng.","The colossal being had dodged the attack and flitted behind Song Changsheng before launching an attack with its whisker. Even though it was just a single whisker, it was already huge enough to resemble a heaven-devouring monster from Song Changsheng’s perspective."]},{"number":6442,"title":"Chapter 6442: Chapter 6440: None of Your Business","paragraphs":["What covered Song Changsheng’s sight was neither a blue sky filled with white clouds nor the starry expanse of space, but a gigantic mouth filled with sharp teeth. Anyone in his place would have been scared out of their wits.","Something like that could have easily devoured an entire realm and all the lives in it.","But Song Changsheng was unfazed.","Shoosh!","There was a cold flash of light, and fresh blood that could fill oceans poured out. The whisker with the massive mouth had been cut down.","It was Tianjian Qingyuan.","“You didn’t have to do that,” Song Changsheng said.","“I don’t like to be exploited,” Tianjian Qingyuan replied.","She swiped two fingers across her sword, and glowing runes appeared on its surface. Then, she thrust her sword forth.","Humongous sword intents manifested before her and gushed into the sky. These were the sword intents she had used to massacre the behemoths earlier, and there were thousands of them.","This was an attack that could easily destroy a smaller starfield.","Before this torrent of sword intents, the colossal being looked small. Yet, he remarked with a grin, “Interesting.”","...","Meanwhile, Tianjian Canhua walked up to the Lightning Flame Sword and stared at it with hesitant eyes. Can I really pull out this sword? Will I be in danger if I fail to do so?","“Canhua, do you intend to continue waiting? Do you not desire the sword?” the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master urged her.","So, Tianjian Canhua cast aside her hesitation and grabbed the Lightning Flame Sword.","Boom!","A powerful surge of oppressive might suddenly swept across the area, only to dissipate before it could reach Tianjian Canhua. It was the Palace Master who blocked it.","After blocking the oppressive might, the Palace Master turned to Ye Xiancheng with a look of surprise. “It’s you?”","Ye Xiancheng emanated a divine aura, and his cultivation had risen to rank five Heavenly God level.","“Xiancheng...” Ye Xiancheng’s parents looked at him with conflicted eyes.","They knew that Ye Xiancheng had tapped into the Immortal Legacy’s power, but this power was non-regenerative. This meant that every bit of energy depleted from the Immortal Legacy would be gone for good.","The Immortal Legacy had great significance to the Ye Immortal Clan. Ye Xiancheng understood that and wouldn’t have used it unless forced to a corner.","But the current situation called for it.","“I’m warning you right now. Don’t even think about touching that sword,” Ye Xiancheng growled at Tianjian Canhua.","Tianjian Canhua dared not to make a reckless move, intimidated by Ye Xiancheng’s aura.","“I can see now that it’s not without reason you became the Ye Immortal Clan’s Clan Chief despite being a junior. You do have some substance. Someone with your potential is destined to achieve greatness. If we join hands, given your and Canhua’s talent, we can make a place for ourselves even in the Ninth Galaxy,” the Palace Master said.","“Leave that talk for the future. Please don’t touch that sword right now,” Ye Xiancheng said.","“Are you planning to interfere in our business, too?” The Palace Master narrowed her eyes.","“Not at all. I’m not that nosey.”","Ye Xiancheng waved his hands as if to profess his innocence, only to abruptly shoot out three beams of golden light from his fingertip and consecutively use three God Taboo Martial Skills: Immortal Protection, Immortal Footwork, and Immortal Suppression.","He flitted behind the Palace Master and thrust his spear toward her head.","The Palace Master hurriedly raised her sword to block the attack, but Ye Xiancheng’s spear suddenly vanished. Before the Palace Master could react, Ye Xiancheng’s spear had already impaled her dantian.","It was Formless Spearmanship.","“You little bastard...” The Palace Master glared at Ye Xiancheng.","But Ye Xiancheng fearlessly replied, “You old hag. Chu Feng is my brother. His problem is my problem. You’re the one who shouldn’t be interfering.”","Ye Xiancheng suddenly lurched. To his astonishment, the Palace Master revealed an eerie smile despite glaring at him with gritted teeth. Sensing something amiss, Ye Xiancheng quickly channeled his martial power into his spear and pulled his spear downward.","He was planning to kill the Palace Master for good.","But as he swung his spear, his heart clenched. He could already feel that his spear had missed, striking thin air. But that shouldn’t have been the case.","He took a closer look and finally understood what happened.","The Palace Master had dissipated into a whiff of golden aura. The golden aura drifted into the distance before converging back into the Palace Master. Her dantian injury was still present, but her disposition suddenly changed, and all her injuries began swiftly healing.","Even her clothes regenerated.","Ye Xiancheng realized the situation had gone awry.","He was planning to curb the Palace Master in a single strike, for a prolonged battle wouldn’t be to his benefit. However, it turned out he had underestimated the Heavensword Sacred Palace.","All members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace rose into the air and took their places behind their Palace Master. They formed hand seals and emanated peculiar lights. They were probably the ones who rescued and healed the Palace Master.","“Someone as young as you wants to preach to me about loyalty? Do you understand the price you have to pay for your loyalty? The Ye Immortal Clan will be wiped from the face of the world because of your folly!”","The Palace Master pointed her finger at Ye Xiancheng, and a sword rain descended.","Ye Xiancheng easily deflected the sword rain with a sweep of his spear.","“I don’t think you’re capable enough to erase our Ye Immortal Clan,” Ye Xiancheng scoffed as he charged at the Palace Master once more.","This time, the Palace Master was prepared. She stepped forth to face him.","However, she couldn’t see through Ye Xiancheng’s moves. His Formless Spearmanship was impossible to read. In just a few clashes, she suffered yet another strike to her dantian.","But the same thing happened again. After the Palace Master was stabbed, she dissipated into a golden aura and converged elsewhere.","“Get into formation!” the Palace Master shouted.","A massive sword of golden light descended from the sky and plunged into the square.","Meanwhile, Ye Xiancheng performed a feint before suddenly turning his martial power toward the members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace. Since he couldn’t kill their Palace Master, he decided to deal with the ones protecting her first."]},{"number":6443,"title":"Chapter 6443: Chapter 6441: A Vile Means","paragraphs":["A golden aura suddenly appeared before the members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace, protecting them from Ye Xiancheng’s aggression. Their Palace Master had stepped in to save them.","The Palace Master followed up with a sweeping slash directed at Ye Xiancheng.","Ye Xiancheng noticed the Palace Master’s strength and speed had greatly increased, but he still held the upper hand in this situation.","Seeing that, the Heavensword Sacred Palace continued channeling their formation, and another sword of golden light descended. Once again, the Palace Master grew stronger.","Ye Xiancheng was starting to feel pressured.","“Immortal Suppression!” Ye Xiancheng roared.","He unleashed the power of Immortal Suppression to curb the Palace Master.","“Activate the formation!” the Palace Master shouted again.","More swords of golden light descended.","By the time the fifth sword descended, Ye Xiancheng could no longer hold his ground. The Palace Master severed him into two by his waist.","The Palace Master couldn’t be killed because of the Heavensword Sacred Formation, but Ye Xiancheng didn’t enjoy the same benefit.","“Xiancheng!” Ye Xiancheng’s parents rushed to catch Ye Xiancheng.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","But several blades of light pierced their bodies, pinning Ye Xiancheng’s parents to the ground. They could only watch with a pained heart as Ye Xiancheng crashed into the ground not too far away from them.","“Father, mother...”","Ye Xiancheng was still alive, but he was in no condition to continue the fight. Seeing his lofty parents pinned to the ground filled his heart with misery. He dragged his tattered body to his parents’ side, leaving a blood trail in his wake.","More blades of light descended, pinning his tattered body in place.","“You might be talented, but a fool will never achieve anything substantial.” The Palace Master waved her sleeves and coldly eyed Ye Xiancheng. She had intentionally spared Ye Xiancheng to watch him suffer.","“The rest of you have nothing to worry about. I bear no animosity. On the contrary, I am sincere about working with you all. Please don’t intervene in our private affairs and make things difficult for me,” the Palace Master addressed the other powers.","She even retracted her oppressive might as a show of sincerity.","Then, she turned to Tianjian Canhua and ordered, “Canhua, draw the sword.”","Tianjian Canhua flitted back to the Lightning Flame Sword. But once again, just as she was about to draw the sword, several figures suddenly landed beside her. This time, it was the Spirit God Clansmen.","The Spirit God Clansmen had recovered considerably after a brief moment of recuperation. Their bodies emanated divine auras reminiscent of gods. They must have used some kind of secret skill.","Shen Hui grabbed Tianjian Canhua’s neck. “Palace Master, I suggest you stop this farce.”","“Isn’t it beneath the Spirit God Clan to threaten me with a junior?” the Palace Master asked.","“It is beneath us to hear you talk about dignity,” Shen Hui scoffed.","“Hahaha!” The Palace Master laughed. “Since time immemorial, the strong have always preyed on the weak. Such is the law of the jungle. Such is humanity. Principles do not bring food to the bowl, but treasures do. I am the leader of the Heavensword Palace Master. What wrong have I done in securing the interests of my sect?”","“Treasures can be shared. My master has already said so. You let your greed get ahead of yourself,” Shen Hui replied.","“How can you share true treasures? I can share the beads on the floor. I can relinquish this sword. But I cannot remain unmoved to the treasures Chu Feng has. He has the legendary Ruler’s Bloodline and Genesis Bloodline. Even you are rare treasures in the world of cultivation as well. This is a rare opportunity, and it won’t come by a second time.”","The crowd finally understood the reason behind the Palace Master’s abrupt change in attitude after Tianjian Qingyuan’s death. She had coveted Chu Feng’s treasures right from the start, but she had to drop that thought out of deference for Tianjian Qingyuan.","“The Spirit God Clan, I have high regards for you. Why don’t you serve our Heavensword Sacred Palace instead of Chu Feng? Our palace can offer you more than what Chu Feng has,” the Palace Master said.","“Our Spirit God Clan will not turn our back on our master,” Shen Hui declared.","“I see.” The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master narrowed her eyes.","She flitted up to Shen Hui and severed her arms before the latter could react.","Boom!","Powerful oppressive might crushed the Spirit God Clansmen down to the ground, rendering them immobile.","“I’d have thought Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists like you would understand that the gap between cultivation ranks cannot be bridged,” the Palace Master scoffed.","She turned her gaze back to Tianjian Canhua.","Without any hesitation, Tianjian Canhua wrapped her hand around the Lightning Flame Sword.","Clang!","She pulled it out.","“How do you feel?” the Palace Master asked.","“I can feel its sharpness and sturdiness, but it doesn’t boost my fighting prowess,” Tianjian Canhua replied.","“Does it not contain a legacy?” the Palace Master asked.","“I don’t think so.” Tianjian Canhua shook her head.","“Put it back first.”","“Ah?”","“Chu Feng hasn’t completed the trial yet. Perhaps he has to finish the trial for the sword to reveal its true prowess,” the Palace Master explained.","So, Tianjian Canhua placed the Lightning Flame Sword back down.","The Palace Master flicked her wrist and took out a sinister compass with countless skulls shackled to its surface. It emanated the Ancient Era’s aura. Clearly, it was a demonic item.","“I’ll give you one last chance. Will you serve our Heavensword Sacred Palace or die here?” the Palace Master asked Shen Hui.","“You scum. Our answer will be the same even if you ask a thousand times. You’ll never receive the recognition of our Spirit God Clan!” Shen Hui roared.","“I have extended a hand to you, but you refuse to take it. Very well. I’ll grant you your wish.”","The Palace Master formed a hand seal, and wails of agony followed. The skulls emerged from the compass and dove their way into the Spirit God Clansmen’s bodies.","GAH!","The Spirit God Clansmen screamed. Their energy flowed through the shackles into the compass.","The members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace widened their eyes in greed. The energy flowing into the compass was far greater than the beads scattered around the square. This was the true power of the gods, nourishment comparable to top cultivation resources!","The Spirit God Clansmen were drained till they resembled skeletons wrapped in skin. Their blood and flesh had been sapped dry. There was a breath left in them, but they wouldn’t survive long.","“All our members shall get a share!”","The Palace Master waved her sleeves, and the compass flew into the air and covered the sky. Divine lights descended and flowed into each Heavensword Sacred Palace’s member.","The palace members were overjoyed. Even those who felt bad for the Spirit God Clansmen couldn’t curb their excitement. Their bodies glowed with divine light as they experienced the benefits brought about from the Spirit God Clansmen’s powers.","The Spirit God Clansmen might be world spiritists, but their powers were highly beneficial to cultivators as well. Their conscience meant nothing in the face of tangible benefits."]},{"number":6444,"title":"Chapter 6444: Chapter 6442: My Honor","paragraphs":["“Thank you, Lord Palace Master.” Tianjian Canhua bowed to the Palace Master.","The other members did the same, too.","Tianjian Canhua, in particular, was extremely excited, for she had gotten the biggest share of the Spirit God Clansmen’s power compared to the others, including the Palace Master.","“Canhua, I am getting old. You are the future of our Heavensword Sacred Palace.” The Palace Master supported Tianjian Canhua to her feet.","The Palace Master’s face suddenly lit up. Something was happening to the realm, and she was familiar with this change. Most likely, the Seven Stars Orbs had been formed.","She turned her eyes to the spirit formation gate and saw Chu Feng and the others inside. Not only was he unharmed, but there was also a rune imprint on his forehead that resembled those on Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, Bai Yunqing, and the others.","This affirmed her conjecture.","At the same time, the imprisoned Little Fishy and the others were freed.","Those inside the spirit formation gate couldn’t see the situation outside, so they were oblivious to the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s betrayal. They rushed to Chu Feng’s side and confirmed his condition before making their way out together.","As soon as they stepped out, they were stunned by what they saw.","“Run, Chu Feng!”","Many voices echoed at the same time. They came from Zhao Zhuyin, Ye Xiancheng, Little Fishy’s parents, and many others.","But they were immediately silenced. The Palace Master had sealed their mouths with her oppressive might.","“You’re too talkative,” the Palace Master snorted before turning to Chu Feng. “Young friend Chu Feng, it’s thanks to you that we have gathered the Seven Stars Orbs.”","But Chu Feng was in no mood to entertain her. He cast a sweeping gaze across the field and saw Eighth Zhao with a sword impaling his head, Ye Xiancheng with his lower body severed and was pinned to the ground, his parents who suffered a similar fate, and the emaciated Spirit God Clansmen.","He also noticed the divine aura shrouding the members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace. That divine aura clearly belonged to the Spirit God Clan.","“Are you behind this?” Chu Feng looked at the Palace Master and asked nonchalantly.","“I told Tianjian Canhua to try drawing the Lightning Flame Sword, but those people came after me right away. You can’t expect me not to retaliate, right?” the Palace Master replied.","“Rubbish! You wanted to monopolize the legacy! I’ll kill you!” Yuwen Yanri roared.","The members of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion were only crushed to the ground, but he was still infuriated by that sight.","Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and all the juniors standing alongside Chu Feng also flared with killing intent. None of them could retain their composure. But Chu Feng raised his hand to stop them as he continued staring coldly at the Palace Master.","The Palace Master was unfazed by Chu Feng’s cold stare. She turned to Yuwen Yanri and the others and smiled, “Calm down. Your clans are still safe because I have a high opinion of your talents. As long as you cooperate with us, I’ll ensure their safety. I’ll even share a portion of the Spirit God Clan’s powers with you. But this deal isn’t extended to Chu Feng.”","The Palace Master’s face suddenly turned cold as she directed her oppressive might toward Chu Feng and the others.","A mighty spirit power suddenly shrouded Chu Feng and the others, transporting them out of the realm and into a teleportation passageway. The same happened to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, the Zhao Immortal Clan, the Ye Immortal Clan, and even the severely injured Ye Xiancheng.","But the Spirit God Clansmen weren’t transported.","It was the teleportation formation previously prepared by the Spirit God Clansmen. They had been holding onto it thus far, and now was the best chance to use it.","But the Spirit God Clansmen should have been in no shape to activate the teleportation formation; they must have paid a heavy price to activate it. The crowd could barely imagine what they had to fork out.","The thought of that made their faces grim.","Weng!","A gate suddenly opened beside Chu Feng. It was Eggy.","She had been reserving her means to protect Chu Feng, and she understood the hefty price she would have to pay if she wanted to bring down the Palace Master, but she couldn’t turn a blind eye to the situation anymore.","Whoosh!","Just as Eggy was about to walk out of the gate, formation chains suddenly sealed it off.","“What are you doing, Chu Feng? You said you’d let me leave freely. Are you breaking your promise? You bastard! Let me out. I’ll slaughter those beasts!”","Eggy was agitated, but she couldn’t break the chains.","“Are you going to abandon the Spirit God Clan? They aren’t dead yet! I can still save them!” she roared.","But Chu Feng ignored her. Thinking about the Spirit God Clansmen’s horrendous conditions made his eyes turn red. Even his lips quivered. “They said it’s their honor to sacrifice their lives for me, and they followed through with their words.”","“What?”","Chu Feng mumbled under his breath, but the others overheard him and were at a loss.","...","Whoosh!","Golden swords covered the sky above the square. There were a total of 1111 of them, and they were pointed at every Spirit God Clansmen.","The Palace Master personally held the blade aimed at Shen Hui. She understood what happened earlier, and she gnashed her teeth in anger. “I underestimated you, the Spirit God Clan. Are you that eager to die?”","She had only spared the Spirit God Clan because they still had value to them, but those wretches dared to activate the teleportation formation, allowing Chu Feng and the others to escape. How could she not be infuriated?","She was so furious that she decided to kill the Spirit God Clansmen right away, or else her anger couldn’t be quelled.","Shen Hui and the other Spirit God Clansmen didn’t even have the energy to stand. They kneeled on the floor with their heads slumped. They were in a worse condition than before. On top of being emaciated, their bodies had grown translucent.","Activating the teleportation formation had sapped the final sliver of their energy. Their bodies were ruined, and even their souls were on the brink of flickering out.","They wouldn’t last long even if not for the swords hanging above their heads.","Clang!","As the swords fell, Shen Hui and her clansmen closed their eyes as they geared themselves up for their imminent death.","But the swords never landed.","Instead, they heard a voice.","“You said it’s your honor to sacrifice yourselves for me. I see it as my honor to protect you.”","Shen Hui and the others were startled. It was Chu Feng’s voice, and it was accompanied with a thunderous boom!"]},{"number":6445,"title":"Chapter 6445: Chapter 6443: Bloodline Rampage","paragraphs":["The Spirit God Clansmen raised their heads and saw Chu Feng floating in the sky, standing right before the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master.","Chu Feng had stopped the Palace Master’s sword with his palm.","The thunderous boom had come from Chu Feng as well. His body was enveloped in nine-colored lightning. Even his eyes were crackling with lightning. It was not Lightning Armor, for this was far stronger than Lightning Armor.","“Chu Feng?” The Palace Master was initially startled, then her face erupted with joy. “I didn’t think you’d dare return to offer yourself up. You’re indeed as loyal as I’ve heard. I’ll fulfill your wish and send you and the Spirit God Clan on your way!”","She tightened her grip around her God Armament, channeling her martial power through it to sever Chu Feng’s palm.","The next moment, she froze in place. To her shock, her sword wasn’t moving at all as if it was stuck to Chu Feng’s palm.","Kacha!","Chu Feng clenched his fist, and lightning ravaged in his grip. The Palace Master’s sword shattered into pieces.","At the same time, the lightning flowed from the sword into the Palace Master, leaving many burn marks all over her body and even her face.","The Palace Master realized something was amiss and hurriedly fled as a whiff of golden aura.","“Get into formation!”","The members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace also sensed Chu Feng’s anomaly. The eighteen rank four Heavenly God level elders quickly got the palace members in position to construct the Heavensword Sacred Formation.","The Palace Master’s golden aura converged before the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s army, and she was infused with healing energy.","A second later, her face warped in shock. The burn marks left by Chu Feng weren't healing at all!","This shouldn’t have been possible.","Chu Feng didn’t chase the Palace Master. Instead, he tossed out a thousand talisman papers that seeped into Shen Hui and the other Spirit God Clansmen’s bodies. These were treasures to stabilize their conditions.","“Is this bloodline rampage?” the Palace Master asked.","It was not just Chu Feng’s body that was shrouded in nine-colored lightning; even the sky was enveloped in dark clouds that crackled with nine-colored lightning, too.","On top of that, the strength Chu Feng displayed was far beyond his cultivation level. He now wielded the power to rival the Palace Master.","“Chu Feng, you... Could it be...” Eggy’s eyes widened in disbelief. She had witnessed such a sight before. It was indeed a bloodline rampage.","Chu Feng had obtained a mysterious metal piece from God’s Era, which detailed a method to trigger and utilize bloodline rampage. Since then, he would study the metal piece whenever he had free time. In recent days, his time had been devoted to the metal piece and his Bloodline Soul Puppet.","Eggy knew he had made some advancements in the method.","This was the reason Chu Feng had stopped her from interfering. He was planning to resolve it personally!","Boom!","Nine massive lightning beasts appeared in the sky. They morphed into nine-colored lightning and zapped down on Chu Feng. Chu Feng absorbed the nine-colored lightning, which made the lightning shrouding him even more resplendent.","Four lightning bolts converged behind Chu Feng and manifested into a pair of wings. These wings were much larger and more imposing than his usual Lightning Wings. Rather than a skill, it felt more like a manifestation of divine lightning.","“It’s indeed the bloodline rampage. You must have lost your senses,” the Palace Master sneered.","“All of you must die today,” Chu Feng spat murderously.","“Activate the formation!” the Palace Master ordered.","Five golden swords descended consecutively from the sky, tearing open five gaping holes through the dark clouds. The five swords emanated overwhelming oppressive might even without the Palace Master channeling them.","They appeared to be on par with Chu Feng’s nine-colored lightning.","“Chu Feng, I know about bloodline rampages. A cultivator suffering from bloodline rampage wields strength proportionate to the potency of their bloodline. I don’t doubt the strength of your bloodline, but how much of it can you exert?","“The Ye Immortal Clan’s brat tapped into his ancestors’ powers, but still, he was powerless against my five celestial swords. Let’s see if your Heavenly Lightning Bloodline is capable of withstanding the might of my celestial swords!” the Palace Master said.","Her oppressive might gushed toward Chu Feng and the Spirit God Clansmen.","Chu Feng narrowed his eyes.","Whoosh!","A bolt of lightning whizzed forth and shattered the oppressive might.","The Palace Master widened her eyes in disbelief. It finally dawned on her that she had severely underestimated what Chu Feng was capable of.","Bzzt!","Her nerves went taut. The crackling had come from behind her. She hurriedly turned around, and her face turned pale with fright.","Unbeknownst to her, Chu Feng had flitted behind her to unleash his lightning. His target was not her but the eighteen rank four Heavenly God level old women behind her.","By the time the Palace Master understood what was going on, the eighteen old women already had their bodies decapitated and souls vaporized by Chu Feng’s lightning. Chu Feng had massacred all of them in a single strike!","“Chu Feng, I’ll rip you apart!” the Palace Master roared furiously.","She formed a hand seal. At the same time, her palace members also emanated thick auras. More golden swords descended from the sky, leaving holes in dark clouds. All in all, there were thirteen celestial swords.","The Palace Master’s body grew larger. She was glowing so brightly from within that it felt as if she would transform into an entity of light. She whipped out a God Armament sword.","This God Armament sword channeled the power of the thirteen celestial swords, its sheer power so great that it distorted the surrounding space.","Chu Feng coldly eyed the Palace Master as if she was a child throwing a tantrum.","The Palace Master was irked by his gaze. She charged at Chu Feng with her sword, moving at a speed surpassing rank five Heavenly God level. Yet, her blade stopped just ten centimeters in front of Chu Feng’s face.","Chu Feng had raised his hand to grab the sword.","Kacha!","He tightened his grip, and the God Armament sword channeling the power of thirteen celestial swords shattered. It was as frail as the earlier sword."]},{"number":6446,"title":"Chapter 6446: Chapter 6444: Summoning the Ancestors With My Life","paragraphs":["The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master hurriedly retreated. She knew she had to go all out.","More streaks of golden lights tore through the dark clouds. This time, six celestial swords fell at the same time.","Tianjian Canhua and the others looked at the nineteen celestial swords in the square with conflicted eyes. This was the furthest their line had ever gone with the Heavensword Sacred Formation. They couldn’t believe that Chu Feng, a junior, had pushed them this far.","Putting aside the Ninth Galaxy, their Heavensword Sacred Palace wielded the strength to unify the world of cultivation!","“Chu Feng!!!” the Palace Master roared.","Her appearance had changed once more under the influence of the Heavensword Sacred Formation. Her body glowed with divinity as if she was a deity descending to the mortal world, but her wretched expression resembled a demon more.","She formed a hand seal, and the nineteen celestial swords shook. All nineteen swords simultaneously unleashed a ray of golden light that converged before her, forming a golden sword that could be wielded.","This golden sword was far stronger than the God Armament sword she had wielded earlier, to the point where the latter couldn’t even begin to compare.","Clang!","Golden beams shot out from the sword and flooded the surroundings with light. This was no ordinary light but sword intent. It shone even brighter than the nine-colored lightning in the sky, as if claiming its spot as the dominant force here.","“That is the True Heavensword Manifestation! Lord Palace Master is able to use the Heavensword Sacred Formation to this extent?”","The members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace couldn’t believe their eyes, but this was terrific news. They understood the significance of this. The True Heavensword, as the name suggested, was the true Heavensword.","Its prowess was unrivaled, especially since it was a fusion of nineteen celestial swords.","But the True Heavensword was extremely difficult to control, even by inheritors of the Heavensword Bloodline. However, the fact their Palace Master could manifest the True Heavensword to this point hinted that she had the ability to control it.","Their Palace Master was stronger than they had expected.","The Palace Master smirked in confidence, knowing the prowess of the True Heavensword. Victory was hers now that she had summoned this blade. There was nothing Chu Feng could do to turn the tables anymore.","“Chu Feng, you’re already a dead man once your bloodline rampage dies down, but I’ll personally slay you for daring to kill eighteen of our rank four Heavenly God level elders! Consider it your honor to die to the True Heavensword!”","The Palace Master suddenly widened her eyes after saying those words.","Chu Feng had flitted up to her and grabbed the True Heavensword. What was even more shocking was that he actually swung it against her.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","There were flashes of cold lights, followed by splatters of blood. The Palace Master had been shredded into pieces.","Chu Feng had moved so quickly that others couldn’t even follow his movements. By the time they snapped out of it, their Palace Master’s corpse was already floating in mid-air, whereas the True Heavensword had fallen in Chu Feng’s hand.","The True Heavensword was a weapon that even Heavensword Bloodline inheritors struggled to control, let alone outsiders!","Even the Spirit God Clansmen were flabbergasted.","“Lord Chu Feng...” Shen Hui exclaimed in shock.","The power Chu Feng displayed shocked her.","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members trembled in fear. There was no hope left, not after their Palace Master had been shredded apart.","But light specks suddenly floated out from the Palace Master’s body and drifted over to the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members before converging back into the Palace Master. It was unknown what means she had resorted to, but she was still alive!","The Palace Master had lost her physical body and was now only a soul entity, but her soul was a unique one. It was covered in runes resembling blades. These runes quivered with power that exceeded her own.","“Lord Palace Master, you...” Tianjian Canhua and the others exclaimed in shock as if they already knew what their Palace Master was going to do next.","The Palace Master ignored them and formed a hand seal. “Chu Feng, you must have thought you could destroy our Heavensword Sacred Palace in exchange for your life? Naive! You aren’t the only one who can put their life on the line!”","The Palace Master changed her hand seal as she deferentially called out, “I offer my life to summon the ancestors. I beseech the ancestors to curb invaders who dare point their blades on our palace!”","The runes on her soul flew forth and fused into the nineteen celestial swords.","Boom!","The nineteen celestial swords suddenly grew until they extended out of the tombstone realm. Even those outside the realm could clearly see the swords.","“My gosh. Am I seeing things?”","“Look! W-what are those?”","The crowd gathered at the Immemorial Cemetery’s entrance noticed nineteen massive sword hilts extending out of the tombstone realm covered in lightning and flames. These swords grew further, eventually reaching a point where even their blades peeked out.","It looked as if nineteen massive swords had been plunged into the massive tombstone realm.","“What’s that?”","Wang Qiang and the others, who had been teleported to safety, were rushing back to the tombstone realm on warships. They were still a distance away from the tombstone realm, but they could still see what was happening due to the tombstone realm’s massive size and their observation formations.","Nineteen light figures appeared around the tombstone realm. They were dressed in the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s robes, commanding the disposition of an immortal, but they were even larger than the tombstone realm itself.","It was as if deities had descended upon the world.","The nineteen light figures simultaneously grabbed the nineteen celestial swords and declared, “Death to those who dare infringe on the Heavensword Sacred Palace!”","As the nineteen figures wrapped their hands around the sword hilts, they suddenly noticed something and cast their gaze into the depths of the Immemorial Cemetery."]},{"number":6447,"title":"Chapter 6447: Chapter 6445: Everyone Gets a Share","paragraphs":["The nine-colored lightning reappeared.","Four massive lightning beasts appeared before the nineteen light figures, and they didn’t just cover the sky but the vast expanse of space. The nineteen light figures looked as small as ants before the four massive lightning beasts.","But the four lightning beasts only appeared for a brief instant. No one aside from the nineteen light figures noticed them.","Just then, countless streaks of lightning surged out from the tombstone realm as if sharp blades. They were coming from Chu Feng!","Chu Feng’s body emitted countless bolts of lightning that whizzed out of the realm, toward the nineteen light figures. The lightning bolts looked powerful, but they paled in comparison to the humongous celestial swords and the light figures.","The Palace Master was not worried.","“It’s unseemly to see you struggle in futility, Chu Feng. There’s a limit to what you can do through bloodline rampage due to your limited cultivation. You don’t stand a chance against the powers of our ancestors. You have lost,” the Palace Master said.","Chu Feng waved his sleeves.","Boom!","Not only did the dark clouds crackling with nine-colored lightning scatter, but even the lightning and flames shrouding the tombstone realm dispersed as well. This allowed those outside to look into the tombstone realm.","The nineteen massive light figures resembling deities came into full view. It was an incredible sight to see them encircling the tombstone realm. This was what the Palace Master had gave her life away to summon.","But no one from the Heavensword Sacred Palace could bring themselves to smile.","The faces of the nineteen ancestors were scrunched up in pain, and their bodies were covered in cracks. They had been impaled by the nine-colored lightning emitted from Chu Feng’s small body.","“The powers of your ancestors?” Chu Feng scoffed.","There was a cold glint in his eyes as the nine-colored lightning devastated everything around him. The nineteen ancestors were sliced into pieces and reduced into wisps that dissipated into the surroundings.","“Gosh! It’s Chu Feng! It’s Chu Feng! It’s Chu Feng!!!”","Some cultivators used their observations means to uncover the source of the nine-colored lightning. They witnessed how Chu Feng obliterated the nineteen terrifying light figures with overwhelming might.","“To think you are this powerful...”","Ye Xiancheng and the others also used their means to look into the tombstone realm, and all of them got goosebumps. That was power beyond their comprehension, and it originated from a junior who was only at True God level!","Putong!","In the tombstone realm, Tianjian Canhua fell to her knees. Despair was written all over her face.","Their Palace Master had given up her life to summon those nineteen ancestors. No one in the eight galaxies should have had the power to defy them, yet Chu Feng massacred all of them!","How can he be this powerful? Even our nineteen ancestors are helpless against him. We don’t stand a chance against someone like that!","Tianjian Canhua felt someone grab her, and before she knew it, she was already standing before the Lightning Flame Sword. It was the Palace Master’s soul.","“Pull it out!” the Palace Master urged.","Tianjian Canhua was confused, but she did as she was told.","The Palace Master hurriedly formed a hand seal, and a tremendous surge of teleportation energy suddenly flowed out from Tianjian Canhua and the other palace members’ bodies.","In the blink of an eye, everyone from the Heavensword Sacred Palace vanished, except for the Palace Master’s soul. She turned to Chu Feng and laughed manically.","“You think you have won, Chu Feng? You’re looking down on our Heavensword Sacred Palace! You’re looking down on the means left behind by our ancestors. Every one of our palace members has a teleportation formation superior to that constructed by the Spirit God Clan hidden in their body.","“Did you think I sacrificed my life just to summon our ancestors’ powers? No, I’m also awakening the teleportation formation as well. Not only have you failed to extinguish our Heavensword Sacred Palace’s lineage, but you have even lost your legacy as well.","“I won! I won!!!” The Palace Master laughed manically as if she had lost her senses.","She remained fearless and excited even though she was already marked for death. She might have lost the battle, but she had won the war. She conceded that it was a wrong move to have provoked Chu Feng, but she still protected the Heavensword Sacred Palace in the end.","On top of that, she had also eliminated a huge rival for Tianjian Canhua. No matter how talented Chu Feng was, he was bound to die once his bloodline rampage died down.","Chu Feng paid no heed to the frenzied Palace Master.","Instead, he raised his arm and pointed his palm upward. He first opened his palm before clenching it shut.","Boom!","The world quaked.","A colossal lightning hand suddenly appeared and plunged its five fingers into the fabrics of space, tearing open a massive spatial rift.","...","Meanwhile, Tianjian Canhua and the others were transported into a teleportation passageway. Cries of misery and despair echoed. The arrogant members of the Heavensword Sacred Palace looked as if they had suffered a huge blow.","They might have survived the crisis, but they had lost their greatest backing.","Even Tianjian Canhua’s eyes were brimming with tears. She clutched the Lightning Flame Sword as she spat murderously, “Chu Feng, I shall massacre your clan. I won’t spare anyone who is associated with you.”","Bzzt!","The teleportation passageway suddenly shook. Lightning surged through the teleportation passageway and swiftly suffused it.","“What’s that?!”","The palace members froze in place. That question had been unnecessary, for all of them had already recognized the lightning to be Chu Feng’s nine-colored lightning.","Their fear intensified as the nine-colored lightning siphoned teleportation energy from the teleportation passageway, resulting in them being pulled back as well.","Meanwhile, the spatial rift clawed open by the lightning hand grew larger. Energy spewed out from the spatial rift—it was teleportation energy!","“What are you doing, Chu Feng? What are you trying to do?!” the Palace Master questioned Chu Feng in a fluster, but there was no reply. In truth, she could already fathom a guess as to what was happening.","“No, this is impossible. Such a thing can’t possibly happen.”","Her common sense told her this was an impossible feat, but her unease only amplified.","Screams echoed as people began pouring out from the spatial rift as if it was raining. These people were all from the Heavensword Sacred Palace. Even Tianjian Canhua was among them.","Chu Feng finally spoke, “All of you get a share. We shouldn’t be leaving anyone out now.”","His nine-colored lightning transformed into nine colossal lightning blades that swept across the sky, felling everyone in the Heavensword Sacred Palace amid a rain of blood.","Not a single person from the Heavensword Sacred Palace was left with an intact corpse."]},{"number":6448,"title":"Chapter 6448: Chapter 6446: Chu Feng’s Hidden Card","paragraphs":["With a single move, Chu Feng massacred almost everyone in that Heavensword Sacred Palace’s line.","The only survivor was the Palace Master, and her eyes were completely widened in horror. Witnessing Chu Feng rip the bodies and souls of their line’s future rendered her incapable of words. Extreme sorrow and despair gripped her. She quietly lowered her head.","“I have let you down, my ancestors,” she weakly murmured before her soul dissipated.","The crowd outside, be it out of shock or fright, fell silent. They stood in a daze as if petrified, staring intently at the tombstone realm.","As the nine-colored lightning dissipated, lightning and flames began shrouding the tombstone realm once more, blocking the crowd’s view.","Yet, the crowd couldn’t snap out of their daze. Their minds replayed the moment of Chu Feng obliterating those deity-like, light figures. Fear seeped into their very beings, regardless of how they had treated Chu Feng before.","This included Jie Tian’s father, Jie Mubai.","Jie Mubai had been secretly watching the spectacle not too far away, and the proximity and his relatively high cultivation granted him a deeper insight into the intricacies of that battle. For that reason, he was more shocked than anyone else.","He was a powerful Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist himself, but he felt like a mortal witnessing a fight between deities. It was a fight completely beyond him.","“Chu Feng is this powerful?!” Jie Mubai was conflicted. He felt both fearful and relieved.","Many times, he had wanted to make a move on Chu Feng, but the latter always slipped past his fingers with the help of others. Only now did he realize that it was not Chu Feng’s allies that he ought to fear, but Chu Feng himself.","There was not a single person he knew who could withstand Chu Feng’s earlier rampage.","“Chu Feng, I doubt you can survive after your bloodline has rampaged to this extent. I can’t let your treasures fall into someone else’s lap.”","Jie Mubai had heard about bloodline rampage and was fortunate to have witnessed it once.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had once encircled a prodigy, who, in a fit of desperation, went into bloodline rampage. That prodigy suddenly attained tremendous power and proceeded to kill many of their members.","That prodigy’s performance was nothing compared to Chu Feng’s, but ultimately, he failed to withstand the backlash of his bloodline rampage. His bloodline devoured his soul, and he died.","Based on that precedent, Chu Feng’s death felt inevitable.","There was no need to fear someone who was already on death’s door. Thinking about Chu Feng’s treasures stoked Jie Mubai’s greed. Thus, he mustered his courage to conceal himself and slip into the tombstone realm.","He first used his observation means to identify Chu Feng’s location.","What he saw shook him.","The nine-colored lightning had receded, signaling the conclusion of the bloodline rampage, but Chu Feng stood unfazed. He was even collecting the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s energies.","“How is he unaffected despite his bloodline having rampaged to that extent? What kind of monster is he?! No, this is impossible. It has to be a treasure protecting him, right? Could it be the Genesis Bloodline? Or is it something else? That brat is hiding so many secrets!”","Despite being shaken up, Jie Mubai still did his best to rationalize the situation.","“How are you feeling, Chu Feng? Say something!” Eggy nervously asked Chu Feng about his condition.","Chu Feng had begun cleaning up the scene after the nine-colored lightning receded, but he hadn’t responded to Eggy’s questions.","It was because he didn’t know how bad the backlash would be, so he thought he should quickly collect the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s origin energies and the Spirit God Clan’s powers. His priority was the Spirit God Clan’s powers, as that was the only thing that could save them.","It was only after confirming he was truly fine that Chu Feng replied, “I’m fine, Eggy.”","The Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members had already assimilated the Spirit God Clan’s powers, so he had to construct a formation to reverse the fusion. In his view, the Heavensword Bloodline brought nothing but impurities to the Spirit God Clan’s powers.","He had to first remove the impurities before returning the Spirit God Clan’s powers to them. Otherwise, he would only be harming them.","“Are you sure you’re fine? You just went on a huge bloodline rampage,” Eggy asked.","“I did, but I’m fine. It’s because of the Bloodline Soul Puppet[1],” Chu Feng replied.","Chu Feng proceeded to explain what happened.","The Bloodline Soul Puppet nourished a cultivator’s bloodline, but its greatest use was to serve as a scapegoat from backlash.","After Chu Feng obtained that mysterious metal piece from God’s Era, he had been cultivating the method on it to tap into the power of bloodline rampage.","While bloodline rampage was a powerful hidden card in times of desperation, it came with severe side effects. Putting aside the backlash, he also risked being consumed by his bloodline and losing his senses.","That would turn him into a slaughter machine until his soul and his body were finally depleted.","The more times one underwent bloodline rampage, the greater the risk became.","The mysterious metal piece detailed a method to control their bloodline rampage and not be devoured by their bloodline. It allowed one to retain their senses, but it couldn’t neutralize the backlash. When the bloodline rampage ended, one still had to face the backlash of wielding powers beyond their means.","Death awaited those too weak to withstand the backlash.","From the moment Chu Feng obtained Bloodline Soul Puppet and realized what it was capable of, he knew right away it was the perfect skill for him.","Bloodline Soul Puppet could be impeccably fused into his bloodline, becoming yet another part of him. He could first direct the backlash to Bloodline Soul Puppet, and as long as it was sturdy enough to withstand the backlash, he wouldn’t sustain any damage at all.","1. Chapter 6201 - In the Immemorial Massacre Sea, to save Eggy, he had to fight someone from the Asura World’s Shahun Clan, and he received this secret skill upon victory. ☜"]},{"number":6449,"title":"Chapter 6449: Chapter 6447: Poisoned Origin Energies","paragraphs":["That was why Chu Feng was so eager to forge a Bloodline Soul Puppet. Once he succeeded, he wouldn’t have to fear backlash from bloodline rampage.","This worked on other backlashes as well, but bloodline rampage was the strongest means he had at hand, so he was naturally more concerned about that.","Once he successfully forged a Bloodline Soul Puppet, the only thing left for him to do was to master bloodline rampage. That was why he devoted his time not to absorbing natural energies but to study the mysterious metal piece.","Having met the God Clan and other Ancient Era’s races, he knew raising his cultivation by a rank or two wouldn’t matter much, unless he had reached Heavenly God level. But if he could grasp bloodline rampage, he could turn the tables during moments that counted.","That was why he didn’t lose his composure despite all the dangers he had encountered in the Immemorial Cemetery. With this hidden card up his sleeve, he wouldn’t have to fear opponents like Jie Mubai.","He hadn’t planned on using this move unless necessary. He was reserving it for Jie Tianran.","But when the Heavensword Sacred Palace stole the Spirit God Clansmen’s powers and threatened their lives, he knew he had to make a move. It also didn’t make sense to leave it to Eggy when he still had cards up his sleeves, especially given the hefty price Eggy would have to pay to deal with an opponent like the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master.","He didn’t think it was worthwhile to use his bloodline rampage on the Heavensword Sacred Palace, but he had no other choice. He had to kill every single palace member to reclaim the Spirit God Clan’s powers, for that was the only way to save them.","“Can you still use your Bloodline Soul Puppet?” Eggy asked.","“It has completely shattered under the backlash. I won’t be able to use it anymore,” Chu Feng replied.","Eggy frowned. “Won’t the backlash go after you now that you don’t have your Bloodline Soul Puppet anymore?”","“I was also worried about that. I thought I’d be next after the backlash destroys my Bloodline Soul Puppet, so I was in a rush to recollect the Spirit God Clan’s powers. Otherwise, I wouldn’t be able to save them before I collapse. That’s why I didn’t reply to you right away.","“Fortunately, the Bloodline Soul Puppet absorbed the brunt of the backlash. I did suffer a bit from the backlash, but it’s still within my means to take,” Chu Feng replied.","He was speaking the truth. His complexion was slightly paler and his aura was slightly weaker, but that was all there was to it.","“The Heavensword Sacred Palace deserves to die!” Chu Feng suddenly cursed.","“What’s wrong? Are you unable to remove their bloodline from the Spirit God Clan’s powers?” Eggy asked.","“No, their bloodline is not a problem for me. I’m talking about their origin energies. I thought you could feast on their Heavenly God level cultivators’ origin energies, but they mixed poison into their origin energies, making it dangerous to assimilate them. The poison appears to have been injected into them at birth,” Chu Feng said.","“How underhanded. Let me take a look,” Eggy said.","Chu Feng transferred the origin energies he had just collected into his World Spirit Space.","Eggy picked up a sliver of the origin energies and placed it on her palm. With her bare eyes, these origin energies didn’t appear any different from normal origin energies. But upon careful examination, she sensed extreme malice in them.","It was not just any poison but lethal poison.","“Why does it seem like the orthodox sects are viler than the malevolent sects? Who, in their right mind, injects poison into their origin energies?” Eggy cursed.","“They are just a bunch of self-righteous scum. It is disgusting to see people pretending to be upright while committing all kinds of atrocities,” Chu Feng spat.","Self-righteous people tended to disguise themselves well.","Chu Feng had a good impression of Tuoba Yijian, Tuoba Tianxue, and Tianjian Canhua. He harbored goodwill to the Heavensword Sacred Palace as well, given that they had rushed to his aid upon receiving his call for help.","But that all turned out to be superficial.","As soon as the Heavensword Sacred Palace learned about Tianjian Qingyuan’s death, they changed their tune and backstabbed Chu Feng. This was no accident. They had been harboring malice toward him, just that they couldn’t make a move due to Tianjian Qingyuan’s intervention.","None of them rejected the Spirit God Clan’s powers. That made all of them guilty. None of them deserved to live.","“Chu Feng, do you think Tianjian Qingyuan is really dead? Does that mean that we won’t be able to find your grandmother anymore?” Eggy asked.","While Chu Feng was conversing with Eggy, a Spirit God Clansman told Chu Feng that the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s change of attitude arose due to Tianjian Qingyuan’s death.","“I’m not sure. Actually, I can’t sense my grandmother anymore,” Chu Feng said.","“Ah?” Eggy was taken aback.","She couldn’t care less about Tianjian Qingyuan’s death, but she was concerned about Chu Feng’s grandmother.","“It’s fine. I was worried about it at first, but I don’t think anything would happen to my grandmother,” Chu Feng said.","He panicked when he first realized he could no longer sense his grandmother, but his worry faded as his intuition told him that his grandmother was fine. He could only trust his intuition now and his grandmother’s strength.","It was meaningless to worry here.","“Chu Feng, your grandmother will be fine. She is very strong,” Eggy said.","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded.","“I have good news for you,” Eggy continued.","“What is it?” Chu Feng asked.","“As underhanded as the Heavensword Sacred Palace is, they are unlucky to have met me,” Eggy said with a smile.","Eggy, are you able to assimilate it?”","“I can. It’ll take longer, but it doesn’t matter since I’m not in a rush.”","“That’s good.”","That was excellent news, but Chu Feng couldn’t bring himself to smile, not with the Spirit God Clan still being in a terrible state. He might have reclaimed their powers, but it wouldn’t be easy for them to recover to their former states.","It was the equivalent of a mortal having their limbs severed. Even if a divine physician reattached their limbs, they would still never be able to move their bodies the way they used to. Their reattached limbs might just be mere decoration.","That was the problem Chu Feng was facing. It wouldn’t be easy for him to properly fuse the Spirit God Clansmen’s powers back into them.","“Chu Feng,” a familiar voice echoed.","A flying warship appeared in the tombstone realm. Little Fishy and the others had returned.","“Big brother, how are you feeling?” Little Fishy ran to Chu Feng’s side, but she stopped when she realized that the latter was treating the Spirit God Clansmen. She dared not interrupt him. Nevertheless, she remained worried about him even though he looked fine.","“Don’t worry, I’m fine,” Chu Feng reassured her.","The others were also examining Chu Feng, and the latter appeared fine in their eyes. It was inconceivable to them, but it didn’t seem like Chu Feng had suffered any adverse effects from his bloodline rampage.","“Holy shit! B-b-brother, you’re a monster! We saw what y-y-you did just now! I didn’t expect the Heavensword Sacred Palace to be this p-p-powerful. Those nineteen old hags were even taller t-t-than this realm! Yet, you easily obliterated them!”","Wang Qiang appeared more relaxed than Little Fishy. He spoke with huge body motions, still feeling awed by the earlier scene.","As for the others, they looked at Chu Feng with greater respect than before. They thought they already had a high evaluation of Chu Feng, but it turned out they were still underestimating him."]},{"number":6450,"title":"Chapter 6450: Chapter 6448: We Aren’t Out of Danger Yet","paragraphs":["The crowd knew that Chu Feng was preoccupied with saving the Spirit God Clan.","“Young friend Chu Feng, do you think these will be useful?”","All the powers opened their secret stashes, hoping to contribute to healing the Spirit God Clansmen. It was not without reason that they were powerhouses in the world of cultivation; some of the items they offered were indeed useful to Chu Feng.","“Thank you.” Chu Feng was moved.","Even though these items were of limited effectiveness, they were still invaluable natural oddities. These powers wouldn’t have offered the treasures to him if they didn’t treat him with sincerity.","Some time later, Chu Feng finally purged all the Heavensword Bloodline from the Spirit God Clan’s powers. He added the natural oddities into a formation and started fusing the powers back into the Spirit God Clansmen.","As soon as the formation was activated, Chu Feng revealed a strained expression and began to sweat profusely. The difficulty of the formation was incredible.","“Master, we’re fine now. You don’t have to strain yourself for us,” Shen Hui and the others said.","Even activating the formation was so strenuous. At this rate, Chu Feng would be extremely weakened, perhaps even facing a threat to his life.","“You should listen to me since you have acknowledged me as your master. I know what I’m doing,” Chu Feng said.","The Spirit God Clansmen fell silent.","The others were worried about Chu Feng as well, but there was nothing they could do or say. They couldn’t possibly dissuade Chu Feng from saving the Spirit God Clansmen.","Finally, Chu Feng managed to fuse the Spirit God Clan’s powers back into the Spirit God Clansmen. This wasn’t enough to bring them back to their former states, but at least they were in a stable condition now.","Chu Feng had expended himself so much that he struggled to remain standing. He was in a terrible state, and it didn’t look like he would recover soon. No one in the crowd knew how to help him.","Little Fishy and the others felt sorry for him.","Just then, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief marched through the crowd with the Lightning Flame Sword. “Young friend Chu Feng, I’m sorry for asking this now, but the energy sealing the Immemorial Cemetery has not been lifted, and the dangerous aura looming above us is getting thicker. Is it because the Seven Stars Orbs haven’t been completed?”","No one blamed the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief for raising that topic.","That was indeed an urgent problem, and if it wasn’t resolved, all of them, including Chu Feng, could lose their lives.","“Let me give it a try.” Chu Feng gestured for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief to hand the Lightning Flame Sword to him.","“Big brother, shall we wait a little more?” Little Fishy was worried. She was worried Chu Feng would be burdened by the sword.","“I’m fine. We need to deal with this as soon as possible, or else we will be in danger,” Chu Feng said.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief handed the Lightning Flame Sword into Chu Feng’s hand.","Boom!","The lightning and flames shrouding the tombstone realm suddenly began twirling like a hurricane, brewing a devastating force.","Chu Feng raised the Lightning Flame Sword, and it pulled his weakened body into the sky.","Roars and bestial cries echoed from the hurricane. Light reminiscent of a formation surged through the lightning and flames, and an incomparably powerful aura enveloped the tombstone realm.","Everyone felt chills.","The aura was so domineering that it intimidated them more than Chu Feng’s earlier bloodline rampage. The crowd felt like ants in a storm. Should the storm strike them, their bodies would be torn apart and their souls vaporized.","Boom!","The world shook.","The light, accompanied by some lightning and flames, surged into the Lightning Flame Sword. The domineering aura faded, and the Lightning Flame Sword reverted to its previous state as if nothing had changed.","The only things that changed were the lightning and flames shrouding the tombstone realm. They were still present, but they lost their earlier spirit and intensity.","Where could all that energy have gone?","The crowd turned their gaze to the Lightning Flame Sword.","“I see.” Che Feng looked at the Lightning Flame Sword and smiled.","But then, the Lightning Flame Sword suddenly stopped supporting Chu Feng, and the duo plunged from the sky.","Countless people rushed to catch him. Huangfu Zhantian moved the fastest and caught Chu Feng first.","“Young friend Chu Feng, do you sense anything?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“This sword is indeed extraordinary. Not only is it an extremely powerful God Armament, but it is also capable of opening Heaven Gate,” Chu Feng replied.","“Heaven Gate?”","The crowd was overjoyed. Many people revealed looks of envy.","Entering Heaven Gate would bring one into a land filled with fortuitous encounters in the Ninth Galaxy, as if ascending heaven in a single step. The next moment, the crowd shuddered.","The dangerous aura was intensifying at a terrifying pace.","The crowd quickly brought out their observation means. The lightning and flames shrouding the tombstone realm had lost their intensity, so they could see what was happening outside from within now.","Only then did they notice a large congregation of storm clouds above them, spanning not just a realm but the entire Immemorial Cemetery. When they took a closer look, they realized those were not storm clouds but a billowing black aura.","Boom!","Thunder boomed from the black aura, and a thick red light flashed like a lightning bolt.","The faces of the crowd turned pale. Even Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, and the others looked unnerved.","When the red light flashed, everyone suddenly felt a sense of suffocation. There was a tug on their souls as if the red light was siphoning them away.","“Did I feel it wrongly? I thought my soul was going to be dragged out by that red light.” Huangfu Zhantian panicked.","Even the fearless elder of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was feeling anxious."]},{"number":6451,"title":"Chapter 6451: Chapter 6449: Tribute Formation","paragraphs":["“You felt that too? I thought it was only me,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Through their exchanges, the crowd realized all of them had experienced the same feeling.","“Brother, w-w-what was that? Was it the tribute formation?” Wang Qiang asked.","“It is indeed a tribute formation,” Chu Feng replied.","“A tribute formation? But we obtained the Seven Stars Orbs! Was it a failure?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked nervously.","“We did manage to combine the Seven Stars Orbs, but we have underestimated our opponent. The other party hasn’t been idling around. They must have been preparing this tribute formation while we were busy with the Seven Stars Orbs, and they completed it ahead of us,,” Chu Feng replied.","“What should we do now?” someone asked.","“We have to breach the tribute formation to leave this place, but it appears to be linked to the Immemorial Cemetery. Otherwise, it wouldn’t have been able to envelop the entire Immemorial Cemetery. We’re dealing with power from the Immemorial Era. It’s nigh impossible to breach it by force. Our best bet is to find the person behind the formation,” Chu Feng said.","...","Meanwhile, devastating shockwaves ravaged the depths of the Immemorial Cemetery.","A sweeping, glowing axe sent the colossal being flying into the distance. Even though it was covered in glaring wounds, the colossal being displayed no fluster. Instead, it raised its head and snickered.","The tribute formation had already enveloped the Immemorial Cemetery.","Shoosh shoosh!","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan flitted over from different directions to regather. Neither was wounded, but they were gasping for air. It was not easy for them to bring down the colossal being even when combining their strengths.","“You’re the one behind the tribute formation?”","The two of them looked at the colossal being.","The colossal being scoffed, “Tsk tsk. I have to admit the two of you are formidable. You are limited by the world of cultivation. You could have achieved great things if you had entered the Ninth Galaxy, but you won’t have the chance to do so anymore.”","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan didn’t answer. Instead, they continued raining axes and swords down on the colossal being, knowing that they had to slay the other party to resolve this crisis.","The colossal being retaliated with his whiskers, the eerie smile persisting on his face.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng and the others fell into despair.","“The Immemorial Cemetery is humongous. How do we find the person behind the tribute formation?”","The person behind the tribute formation would have known that too and gone into hiding. Considering how vast the Immemorial Cemetery was, searching for that person would be no different from finding a needle in a vast ocean.","“You don’t need to worry about that. You’re going to die here today anyway,” a voice echoed from the distance.","Jie Mubai appeared.","“How dare you show yourself!”","Several powerful energies assaulted Jie Mubai the moment he revealed himself, but all the energies vanished before they could reach him, as if devoured by some entity.","The crowd frowned. It was evident Jie Mubai had come prepared.","“Hah! A bunch of dying fools wishes to bring me down with them? Dream on. You’ll die to the tribute formation, but I’ll survive.”","Jie Mubai confidently pulled out the black talisman paper he had obtained from the mysterious expert who proclaimed himself emperor, but the talisman paper was now empty.","A humanoid figure standing at over a hundred meters tall appeared behind Jie Mubai. It unleashed a powerful aura that overpowered the crowd.","It had six limbs, each equipped with sharp claws. It had a face resembling a human, but it looked so hideous that it felt unnerving. Its eyes were as big as fists. Its nose was flipped inside out. Its mouth reached up to its ears, and it was filled with sharp teeth.","It was the monster residing in the talisman paper.","Jie Mubai had been reluctant to summon it as he would have to offer his soul up to do so. He didn’t want to be controlled by someone else. But he knew there was no other choice when the tribute formation appeared. Waiting would only result in death.","He had to swear fealty to the mysterious expert who proclaimed himself emperor.","“Hah...” A chuckle echoed from Song Yun. “Who are you trying to intimidate with that hideous thing?”","Even those on Chu Feng’s side were startled by those words. That monster’s aura was so powerful that they didn’t think it could be fake.","“Do you think this is a mere intimidation, lass?” Jie Mubai glanced at Song Yun.","Song Yun didn’t answer. She raised her head and looked at the tribute formation before uttering words that confused others. “So be it.”","Even Jie Mubai was bewildered. “Has fear eroded your mind?”","What Song Yun did next further confused the crowd. A step at a time, she made her way toward Jie Mubai.","“Are you provoking me right now? Or do you seek to join me?” Jie Mubai asked.","“Join you?” Song Yun suddenly stopped to look at Jie Mubai. Her face scrunched in disdain. “ You? ”","GWAH!","A scream echoed.","A huge mouth had suddenly appeared behind Jie Mubai and devoured the humanoid monster.","The culprit was an aura monster spanning over ten thousand meters in length. It resembled a lion, having four muscular limbs and a tail.","But its most eye-catching trait was its eyes. It had a massive eye that covered half of its head, and within that eye were nine pupils. It looked sinister, disgusting, and horrifying.","The crowd was no stranger to this monster.","It was Nine Pupils Demon Aura, the monster conjured by Demon Heavenly Exalted.","When Song Yun and the new king obtained the Demon Heavenly Exalted’s legacy, the new king underwent a challenge in hopes of gaining control of the Nine Pupils Demon Aura, but he failed. That resulted in the Nine Pupils Demon Aura breaking free of its seal.","Everyone would have been dead if Song Changsheng hadn’t arrived in time to slay the Nine Pupils Demon Aura.","But why would the bloodthirsty Nine Pupils Demon Aura suddenly appear at this juncture?","While the crowd was contemplating this question, the Nine Pupils Demon Aura made its way toward Song Yun, contracted its massive body until it was only ten meters wide, and obediently lay down in front of her like a little kitten, allowing her to stroke it.","The answer was apparent."]},{"number":6452,"title":"Chapter 6452: Chapter 6450: The Nine Pupils Demon Aura’s Master","paragraphs":["“Hm?”","Song Yun, while stroking the Nine Pupils Demon Aura, suddenly frowned. She looked around the sky as if searching for something.","“It’s you.” The new king glared at Song Yun. “I was wondering why I failed. You took control of the Nine Pupil Demon Aura before me. It attacked the crowd the moment it was unsealed not on its own volition but under your control.”","The crowd was stunned. This revelation made a huge difference.","“Could there be a misunderstanding?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","Jie Mubai’s humanoid monster would have massacred all of them if Song Yun hadn’t intervened. It didn’t make sense for her to harm them, only to save them afterward.","“Yes, it was me,” Song Yun replied.","Even the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief was dumbfounded. They struggled to make sense of her intention.","Chu Feng’s eyes turned cold.","Song Yun couldn’t care less about the others, so her eyes were only focused on Chu Feng. “Big brother Chu Feng, you’re looking at me coldly. Do you intend to kill me just because I hurt those few people? They are your friends, but am I not your friend, too?”","She was only concerned about Chu Feng’s attitude.","“Why did you do that?” Chu Feng asked.","“I just don’t like them, especially that lass.” Song Yun glanced at Little Fishy. “She’s hardly young anymore, yet she still goes around calling you big brother. How repulsive.”","Little Fishy’s gaze turned cold.","Xianhai Shaoyu’s killing intent flared. Little Fishy was his little sister. Even though they often teased each other, he would put his life on the line to protect her.","“So what if s-s-she calls him big brother? Our Yu’er was still a child w-w-when she first met my brother. The s-s-shit you know anything about the bond they share. Besides, aren’t you calling h-h-him big brother, too?","“Truth be told, I’m more disgusted by you than a-a-anything else. There’s nothing I, Wang Qiang, hate m-m-more than manipulative women,” Wang Qiang cursed.","“A pathetic stutterer who can’t even talk properly is speaking on someone’s behalf? I only wanted to teach you a lesson, but I have changed my mind now. I’ll claim your lives!” Song Yun spat.","The Nine Pupils Demon Aura roared, and its body expanded to over ten thousand meters wide once more.","“What are you trying to do, Song Yun?” Chu Feng asked.","“Big brother Chu Feng, you should know better than anyone. There’s no way to breach the tribute formation. They are doomed to die here. But we are different. We can leave this place.”","Song Yun clenched her fist. There was an object resembling a light key in her grasp. She swung the light key, and it flew forth as a blade of light.","A humongous gate manifested out of thin air.","It was only a hundred meters in width but over ten thousand meters in height. Rather than a gate, it looked more like a flight of stairs leading into the distant horizon.","On the other side of the gate was a starry world overflowing with natural energies. It didn’t feel like a formation realm but a real world.","“Could that be Heaven Gate?”","The crowd felt instinctively drawn to the gate.","“If they are going to die anyway, they might as well share their legacies with us,” Song Yun said.","“Go ahead and enter Heaven Gate since you have opened it, but do not hurt anyone. Otherwise...”","“Otherwise what?” Song Yun asked.","“It’ll be over between us,” Chu Feng replied.","“You want to sever ties with me over such trash? Big brother Chu Feng, shouldn’t the Immemorial Cemetery have shown you how powerless we currently are? The world of cultivation we currently live in is incomplete. It limits our growth.","“The real world of cultivation lies inside that gate. We have to venture in there to reach our peak. But the Ninth Galaxy is filled with powerhouses who have been there since the Ancient Era or even earlier. Those people have already claimed the initiative. Not everyone can thrive there.","“But we can. I am the only one who can accompany you to the peak. The others are a burden. They aren’t worthy of these legacies. These legacies should go to those more deserving of them—us.","“Do you truly intend to sever ties with me over mere baggage?” Song Yun asked.","“I trust their potential, but even if not for that, they are still my friends. I, Chu Feng, will not abandon my friends. Song Yun, if you still take me to be your friend, you should leave without hurting anyone,” Chu Feng replied.","Chu Feng was infuriated after learning that Song Yun was the one who ordered the Nine Pupils Demon Aura to hurt Little Fishy and the others, but he knew this was not the time to turn against her.","Song Yun had obtained the Demon Heavenly Exalted’s legacy and gained possession over the Nine Pupils Demon Aura. The Nine Pupils Demon Aura must have been truly powerful to have feigned death before Song Changsheng.","He could have subdued the Nine Pupils Demon Aura with his bloodline rampage, but he was now so feeble that he couldn’t even stand up. He definitely wasn’t a match for Song Yun right now.","Eggy would surely make a move if he turned against her now, but that would come at a price. He had chosen to resort to bloodline rampage earlier, knowing he would expend the Bloodline Soul Puppet he had forged with great difficulty, because he didn’t want Eggy to pay the price.","That was why he withheld his anger and tried his best to placate Song Yun instead.","The ideal situation was for Song Yun to leave in peace.","“I can’t do that, big brother Chu Feng,” Song Yun said as her killing intent flared.","“I shall teach her a lesson.” Eggy’s killing intent flared as well.","She was fond of Little Fishy, so she wouldn’t allow anyone to kill the latter in her presence.","Boom!","A powerful aura suddenly surged from Chu Feng’s side, and it was no weaker than the Nine Pupils Demon Aura."]},{"number":6453,"title":"Chapter 6453: Chapter 6451: The Prodigies’ Hidden Cards","paragraphs":["Chapter 6451: The Prodigies’ Hidden Cards","It was Xian Miaomiao. Her green aura surged into the sky, contrasting against Song Yun’s.","“Miaomiao, you...” Chu Feng murmured.","It was the Soul Fog, Xian Miaomiao’s hidden card.","“Song Yun, you wouldn’t even have been qualified to face me if you hadn’t obtained the Heavenly Demon Exalted’s legacy here. If we are a burden, you are even less than a burden,” Xian Miaomiao sneered.","“Is our Princess Miaomiao angry? You claim that I’m reliant on the Heavenly Demon Exalted’s legacy, but I obtained it myself. Can you say the same about your legacy? If not for that master of yours, you would have never risen to such a height.","“That green aura is the Soul Fog, right? Let me guess—you got that from your master, too. I don’t believe you are capable enough to earn the Soul Fog’s acknowledgment by yourself. The Soul Fog is a legendary power. You aren’t worthy of it. Why don’t you hand it to me instead?” Song Yun sneered.","The Nine Pupils Demon Aura released a sharp blade at Xian Miaomiao.","“Hmph!” Xian Miaomiao harrumphed.","She unleashed her Soul Fog, and it eroded and devoured the sharp blade in an instant.","The Soul Fog proceeded to gush at the Nine Pupils Demon Aura. The latter roared and unleashed overwhelming currents of black aura in response. The black aura and the green aura clashed in the sky, and it appeared to be a stalemate.","Xian Miaomiao formed a hand seal, and her Soul Fog intensified.","“Destroy her,” Song Yun ordered.","The Nine Pupils Demon Aura opened its mouth, and an endless stream of black aura erupted from it as if a volcano.","The scale of their clash was so overwhelming that it divided the tombstone realm into two, with both sides appearing to be equally matched.","Xian Miaomiao changed her hand seal, and the Soul Fog began fusing with her body. Green runes covered her body, and even her eyes turned green as well. The change in appearance complemented her delicate features, granting her an exotic beauty.","More importantly, her aura became stronger.","“Come,” Song Yun ordered.","The Nine Pupils Demon Aura dissipated before surging into Song Yun’s body. An eye with nine pupils appeared on her forehead. On top of controlling the Nine Pupils Demon Aura, she could also harness its power for her own use.","Both Xian Miaomiao and Song Yun whipped out their God Armaments and charged at each other. Their weapons clashed, and each strike caused black and green auras to ripple into the surroundings.","Xian Miaomiao tried to lead the battle elsewhere to avoid implicating others.","“Heavens! No wonder this is God’s Era. Young friend Chu Feng’s bloodline rampage is amazing, but so are the means of those two ladies. Aren’t the juniors of this generation too powerful? How many people in the Ancient Era can compete with them?” Huangfu Zhantian exclaimed.","He realized his talents were nothing compared to these juniors.","He soon turned to Wang Qiang and asked, “What about you? What’s your hidden card?”","Wang Qiang was speechless. Is this the time to ask that? That said, he still put on airs and replied, “Elder, I-I-I’m withholding my hidden card to not terrify you.”","“Then you should go and help Miss Miaomiao!” Huangfu Zhantian said.","“Y-y-you believe me?” Wang Qiang rolled his eyes.","Meanwhile, the others had their eyes locked on the intense battle in the sky.","Xianhai Shaoyu glanced at his little sister. Knowing what was on her mind, he placed his hand on her shoulder, and when she turned around to look at him, he shook his head. He sent a voice transmission over, “I know you want to join the battle, but I’m sure you don’t want to worry Brother Chu Feng, right?”","He was the only one who knew his little sister had obtained tremendous power from their Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land, but that power was of a similar nature to bloodline rampage. Not only did it deplete one’s bloodline, but it also inflicted great damage on one.","It should only be used when truly cornered.","Upon hearing his words, Little Fishy hesitated, and her killing intent diminished.","Xianhai Shaoyu continued, “We should trust Miss Miaomiao. Also, I suspect that there’s a time limit to Heaven Gate once manifested. That wench wants to enter the Ninth Galaxy, so she can’t afford to be stalled here.”","Boom!","The clash between the black and green auras in the sky intensified.","“That gate is about to disappear. Song Yun is the one who should be panicking now,” Xianhai Shaoyu glanced at Heaven Gate and remarked.","Heaven Gate remained perfectly visible even though the sky was enveloped by black and green auras, which was why Xianhai Shaoyu could clearly see it weakening.","“Be careful!” Xian Miaomiao suddenly shouted.","A black aura shot straight at Chu Feng.","Song Yun had struggled free of Xian Miaomiao, and she used this opportunity to go straight for Chu Feng. Her right hand was taut like a sharp knife, emanating a peculiar light.","Little Fishy’s eyes glowed with an iridescent light. A powerful aura flared from her body. Astonishingly, she was no weaker than Xian Miaomiao and Song Yun.","But just then, Eggy relayed a voice transmission to Little Fishy, “Yu’er, leave this to me.”","A gate appeared in front of Chu Feng. Eggy marched out with a black scythe and swung it down on Song Yun’s glowing arm.","Pu!","Blood splattered. Song Yun’s right arm had been severed.","Song Yun frowned in pain, but she continued advancing.","Before Eggy could react, Song Yun had already flitted past her to reach Chu Feng. She grabbed her severed right arm and plunged it into Chu Feng’s body.","“Chu Feng!!!”","Everyone was horrified, but their horror soon turned into astonishment.","Even Eggy, who was about to decapitate Song Yun with her scythe, suddenly halted.","Xian Miaomiao had caught up, but she didn’t continue her assault on Song Yun.","Chu Feng was emanating a peculiar light that was identical to the light coming from Song Yun’s right hand. Under the light, Chu Feng’s weakened body miraculously healed up at a swift pace."]},{"number":6454,"title":"Chapter 6454: Chapter 6452: The Sentimental Type","paragraphs":["Chapter 6452: The Sentimental Type","“Song Yun, you...” Chu Feng looked at Song Yun with conflicted eyes.","Her face was pale from the severance of her arm, and blood seeped from the corner of her lips. Yet, she smiled sweetly at him as if she couldn’t feel pain. It reminded him of the first time they met.","“Don’t worry, this is a protection means I obtained from the Netherworld Tower. I didn’t shed any innocent blood for it.”","Song Yun took back the severed arm before turning around to face Eggy. She carefully assessed Eggy from head to toe before speaking with a smile, “How beautiful. And you’re always with big brother Chu Feng, too. You’re actually my biggest threat.”","Eggy frowned. “What do you mean?”","She was still holding her scythe tightly.","Song Yun had yet to rein in her power. Even if she wouldn’t hurt Chu Feng, there was no guarantee she wouldn’t hurt the others.","“Don’t worry, I won’t make a move on you. I have never thought of killing you. You’re different from the others—you’re useful. You’d save big brother Chu Feng when it counts,” Song Yun said.","Eggy didn’t say a word, but her gaze remained conflicted. She wasn’t fond of Song Yun, but the latter had helped Chu Feng several times.","Song Yun then turned to Xian Miaomiao and said, “You’re qualified to hold onto the Soul Fog for the time being.”","Last but not least, she turned to Little Fishy and remarked, “Keep your power, lest your body crumbles and you need big brother Chu Feng to save you again.”","After saying her piece, she morphed into a black aura and surged toward Heaven Gate. She stopped at the entrance, turned around, and looked at Chu Feng.","“Jie Mubai isn’t dead. I don’t know how he escaped, but he isn’t the one behind the tribute formation. I also sense power far surpassing us hidden here.","“Remember this, big brother Chu Feng. The world doesn’t care about us. They’ll kick us when we’re down and use us as conversation fodder when we’re dead. The world isn’t worth risking your life for. Don’t ruin your future over baggage. You have to survive, even if for your family members.","“As for your opinion of me...”","Song Yun fell silent, and her eyes reddened. She looked down for a second before smiling. Her smile carried a hint of liberation.","“It doesn’t matter. You may enter the Ninth Galaxy, but we might not meet again.”","Despite her words, her teary eyes carried yearning. She cut her speech there and entered Heaven Gate without turning back. At the same time, Heaven Gate appeared to have reached its limit and vanished in space.","She might have left, but the crowd remained tense.","The drama she caused before leaving felt like a farce, but her killing intent was the real deal. She would have killed everyone if Xian Miaomiao hadn’t stopped her.","Wang Qiang turned to Chu Feng with a rare hint of solemnity, seemingly curious to know his opinion of her.","Eggy returned to the World Spirit Space, sat down, and formed a hand seal. She had tapped into the Godsoul’s power to sever Song Yun’s arm. It might have only been for a brief moment, but she needed to raise her strength high enough to match the Nine Pupils Demon Aura. As a result, the burden on her was considerable.","Xian Miaomiao and Little Fishy also began recuperating.","The one who was now in the best condition was Chu Feng. The energy Song Yun had injected into him was extremely potent, fully healing him in an instant.","Chu Feng looked at Little Fishy and Xian Miaomiao.","Little Fishy was still faring fine. She didn’t enter the fight despite having activated her means, so her condition was not too bad.","But Xian Miaomiao was in a terrible state. Her aura was severely weakened to the point where her life was at risk.","But she was prepared for this. She took out a jade bottle and uncorked it. Rich energy wafted out; it was so invigorating that it felt like one could live for a thousand years more just by taking a whiff of it.","She swallowed the pill before smiling at Chu Feng. “Don’t worry. My master specially prepared this for me to deal with the backlash after using Soul Fog.”","Then, she closed her eyes and formed a hand seal.","Despite telling Chu Feng not to worry, her gritted teeth and distorted expression showed that she was facing excruciating pain. That extraordinary pill might have lessened her backlash, but it wasn’t enough to free her from its consequences.","Chu Feng couldn’t do anything to help Little Fishy, Xian Miaomiao, or Eggy. Even he had to rely on his Bloodline Soul Puppet to offset the backlash of his bloodline rampage.","“Chu Feng, don’t worry about me. I’d have taken a long time to cultivate using these origin energies, so it’s a good thing that I’m using them for recuperation instead,” Eggy said as she began devouring the origin energies.","Chu Feng remained worried, so he continued keeping an eye on his World Spirit Space. Fortunately, Eggy’s condition appeared to be improving after assimilating the origin energies. Even the toxins were removed while they were being converted to healing energy.","The only problem was that she was depleting the origin energies so fast that he was worried there wouldn’t be enough for her to use. These origin energies were from the Heavensword Sacred Palace, a power comprising many Heavenly God level cultivators. It would be difficult to find such a huge amount of origin energies anywhere else in the world of cultivation.","This reflected the severity of Eggy’s backlash. She wouldn’t have required this many resources for her recovery otherwise.","“Do you see it, Chu Feng? I’m truly all right. Go and deal with the tribute formation instead,” Eggy sensed Chu Feng’s observation and urged him to leave.","“All right.” Chu Feng retracted his consciousness from his World Spirit Space.","Ye Xiancheng was standing before him with a heavy and melancholic look.","“Brother Chu Feng, I hope you don’t blame Song Yun too much for what happened earlier. I might not know her well, but I can tell she truly cares for you. Not to mention, she’s terminally ill, and no one knows whether she can be treated or not.” Ye Xiancheng sighed as he walked away with deepening melancholy.","He was a sentimental man. He had most definitely fallen for Song Yun despite the latter backstabbing him."]},{"number":6455,"title":"Chapter 6455: Chapter 6453: Light and Darkness","paragraphs":["Chapter 6453: Light and Darkness","Chu Feng felt conflicted, especially after hearing Ye Xiancheng’s words about Song Yun being terminally ill. He recalled Song Yun’s parting words about how they might never meet again.","Song Yun knew her condition the best. Could her condition be truly that bad?","He could tell that Song Yun truly intended to kill the others earlier. Had Xian Miaomiao not stalled her till Heaven Gate was about to close, she would have killed Little Fishy and the others and stolen their legacies.","But at the same time, she used her life preservation means to heal him before leaving.","Chu Feng was in a weakened state earlier, but it was not a threat to his life. He would have recovered in due time. In contrast, Song Yun’s healing energy was extremely potent, to the point where it felt like a waste to use it here.","Song Yun was vicious to others, overlooking past ties as if she had no feelings. But she was earnestly good to Chu Feng. How could he judge something like that?","...","Deep in the Immemorial Cemetery, there had been an intense battle that left many spatial rifts. Anyone else who witnessed this sight would have been horrified. Some of the spatial rifts were large enough to devour entire realms.","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan stood in space, their eyes locked on the colossal being falling into deep space. Only when they saw the colossal being’s life being snuffed out and its body disintegrate into ashes did they breathe a sigh of relief.","These two powerful entities sat on the ground and took out their treasures. They were exhausted. Their bodies were trembling so much that they couldn’t even summon the strength to hold their weapons.","They managed to defeat the colossal being by joining forces, but they paid a hefty price for it. Both of them had lost their fighting ability.","“It’s finally over. It wasn’t easy at all,” Tianjian Qingyuan remarked with a sigh. Had Song Changsheng not been here, it was unlikely that she could have defeated the colossal being by herself.","She had no idea why there was such a powerful entity here, but it was fortunate they had won.","“It’s good that you’re here. I wouldn’t have been able to defeat that monster alone,” Song Changsheng said. He shared the same sentiment as Tianjian Qingyuan.","After those two left for the Ninth Galaxy, the strongest person he had met in the world of cultivation was Tianjian Qingyuan. He didn’t expect there to be something even more terrifying in the Immemorial Cemetery. He wouldn’t have been able to deal with it alone.","It could have been due to the joy of victory or the camaraderie built up from their partnership, but Tianjian Qingyuan revealed a rare smile and asked, “What do you intend to do next? Are you heading into the Ninth Galaxy?”","Instead of answering the question, Song Changsheng asked, “What about you?”","“I felt the natural energies in the Ninth Galaxy earlier when Chu Feng’s grandmother opened that gate. It was even more concentrated than it was in the Ancient Era. I have a speculation. Perhaps the weakening of the other eight galaxies has something to do with the Ninth Galaxy,” Tianjian Qingyuan said.","Song Changsheng narrowed his eyes. “Are you saying that the Ninth Galaxy is absorbing the energies of the other eight galaxies?”","“It is possible,” Tianjian Qingyuan replied.","“I’m curious to know what happened in the final years of the Ancient Era.”","“I’m curious to know, too.”","“You don’t know?”","“I can’t remember. It’s as if something has sealed my memories. In fact, a lot of my memories have become blurry.”","“I’ll go to the Ninth Galaxy,” Song Changsheng suddenly said.","“Hm?” Tianjian Qingyuan was surprised by the sudden declaration.","Song Changsheng smiled. “I’m preparing to head to the Ninth Galaxy. Someone told me that we’re being limited by the eight galaxies, and only by entering the Ninth Galaxy can we shake free these restraints. I doubted his words, but I believe it now.”","Tianjian Qingyuan remarked, “Your friend has quite the foresight.”","“I’ll introduce you to him if there’s a chance, but you have to be mentally prepared,” Song Changsheng said.","“Mentally prepared?” Tianjian Qingyuan was confused.","“He is a charming man, unlike me. I heard all the women he met have fallen for him.”","Tianjian Qingyuan chuckled. “I didn’t think you would be the kind to crack jokes.”","Song Changsheng innocently replied, “I’m not joking.”","“Is that so? That makes me even more curious.”","Boom!","A loud explosion suddenly echoed from the horizon.","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan immediately looked over. To their horror, the tribute formation didn’t dissipate. Instead, its red light was flickering with greater frequency than before.","“What’s going on?”","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan felt uneasy. They thought the colossal being was behind the tribute formation, and slaying it would resolve the crisis. But that didn’t happen.","Perhaps the colossal being was not the mastermind behind the tribute formation.","...","On Chu Feng’s side, other than Xian Miaomiao and those who were recuperating, everyone else was looking at the sky with frightened eyes.","The tribute formation had enveloped the entire Immemorial Cemetery, and each time the red light flickered, the crowd felt like their souls would be siphoned away.","In their panic, the crowd turned to Chu Feng. They couldn’t think of anyone else who could resolve this crisis. But what they saw left them confused.","Chu Feng’s head was lifted, but his eyes were closed. Only upon sensing the crowd’s gaze did he open his eyes. “Don’t worry, I have already found the opening in the tribute formation. There is no need to find the mastermind to decipher the tribute formation.”","“R-r-really?” Wang Qiang asked.","The others looked at Chu Feng with skeptical but hopeful eyes. It would be amazing if that were true.","“Of course.” Chu Feng was confident.","He took some time to construct a formation.","The formation consisted of two parts. One encompassed a vast area and contained many formation cores. The other was the size of a jar but contained tremendous energy comparable to a realm. The formation occasionally emanated a golden glow, though it was impossible to peek into it.","The crowd quickly realized that the formation’s golden glow and the tribute formation’s red light appeared at the same time, as if they were synchronized. Yet, they gave off different feelings, as if light and dark, good and evil."]},{"number":6456,"title":"Chapter 6456: Chapter 6454: The Person Who Chose the ‘Dark’ Option","paragraphs":["Chapter 6454: The Person Who Chose the ‘Dark’ Option","“Someone needs to take this formation into the tribute formation,” Chu Feng said with the golden formation in hand.","“I’ll go.”","“Let me go.”","“I-I-I’ll go.”","There was no lack of brave volunteers, ranging from prodigious juniors to older cultivators. Despite knowing the tribute formation was fraught with danger, they remained fearless.","“On top of bringing the formation in, that person has to activate it as well.” Chu Feng turned to Bai Yunqing and said, “Brother, I’ll entrust this important task to you.”","“Big brother Chu Feng, how do I activate the formation?” Bai Yunqing asked.","Chu Feng’s formation was extremely complicated. Bai Yunqing couldn’t see through the formation despite his higher spirit power.","“You just have to channel the formation after entering the tribute formation,” Chu Feng replied.","“Understood.” Bai Yunqing nodded.","“Brother, you should go as well. It’d be good to have someone to cover him,” Chu Feng told Wang Qiang.","“N-n-no problem,” Wang Qiang replied.","“I’ll go, too,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“Why don’t we all go together?”","Huangfu Zhantian, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, and the others offered their help.","“We don’t need that many people there. The tribute formation appears dangerous, but it is flawed. It just looks intimidating until it finally activates. I’m telling Wang Qiang to tag along in case something happens. Rather, I need your help to channel the formation below,” Chu Feng said.","He formed a hand seal, and the formation cores glowed.","The crowd realized that the formation was not channeled using spirit power but bloodline power. That was the reason Chu Feng wanted them to stay behind.","“Young friends, take this warship. It’ll be faster.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief took out a glowing ship. It was a one-time-use treasure that could only transport several people at once, but it had formidable speed.","Wang Qiang and Bai Yunqing boarded the ship and whizzed out of the tombstone realm, toward the tribute formation.","The others, except for those recuperating, entered the formation cores.","“Let’s begin,” Chu Feng said.","As the crowd channeled the formation, the formation began to radiate bright light and luminosity.","Chu Feng sat down in a formation core while looking at the horizon with conflicted eyes. Beneath him was a formation plate inscribed with countless runes. All the formation’s energy was flowing toward the formation plate.","...","After traveling for some time, Bai Yunqing and Wang Qiang arrived at the tribute formation.","It was even more frightening here. Now that they were closer to the red light, the frequency of its flickering was much greater. Normal people wouldn’t have been able to withstand it.","But Bai Yunqing was unfazed. He took out the formation to activate it.","A black aura suddenly assaulted him. A palm smacked his nape, and he fainted.","It was Wang Qiang.","He looked at the collapsed Bai Yunqing and murmured, “I’m sorry, Brother Bai. This tribute formation mustn’t be undone.”","He turned his sight toward the formation Bai Yunqing held in his arms. He channeled his martial power over to destroy it, but the formation suddenly radiated a brilliant light.","Teleportation energy surged out, and a sitting individual emerged from it.","It was Chu Feng.","“Brother?” Wang Qiang was taken aback.","Chu Feng glanced at the fainted Bai Yunqing, looking unsurprised but helpless.","“Haa!” Chu Feng first sighed before rising to his feet. He descended over to Wang Qiang and stared sharply at him. “Why are you doing this?”","Wang Qiang was momentarily stunned before he snapped out of it. He first examined the formation Bai Yunqing had brought over. It was formidable, but it only contained teleportation energy.","How could a formation like that breach the tribute formation?","Then, Wang Qiang sighed bitterly.","“I see. This was merely a powerful teleportation formation. There’s no way it could have destroyed the tribute formation. You sent me here with Bai Yunqing because you knew I was related to the tribute formation. You knew I’d stop Bai Yunqing, and you did it on purpose.","“But how did you know?” Wang Qiang stopped stuttering and instead looked at Chu Feng with curious eyes.","Chu Feng still felt conflicted. Despite having guessed the truth, he still struggled to accept it.","“Why did you do it? What did you go through in the Immemorial Cemetery?” Chu Feng asked.","He was certain the person before him was still Wang Qiang, even though the latter was no longer stuttering. This made him think that something must have happened for him to resort to this.","Wang Qiang revealed the same despicable smile that Chu Feng was so familiar with. “You speak first, then I’ll tell you.”","“There’s one thing I didn’t say. Both the good path and the bad path revolve around the Seven Stars Orbs, so the person behind the tribute formation must have inherited one of the legacies. Brother, you entered the Immemorial Cemetery as soon as it appeared, earlier than any of us.","“Furthermore, you didn’t just inherit the Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor’s legacy. You teleported from somewhere else in the Immemorial Cemetery to where I was. This suggests that you have obtained another power.","“That was no ordinary warp portal. The aura and pressure it emanated can’t be fake. That black aura was the real deal, and you are in control of it. You must know what it is. You just chose not to speak about it.","“I didn’t probe into it as we all have our own secrets. I trusted you and overthrew my conjecture, though I maintained my skepticism. So, I continued observing you. I noticed you were very concerned about the Seven Stars Orbs and the tribute formation.","“But it is a matter of life and death, after all. That isn’t enough to prove my conjecture.","“As time passed, I began to wonder why the tribute formation hadn't formed, as if it were waiting for something or lacking a vital factor. Then, it struck me. It was awaiting the completion of the Seven Stars Orbs. Only when the Seven Stars Orb is completed can the tribute formation be formed.","“The tribute formation was activated as soon as the Seven Stars Orbs were completed. The person behind the tribute formation must have claimed the initiative and made preparations beforehand. The only one who had the time to do so is you.”","“I have always been confident in my judgment. This is the only time I wished I were wrong. But with so many lives on the line, I have no choice but to find a way to unravel the tribute formation. That’s why I set this up,” Chu Feng replied.","“Haa!” Wang Qiang sighed. “Brother, it’s such a headache to be your opponent.”","Chu Feng’s eyebrows shot up. “Are you admitting that you chose the dark path now?”","“Do I have any other choice?” Wang Qiang smiled."]},{"number":6457,"title":"Chapter 6457: Chapter 6455: Brother","paragraphs":["Chapter 6455: Brother","“Why did you do so? Is it for Heaven Gate?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s right,” Wang Qiang replied.","“Just for that, you stooped to become a malevolent cultivator and were willing to massacre so many people?” Chu Feng asked.","“I have my means to obtain Heaven Gate, but you also know that while Heaven Gate is a path leading into a place inside the Ninth Galaxy that is filled with fortuitous encounters, there is a difference in the fortuitous encounters there. I want the best fortuitous encounter there,” Wang Qiang said.","“You have changed.”","“People change. Sacrifices have to be made once you have confirmed your path.” Wang Qiang maintained an obstinate attitude. He didn’t think he was wrong.","Chu Feng was at a loss. Even if he won the argument against Wang Qiang, that didn’t mean Wang Qiang would listen to him, especially since Wang Qiang had already made up his mind.","Having a brother stand opposite him put him in a huge dilemma. He wished his brother could change his mind, but he didn’t know what he could do or say. He felt helpless.","“I agree with Song Yun. Our path has been fraught with difficulties, and there was no one around to help us. We had to pull through on our own. We don’t owe others anything, so why should we care about them?” Wang Qiang asked.","“That may be true for others, but what about the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion? What about your friends? Don’t you care about them?” Chu Feng asked.","Wang Qiang fell silent for a second before replying, “That’s why I said sacrifices are inevitable.”","Wang Qiang opened his palm, revealing a black aura.","The tribute formation began revolving rapidly, forming a terrifying hurricane around the two of them.","The black aura in Wang Qiang’s palm started out small, but it quickly expanded.","Chu Feng frowned. That was the same black aura Wang Qiang used for his warp portal, but it was stronger than he had expected.","“Chu Feng.”","Eggy frowned in unease. She sensed something eerie about the black aura. She wondered if Chu Feng could rival the current Wang Qiang even if he invoked bloodline rampage.","Pu!","Wang Qiang suddenly clenched his fist, and the black aura dissipated. It was not because he had lost control of the black aura but that he had chosen to dispel it on his own accord.","His breathing hastened. He looked at his clenched fist and murmured, “I was looking at you earlier. I wanted to know how you would view Song Yun after what she had done, if you would still view her as a friend. I wondered how you would view me once you know I was behind the tribute formation.”","Wang Qiang’s head was lowered. He dared not look at Chu Feng.","“Is it the Blood-devouring Demon Exalted?” Chu Feng asked.","Wang Qiang sneered, “Him? He’s beneath me.”","“Something must have happened in the Immemorial Cemetery then. You said you have chosen your path. What have you chosen? What did you encounter in the Immemorial Cemetery?” Chu Feng asked.","Wang Qiang didn’t reply.","Chu Feng continued his questioning. “Brother, you can tell me if you’re facing any troubles or difficulties. We can face them together.”","“It doesn’t matter.”","Wang Qiang finally raised his head to smile at Chu Feng, but the smile only made Chu Feng’s heart clench up. This was Chu Feng’s first time seeing such a smile on Wang Qiang’s face.","“You only need to know one thing, Chu Feng. You’ll always be my brother. With the tribute formation completed, the only way to unravel it is through my death. Do it.”","Wang Qiang opened his arms wide, ready to accept death.","Eggy was nervous. She would rather Chu Feng kill Wang Qiang as soon as possible, or else if Wang Qiang changed his mind, he could destroy them with the power he had displayed earlier. However, she also knew about the bond between Chu Feng and Wang Qiang","So, she held her tongue and waited for Chu Feng to make his own decision. She would accept the outcome no matter what happened. She would accept even dying alongside Chu Feng.","“Do it, brother. Now isn’t the time to get soft-hearted. There’s no way to be friends when our paths diverge,” Wang Qiang said.","Clang!","Chu Feng flicked his wrist and drew the Lightning Flame Sword.","Weng!","The runes on the Lightning Flame Sword emanated a brilliant light. With determined eyes, Chu Feng swung the sword down toward Wang Qiang.","Boom!","Space was torn apart. A gate appeared behind Wang Qiang.","It was Heaven Gate.","The stars inside the gate shone brighter than the others, and the natural energies seeping out from within were more concentrated than ever.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal, slid his fingers across the Lightning Flame Sword, and gathered its light in his palm. He pointed his finger at Wang Qiang, and the light surged into Wang Qiang’s body.","A suction force from Heaven Gate enveloped Wang Qiang, causing him to float upward.","“Brother, you...”","Wang Qiang stared at Chu Feng in disbelief. He couldn’t believe that Chu Feng had handed him the opportunity to enter Heaven Gate.","“The tribute formation will unravel once you leave the Immemorial Cemetery,” Chu Feng said.","“But that’s your fortuitous encounter! It’s the best Heaven Gate in the Seven Stars Orbs’ good path!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","“That’s not important. You just have to know that you’re my brother, no matter what happens,” Chu Feng replied.","He formed a hand seal, and Wang Qiang flew into Heaven Gate.","Heaven Gate closed, and a furious gust blew. The tribute formation encompassing the entire Immemorial Cemetery was collapsing.","“Chu Feng, why did you hand your Heaven Gate to Wang Qiang? He was planning to sacrifice all of you!”","Eggy was so annoyed that she even paused her recuperation. She had refrained from commenting earlier to let Chu Feng make his own decision, but she thought that he was being too self-sacrificial.","“He was planning to sacrifice people, but not me,” Chu Feng replied.","“How do you know?” Eggy asked.","“The tribute formation seeks to assimilate every living being in the Immemorial Cemetery. The only reason it hasn’t been activated yet is due to a flaw in it. The flaw was caused by the person who constructed it. Wang Qiang couldn’t harden his heart.","“He was probably trying to exclude some people from the tribute formation. I can’t say the same for the others, but I’m certain I am one of them,” Chu Feng said.","“How can you be so confident? People change,” Eggy said.","As soon as she asked that question, she realized her question was redundant. Wang Qiang wielded the power to kill Chu Feng, but he chose not to use it. Instead, he told Chu Feng to kill him. This showed his reluctance to cross blows with Chu Feng.","Wang Qiang truly cared about Chu Feng."]},{"number":6458,"title":"Chapter 6458: Chapter 6456: A Roar That Echoes Throughout the World of Cultivation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6456: A Roar That Echoes Throughout the World of Cultivation","“He could have used his power to hold me in place while he activates the tribute formation. There’s not a single person here who can stop him. But he didn’t do so. He’s reluctant to sacrifice so many people,” Chu Feng said with a sigh.","Meanwhile, in Heaven Gate, Wang Qiang sat with crossed legs as he was swiftly transported through a starry expanse of space. His destination was bound to be radiant.","But he couldn’t care less about that right now.","He held an unfurled black scroll in his grasp. It was made from his black aura, and it was slowly disintegrating, possibly due to the tribute formation’s collapse. Names could be seen written in the part that hadn’t disintegrated yet.","Most of them were from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, but Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, Bai Yunqing, the new king, and the others, except for Song Yun, had their names jotted on the scroll as well.","Even though the scroll was filled with names, there was an order to it. The name that was written first was Chu Feng.","This was the exclusion list for the tribute formation.","But Wang Qiang didn’t think the exclusion list was foolproof. Should he activate the tribute formation, many people in the list would still lose their lives. That was the reason he hesitated.","Padah padah...","Tears fell on the scroll. Snot as well.","Wang Qiang held the scroll in one hand while wiping his face with the other, but not only did he fail to wipe off his tears, he even got snot everywhere. He cried loudly. His body trembled like a child who had suffered a huge grievance.","“Y-y-you bastard, Chu Feng! Why do you treat me so well? Are you in love with me? Am I worth you sacrificing so much for? I’m even beginning to doubt my own sexual orientation. Damn it!” He hugged the scroll and shouted out loud. “Brother, I-I-I miss you!”","...","The tribute formation shrouding the Immemorial Cemetery dissipated.","At the same time, the energy sealing the Immemorial Cemetery also lifted, allowing people to freely travel in and out of its premises.","Chu Feng carried the unconscious Bai Yunqing back to where the crowd was. He didn’t speak the truth about the tribute formation; he only said that it had been unraveled. He also explained that Wang Qiang had grasped Heaven Gate as well and was headed to the Ninth Galaxy.","The crowd believed Chu Feng’s words—they had no reason since the crisis had finally been resolved. They were too busy celebrating to bother about where Wang Qiang went.","“Brother Xiancheng, I’ll return your Lord Jade Immortal to you.” Chu Feng handed the God Armament back to Ye Xiancheng. It was the Ye Immortal Clan’s hereditary treasure, after all.","He had borrowed this weapon back then because he realized that the Ye Immortal Clan’s Formless Spearmanship happened to curb that monster. He borrowed Jade Immortal because it could best draw out its prowess.","“Hehe. Lord Jade Immortal is too important to our clan, or else I’d have given it to you.” Ye Xiancheng took back Jade Immortal and carefully stowed it away. “Tell me the truth. Did you steal my hereditary martial skills back then?”","“It’s not stealing. It’s snatching,” Chu Feng corrected him.","“You’re a monster!” Ye Xiancheng was speechless. He had guessed as much, but he still thought that Chu Feng’s secret skill was too overpowered.","...","Meanwhile, deep inside the Immemorial Cemetery, Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan were sitting on a treasure, floating in space. They were still in a severely weakened state. They had exerted themselves too much that it would take them considerable time to recover.","They looked at the dissipating tribute formation and breathed a sigh of relief.","“It has been resolved?” Tianjian Qingyuan felt as confused as she was relieved.","“It’s Chu Feng,” Song Changsheng said affirmatively.","“Chu Feng did this?”","“No one else could have pulled it off. He has accomplished a lot despite his young age. You shouldn’t forget that he’s the one who acquired the Genesis Bloodline.”","“It makes sense when you put it that way.”","The Genesis Bloodline had existed since the Ancient Era, but none of the experts then had been able to obtain it. That was why it became a legendary power. Yet, Chu Feng managed to pull it off. That spoke volumes about his capability.","“The tribute formation has unraveled, but the power sealing the Ninth Galaxy persists. I still feel uneasy.”","Song Changsheng looked at the horizon. The energy sealing the Ninth Galaxy was still there.","Boom!","The world suddenly tremored.","Both Tianjian Qingyuan and Song Changsheng looked toward the end of the path, where a massive black gate stood. That was the black gate where the colossal being was sealed.","Another colossal being emerged from the black gate. It had the same physique, size, and power, but it emanated a different aura.","“Oh no.”","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan’s faces crumbled in despair. It finally dawned upon them why there were two identical beings inscribed on the black gate. There were two identical monsters sealed within the gate!","They had killed one of them, but there was another one lurking inside.","Neither of them had the strength to oppose this colossal being.","The colossal being looked at Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan with mocking eyes.","“I shall massacre every living being in the world of cultivation now. Can the two of you stop me?” the colossal being spoke with a deep voice that shook space.","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan finally understood why the Ninth Galaxy was still sealed. As long as this colossal being existed, everyone in the eight galaxies had nowhere to escape to.","And the two of them were powerless to stop the colossal being.","The world of cultivation was going to be destroyed.","Much to their surprise, the colossal being didn’t attack them. Instead, it rushed out to the outer areas of the Immemorial Cemetery.","“He’s going after Chu Feng!”","Tianjian Qingyuan was horrified. She picked up her sword and forced herself to her feet, wanting to stop the colossal being. But Song Changsheng grabbed her hand and stopped her.","“We have nothing to worry about if it’s going after Chu Feng,” Song Changsheng said.","Tianjian Qingyuan was confused.","In the meantime, the colossal being was already a far distance away from them. It was astonishingly fast despite its hulking stature that surpassed most realms in size. At this rate, it wouldn’t be long before it reached Chu Feng and the others.","Boom!","Tianjian Qingyuan narrowed her eyes.","A deafening roar suddenly shook the world. It was so loud that it could have been heard throughout the world of cultivation.","The colossal being quickly halted its footsteps, tearing open a massive spatial rift in its wake. A nine-colored lightning wall was blocking its path.","Taking a closer look, it wasn’t a wall but a sharp claw made out of nine-colored lightning.","The sharp claw belonged to a humongous lightning beast that was even larger than a starfield. Even the colossal being looked insignificant before this lightning beast. Upon meeting the eyes of the lightning beast, the colossal being trembled.","At the same time, a middle-aged man cultivating in the Ninth Galaxy suddenly opened his eyes. The coldness in his eyes was identical to that of the lightning beast."]},{"number":6459,"title":"Chapter 6459: Chapter 6457: Chu Feng’s Father","paragraphs":["Chapter 6457: Chu Feng’s Father","It was a roar transcending all beings. It echoed loudly throughout the entire world of cultivation.","Jie Tianran, who had been cultivating in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, opened his eyes. He looked uneasy.","“This voice?”","That roar had evoked his memory. He had heard a similar roar when Chu Feng invoked the protective formation that Chu Xuanyuan had left in him in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith.","Back then, most people thought an Ancient Era’s expert had awakened.","But this time, Jie Tianran heard it loud and clear. It gave off the same feeling as it did back then, suggesting that it was from the same entity.","“The Immemorial Cemetery? It isn’t a cultivator. Is it a monstrous beast?” Jie Tianran murmured.","That voice had come from the Ancestral Martial Galaxy back then, but now, it was coming from the Immemorial Cemetery. But both roars should have been from the same entity.","“This won’t be easy,” the voice inside Jie Tianran’s body said.","“Did I underestimate the Immemorial Cemetery?” Jie Tianran was unnerved.","“You need to make haste,” the voice reminded.","“All right. I’ll stop cultivating for the time being.”","Jie Tianran stood up, formed a hand seal, and released an aura that enveloped the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Upon sensing the aura, everyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s upper echelons, including the Saint-tier elders, rushed to assemble.","That was the Mansion Master’s summon, a tool that was only used when major events happened.","...","The crowd in the Immemorial Cemetery was also alarmed, and they looked toward the depths of the Immemorial Cemetery.","“Was that roar related to the Immemorial Cemetery?”","The joy on the faces of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and the others vanished, replaced by endless horror.","“Quick, we need to leave this place!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and the others brought their clansmen out of the Immemorial Cemetery. They sensed that the person who had just roared would take their lives despite the unraveling of the tribute formation.","In fact, the person who had just roared might even be more dangerous than the tribute formation.","...","Such horror swept across the world of cultivation.","That roar had only left them intrigued back then, but this time, it induced terror in them. The powers of the eight galaxies couldn’t tell if this entity was friendly or hostile, but the unknown usually spelled danger.","Naturally, the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Hidden Dragon Martial Sect was affected as well.","Deep in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, there was a formation realm filled with a dragon’s silhouette. It was the mastermind behind the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, Lord Long Xie.","Long Xie seemed to see what was happening inside the Immemorial Cemetery, and that allowed him to maintain his composure. Instead, he chuckled, “I see. Chu Feng’s father has hidden a hand here.”","...","Deep in the Immemorial Cemetery, the colossal being whose size spanned a realm and harnessed the power to easily destroy entire starfields revealed a look of fear. Its thick legs shivered, and the tentacles behind it wailed miserably.","It was like a puppy standing before an adult tiger. Fear arose from its very soul. It was bloodline suppression.","Bzt!","The lightning beast unleashed a bolt of lightning.","This single bolt of lightning morphed into a humongous lightning cage that trapped the colossal being in place. The colossal being tried to flee, only to realize there was nowhere to escape.","The lightning beast transformed into a surge of lightning before re-converging inside the cage, but this time, it took the form of a middle-aged man. The middle-aged man’s appearance could be clearly seen even though his body was manifested from lightning.","He had his back against the colossal being, his eyes gazing into the depths of the Immemorial Cemetery.","But the colossal being still dared not make a move against this insignificant human. On the contrary, its breathing hastened. It knew this middle-aged man was the true body of the lightning beast.","“Milord, I...” the colossal being carefully spoke up, hoping to resolve this situation diplomatically.","Bzt!","Before it could finish its words, the lightning cage suddenly unleashed powerful lightning that burned the colossal being into ashes in an instant. The colossal being was vanquished before it could even let out a yelp.","Tianjian Qingyuan’s eyes widened in shock.","Having fought the colossal being, she knew how sturdy its scales were. It was not an easy opponent to defeat. Yet, the middle-aged man defeated it with ease!","There was a vast gap in their strengths.","What the middle-aged man did next left Tianjian Qingyuan with goosebumps.","He took a step forward and appeared right above Tianjian Qingyuan and Song Changsheng.","Tianjian Qingyuan was so nervous that she couldn’t speak. As a prodigy of the Heavensword Sacred Palace in the Ancient Era, she had met many powerful experts. This middle-aged man’s aura was something she had only felt from top experts in the Ancient Era.","Song Changsheng was surprised as well, but there was a smile hanging on his lips.","“You couldn’t put down your son in the end,” Song Changsheng remarked.","He could tell at a glance who the middle-aged man was. That was a face he would never forget in his lifetime.","Chu Xuanyuan.","“He’s Chu Feng’s father?” Tianjian Qingyuan could guess based on Song Changsheng’s words.","Chu Xuanyuan glanced over, his eyes falling on Song Changsheng’s axe. “Woodcutter, you haven’t fixed your axe yet?”","Song Changsheng was irked. Chu Xuanyuan should have known better than anyone how his axe cracked. Song Changsheng grumbled, “It isn’t that easy.”","“Come to the Immemorial Domain of Gods. I’ll give you a better one,” Chu Xuanyuan replied.","“There’s no need for that.” Song Changsheng turned down the request. “You have grown a lot. I’m not a match for you anymore.”","“You also weren’t a match for me before I left,” Chu Xuanyuan pointed out.","Song Changsheng was so angry that he could pop a vein.","Chu Xuanyuan laughed. “My time is limited. Let’s catch up another day.”","He looked into the depths of the Immemorial Cemetery. He clenched his right fist, and the lightning cage dissipated into sparks that re-converged in his grasp, transforming into a lightning sword. And then he swung the lightning sword.","Boom!","Space was divided into two. There was a huge spatial rift containing a formation realm hidden in the fabric of space.","Song Changsheng and Tianjian Qingyuan were startled. Neither had known a formation realm was hidden there.","Weng!","A golden light shone from the spatial rift. A figure emerged.","“The later generations are getting increasingly scary.”","It was a man’s voice. It didn’t sound old, but it clearly didn’t belong to this era. It was the man who had proclaimed himself as emperor to Jie Mubai.","“You must be the mastermind here. I don’t know what you’re after, but this is enough. Let’s not disrupt this world’s balance,” Chu Xuanyuan said.","“Balance? Are you responsible for maintaining balance in the world of cultivation?” the man who proclaimed himself an emperor asked.","“I might not have the means to maintain balance in the entire world of cultivation, but I don’t intend to let the likes of you wreak havoc in these eight galaxies.”","“I’m surprised your clone is linked to your main body, but it doesn’t change the fact that your main body is trapped inside the Ninth Galaxy. The people of the Ninth Galaxy can’t return here. You don’t have the means to stop me.”","All the stars extending to the horizon suddenly emanated golden lights. The man who proclaimed himself an emperor influenced surrounding planets through his will, a testament of his overwhelming strength.","But Chu Xuanyuan was unfazed. “Why don’t you give it a try?”"]},{"number":6460,"title":"Chapter 6460: Chapter 6458: The Cemetery’s Disappearance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6458: The Cemetery’s Disappearance","Silence settled upon the endless space.","“Hahaha!”","The man who proclaimed himself an emperor laughed. His laughter shook the surroundings. The golden lights receded, and the world reverted to its original appearance.","“You want to fight this emperor? No rush. You’ll have a chance in the future, but not now.”","A brilliant, golden light manifested and revolved on the man’s hand.","At the same time, a humongous golden whirlwind enveloped the Immemorial Cemetery, distorting the stars and space.","Chu Xuanyuan didn’t make a move, knowing the other party had chosen to retreat. Instead, he turned to Song Changsheng and said, “You should come as soon as possible. Your Nine Souls Sacred Clan is in dire straits in the Immemorial Domain of Gods.”","With that, Chu Xuanyuan’s lightning body dissipated.","In the Ninth Galaxy, Chu Xuanyuan stood in the middle of a plain-looking palace.","“Why would an entity of that caliber remain in the eight galaxies? And why are there no historical records about the Immemorial Cemetery?”","Chu Xuanyuan was concerned about the recent developments.","...","A golden whirlwind swept through every nook and cranny of the Immemorial Cemetery, transporting everyone out to its entrance. Then, the Immemorial Cemetery vanished as if it had never been there.","Even the energy sealing off the Ninth Galaxy had dissipated. Everything reverted to normal.","Chu Feng and the others were still together, though they were concealed so that outsiders couldn’t see them. Their hearts were palpitating from what happened earlier.","“Damn. Was I dreaming?” Huangfu Zhantian murmured in a daze.","But it couldn’t have been a dream, especially since Chu Feng and the others still carried the legacy imprints, though the imprints were fusing into their bodies and disappearing.","“Miaomiao, you still used that power in the end?” a voice echoed.","Song Changsheng appeared before Chu Feng and the others. He easily found them even though they were concealed.","“Elder, you...”","Chu Feng and the others were shocked to see Song Changsheng’s state. While Song Changsheng didn’t sustain any injuries, he looked to be in a terrible state.","“I’m fine,” Song Changsheng replied.","“Elder, were you behind the sudden disappearance of the Immemorial Cemetery?” Chu Feng asked.","Even though he had completed the Seven Stars Orbs and lifted the tribute formation, he didn’t think the Immemorial Cemetery had disappeared because of him. The most likely suspect was Song Changsheng.","From Song Changsheng’s current state, it was apparent he had been doing something and had paid a price for it.","“It’s not me but you.” Song Changsheng smiled at Chu Feng.","“Me?” Chu Feng was surprised. The only possibility he could think of was that the Immemorial Cemetery had disappeared because they had cleared all of its trials.","“Don’t worry, I’m fine,” Song Changsheng replied before flitting to Xian Miaomiao’s side.","Xian Miaomiao was too focused on her recuperation to register what was happening around her.","“I’ll take Miaomiao with me. Is there anything you want to tell her? I can relay it to her,” Song Changsheng asked.","“Elder, I have a question I’d like to ask,” Chu Feng said.","Weng!","A white fog suddenly settled in. Everyone vanished except for Chu Feng, the meditating Xian Miaomiao, and Song Changsheng. It was Song Changsheng’s means.","“Shoot off,” Song Changsheng said.","“Elder, do you still remember this girl[1]?” Chu Feng was referring to the Three Saints Monstrous Clan’s sacred treasure, the Darkness Monstrous God’s soul.","Back then, a Netherworld Envoy had captured the girl together with Chu Feng and Song Yun, planning to bring the three of them to the Netherworld Sect. But Song Changsheng arrived and took the girl with him.","“I know she has ties with you, but I’m afraid she has gone missing,” Song Changsheng replied.","“Missing?” Chu Feng was surprised.","Song Changsheng had kept that girl by his side because he knew she was dangerous.","One day, the girl suddenly emanated a terrifying power, and before he could react, she had already vanished. He had been looking for her since, but he couldn’t find any clues.","Chu Feng didn’t think Song Changsheng would lie to him. He was a little disappointed, as he had thought he could finally bring the Darkness Monstrous God’s soul back to the Three Saints Monstrous Clan.","It wouldn’t be easy to find the girl if even someone like Song Changsheng had no idea where she went.","“Elder, I’m fine. I’m thankful to you for helping us,” Chu Feng said gratefully.","“You don’t have to thank me. You contributed the most here,” Song Changsheng said with a meaningful smile. “Is there anything you’d like to say to Miaomiao?”","“Please thank Miaomiao on my behalf. She protected us this time,” Chu Feng said.","“I’ll relay your words to her.” Song Changsheng smiled.","He turned around and vanished into thin air. The white fog dissipated, and the crowd returned.","From the crowd’s perspective, Chu Feng had disappeared with Song Changsheng and Xian Miaomiao, but only Chu Feng reappeared afterward. They didn’t probe into it, knowing that they must have had a private conversation.","Instead of leaving the area, Song Changsheng slipped into a hidden space, where Tianjian Qingyuan was sitting with crossed legs and recuperating. Her complexion looked much better than before.","“Are you here to bid me farewell?” Tianjian Qingyuan asked.","“Mm.” Song Changsheng nodded.","“That man was Chu Xuanyuan?”","“Mm.”","“No wonder you said no one in these eight galaxies can hurt Chu Feng.”","“He’s also the person I was talking about earlier.”","“The charismatic man who charms all ladies he meets?”","“That’s right.”","“He has a refined disposition.” Tianjian Qingyuan nodded. She thought about what Chu Xuanyuan had said to Song Changsheng and added, “But he has a venomous tongue.”","“He does.” Song Changsheng smiled.","“When do you plan to enter the Ninth Galaxy?”","“I’ll wait a while more. You?”","“I’ll head in right now. I’ll be waiting for you on the other side.”","“All right.” Song Changsheng nodded before leaving with Xian Miaomiao.","Now that she was alone, Tianjian Qingyuan stood up and looked at Chu Feng. Even though there was a vast distance between them, with a simple tap of her finger, Chu Feng suddenly appeared right in front of her.","Chu Feng was surprised. “Tianjian Qingyuan?”","Eggy tensed up. She stopped her recuperation and stood up.","Chu Feng had massacred everyone in the Heavensword Sacred Palace, a power Tianjian Qingyuan was affiliated with. She naturally assumed Tianjian Qingyuan had dragged Chu Feng here to avenge her descendants.","But what Tianjian Qingyuan said next surprised her.","“I’m sorry, Chu Feng.”","1. Chu Xuanyuan stole this girl from the Three Saints Monstrous Clan and brought her before Chu Feng, so that she would view Chu Feng as her master. It was revealed in Chapter 5904. ☜"]},{"number":6461,"title":"Chapter 6461: Chapter 6459: Tianjian Qingyuan’s Attitude","paragraphs":["Chapter 6459: Tianjian Qingyuan’s Attitude","“I couldn’t bring your grandmother back,” Tianjian Qingyuan revealed the reason for her apology. She continued, “Your grandmother has entered the Ninth Galaxy.”","“My grandmother has entered the Ninth Galaxy?” Chu Feng finally understood why he couldn’t sense his grandmother anymore.","Tianjian Qingyuan told Chu Feng what happened.","Chu Feng heaved a sigh of relief and was happy for his grandmother when he heard that she had entered the Ninth Galaxy via Heaven Gate. He had no means to treat his grandmother at the moment, whereas Heaven Gate contained many fortuitous encounters.","His grandmother might recover from one of those fortuitous encounters.","“Elder, you aren’t to be blamed for my grandmother’s plight, but there’s one thing I’m worried you might blame me for,” Chu Feng said.","“You’re the one who massacred this line of the Heavensword Sacred Palace, right?” Tianjin Qingyuan asked.","“Elder, you already know about it?” Chu Feng was surprised.","Eggy heaved a sigh of relief. Tianjian Qingyuan had known about the massacre beforehand, but she still apologized to Chu Feng about his grandmother and explained the matter. This hinted that she wasn’t angry about the massacre.","Someone of Tianjian Qingyuan’s strength had the privilege of not having to be reasonable; she could have done whatever she wanted without beating around the bush.","Despite knowing that, what TIanjian Qingyuan said still surprised Chu Feng and Eggy.","“You don’t need to feel apologetic, Chu Feng. I should be apologizing to you on behalf of our Heavensword Sacred Palace for what this line did to you.” Tianjian Qingyuan shockingly bowed to Chu Feng.","“Elder, you...” Chu Feng was someone who had weathered storms, but he was still surprised by Tianjian Qingyuan’s attitude.","Even if Tianjian Qingyuan generously chose not to blame him for the massacre, there was no need for her to turn around and apologize to him. That was being way too generous.","“In the Ancient Era, our Heavensword Sacred Palace expanded our influence and recruited more talents by establishing subsidiaries. These subsidiaries became our branches. We didn’t set stringent requirements for our recruitment—those who are talented enough can join us.","“Our initial goal was to nurture more outstanding cultivators while boosting our overall strength. We discovered that many talented individuals are limited by their weak bloodline, so we decided to set up trials for our branches. Prodigies who proved themselves in the trials are brought into the Heavensword Sacred Palace to receive our bloodline legacy.","“Prodigies who received our bloodline legacy shone even brighter afterward, so we went a step further and imparted our bloodline legacy to all branches. Anyone who joined our Heavensword Sacred Palace can receive our bloodline legacy.","“This allowed our Heavensword Sacred Palace to swiftly expand its influence and strength, but having too many people brought about new troubles. People with questionable characters began appearing in our ranks, but our Heavensword Sacred Palace, being a subsidiary of the Heavenly Sacred Temple, can never condone evildoers.","“So, we made a rule that evildoers will be expelled from the Heavensword Sacred Palace. Ha...”","Tianjian Qingyuan let out a sigh before continuing, “I don’t know what happened in the final years of the Ancient Era, but it must have been a huge crisis. That’s why when I discovered that there is still a surviving branch of our Heavensword Sacred Palace here, I took care of them.","“But the rules are the rules. Those who have done wrong ought to be punished. I would have done something even if you didn’t. I apologized to you because I didn’t want such black sheeps to leave you with a bad impression of our Heavensword Sacred Palace.","“Since a branch survived, our main line in the Ninth Galaxy should have survived as well. I suppose you will enter the Ninth Galaxy in due time, right? I don’t want you to be prejudiced against our Heavensword Sacred Palace when you meet them again.”","Tianjian Qingyuan revealed the reason behind his apology.","“To be honest, elder, I doubted the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s accomplishments in the Ancient Era when I saw them, but after meeting you, I can see why the Heavensword Sacred Palace was one of the strongest powers in the Ancient Era.” Chu Feng’s awe toward Tianjian Qingyuan deepened.","Stronger people tended to side with their own people and oppress the weak. It was rare to meet someone like Tianjian Qingyuan who sided with reason. That gave Chu Feng a good opinion of her.","“Elder, these are the treasures I collected by the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members. I’ll return them to you,” Chu Feng said as he handed a Cosmos Sack over with both hands.","“You can take them. Think of it as our compensation to you.” Tianjian Qingyuan rejected the Cosmos Sack.","“Thank you, elder.” Chu Feng stowed away the Cosmos Sack with a smile.","There were plenty of God Armaments, treasures, and cultivation resources that were highly beneficial to Chu Feng inside the Cosmos Sack. He was nowhere close to Heavenly God level yet, but he had to make his way there a step at a time.","Considering his bloodline’s huge appetite, each breakthrough would be more difficult than the previous.","He chatted a while more with Tianjian Qingyuan before the latter took her leave.","Chu Feng made his way back to Little Fishy and the others. He thanked the Zhao Immortal Clan, the Ye Immortal Clan, and the Huangfu Heavenly Clan for their help in the Immemorial Cemetery earlier.","“You’re being too courteous. We would have all died if not for you. We should be thanking you instead,” Huangfu Zhantian said.","“He’s right.”","Eighth Zhao and Ye Xiancheng’s parents agreed with that sentiment.","Ye Xiancheng’s parents had agreed to forge better relations with Chu Feng before their reunion, and their encounters at the Immemorial Cemetery affirmed their decision.","Chu Feng was bound to accomplish great things in the future, not to mention that his grandmother was formidable as well.","All banquets were bound to come to an end, especially now that they had escaped from the Immemorial Cemetery. After some pleasantries, the Zhao Immortal Clan and the Ye Immortal Clan took their leave.","Before leaving, they expressed their intent to enter the Ninth Galaxy soon and asked if Chu Feng would be heading there, too.","Chu Feng told them that he would head there in due time."]},{"number":6462,"title":"Chapter 6462: Chapter 6460: The Voice Deep in the Cemetery","paragraphs":["Chapter 6460: The Voice Deep in the Cemetery","The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master led his people up to Chu Feng.","“Young friend Chu Feng, is the Immemorial Cemetery truly just a trial? Do you feel anything unusual from the rune imprint?”","He had asked Yuwen Yanri about it, and the latter had told him that the rune imprint was now reflected on his soul instead of his skin. Yuwen Yanri had no idea what effects that rune imprint had, so out of concern, the Mansion Master decided to ask Chu Feng about it.","“It should just be a trial. I can’t discern the purpose of the rune imprint either, but it’ll likely be tough to erase,” Chu Feng said.","“See you at the Ninth Galaxy, Brother Chu Feng.” Yuwen Yanri bade Chu Feng farewell on behalf of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.","“Take care, Brother Yanri, elders,” Chu Feng replied with a bow.","Unlike the Zhao Immortal Clan and the Ye Immortal Clan, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion was planning to enter the Ninth Galaxy right away. It was unknown when or whether they would ever meet again.","The world was huge; not every separation was guaranteed a reunion.","The new king walked up to Chu Feng.","“Are you heading into the Ninth Galaxy, too?” Chu Feng asked.","“Are you not heading in?” the new king returned the question.","“I still have matters to attend to.”","“I’ll be going in ahead of you.”","“May we meet again.”","“May we meet again.”","The new king took his leave as well.","The only ones remaining were Chu Feng’s close friends.","“Yu’er, how are you feeling?” Chu Feng asked with concerned eyes.","Little Fishy might not have engaged Song Yun in battle, but the incredible power she emanated must have come at a price.","“I’m fine, big brother,” Little Fishy replied with a radiant smile. Moments later, she lowered her head in shame and said, “I’m sorry I wasn’t of any help to you.”","“You silly lass. When did you learn how to talk nonsense? You have helped me a lot. We wouldn’t have been able to complete the Seven Stars Orbs without your and Brother Shaoyu’s help. You’re forbidden from saying such words in the future,” Chu Feng consoled with a smile.","Chu Feng had watched Little Fishy grow up, so he doted on her more than his other friends.","“My little sister is right. While we did contribute to the Seven Stars Orbs, we were rewarded for that. However, we would have all been dead if not for you unraveling the tribute formation. We wouldn’t have been able to bring those rewards out,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","He then turned to Little Fishy and continued, “But little sister, I ought to criticize you for this. What’s the point of apologizing? If you feel indebted to Brother Chu Feng, you should marry him.”","Little Fishy’s face immediately reddened.","“What nonsense are you spouting?”","Feeling embarrassed and angry, Little Fishy smashed her fist into Xianhai Shaoyu’s chest, sending him flying a far distance away. She then turned her reddened face to Chu Feng and said in embarrassment, “Big brother, don’t listen to my brother’s nonsense.”","But then, Little Fishy’s grandfather suddenly interjected, “How is it nonsense? I think Shaoyu is right.”","“Grandfather, why are you playing along?” Little Fishy was speechless.","“Yu’er, I’ll make things clear here. The only person I recognize as my grandson-in-law is Chu Feng. I won’t die in peace if you don’t marry him,” Little Fishy’s grandfather said.","Little Fishy’s face reddened, but there was nothing she could do. She turned to her parents and said, “Father, mother, look at grandfather.”","“That’s your grandfather. I can’t do anything about it.” Little Fishy’s father shrugged.","Little Fishy’s mother secretly chucked by the side.","Xianhai Shaoyu, who had just flown back, asked, “Little sister, you shouldn’t forget that Brother Chu Feng is our Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s benefactor. We have no way of repaying what he has done for us except for you to marry him. If you aren’t willing, I’ll have to marry him on behalf of our Immortal Sea Fish Clan.”","Little Fishy whipped out her God Armament. “Brother, you’re getting more and more ridiculous!”","“Gah! Brother Chu Feng, save me! My little sister is jealous of me and wants to silence me!” Xianhai Shaoyu shouted as he fled.","Little Fishy gave chase.","No one stopped them. They were already accustomed to the siblings’ antics.","In Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space, Eggy remarked with a chuckle, “Chu Feng, I approve of your marriage with Yu’er.”","Chu Feng was rendered speechless. “Milady Queen, why are you playing along as well?”","“Chu Feng, Yu’er is a wonderful child. Aren’t you moved by her at all?","“In terms of talent, she is a match for you. Didn’t you notice how domineering her gaze was earlier? I reckon her trump card isn’t any weaker than your bloodline rampage. In terms of appearance, you are a far cry from Yu’er. It’s almost as if a swan has lowered itself to a toad,” Eggy said.","“Why are you attacking me? Am I that ugly?” Chu Feng was speechless.","“You’re not ugly. Yu’er is just too beautiful. You’re not much different from a toad compared to her,” Eggy replied with a laugh.","“Milady Queen, hurry up and continue recuperating.” Chu Feng could only change the topic.","Eggy did as she was told. She hadn’t recovered from her injuries yet.","“Big brother Chu Feng, where should we go next?” Bai Yunqing asked Chu Feng.","He had decided to follow Chu Feng wherever he went.","Chu Feng revealed his plans.","The Spirit God Clan was safe for now, but they were so severely weakened that they had fallen into hibernation. It would be extremely difficult for them to recover to their previous state.","Even Bai Yunqing, despite having inherited the Physician Immortal’s legacy, couldn’t do much to help them. Chu Feng was helpless as well.","So, Chu Feng wanted to bring the Spirit God Clan to the Spirit God to see if the latter could do anything to help them. He didn’t think it was a good idea to bring others before the Spirit God, so he told Bai Yunqing and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan to return to the Totem Dragon Clan and gather with the others.","The others did as they were told. Before parting ways, they exchanged contact information and told Chu Feng to contact them if he needed help.","Meanwhile, in the Immemorial Cemetery, there was another hidden realm in the space Chu Xuanyuan had previously breached. This space was nowhere as desolate as the rest of the Immemorial Cemetery.","In contrast, it was brilliant like the Ninth Galaxy.","“That arrogant little punk, Chu Xuanyuan! You should have let me teach him a lesson!” a resonant voice echoed throughout space. It was a masculine voice, but it harnessed boundless power as if it didn’t come from an entity but the world itself.","Another ancient voice echoed in the realm, but it sounded more domineering, “That’s the father of my successor. Try laying your hands on him.”","The masculine voice grumbled, “Why are you siding with outsiders?”","“Who cares? I won’t stand for it if you dare touch my successor’s father,” the domineering voice replied.","“Enough. What’s the point of arguing when the person has already left? You’ll have to enter the Ninth Galaxy if you wish to find him,” a woman’s voice sounded.","If Chu Feng were here, he would have found the woman’s voice familiar. It was the voice of the Spectral Fairy."]},{"number":6463,"title":"Chapter 6463: Chapter 6461: Jie Mubai’s Gains","paragraphs":["Chapter 6461: Jie Mubai’s Gains","Chu Feng was capable of swiftly traveling from one realm to another by using the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s teleportation formations, but he had to get to one of its teleportation formations first.","Fortunately, his traveling speed was faster than usual due to a sword. The sword was ten meters long and crackled with lightning when activated, thus its name—Surging Lightning.","Surging Lightning was not a weapon but a transport medium. It was a treasure from the Ancient Era acquired from the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s Palace Master’s Cosmos Sack.","There were other incredible treasures inside the Cosmos Sack as well, but there weren’t as many cultivation resources. They must have all gone to Tianjian Canhua. That said, there were still enough resources for him to advance a cultivation rank.","Chu Feng could have assimilated the cultivation resources right away, but he didn’t do so. His thoughts were still on the Immemorial Cemetery. Too many things had happened even though he had only been there for a short time.","“Were we lured into the Immemorial Cemetery just to inherit their legacies? But what was it that Wang Qiang went through? Why was there such a huge change in him?”","Wang Qiang had clearly stated that he would sacrifice everyone to the tribute formation to open the strongest Heaven Gate, but Chu Feng didn’t think he was the kind of person who would use the lives of the innocent as stepping stones.","Chu Feng believed that something must have happened to Wang Qiang in the Immemorial Cemetery.","“Could Wang Qiang have met the Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor? The latter doesn’t sound like a good person just from the name itself.”","Since he had met the Spectral Fairy, the masters of the other legacies could be around as well.","Yuwen Yanri’s legacy was from the Skyblaze Lord.","Bai Yunqing’s legacy was from the Profound Acupuncture Physician Saint.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s legacies were from the Sea Conqueror Saint Exalted.","Song Yun and the new king’s legacies were from the Demon Heavenly Exalted.","Xian Miaomiao’s legacy was from the Spectral Fairy.","Wang Qiang’s legacy was from the Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor.","Chu Feng’s legacy was from the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor.","Despite the Immemorial Cemetery’s massive size, Chu Feng had a feeling that their legacies were all extraordinary. There could be something more to the rune imprinted on their souls, just that he couldn’t see through it yet.","“Forget it.” Chu Feng gave up on making sense of the situation.","This experience had taught him something. Cultivators like them were similar to boats navigating a river. They could steer their boats wherever they wanted to when the water was calm, but when a storm hit, they would either be forced to go with the flow or capsize.","The Immemorial Cemetery was such a storm.","Such was the nature of the world of cultivation. Powerful individuals could dictate the fate of weaker ones. The only way to break free of those powerful individuals’ control was to either surpass them or at least obtain the power to rival them.","So, Chu Feng decided to stop thinking and focus on his cultivation.","...","Meanwhile, powerful voices continued to echo deep within the Immemorial Cemetery.","Other voices had joined the conversation, and they coincidentally corresponded to the number in the Seven Stars Orbs. Their conversation had moved on from Chu Xuanyuan to Jie Mubai.","“I don’t get why we’re supporting such trash. It’s a waste of time and resources,” the domineering voice said.","“Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor, are you worried that Jie Mubai will harm Chu Feng?’ the Spectral Fairy revealed the other party’s identity.","“I’m not worried about that. A trash like that can’t pose a threat to Chu Feng, even if you support him,” the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor replied.","“Aren’t you a generous one, Lightning Flame? The rest of us have only imparted our secret skills to our inheritors, but you gave him your personal weapon straight. But what’s the point of that when he’s incapable of controlling it?” another voice asked.","“You know shit. I have my plans,” the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor scoffed.","“Chu Feng is indeed the most talented of them all. I’d have chosen him if not for my legacy being more compatible with Xian Miaomiao,” the Spectral Fairy replied.","“Compatibility is more important. Chu Feng might be more talented now, but that might not be true in due time,” another voice said.","“Hmph...” The Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor harrumphed with a confident smile.","“Elders, can you quieten down for a while?” a voice echoed from a realm.","It was the man who proclaimed himself emperor.","Surprisingly, the space fell silent. The seven powerful entities held their tongues, and once they had fallen silent, their existence could no longer be perceived as if they weren’t there in the first place.","The man who proclaimed himself emperor was in a majestic palace suffused with formation energy. This palace bore a striking resemblance to an altar, and an unconscious Jie Mubai lay at its center.","Energy shaped like the humanoid creature Jie Mubai had previously summoned was flowing into his body. The humanoid creature might have become incorporeal, but it was now much larger and more imposing than before.","“Gather!” the man shouted.","The martial power formation intensified as the humanoid creature fully fused into Jie Mubai’s body.","Jie Mubai opened his eyes.","“I-I’m still alive?” Jie Mubai murmured fearfully.","He remembered being devoured by Song Yun’s summoned monster. He felt death closing in on him before passing out.","“It’s more than that. Feel your own body,” the man said.","Jie Mubai realized that the mysterious entity must have saved him. He did as he was told, and his eyes swiftly lit up in delight. In his view, the power he had obtained was more than enough to conquer the world of cultivation.","He would have absolute say even within the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Such power was worth pledging his soul away to someone else.","“Thank you, milord.” Jie Mubai hurriedly got up and kowtowed."]},{"number":6464,"title":"Chapter 6464: Chapter 6462: A Stronger Legacy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6462: A Stronger Legacy","“Milord, is there anything you need me to do?” Jie Mubai asked.","He was not so naive as to think that such great power was bestowed on him without a price, though he was still grateful to the other party for not only granting him power but also saving his life.","Weng!","The palace walls suddenly vanished, revealing an even larger palace. At the center of the palace was a legacy formation.","As a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, Jie Mubai sensed that the legacy formation contained power far stronger and viler than what was within his body. Someone else had already claimed the legacy, and it was not him.","“Milord, has someone else obtained your legacy?” Jie Mubai asked bitterly.","He thought the man who proclaimed himself emperor had high expectations of him, yet the other party had bestowed far greater power on someone else. Naturally, he felt tilted. He didn’t think anyone in the world of cultivation was more qualified than him.","“Don’t ask questions you shouldn’t ask,” the man who proclaimed himself emperor replied with unquestionable authority.","“I was too nosy.” Jie Mubai dared not probe despite his curiosity, knowing he was nothing before the man.","Shoosh!","A light suddenly appeared on the horizon of the palace. It slit open a spatial rift before manifesting into a peculiar gate reminiscent of a flight of stairs. It was a Heaven Gate.","“Go in,” the man said.","Jie Mubai instinctively understood the significance of Heaven Gate and knew this was a massive fortuitous encounter, but he hesitated. It hadn’t been easy for him to obtain such great power. He didn’t want to enter the Ninth Galaxy just like that.","There were many untapped fortuitous encounters in the eight galaxies.","So, Jie Mubai asked, “Milord, can I enter the Ninth Galaxy later?”","“I didn’t bestow you power just so you can flaunt it here,” the man replied. “I chose you because you possess some talent, but that’s all there is to it. The current world of cultivation is limiting your growth. You have to enter the Ninth Galaxy to overcome your limits.","“You have built up a strong foundation. Your spirit power will grow swiftly once you enter the Ninth Galaxy, but the sooner you enter, the faster you'll grow. Your job is to grow at all costs, so that you may become useful to me one day.”","“Milord, may I know what you intend me to do, so that I may make preparations beforehand?” Jie Mubai asked. He felt insecure, not knowing the man’s intention.","“I’ll look for you if you manage to grow to a satisfactory level. Otherwise, you won’t even qualify to serve me,” the man replied.","Jie Mubai felt uncomfortable. Even from a young age, he had been a celebrated prodigy in the world of cultivation. It was his first time being evaluated so lowly by someone. To think he would be unqualified to even serve someone.","This pricked his ego, but he dared not complain about it.","“Milord, I will not let you down. I’ll await your summons.”","Despite his reluctance, Jie Mubai bowed deeply before obediently entering the Heaven Gate. The Heaven Gate closed shortly after, and the two palaces reverted to normal.","A middle-aged man stepped out. He was incredibly dashing, with long black hair that naturally cascaded in place. He wore a simple white robe embroidered with golden threads, exuding an ethereal air of nobility.","He was a translucent soul entity—an incomplete soul, at that—yet even his simplest gestures moved the natural energies around him.","“Who says no prodigy can’t rise from commoners? This emperor has long said that there are talents among commoners with seemingly ordinary bloodlines, just that they lack the resources to bring out their potential. With sufficient resources, they can rise to the top as well. Look, aren’t there plenty of talented individuals in this era?” the middle-aged man spoke.","He was the man who proclaimed himself emperor.","“The Chu father and son are perfect examples. Not only is the father strong, but the son is even more incredible. He has obtained the legendary Genesis Bloodline and acquired a portion of Qin Jiu’s legacy. Even the Spirit God has temporarily lent him the Three Realms Divine Eyes. From the looks of it, he has won the acknowledgment of the Nine Realms Secret Domain.","“Chu Feng and Chu Xuanyuan. I look forward to seeing how far they can go in this era. It’ll make an unprecedented tale if both father and son reach the top of the world of cultivation.”","The man nodded in approval as he spoke about Chu Feng and Chu Xuanyuan.","He looked into the distance. His eyes peered across space to gaze upon the hidden base of the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s guild leader, where Zi Ling was in closed-door training.","“That lass’ treasure carries the Blood Emperor’s aura. That pulsating aura... The Blood Emperor is still alive. Does that mean you’re alive too, Qin Jiu?”","The man who proclaimed himself emperor frowned. It was hard to read his mind, whether he was feeling anticipation or worry."]},{"number":6465,"title":"Chapter 6465: Chapter 6463: The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s Main City","paragraphs":["Chapter 6463: The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s Main City","Chu Feng finally arrived at the Nine Heavens Secret Domain.","As soon as he stepped out of the teleportation passageway, he saw a veiled woman with three-colored pupils accompanied by a girl with twintails. They were the Spirit God and the Brush God.","“Lord Spirit God. Lord Brush God.” Chu Feng respectfully bowed to the two of them.","Neither of them was to be underestimated. Even the Brush God, who was the Spirit God’s subordinate, was a powerful entity far beyond his reach.","Chu Feng had come here to seek the Spirit God for help. He had been worried that the latter would refuse to meet him, so it was a relief to see her here.","“I have seen everything through the Three Realms Divine Eyes. I’ll inspect their conditions,” the Spirit God said.","Chu Feng hurriedly took out the hibernating Spirit God Clansmen from his spatial formation.","The Spirit God took out an ancient tower that was the size of a fingernail. The tower was beautiful as if it was made out of crystal. It consisted of nine levels, each harnessing different energies.","The Spirit God gently tossed it into the air, and the tower swiftly expanded. The hibernating Spirit God Clansmen were sucked into the tower.","The Spirit God formed a hand seal, and the lowest level of the tower emanated a divine light. The light ascended the tower as if an encroaching fog, and it only stopped upon reaching the eighth level.","“Woah, this line has incredibly pure bloodlines! But why is their cultivation so weak?” the innocent Brush God blurted out.","“Lord Brush God, do you know the background of the Spirit God Clan?” Chu Feng took this opportunity to ask.","The Brush God placed her hands on her hips and scoffed, “Stop pretending, you little brat! Didn’t you bring the Spirit God Clansmen here because you thought they were related to Lord Spirit God?”","“Ah...” Chu Feng scratched his head awkwardly at having been exposed. “Yes, that was what I was thinking. So... is it true?”","The Brush God looked at the Spirit God.","“There’s no need to keep this a secret from Chu Feng,” the Spirit God replied with a faint smile.","Only then did the Brush God reveal, “This line of Spirit God Clansmen is nothing compared to Lord Spirit God. How should I put this? They aren’t from the same clan, but they share the same bloodline.","“It’s similar to the case of your Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. You possess the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline, but that doesn’t mean you have blood relations with others who possess the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. Do you get what I’m saying?”","“Yes, I understand.” Chu Feng nodded.","“While there are many people with the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline out there, the Spirit God Bloodline is much rarer. You’re lucky to have earned their favor,” the Brush God said.","“I am indeed lucky. I am blessed to have been able to meet Lord Spirit God and Lord Brush God, ” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“That’s true.” The Brush God smirked in glee, only to frown seconds later. “You stinky Chu Feng. Why are you interrupting me? I was asking my master a question.”","The Brush God then turned to the Spirit God, curious to know the answer to her earlier question.","“This line has a restriction placed on it by its ancestor. Only when they find a master will their potential be released,” the Spirit God replied.","That explained the Spirit God Clansmen’s relative weakness despite their incredibly pure bloodline.","“I see. Chu Feng, you have struck gold,” the Brush God said.","“Chu Feng, do you want them to make a partial or full recovery?” the Spirit God asked.","“Lord Spirit God, I’d rather they make a full recovery if possible,” Chu Feng replied.","“You should be aware of their conditions. I’m impressed you were able to stabilize their conditions at all. I can restore their spirit powers to their previous levels, but their potential will be capped. However, there is another solution,” the Spirit God said.","“What do I have to do?” Chu Feng asked.","“While this line of Spirit God Clansmen has acknowledged you as their master, the master-servant contract has yet to be sealed. You can unlock their sealed potential by sealing the contract. Not only will they make a full recovery, but the speed of their cultivation will also rise to reflect their true talent.","“But it isn’t that easy to seal the contract. Your aptitude and willpower are top-notch, but your cultivation is still lacking. You have to at least reach Heavenly God or Heavenly Dragon, though Heavenly Dragon will be better,” the Spirit God said.","“How long can they last?” Chu Feng asked.","He was closer to reaching Heavenly God than Heavenly Dragon.","“I can sustain them for a while, but not too long. There should be a power known as the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect in this era that left behind some legacies. They might be beneficial to your growth,” the Spirit God said.","“Lord Spirit God, are you referring to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city?” Chu Feng asked.","The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect was the dominant world spiritist power in the earlier years of the present era. It was only when its experts left the world of cultivation for the Ninth Galaxy that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion finally rose to prominence.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had benefited greatly from the remnants left by the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, and there were even some remnants that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion struggled to decipher even to this day.","The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city was one of them.","After the Nine Heavens’ Zenith, the Ancient Era’s powers joined forces to attack the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, claiming it was hiding treasures. That forced the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect to employ their defensive formation to protect the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","In truth, the true goal of the Ancient Era’s powers was to use the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s defensive formation to force the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city to appear.[1]","They succeeded in forcing the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city to appear, but they failed to enter it.","Five key fragments had to be gathered to access the main city, and they were hidden in the Immortal Sea Galaxy, the Totem Galaxy, the Seven Realms Galaxy, the Divine Body Galaxy, and the Bloodline Galaxy.","Chu Feng had obtained two key fragments from the Immortal Sea Galaxy and the Totem Galaxy, but unfortunately, there was a rival competing with him over the key fragments—Jie Tianran.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had been maintaining a tight control over the Seven Realms Galaxy's and the Divine Body Galaxy’s remnants. A while back, he heard rumors that the two remnants had been deciphered. Jie Tianran should have obtained their key fragments.","The only one left was the Bloodline Galaxy’s key fragment.","Chu Feng had to pause his search for the key fragments, but he had been keeping an eye on this matter. He learned that the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant in the Bloodline Galaxy had suddenly disappeared, making it tougher to obtain the last key.","He figured that he wouldn’t be able to gather all five keys anyway, given that two of them had fallen into the hands of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, so he dropped it from his mind for the time being.","“Indeed.” The Spirit God nodded.","—","T/N:","Ancestral Martial Realm Sect > Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect (to properly reflect the meaning of the term)","1. Recap: The Ox-nosed Old Daoist was the one who reached out to all the Ancient Era’s powers to attack the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. His goal was to use their bloodlines as mediums to open the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, while eliminating everyone who threatens the Ancestral Martial Galaxy at the same time, before he enters the Ninth Galaxy. ☜"]},{"number":6466,"title":"Chapter 6466: Chapter 6464: Huge Surprise, Rank Eight True God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6464: Huge Surprise, Rank Eight True God","“Lord Spirit God, the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city can only be accessed after acquiring five keys,” Chu Feng said. “Unless there’s another way to enter it.”","“You cheeky lad.” The Spirit God saw through Chu Feng’s thoughts. “You’ll have to acquire the legacy with your own means.”","The Spirit God placed her finger on Chu Feng’s forehead. “I can lend you my Three Realms Divine Eyes for a while longer. If you can obtain the Bloodline Galaxy’s key fragment, you can try paying a visit to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. You might be able to open it with three key fragments. Otherwise, you’ll have to find another way out. I’ll offer you my support if you find other ways to swiftly advance your spirit power.”","The Spirit God retracted her finger.","Chu Feng’s Three Realms Divine Eyes’ energy had weakened considerably after his trip to the Immemorial Cemetery, but now, it had been restored to a high level.","“I’ll pay a visit to the Bloodline Galaxy,” Chu Feng said.","He had no idea what kind of legacy was in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, but it should be something considerable if even the Spirit God had mentioned it. He had to give it a try no matter what.","He had chosen to stay in the eight galaxies to claim the other legacies here, after all.","Thus, he stepped into the teleportation formation leading to the Bloodline Galaxy.","After Chu Feng left, the Spirit God made her way over to where the Monstrous God was.","She had seen everything Chu Feng saw in the Immemorial Cemetery via the Three Realms Divine Eyes, even after the place was sealed, so she went over to tell the Monstrous God about it.","“What do you think, Monstrous God?” the Spirit God asked.","“Are you referring to Chu Feng?” the Monstrous God asked.","“Chu Feng’s accomplishments thus far show that we have chosen the right person, but no, I’m talking about the Immemorial Cemetery.”","“The place is deeper than I thought. I wonder how many Immemorial Era’s figures are buried there. Those seven whose legacies are in the Seven Stars Orbs are all renowned figures in the Immemorial Era, but they didn’t appear in the Ancient Era. I thought they were dead. I would have never expected them to appear in this era,” the Monstrous God said.","“If the Spectral Fairy is alive, it should be the same for the other six, too.”","“I wonder how much strength they have retained. If they were at their peak strength, they could have influenced the trajectory of the current world of cultivation.”","“Yeah. None of them are pushovers, especially the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor and the Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor. Do you remember how their fight back then had obliterated a powerful starfield?”","The Spirit God recalled the past and frowned.","The starfield mentioned by the Monstrous God was at a completely different scale. The current eight galaxies were mere shells of their former selves, such that even an entire galaxy could be smaller than a slightly larger starfield in the Ninth Galaxy.","And the starfield in question was one of the biggest ones in the Immemorial Era. It could house all of the present eight galaxies.","In other words, if that battle had happened in the present day, it could have destroyed all eight galaxies.","“There’s no need to worry. That battle resulted in severe injuries for the Demonic Flame Dao Ancestor and the Lightning Flame Dao Ancestor. They disappeared after the battle, and many believed they had died.","“Come to think about it, it’s the same for the other five as well. They also sustained severe injuries before their disappearance. It’s already a miracle to survive from the Immemorial Era till now, even if one didn’t sustain any injuries. Even if they are alive, they must already be on their last leg. There’s no way they are as strong as they used to be.","“Rather, I’m more concerned about the mastermind behind the Immemorial Cemetery.”","The Monstrous God’s tone finally became grim.","“Monstrous God, you also think that there’s someone else behind the Immemorial Cemetery?” the Spirit God asked.","“My gut feeling says so. That person gathered the most talented prodigies in the world of cultivation. Is he truly looking for successors, or does he have other motives in mind?” the Monstrous God murmured.","“I inspected Chu Feng’s rune imprint earlier. I can tell it’s fused with his soul and can’t be removed, but I couldn’t gather anything else aside from that. That person is extremely strong,” the Spirit God said.","“Spirit God, do you reckon that person is from the Immemorial Era as well? There aren’t many people who tower over those seven in the Immemorial Era. Could it be someone we know?” the Monstrous God asked.","“Whether that person is from the Immemorial Era or the Ancient Era, he must be a person of incredible capability. It’ll be troublesome if it’s someone we know,” the Spirit God said.","“Indeed... Haa, forget it. It has nothing to do with us. We can’t do anything about it anyway,” the Monstrous God said.","They ended the conversation there, but the Spirit God’s beautiful Three Realms Divine Eyes continued to look troubled.","...","Chu Feng made his way to the Bloodline Galaxy, where the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant was recorded to be. However, the remnant had already transformed into a mountain valley.","“It looks like someone has moved the remnant away instead,” Eggy remarked.","“Are you fine now, Eggy?”","Chu Feng hurriedly projected his consciousness into his World Spirit Space. Eggy’s voice sounded fine, and her complexion had been restored to a healthy glow.","“I’m more than just fine,” Eggy replied as she released her aura.","“Rank eight True God level?” Chu Feng exclaimed in delight.","That meant that Eggy was only two ranks away from reaching Heavenly God level! Given her strength, if she could advance to Heavenly God level, Chu Feng wouldn’t have to fear anyone in these eight galaxies anymore.","“The Heavensword Sacred Palace is truly something. I underestimated their origin energies. I thought they would barely be enough for me to recuperate from my injuries, but my cultivation grew by leaps and bounds. If I had used them solely for my cultivation, I might have reached Heavenly God level by now,” Eggy remarked."]},{"number":6467,"title":"Chapter 6467: Chapter 6465: The Netherworld Sect is Behind It?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6465: The Netherworld Sect is Behind It?","“Heavenly God level?”","The origin energies of the Heavensword Sacred Palace’s members must have been much stronger than those of normal cultivators.","“I can see why they conceal poison in their origin energies now. They are an incredible nourishment for world spirits,” Eggy said. She was delighted to have both recovered from her injuries and advanced her cultivation.","This was a massive surprise.","“Since that’s the case, we should specifically look for people from the Heavensword Sacred Palace after we enter the Ninth Galaxy. If they turn out to be scoundrels, we’ll slay them and offer them up to Milady Queen,” Chu Feng said.","“Sounds great to me.” Eggy’s eyes glowed in excitement. “Tianjian Canhua mentioned that the Heavenly Sacred Temple has 36 subordinate sacred palaces, and more than a dozen of them survived into the Ancient Era. The origin energies from the other sacred palaces could also be highly nourishing. Don’t spare any of them. They shall all become my nourishment!”","Like Chu Feng, she needed far more resources than usual to advance her cultivation. This was her first time tasting such potent origin energies, and she was very fond of it.","“Definitely! We shall target those affiliated with the Heavenly Sacred Temple once we enter the Ninth Galaxy,” Chu Feng said.","“Wonderful!” Eggy was overjoyed, but her face soon turned grim. “Hold on, Chu Feng. Why didn’t you make a breakthrough? Didn’t the Heavensword Sacred Palace leave some cultivation resources behind? Are they insufficient?”","“I need a bit more to reach rank seven True God level, but it isn’t a problem. I should be able to make a breakthrough if I just cultivate a bit more. My priority is to reach Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist first, though,” Chu Feng said.","“I know. I overheard your conversation with the Spirit God. You should scan the area with your Three Realms Divine Eyes and look for clues. Let’s quickly find the remnant and obtain the key fragment,” Eggy said.","“Mm.” Chu Feng pulled his consciousness back to his body and observed the surroundings.","He first tried his Heaven's Eyes and managed to find some clues—there were traces of the Netherworld Sect’s aura, even though they had attempted to erase them.","He formed a hand seal and activated the Three Realms Divine Eyes. The traces became much more conspicuous.","“It’s the Netherworld Sect,” Chu Feng said.","“The Netherworld Sect? Why would they be interested in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant?” Eggy asked.","That was also what Chu Feng was curious about. The Netherworld Sect was filled with cultivators; they shouldn’t have any interest in a world spiritist remnant.","“Hm?”","Chu Feng suddenly cast his gaze into the distance.","A carriage was making its way over. It was a simple carriage carrying a huge wooden bucket, driven by a young man. The young man had a dark skin tone and had a radiant smile, looking like the type who was passionate about life.","“Chu Feng, is there something special about that brat?”","Eggy didn’t understand why Chu Feng was paying attention to the young man.","The young man had an ordinary face and a weak cultivation. His background was likely not noteworthy, considering he was driving a carriage despite living in an Upper Realm, where better forms of transport were available.","The horse was not a mortal horse, but it was only used by poorer people.","“He carries the Netherworld Sect’s aura inside him,” Chu Feng replied.","“Oh? Does he have a Netherworld Embryo planted in him?” Eggy asked.","“I don’t know, but it doesn’t feel like a Netherworld Embryo. Something is unnerving about his aura.” Chu Feng shook his head as he continued observing the young man.","Few people visited this area as the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnants were famous for being dangerous. Even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had lost plenty of people to them, let alone others.","But since the disappearance of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant, the area grew safer and more peaceful. Curious people began visiting this place to check it out. As a result, the sides of the valley were filled with people.","It had become a must-visit scenic spot for cultivators passing by the area.","The young man drove his carriage to the crowd and took out a flag that read ’ Home-brewed flower tea. Feel free to have a drink. ’ He shouted, “Have a taste of my home-brewed flower tea. It’s sweet, fragrant, and delectable. It’s guaranteed to perk you up right away. It’s beneficial to cultivators and world spiritists alike, and it’s free. Have a taste!”","Many scoffed upon hearing his words. He was too weak for anyone to believe those words.","“Since he carries the Netherworld Sect’s aura, could the flower tea be spiked? The Netherworld Sect might have sent him here to poison others,” Eggy asked.","“Let me take a look.”","Chu Feng dispelled his concealment and disguised himself as a youth. He walked up to the young man and asked, “Is it free?”","“Yes, it’s free. Would you like to have a taste?”","The young man lifted the wooden bucket’s lid and scooped out a bowl of flower tea.","Chu Feng took a sip and was surprised. The young man might have lied about the flower tea being beneficial to one’s cultivation, but the rest was all true.","“It’s good,” Chu Feng replied.","“Have more if you like it.” The young man was delighted to receive Chu Feng’s compliment.","“Is it that good? Let me have a taste, too,” Eggy said.","“May I have two bowls?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course. Give me a moment.”","The young man grabbed another bowl and filled it up before topping up Chu Feng’s bowl.","Chu Feng took the flower tea. A mini spirit formation gate appeared next to him.","“Woah, you’re a world spiritist?” The young man recognized the spirit formation gate.","Eggy was so eager to try the flower tea that she couldn’t wait for Chu Feng. She reached out and grabbed the bowl herself.","“It’s a female world spirit! How fragrant. She must be a beautiful lady,” the young man said.","Eggy took a sip of the flower tea, and her face lit up in delight. “Waa, it’s a flavor I love! It must have been made traditionally.”","Chu Feng asked, “Oh? What do you mean?”","“I can taste the breath of life,” Eggy replied.","“I’ll make it for you if you like,” Chu Feng replied.","“Out of spirit power?”","“Of course not. Don’t you prefer it to have the breath of life?”","“So you say, but you haven’t even made the buns you promised me yet.”","Eggy pouted before taking another gulp of the flower tea. Her smile deepened as her eyes curled in pleasure. She looked incredibly cute."]},{"number":6468,"title":"Chapter 6468: Chapter 6466: Kindness Begets Kindness","paragraphs":["Chapter 6466: Kindness Begets Kindness","So, Chu Feng turned to the young man and asked, “Can you sell your flower tea recipe to me?”","“Do you like it that much? You don’t have to buy it; I’ll give you the recipe. It’s a simple recipe, but it’s time-consuming, and you have to use our family’s tea leaves and flowers. I’ve brought the tea leaves, but you have to plant the flowers yourself, and I didn’t bring the seeds with me.","“If you aren’t in a rush, please wait for a while. I’ll be giving out flower tea here for the next six hours. Once I’m done, I’ll return home to take some seeds for you.”","The young man was very friendly.","“All right.” Chu Feng nodded.","He didn’t have any clues at hand anyway, and this young man could be a lead.","“How do I address you?” the young man asked.","“I am Chu Feng.”","“Chu Feng? This name sounds familiar. I’ll call you big brother Chu then!”","“What’s your name?”","“I am Huang Canlan. My mother gave me this name because she hoped I’d be as radiant as the sun. I have an older brother named Huang Yunxiao. My mother hoped he could rise above the clouds in his martial cultivation.” The young man gestured with his arms as he spoke, displaying incredible liveliness.","“Big brother Chu, I remember it now! You share the same name as Lord Chu Feng, the grandson of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, as well as the world of cultivation’s number one prodigy!”","The young man suddenly leaned closer to Chu Feng and whispered, “Do you know how the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant disappeared?”","“How?” Chu Feng asked.","“I heard it was stolen by Lord Chu Feng.”","“Where did you hear that from?”","Chu Feng was rendered speechless, but he wasn’t surprised. There were bound to be wild theories about the disappearance of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect.","“I heard from an old man. He said he witnessed it with his own eyes.”","“You believe him?”","“I was skeptical at first, but it sounds plausible. That’s the guy who conquered the Genesis Bloodline and doesn’t fear the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. There’s nothing he’s incapable of. As a world spiritist, he must covet the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy, right?","“I heard Chu Feng claimed the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant in the Totem Galaxy right under the watch of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They all say Lord Jie Ranqing is incredible, but I think Lord Chu Feng is even more incredible.","“Lord Jie Ranqing was protected by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion back then, but Lord Chu Feng is going up against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Ancient Era’s races without any backing. How cool is that?” the young man spoke with glowing eyes.","His praises put Chu Feng in a good mood. He asked, “You seem to be very fond of Chu Feng?”","“Yes, I like him a lot. This world is full of lies and betrayals. Brothers turn against each other due to greed, and being betrayed by friends is commonplace. But Lord Chu Feng braves danger to protect his friends. He’s a beacon of hope in this world. I don’t think there’s anyone who doesn’t like Lord Chu Feng other than the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Ancient Era’s races.","“But such figures are too distant to people like us. That’s why I like Lord Shi Mo more.”","“Who’s Lord Shi Mo?”","Chu Feng quickly learned that Shi Mo was a cultivator from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion. He was a prodigy, having reached rank three True God level despite being only centuries old. Given his rate of cultivation, he could reach pinnacle True God level in the next few millennia.","That would put him in the upper echelons of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.","It was by coincidence that the young man became acquainted with Shi Mo. The latter was extremely friendly and would often visit them. The young man viewed his encounter with Shi Mo as heaven’s blessing and idolized him a lot.","It felt like the young man had an endless stream of words to say.","Six hours swiftly passed.","Within this time frame, there was not a second person who stepped forward to try Huang Canlan’s flower tea despite it being free.","Chu Feng understood why.","It was normal for people to be skeptical about things that were offered for free, so they judged the goods by the person giving those things out. The crowd gathered here looked down on the young man, and by extension, the flower tea he was giving out as well.","They felt that drinking the young man’s tea would sully their palate.","“Let’s go, big brother Chu.”","But the young man wasn’t disheartened. He beckoned Chu Feng to board his carriage. He appeared to have expected such a situation.","“Why are you giving out flower tea here?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s a long story. Big brother Chu Feng, are you curious to know?”","“I am.”","So, the young man shared his story.","While the young man might not look like much now, he was born in an affluent clan.","His clansmen weren’t talented in martial cultivation, and they had only amassed their wealth because their ancestor had once helped a downtrodden cultivator. The cultivator later made it big and came back to return the favor.","That fortune became the foundation for their clan to begin cultivating.","Their clan motto preached doing good things, for kindness begets kindness.","“So, has your kindness beget kindness yet?” Chu Feng asked, knowing the young man wasn’t doing well.","“Haa! My clan was mired in internal strife. My grandfather was even expelled due to a power struggle within the clan. But it turned out to be a blessing in disguise. Our clan was massacred shortly after.","“Even though my grandfather was kicked out of the clan, he had some savings and was able to live a fairly comfortable life.","“But shortly after my father was born, my grandfather came across a severely injured cultivator. When he learned that the cultivator was betrayed and assaulted by his lover and trusted martial brothers, my grandfather depleted our family fortune to purchase medicine for his treatment.","“Before that cultivator left, he handed my grandfather a token, saying he would return to properly relay his gratitude to my grandfather if he succeeded in his vengeance. But that cultivator never returned, presumably because he failed in his vengeance.","“Even so, my grandfather believes that he has done the right thing. He still tells us to do good things and that kindness begets kindness. We have been struggling since my father’s generation, but we followed my grandfather’s teaching and continued to do good. That’s not much I can do. I thought since we live nearby, and there are many people here, I should let them try my ancestral flower tea for free,” the young man said."]},{"number":6469,"title":"Chapter 6469: Chapter 6467: Lord Shi Mo","paragraphs":["Chapter 6467: Lord Shi Mo","“It’s not your first time giving out flower tea, right? Is it the same every time?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, such a situation is normal. Most of the visitors are foreign cultivators of a certain stature and strength. They have seen the world and eaten all kinds of delicacies. I understand why they might not like my family’s flower tea,” Huang Canlan replied.","“Then why do you still insist on giving out your flower tea?” Chu Feng asked.","“From time to time, I’d meet people who relish in my flower tea like big brother Chu Feng. That gives meaning to what I’m doing.”","“So, you’re doing this not because of your grandfather’s teaching but because you enjoy it?”","“You can say so. I lack the talent to become a powerful cultivator, but just doing things like this brings meaning to my life.”","Chu Feng revealed a rare smile. It was rare to meet people who could retain their kindness even after experiencing the cruelty of the world.","“What would you do if you became a powerful cultivator?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’ll develop a flower tea that’s truly beneficial to cultivators before giving it out,” Huang Canlan replied.","“I imagine that would be all snapped up in a heartbeat.”","“I’d love that.” The young man chuckled. “But I doubt that day will ever come. I’m aware of my limitations. I don’t have the ability to pull that off.”","Chu Feng asked, “Do you really believe kindness begets kindness?”","“I do. My whole family believes in that. And our kindness did pay off. We met Lord Shi Mo.”","“Where’s your home? Point it out for me.”","“It’s there.” The young man pointed in a direction.","Chu Feng looked over. His gaze peered through everything that stood in its way before finally falling upon a city. It was a small city with a dense population. Every household buzzed with life.","He quickly found a house in the city’s outer perimeter that looked like Huang Canlan’s house.","It was a shabby house with a simple courtyard.","A middle-aged man and an old man lay inside the house. The old man was over a thousand years old, but he was extremely aged due to his low cultivation. His body was emaciated, and his physical functions had all deteriorated. He was bedridden and could die at any moment.","The middle-aged man was ill as well, but one could still see the resemblance between him and Huang Canlan.","There was also a woman in the house, presumably the young man’s mother. She was taking care of those two.","A young man who appeared to be in his twenties was training in the courtyard. He was practising a martial skill, but he was lacking in aptitude. Chu Feng could grasp the martial skill at a single glance, but the young man, despite repeating the motions, couldn’t grasp its crux.","“The problem doesn’t lie with them but external factors,” Chu Feng suddenly said to Eggy.","“What do you mean?” Eggy knew Chu Feng must have realized something.","Everyone in the city was afflicted with the Netherworld Sect’s aura, and there were decently talented children in the city.","“Is the Netherworld Sect raising them as livestock?” Eggy asked.","It was common for malevolent cultivators to use other humans as cultivation resources. Even though the Netherworld Sect proclaimed itself as an orthodox sect, most people viewed it as the vilest sect in the world of cultivation.","In the first place, it was immoral to plant Netherworld Embryos into others without their consent. No one would be surprised if they used other humans as cultivation resources, too.","“It’s possible,” Chu Feng replied.","“Are you going to help them?” Eggy asked.","“It’s one thing if I didn’t see it, but I can’t turn a blind eye to it now that I know about it.”","“Mm.”","Eggy knew Chu Feng better than anyone else in the world. Even though Chu Feng often said his goal of cultivating was to protect his friends and family, she knew that he held justice in his heart as well. He frowned on the strong oppressing the weak.","The carriage moved extremely slowly, so Chu Feng tampered with it to significantly raise its speed. It didn’t take long for them to arrive in the city.","“The road seems oddly short today,” the young man exclaimed.","Chu Feng’s means were so advanced that the young man failed to notice anything amiss, except for the shorter travel duration. The young man’s house was indeed the one Chu Feng had spotted earlier.","“Grandfather, father, mother, big brother, I have brought a guest back,” the young man shouted excitedly even before stepping into the house.","“There’s a guest? Welcome!”","The young man’s big brother was the first to come out, followed by his mother supporting his father. Even the bedridden grandfather also grinned, revealing the few teeth he had remaining. They were a warm-hearted household.","Upon learning that Chu Feng was fond of their family’s flower tea, the grandfather was so delighted that he insisted on chatting with Chu Feng. So, Chu Feng entered the house, sat down with the family, and began conversing.","The grandfather naturally shared how he had bankrupted himself trying to treat a powerful cultivator so that he could exact vengeance on his enemies. Despite knowing that the cultivator had likely failed in his vengeance and died, he displayed only sorrow and not regret.","In the meantime, Chu Feng obtained the flower tea’s recipe, their flower tea’s seeds, and their tea leaves. However, he had another goal here aside from the flower tea’s recipe.","“Have you heard of the Netherworld Sect?” Chu Feng suddenly asked.","The atmosphere immediately changed.","“The Netherworld Sect? Of course we do. That’s the vilest power in the world of cultivation!” the young man said.","“They deserve to die!” the young man’s big brother added.","Chu Feng asked if they had seen any Netherworld Sectmembers in the area, but they didn’t. This was perplexing. Everyone in this city carried the same aura, hinting that all of them had encountered something similar. He had checked the common drinking water and food, but there was nothing wrong with those.","After probing deeper, Chu Feng learned that Lord Shi Mo visited this place thrice each year, and he would distribute pills to every household each time.","That gave Chu Feng a good idea as to what was going on.","“Looks like Shi Mo is behind this. Is he a Netherworld Sectmember pretending to be from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion?” Eggy asked.","“It’s also possible that he’s a spy the Netherworld Sect had planted in the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6470,"title":"Chapter 6470: Chapter 6468: Chu Feng’s Fanboy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6468: Chu Feng’s Fanboy","“Do you know when Lord Shi Mo will visit this city again?” Chu Feng asked.","“Lord Shi Mo is coming tomorrow. Everyone returned to the city ahead of time for that. Lord Shi Mo has to channel the pills in person to maximize their effectiveness,” the young man replied.","That explained why the city was bustling with life. They were awaiting Shi Mo’s arrival.","I can afford to wait if it’s tomorrow, Chu Feng thought. He wouldn’t have waited if Shi Mo wouldn’t come by any time soon. He would have just outright told them Shi Mo was not a good person, removed the aura inside their bodies, and instructed them to leave the place.","But since Shi Mo was coming by, he could eliminate the problem at its roots and gather information from him. If Shi Mo was as strong as the young man described, he should be of considerable standing in the Netherworld Sect and would be privy to some secrets.","“What’s the name of this young hero?” the young man’s father asked.","“He’s Chu Feng,” the young man replied.","“Chu Feng? You are Chu Feng? Is it this ‘Chu (楚)’ and this ‘Feng (枫)’?” The young man’s big brother wrote down Chu Feng’s name on the table with tea.","“Indeed,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s not a good name. You should switch to another one.” The young man’s big brother suddenly didn’t look as friendly anymore.","“Why isn’t it a good name?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s the same name as Lord Jie Ranqing’s son, young hero Chu Feng.”","“Can’t I have the same name as Chu Feng?”","“Forget it. It’s fine.” The young man’s big brother stood up, walked out to the courtyard, and continued practising his martial skills.","“Big brother Chu, don’t mind him. My big brother admires talented prodigies. He has looked up to Lord Jie Ranqing from a young age, listening to every tale about her. Later on, his admiration shifted to Chu Feng. He has gotten into fights with others over Chu Feng, sometimes getting beaten up badly,” the young man explained softly.","“Hoh, he’s your fanboy.” Eggy laughed.","“Yunxiao can be a bit obstinate at times. Don’t mind him,” the mother explained.","“It’s fine. It’s not anything much.” Chu Feng smiled before he stood up and walked outside.","“You’re practising a fist martial skill?” Chu Feng asked the young man’s big brother.","“Aren’t you a world spiritist? Do you understand martial cultivation, too?” The young man’s big brother stopped his training and looked at Chu Feng.","“Actually, I’m more well-versed in martial cultivation,” Chu Feng replied.","“Really? Can you offer me some pointers?” The young man’s big brother was overjoyed.","Even the young man ran out of the house to join the commotion.","“Are you struggling to draw out the full prowess of your martial skill despite your precise movements?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, that’s the problem I’m facing.” The young man’s big brother nodded vehemently.","“You aren’t channeling your force correctly. The form is right, but you failed to grasp the crux. You won’t make any progress if you continue raining like that,” Chu Feng replied.","“Can you take a look and let me know what I’m lacking?” The young man’s big brother took out a scroll detailing the martial skill he was practising.","But Chu Feng didn’t bother glancing at the scroll. He could come up with hundreds of such low-tier martial skills at the snap of his finger.","“Let me teach you another martial skill.”","Chu Feng designed another martial skill on the spot. It was more compatible with the young man’s big brother in terms of his cultivation and his tendencies. With Chu Feng’s guidance, it took only an hour for the young man’s big brother to grasp it.","His comprehension ability frustrates me. I guess I’m not suited for teaching, Chu Feng thought with a sigh.","Someone more talented would have grasped the martial skill with just a single demonstration or a verbal explanation from him, but it took the young man’s big brother an hour. That was a long time for Chu Feng, though for the young man’s family, it was ridiculously fast.","“My gosh! Milord, who are you? How is your martial skill so easy to grasp? It’s even stronger than the fist martial skill I was practising earlier!” The young man’s big brother was thrilled.","“Big brother Chu, teach me as well! Do you have any martial skills that are suited for me?” the young man walked over and said.","“You dumbos. Are you still calling him big brother?” the young man’s mother remarked.","The young man and his big brother might not be talented, but they weren’t dumb. They immediately understood what their mother was driving at and dropped to their knees.","“Master, please accept a kowtow from us!”","The young man’s father berated with a frown, “A master for a day, a father for life. Why are you calling him master? Call him father!”","“...”","The young man and his big brother were dumbfounded.","“Don’t. We’re friends. I can guide you on your martial cultivation, but I can’t take you as my disciples. I don’t have the time,” Chu Feng said as he supported the two brothers to their feet.","The family was extremely polite. They didn’t heap pressure on Chu Feng upon seeing that he wasn’t willing to become their master.","“Please offer me some pointers, big brother Chu Feng,” the young man said.","“Of course.” Chu Feng nodded.","Even if this clue led to a dead end, Chu Feng still had to repay the favor for the flower tea.","“Hm?” Chu Feng suddenly cast his gaze into the distance.","Two individuals dressed in the clothes of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion were swiftly making their way over from the far distance.","One was a middle-aged man who commanded an air of righteousness, whereas the other was an old man. He was a rank three True God level cultivator.","The other was an old man. Somehow, he looked like a scamp despite being dressed in the clothes of an orthodox sect. He was a rank eight True God level cultivator.","The middle-aged man’s features fit the young man’s description of Shi Mo.","“That Shi Mo has arrived in advance?” Eggy asked.","“Mmhm, but it looks like he’s here to reel in the net,” Chu Feng replied.","“That seems to be the case.” Eggy nodded in agreement.","From the duo’s vicious expressions, one could tell they were up to no good.","“Prepare yourself,” Chu Feng told the young man.","“Big brother, are you going to teach me a martial skill?” The young man was enthused.","“Shi Mo is coming,” Chu Feng replied.","“Lord Shi Mo? How do you know?”","The young man’s family was confused.","Weng!","A ray of golden light reminiscent of a comet emerged from the distant horizon, lighting up the night sky.","“Waa, it really is Lord Shi Mo! He has come in advance!” The young man’s family was excited.","That golden light heralded Shi Mo’s arrival. Naturally, the city buzzed to life."]},{"number":6471,"title":"Chapter 6471: Chapter 6469: I’m the One Behind It. What About It?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6469: I’m the One Behind It. What About It?","As the golden light approached, one could vaguely spot two figures in it.","“Lord Shi Mo.”","The crowd cheered. None of them bowed, as Shi Mo had told them not to do so.","“Lord Shi Mo has brought an elder from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion with him!” the young man remarked in excitement.","“Is everyone here?” Shi Mo asked.","“Milord, we are all here.”","“I was cultivating outside, but I rushed back!”","Countless voices tinged with excitement and delight echoed in response.","“That’s good.” Shi Mo nodded. He waved his sleeves, and a formation sealed off the city.","“A formation? Why would Lord Shi Mo construct a formation?”","The crowd was confused, as Shi Mo had never constructed a formation the last few times he was here. Nevertheless, they didn’t probe into it.","But what Shi Mo said next left the crowd in a daze.","“I have something to tell you. I, Shi Mo, have another identity. I am a member of the Netherworld Sect.”","The city was plunged into silence.","“Lord Shi Mo, you are pulling our legs, right?”","“He must be joking.”","“Netherworld Sectmembers are despicable, cunning, vicious, and inhumane, whereas Lord Shi Mo gives us resources and pills every year. He even helps by channeling the pill so that we can better absorb the medicinal energy. How can someone like that be related to the Netherworld Sect?” someone said.","“Indeed. If not for Lord Shi Mo’s pill, I’d have long succumbed to my illness and died!” the young man’s father voiced his agreement.","“I wouldn’t have lasted so long either,” the young man’s grandfather spoke feebly from the house.","“A bunch of fools,” the old man standing next to Shi Mo sneered.","He ripped off his Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s robes to reveal the Netherworld Sect’s robe hidden beneath.","The crowd was horrified.","“Did you really think the pills were to your benefit? Those pills are meant for me. Their effectiveness is amplified when nourished with flesh and blood. The only downside is that I’ll have to extract the pill together with the flesh and blood nourishing it. In other words, you’ll be sacrificed.","“But again, trash like you is a waste of air. Becoming my fodder allows you to become part of something greater than what you can ever be. You’d have brought honor to your ancestors.”","The old man turned to Shi Mo. “Do it.”","“Yes, elder.” Shi Mo bowed to the old man.","“Lord Shi Mo, are you also...”","Seeing Shi Mo bow respectfully to a person dressed in the Netherworld Sect’s robes evoked an ominous feeling in the crowd. Is this... not a joke?","Shi Mo formed a hand seal, and a bizarre formation enveloped the sky.","GAH!!!","Everyone in the city revealed looks of pain. A bizarre power in their bodies was siphoning their blood and flesh.","“It hurts, Lord Shi Mo! It hurts so much! Please stop!”","“Lord Shi Mo, this joke isn’t funny!”","Some people still harbored delusions that this was all a joke.","Chu Feng didn’t plan to intervene right away. It was better for these people to see for themselves what they had gotten into. Had Shi Mo not revealed his true colors, it was doubtful these people would have trusted Chu Feng even if he told them the truth.","Even now, there were still people who thought Shi Mo was a good person, and this was a joke.","They had to suffer a bit before they would see the truth.","“Big brother Chu.”","“Lord.”","A hand suddenly grabbed Chu Feng’s elbow. It was the young man and his big brother.","“You aren’t affected by the formation as you have never taken the Netherworld trash’s pill. Hide in the house. Don’t let him discover you!” the young man’s big brother said. He was still worried about Chu Feng despite becoming so weak that he couldn’t even pull Chu Feng into the house.","The chatter diminished as the crowd grew weaker. Everyone had accepted their fate.","Boom!","The young man’s house suddenly burst open, and a brilliant golden light surfaced.","It was the young man’s grandfather.","He was still lying on the bed, but he held a scroll in his hand. The scroll floated into the air, bringing the young man’s grandfather with it. They formed a standoff against the duo from the Netherworld Sect.","“Don’t be afraid. Our Huang family has a protective treasure from an expert. We won’t let wretches from the Netherworld Sect wreak havoc in our city!” the young man’s grandfather said.","Under the effects of the scroll, his emaciated body gave off the airs of an expert.","He formed a hand seal, and the scroll’s golden light intensified.","Puft.","There was a light sputter reminiscent of a fart, then the scroll exploded without releasing any energy.","The young man’s grandfather plummeted from the sky.","The young man’s family had no strength to catch their grandfather.","Chu Feng casually waved his hand and caught the young man’s grandfather with his formation, allowing him to take no damage from the fall.","“Hahahahaha! Which expert gave you that protective treasure?” Shi Mo mocked.","“How can this be? How can this be?”","The young man’s grandfather stared at the scattered scroll bits in a daze. It had become apparent that the scroll was a fake. And if the scroll was fake, was the cultivator he had saved back then a fake as well?","The answer was obvious.","He had been scammed.","“Hahahaha...” The young man’s grandfather laughed miserly and manically.","His only faith had collapsed.","He had stood by the decision he had made back then even though his family was struggling. But looking back at it now, he was a big fool. His obstinacy had doomed his family to suffer with him. He had brought misery not just to himself but to his loved ones, too.","“You like to play the hero? Very well, I’ll take your life first!” Shi Mo spat.","He swiped his hand toward the young man’s family, only to freeze in horror the next moment. Somehow, he had failed to raise the young man’s grandfather as he had intended. He stared at his hand in disbelief.","Just then, the old man from the Netherworld Sect suddenly appeared in the courtyard and asked, “You’re the one behind this, right?”","The old man was standing right in front of Chu Feng.","The young man’s family was horrified. Despite knowing their deaths were imminent, it still plunged them into greater fear to have this demon appear right in front of them.","What they saw next completely baffled them.","Chu Feng hurled a punch forth. It penetrated the old man’s dantian, and the excruciating pain caused the latter to fall to his knees. Then, he placed his leg on the old man’s head, pinning the latter to the ground.","“Yes, I’m the one behind it. What about it?” Chu Feng asked."]},{"number":6472,"title":"Chapter 6472: Chapter 6470: Love Oneself Before Loving Others","paragraphs":["Chapter 6470: Love Oneself Before Loving Others","By the time the young man’s family realized what had happened, the old man from the Netherworld Sect had already crumbled to the ground in pain, with his head under Chu Feng’s foot. Fresh blood gushed from the bloody gorge in his abdomen.","“This...”","The young man’s family was so shocked that they fell speechless. They could never have expected that the amicable guest they had hosted would be even more frightening than the old man from the Netherworld Sect.","It was not just about Chu Feng’s overwhelming strength but also how he hadn’t batted his eyelid after crippling the old man from the Netherworld Sect, a sign he had much blood on his hands.","“I don’t know who you are, but I’m a Netherworld General from the Netherworld Sect. Our Lord Netherworld Marshalls have already returned from their closed-door training, and their strength surpasses our wildest imagination. It’s only a matter of time before our sect conquers the world of cultivation. Are you certain you want to defy us?”","The old man from the Netherworld Sect understood that he had provoked someone beyond his means, so he name-dropped the Netherworld Sect in hopes of intimidating Chu Feng.","“Aren’t I already an enemy of your Netherworld Sect?”","Bzzt!","Lightning crackled around Chu Feng. He was able to easily defeat the old man because he had secretly raised his cultivation in advance, but he was finally revealing it now. His Lightning Mark, Lightning Armor, and Lightning Wings appeared. He towered in the sky like a lightning god.","Everyone in the courtyard, including Shi Mo in the sky, stared at Chu Feng’s face in shock.","While unleashing his nine-colored lightning, Chu Feng removed his disguise and revealed his true face as well.","“H-h-he is actually...”","The young man’s family thought they were seeing things. In particular, the young man’s big brother's eyes nearly popped out of their sockets. They thought they were seeing a deity in person.","“Y-you are Chu Feng?” the old man from the Netherworld Sect asked with a quivering voice.","He had once met Chu Feng in the Netherworld Sect and was aware of the latter’s means. If the other party was truly Chu Feng, he was doomed. He could only curse his bad luck.","Shoosh!","Just then, the sealing formation around the city unraveled.","Upon seeing that the other party was Chu Feng, and that even the Netherworld General was no match for him, Shi Mo turned tail and fled.","Chu Feng raised his hand. A powerful suction force pulled Shi Mo down, causing him to crash into the courtyard.","Shi Mo quickly got to his knees and crawled his way up to Chu Feng, saying, “Chu Feng... Misunderstanding! Yes, this is a misunderstanding. I am a member of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, but that old man held me hostage!”","He took out a token and presented it to Chu Feng. It was the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s token.","Before Chu Feng could say a word, the old man roared, “How dare you, Shi Mo! Relinquishing your identity as a Netherworld Sectmember just so you can live? You deserve to die a thousand times over!”","“Shut up, shut up! I am from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion. I have nothing to do with the Netherworld Sect. Wang Qiang is from the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion. Isn’t he your brother? Y-you can’t kill me!” Shi Mo said with tears and snot flowing down his face.","He was afraid of death.","Chu Feng took the token and examined it. Not only was it authentic, but it was also inscribed with Shi Mo’s name. “I see that the Netherworld Sect has infiltrated the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.”","Chu Feng raised his hand and exerted a suction force, dragging both Shi Mo and the old man into the formation realm in his palm. Then, he rose into the sky.","“Chu Feng... That’s Chu Feng!”","“Look, it’s Lord Chu Feng!”","“Is Lord Chu Feng here to save us?”","“We’re saved!”","The crowd immediately knew why the excruciating pain had stopped. Chu Feng must have saved them. While there were many rumors about Chu Feng, very few of them were negative. This led them to think that he was a righteous person.","Besides, Chu Feng had a prior conflict with the Netherworld Sect, so it was unlikely for him to turn a blind eye to their misdeeds.","“The Netherworld Sect has planted a toxin in you. You’ll need to channel my formation to expel the toxin,” Chu Feng said as he took out a formation and sucked the entire city into it.","He made his way to a remote area before pulling the entire city out of his formation and placing it there.","“Lord Chu Feng, thank you for saving our lives.”","Everyone in the city dropped to their knees and thanked Chu Feng. The latter had expelled the bizarre aura in their bodies, saving their lives.","“I advise you to leave this city and head elsewhere,” Chu Feng said.","This was all he would do for them. Whatever they did next was none of his business. He took his leave and made his way to the young man’s courtyard.","The young man’s family was kneeling as well, just like the others.","With a wave of his sleeves, Chu Feng pulled them up to their feet and infused them with a peculiar surge of energy. That energy lengthened the grandfather’s lifespan, cured the father’s illness, and raised their cultivation. On top of that, it reforged their bloodline, allowing them to reach greater heights in their cultivation.","Sensing the changes in their bodies, the family was moved to tears.","Chu Feng raised his hand and channeled his spirit power. A scroll manifested in his grasp. He handed the scroll to the young man, saying, “This protective means will work.”","The young man took the scroll, but he was so overwhelmed by the situation that he couldn’t even string a sentence to voice his gratitude. He felt like he was in a dream.","Instead, it was his big brother who replied in an excited but cautious tone, “A-am I dreaming? Are you really Lord Chu Feng?”","“Yes, it’s me. I shouldn’t have to change my name anymore, right?” Chu Feng chuckled.","“N-no, of course not. You’re the Chu Feng. There’s no need for you to change your name. My gosh. I-I-I received pointers from Lord Chu Feng himself. No wonder I grasped such a powerful martial skill so quickly!”","The young man’s big brother was moved to tears. The young man’s parents were so overwhelmed that they couldn’t find the right words to say.","The young man finally snapped out of his daze. Clutching onto Chu Feng’s scroll, his lips curled into a silly-looking smile.","“Kindness begets kindness. The saying holds true!” the young man’s grandfather cried with a smile. He felt like he was finally reaping the rewards from his many years of sacrifice.","“Elder, that’s not necessarily so,” Chu Feng said.","The young man’s grandfather stiffened up.","Chu Feng turned to the young man and offered his advice. “Don’t expect kindness to beget kindness. You can show kindness to those in need, but you need to exercise your judgment and decide who is worth helping. Above all, you ought to take care of yourself. You need to love yourself before loving others.”","He pulled out a Cosmos Sack and handed it to the young man.","“This is my payment for your flower tea. Take good care of your family. Don’t let the tragedy that befell your grandfather happen again.”","With that, Chu Feng took his leave.","The young man and his family opened the Cosmos Sack and were flabbergasted. It contained everything they could think of—martial skills, profound skills, talisman papers, formations, and cultivation resources. It was a treasure they had never seen before.","These might be nothing to Chu Feng, but it was an unimaginable fortune to them."]},{"number":6473,"title":"Chapter 6473: Chapter 6471: The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is Behind It","paragraphs":["Chapter 6471: The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is Behind It","Chu Feng ascended above the city before slipping into his formation realm, where he had thrown the duo from the Netherworld Sect.","“Was the Netherworld Sect behind the disappearance of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes,” Shi Mo replied.","“Audacious! Shi Mo, try spewing another word of our Netherworld Sect’s secrets, and I’ll devour you whole!” the old man from the Netherworld Sect roared.","Chu Feng sealed the old man’s mouth with a wave of his hand.","“Why did the Netherworld Sect do that?” Chu Feng asked.","“I-I don’t know.” Shi Mo shook his head.","“Do you really not know? Or do you need me to make a move?”","Chu Feng whipped out a peculiar-looking sword that was covered in thorns, resembling a cactus. This was the Punishment Sword, a treasure he had obtained from the Heavensword Sacred Palace. It was laced with poison that greatly amplified the sensitivity of one’s nerves, and the thorns transformed upon entering the body, inflicting unbearable pain.","“Lord Chu Feng, I really don’t know. You should ask him... He knows. He’s a Demon-tier Netherworld General. He must know something!” Shi Mo was unnerved by the sword, and he turned his finger to the old man.","But Chu Feng still plunged the Punishment Sword into Shi Mo’s body.","Shi Mo convulsed in extreme pain. White foam sputtered from his mouth. His eyes rolled upward, and his mouth became crooked. It looked as if he was about to die from sheer pain.","Chu Feng pulled out the Punishment Sword.","“I-I-I really don’t know! I don’t know a thing at all!” Shi Mo replied in a weakened and indignant voice while eyeing the Punishment Sword in extreme fear.","Seeing that Shi Mo really didn’t know a thing at all, Chu Feng unsealed the old man’s mouth.","The old man sneered, “I fought alongside the Lord Netherworld Master back then. You won’t get a single word about the Netherworld Sect’s secrets about me... WUU!!!”","Chu Feng plunged the Punishment Sword into the old man’s body before he could finish his sentence. That immediately shut the old man’s mouth, but a split second later, he released a miserable howl.","“It’s the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion! The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion! Pull it out! Pull this darned thing out of my body!” the old man screamed while wailing in pain.","He couldn’t withstand the Punishment Sword’s torture.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?” Chu Feng was baffled.","The Netherworld Sect has gotten together with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?","Chu Feng pulled out the Punishment Sword and demanded, “Tell me what’s going on.”","The old man revealed that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had reached out to the Netherworld Sect for a partnership, but he was not privy to the details of the partnership.","“Where’s the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant right now?” Chu Feng asked.","“I know where it is. I can lead the way,” the old man replied fearfully, showing none of the confidence he had displayed earlier.","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded. He turned to Shi Mo and said, “I do not need you anymore.”","Before Shi Mo could utter a word, Chu Feng beheaded him with his sword. He collected Shi Mo’s origin energies and passed them to Eggy and stowed Shi Mo’s treasures in his Cosmos Sack.","The old man was horrified. “Don’t kill me, Lord Chu Feng. I’ll tell you everything you want to know!”","“What’s your name?” Chu Feng asked.","“I am Liu Kuangkuo,” the old man replied.","“I’ll spare you for the time being,” Chu Feng said before he left the formation realm alone. He formed a hand seal and morphed into the old man. “You can lead the way now.”","He could communicate with the old man even when the latter was still trapped inside his formation realm. The old man began giving him the directions to the current location of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnants.","...","Deep in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s forbidden land, a colossal formation whirred to life.","Standing at the center of the formation was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, Jie Tianran. Seated around the formation were the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s top personnel—the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the Saint-tier elders.","But there were six other people aside from these noteworthy figures. They wore black world spiritist cloaks embroidered with the words, ‘Sacred Mansion Shadow Squad’ and their names, namely ‘Immortal Shadow’, ‘Buddha Shadow’, ‘Demon Shadow’, Cultivator Shadow’, ‘Monster Shadow’, ‘Beast Shadow’.","The Sacred Mansion Shadow Corp was a powerful organization within the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion that only comprised of elites, but this organization only obeyed Jie Tianran’s commands. These seven people were the leaders of the Shadow Corp.","Only six of the seven leaders were gathered here because one of them, Ghost Shadow, had died while carrying out a mission in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","All the most powerful experts in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were gathered here.","A golden lake floated above the formation. It revolved in the sky, glimmering beautifully under the formation’s lights. Contained within the lake was not ordinary water but Immemorial Divine Water, an incomparably valuable resource. It had been specially refined and was bubbling.","Even a single drop of Immemorial Divine Water was priceless, yet there was so much of it here.","“Let’s begin.”","Jie Tianran changed his hand seal.","The Immemorial Divine Water rained on the experts outside the formation. Those struck by the rain immediately buckled under immense pain.","“Pain is inevitable to acquire such power. You’ll succeed with the aid of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation, so bear with it.”","The experts quickly formed hand seals to withstand the ordeal. Fortunately, it didn’t take long before they absorbed the vast amount of Immemorial Divine Water.","“Lord Mansion Master!!!”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, the Saint-tier elders, and the six leaders of the Sacred Mansion Shadow Squad sensed that they had made incredible progress in their spirit power and were overjoyed. They were now rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","Even reaching Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist was beyond them in the past, but Jie Tianran helped them overcome their bottleneck and soar far beyond that.","Jie Tianran had depleted many treasures to help them raise their cultivation, expending even the precious Immemorial Divine Water on them. Even so, they were still astonished. Based on what they knew, Jie Tianran himself was also at rank five Heavenly Dragon.","Never in their life had they imagined they would reach the same level as their mansion master. Naturally, they were delighted.","“There’s one thing I need to tell you. Even though I have devoted many invaluable treasures to this formation, there is bound to be a price to pay for power obtained through external means,” Jie Tianran said."]},{"number":6474,"title":"Chapter 6474: Chapter 6472: Jie Tianran’s Means","paragraphs":["Chapter 6472: Jie Tianran’s Means","“There’s a price?”","The crowd was taken aback. They were in their prime condition, feeling no discomfort whatsoever.","“Feel your own life force,” Jie Tianran instructed.","The crowd did as they were told and were horrified. They were in tiptop condition, but their life force had been greatly diminished. At this rate, they wouldn’t live beyond ten years. What was the point of obtaining such powerful spirit power if they wouldn’t even last ten years?","“Lord Mansion Master...”","Everyone looked at Jie Tianran, be it the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, the Saint-tier elders, or the loyal six leaders of the Shadow Corps. They wanted to know what this meant.","“God’s Era is about to be fully opened. We are up against formidable rivals, not just from the Ancient Era but also present era powers such as the Netherworld Sect. Once God’s Era reveals its true power, no one will be able to resist its allure. It’ll be a desperate fight for it.","“Our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion must obtain the power of God’s Era, but we are up against formidable enemies. I won’t be able to do it alone. I need your help,” Jie Tianran said.","“It’s our honor to lay down our lives for you, Lord Mansion Master.”","The six leaders of the Shadow Corp kneeled and expressed their resolution. The 36 Saint-tier elders also bowed deeply.","But the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief asked, “Lord Mansion Master, I’m too old to fear death, but I’m curious to know what power lies within God’s Era.”","He was willing to lay down his life, but he wanted to know what he was fighting for.","Despite God’s Era’s immense reputation and the benefits it had brought to Jie Tianran, to this day, they still had no idea what kind of power it contained.","“I don’t have a complete idea what it is.”","Jie Tianran’s words sparked disappointment from the crowd, especially since they were laying down their lives for this. Ten years was an extremely short time for them.","“The present world of cultivation is incomplete. What’s limiting us isn’t our talent but the environment. We need to follow our ancestors’ footsteps and enter the Ninth Galaxy. Only then can we be freed of our shackles and claim the cultivation that belongs to us.","“But before that, we need to first acquire God’s Era’s power. This power was coveted by countless experts in the Ancient Era, but none of them succeeded in acquiring it. If our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion can achieve what they have failed at, we can reach the zenith of the world of cultivation.”","Jie Tianran turned to the elders. “Don’t worry. I won’t harm you. I don’t have a complete idea of what God’s Era’s power is, but I know it wields the power to overlook all constraints and extend one’s lifespan. Once we obtain God’s Era’s power, I can remove the adverse effect plaguing you. That means you can enjoy this power without being limited by your lifespan.","“That should already be a huge benefit. Rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist is a height most can’t hope to reach in their lifetime, and you may advance further once we venture into the Ninth Galaxy.”","The crowd calmed down after hearing those words. It turned out they still had a way to survive, and that was to conquer God’s Era.","“Obtaining God’s Era’s power won’t be easy. The powers on the surface are one thing, but we need to be very cautious of those lurking in the shadows. Thus, I want you to handle this matter seriously. I want to see results within the allotted time.”","Jie Tianran took out several scrolls containing instructions and hurled them to those present.","“This isn’t just about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s future but present as well. It’s pointless to talk about the future if we can’t secure the present. Thus, I implore you to put your all into this. We’ll be the heroes of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if we obtain God’s Era’s power. Conversely, anyone who hinders the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s ambition will be my enemy. I won’t hold back, even against my kin.”","Jie Tianran’s eyes narrowed viciously.","“We’ll not let Lord Mansion Master down,” the experts of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion roared, including the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief.","“Go on,” Jie Tianran ordered.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the 36 Saint-tier elders left the premises, leaving behind Jie Tianran and the six leaders of the Shadow Squad.","“Lord Mansion Master, why didn’t you entrust those tasks to us instead?” Immortal Shadow asked.","“Do you think they are incapable? Or do you think they’ll defy my orders?” Jie Tianran asked.","That question intimidated Immortal Shadow into silence. He was worried about both, but he dared not continue voicing his concern after hearing Jie Tianran’s authoritative tone.","Jie Tianran patted Immortal Shadow’s shoulder and said, “Don’t worry. Everyone in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is my aide. They won’t defy my orders, and they won’t dare to, either.”","His expression exuded confidence and ambition.","Meanwhile, the Saint-tier elders rallied the other experts of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and set off via teleportation formations. Most of their destinations were within the Seven Realms Galaxy, though some headed to other galaxies.","There were personnel dispatched to the Ancestral Martial, Nine Souls, Immortal Sea, Totem, Bloodline, Heavenly Dome, and Divine Body Galaxies. Judging from their grim faces, they were about to do something huge.","But they had no choice. This was for the future of not just the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion but them as well.","Jie Tianran issued some tasks to the Sacred Mansion Shadow Squad before sending them off. Now, he was the only one left in the forbidden land.","“How vicious. They are all your aides,” the voice inside Jie Tianran said.","Jie Tianran had lied to them. There was no way to extend their lifespans. The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, the 36 Saint-tier elders, and the six leaders of the Shadow Squad were doomed to die in ten years.","“The future of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion lies in me, Tian’er, and our unborn descendants. Those people have already reached their limits. Death is only a matter of time for them. They might as well make one last contribution to our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion instead of dying of old age. At least their names will go down in history.”","Jie Tianran showed no remorse. On the contrary, he thought those people should be honored to serve the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“I have chosen the right person,” the voice inside Jie Tianran said.","Just then, an elder outside the formation reported, “Lord Mansion Master, a scum from the Netherworld Sect is here!”"]},{"number":6475,"title":"Chapter 6475: Chapter 6473: The Netherworld Sect’s Sincerity","paragraphs":["Chapter 6473: The Netherworld Sect’s Sincerity","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had activated its defensive formation.","Countless elders wielding formation blades nervously stared at the person outside the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The other party wore the Netherworld Sect’s iconic cloak and red bamboo veil. His red cloak was embroidered with the words ‘Netherworld Marshall’.","He was within range of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s defensive formation, but it was powerless against him, even though it had the power to subdue even rank five Heavenly Gods. This could only mean he was stronger than a rank five Heavenly God.","The formation suddenly dissipated.","Those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were horrified.","“Why are you panicking?” an old man’s voice echoed.","The crowd breathed a sigh of relief as they respectfully greeted the old man, “Paying respect to Lord Mansion Master.”","It was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, Jie Tianran. He must have been the one who deactivated their defensive formation.","“Mansion Master, you have finally revealed yourself. Do you want to come out yourself, or should I fight my way in?” the Netherworld Marshall spoke in the voice of a middle-aged man.","Despite being a far distance away, he could see what was happening inside the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Jie Tianran took a step forward and appeared opposite the Netherworld Marshall.","Shoosh!","The Netherworld Marshall suddenly manifested a massive martial power hand to grab Jie Tianran.","However, the hand never landed as an invisible force stopped it in place. It was spirit power. The spirit power morphed into a formation blade and severed the martial power hand before proceeding to do the same to the Netherworld Marshall.","In response, the Netherworld Marshall waved his hand, and the world shook. The formation blade disintegrated.","This sight shook the hearts of those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. It had only been a brief clash, but the power they unleashed surpassed the limits of the defensive formation.","Neither the Netherworld Marshall nor Jie Tianran continued their assault.","“You live up to your reputation, Mansion Master,” the Netherworld Marshall said.","“You’re probing me?” Jie Tianran asked.","“I came here to discuss a partnership. May we head to somewhere private for further discussions?” the Netherworld Marshall asked.","“Those from the Netherworld Sect are not welcome on our premises,” Jie Tianran sneered.","“Mansion Master, you must have some misunderstandings about us. We aren’t a demonic sect. It’s a bias that the world harbors toward us,” the Netherworld Marshall said.","Jie Tianran turned around and left.","The Netherworld Marshall understood Jie Tianran’s intention and followed him.","The two of them traveled some distance away from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion before Jie Tianran pulled out a floating palace. It was a treasure with incredible isolation property. Most notably, it could only be discovered at close range.","Jie Tianran entered the palace, and the Netherworld Marshall followed suit.","The palace was vast and majestic, a place used to host guests. This showed that Jie Tianran harbored no animosity against the Netherworld Sect; on the contrary, he regarded them highly.","“I, Jie Tianran, don’t work with people who dare not show their faces,” Jie Tianran said.","“It’s not that I dare not; I’m just reluctant. Too many people are unworthy of seeing my true face, though that does not include you, Mansion Master,” the Netherworld Marshall said as he took off his bamboo veil, revealing the weathered face of a white-haired, middle-aged man.","“I am Baili Xukong,” the Netherworld Marshall said with a bow.","“Sit down,” Jie Tianran said.","Baili Xukong didn’t hesitate to take a seat.","“Baili Xukong, the head of the Netherworld Sect’s new faction,” Jie Tianran remarked.","“I see that the Mansion Master is well aware of the happenings in our Netherworld Sect,” Baili Xukong replied.","“I have no interest in other powers, but I have no choice but to pay close attention to the Netherworld Sect. Why have you come today? Are you here to propose a partnership to deal with Chu Feng?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Chu Feng does have something we want, and he is a common enemy between us. However, I didn’t come here today for Chu Feng. I’m here to talk about the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect,” Baili Xukong said.","“The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect?” Jie Tianran narrowed his eyes.","“Their remnant in the Bloodline Galaxy is currently in our hands,” Baili Xukong said.","“What about my people?” Jie Tianran’s eyes turned cold.","Baili Xukong opened his palm, revealing a sphere. The sphere contained a formation realm filled with many people—they were from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Those were the people whom Jie Tianran had sent to the Bloodline Galaxy to keep an eye on the remnant.","He’s returning my subordinates unharmed. At least he has some sincerity. Jie Tianran took the sphere before asking, “What do you want from us? Get to the point.”","“We need you to do something for us. Don’t worry, it has nothing to do with God’s Era. I know you’re determined to obtain God’s Era’s power, and you can be assured that our Netherworld Sect has no interest in that. We wish to awaken a place, and we need your help for it,” Baili Xukong said.","“What’s the place you want to awaken?” Jie Tianran asked.","“I’m afraid I can’t reveal it just yet,” Baili Xukong replied.","“What do I stand to gain?”","“We’ll present you with the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant.”","“Hah...” Jie Tianran scoffed. “The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant has been lying dormant there all this while. You wouldn’t have been able to take it away if it could be activated, and there’s no point obtaining a remnant that can’t be activated.”","Baili Xukong laughed. “Does the Mansion Master not know that the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant has been activated?”","Jie Tianran narrowed his eyes.","He was, of course, aware of that. His men had been keeping a close eye on the remnant, and they reported its activation to him right away. However, the remnant had already disappeared by the time he arrived, and his subordinates were nowhere to be found.","“Looks like you already know.” Baili Xukong smiled. “The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant is merely a token of our sincerity. We will compensate you handsomely after the deal is done.”","Baili Xukong stood up and took out an ancient box. He opened the ancient box, and a brilliant light shone from within.","Jie Tianran shot to his feet when he saw the item inside the box. His eyes reflected disbelief.","“This item is with the Netherworld Sect?” Jie Tianran exclaimed in shock."]},{"number":6476,"title":"Chapter 6476: Chapter 6474: Great Demon Slayer Emperor, Demonslayer Saber","paragraphs":["Chapter 6474: Great Demon Slayer Emperor, Demonslayer Saber","Inside the box was a saber.","The saber looked crude, resembling a naturally formed black stone. It emanated an overpowering smell of blood as if it had absorbed the blood of countless beings.","“Many remnants and resources were left behind after the Ancient Era, which the cultivators in the initial years of the present era benefited greatly from. The Ancestral Martial Galaxy had the most remnants and resources, and it produced many powerhouses and renowned unaffiliated cultivators.","“One of them was passionate about helping the weak, a righteous hero. He wielded the Monsterslaying Sword and later became known as the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor.","“An entity from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion received the title of ‘Emperor’ as well, but he was a world spiritist. He wielded an Ancient Era’s treasure known as the Demonslaying Saber. Due to the similarities in their weapon names and their deeds, he became known to the world as the Great Demon Slayer Emperor.","“Later, it became known to the world that only the strongest human experts were worthy of being titled ‘Emperor’, which led to many thinking that the names of the ‘Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’ and the ‘Great Demon Slayer Emperor’ were a laughingstock.","“Even after the two of them passed away, many still mocked them for their titles. Even though they were renowned experts, they were merely one of the many experts in that era. They were nowhere near becoming the strongest.","“In my view, those two were formidable figures to have been able to make a name for themselves in that era, even if they were unworthy of being titled ‘Emperor’.","“The Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor was extremely talented; the Monstrous Slaying Sword played an auxiliary role. But I heard the Great Demon Slayer Emperor’s accomplishments could be attributed to his Demonslaying Saber. The Demonslaying Saber and the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s Celestial Master Sacred Sword were lauded to be the two strongest world spiritist weapons in this era.” Baili Xukong said as he glanced at the black stone saber in the box.","“Many coveted the Demonslaying Saber after the Great Demon Slayer Emperor passed away, but they were unable to find it. Our Netherworld Sect found its location by chance, but it still took us considerable effort to obtain it.”","The saber in the box was none other than the Demonslaying Saber.","“The Celestial Master Sacred Sword was a weapon forged by the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, but the Demonslaying Saber was a weapon crafted by a mysterious world spiritist in the Ancient Era, who is rumored to be a rival of the World Spiritist Emperor. The Celestial Master Sacred Sword is nothing compared to the Demonslaying Saber,” Jie Tianran corrected.","“You have a good eye,” Baili Xukong said.","“I don’t like to beat around the bush. A good weapon is a good weapon. You should know that this weapon will greatly strengthen me, but you’re still willing to hand it over to me?” Jie Tianran asked.","“It’s the same for our Netherworld Sect as well.","“If Lord Netherworld Master were still here, we would have long conquered the world of cultivation. Lord Netherworld Master entered the Ninth Galaxy a long time ago because he realized we were limited by the world of cultivation. He sees no meaning in conquering the eight galaxies; the ruler of the Ninth Galaxy is the true ruler of the entire world.","“Our Netherworld Sect didn’t leave with Lord Netherworld Master because we still have a mission here to accomplish, and for that, I require the Mansion Master’s help. We’ll be able to enter the Ninth Galaxy once we succeed in the endeavor.","“I believe the Mansion Master will be entering the Ninth Galaxy after obtaining God’s Era’s power as well, right? We’d be outsiders there, and navigating the already established order there is bound to pose problems. It’d be better to have another ally than another enemy. We don’t have to be enemies,” Baili Xukong said.","Jie Tianran nodded. “I’d agree if you truly mean those words.”","“I do.”","“Let’s give it a try and see if we can have a pleasant partnership.”","Baili Xukong was overjoyed, knowing he had successfully struck a deal.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng made his way to one of the Netherworld Sect’s hidden bases in the Bloodline Galaxy.","It was a desert, but a gorgeous oasis was hidden beneath its surface. Special means were needed to enter the oasis. It was not created by the Netherworld Sect; it had been around since the Ancient Era, but the Netherworld Sect had discovered and taken control of it.","Chu Feng entered the oasis using the old man’s name without a hitch, but his heart clenched up shortly after.","“There are experts stationed here.”","Chu Feng sensed a powerful aura belonging to a rank four Heavenly God level cultivator.","“Should we call for reinforcement?” Eggy asked.","Chu Feng had many experts stationed at the Totem Galaxy, awaiting his orders.","“It’s a rank four Heavenly God,” Chu Feng replied.","“Rank four Heavenly God? We’d need the help of the Zhao Immortal Clan to deal with that. I wonder if they’d be willing to help us.”","“I’m worried that the rank four Heavenly God can raise his cultivation like Xiahou Jue.”","“That would be a problem. Eighth Zhao wouldn’t be a match if that’s the case. But you have nothing to worry about. I’m here.” Eggy puffed out her chest.","Chu Feng trusted Eggy, but he viewed her as a final resort. She had only made a brief move back in the Immemorial Cemetery, but it still took her a lot of resources to recover. He had no more origin energies to help her recover.","The Divine Deer suddenly spoke up,” Chu Feng, I have recovered my powers.”","Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief. His escape means were secured now that the Divine Deer had regained its powers."]},{"number":6477,"title":"Chapter 6477: Chapter 6475: Audacious","paragraphs":["Chapter 6475: Audacious","“Eggy, we won’t fight them if we get discovered. We’ll run away,” Chu Feng said.","“Run?” Eggy was confused.","Chu Feng told her about the Divine Deer’s recovery.","Eggy nodded in agreement. “All right, let’s escape if the situation seems off.”","The oasis was filled with Netherworld Sectmembers. Chu Feng didn’t know if the Netherworld Sect had powerful anti-detection measures, so he didn’t attempt to use his observation means. However, he could walk around freely using the old man’s identity.","He soon found the whereabouts of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant and obtained two pieces of news.","One, the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant had opened and could be accessed.","Two, a Netherworld Marshall was stationed at the remnant entrance, preventing anyone from entering it.","The aura Chu Feng sensed belonged to that Netherworld Marshall, who was a woman named Wuma Hanshuang.","Chu Feng thought he should at least investigate the place since he was already here, so he made his way to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant. It resembled an ancient city on the outside, but it had an unsettling appearance.","“Why does it look like it was constructed by a demonic sect? Could this Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant be a fake?” Eggy asked.","This remnant looked different from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s usual style.","“It may look unusual, but it carries the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s unique aura,” Chu Feng replied.","This remnant was said to be the hardest one, and activating it was bound to require some effort. There was no barrier around the remnant, and its door was wide open as well. The remnant had been activated.","While one would still have to overcome trials to obtain the remnant’s rewards, the trickiest bit had been resolved. That saved him a lot of trouble. After all, Chu Feng had heard that not even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had been able to activate the remnant.","Chu Feng approached the remnant while looking around.","“Are you looking to die?” an imposing, feminine voice echoed from the door.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng was pushed several meters back, and that was the other party showing mercy to him.","It was Wuma Hanshuang.","Chu Feng quickly bowed toward the door and said, “Milord, I heard the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant has been activated, so I came to take a look out of curiosity. I mean no offense.”","“This is a forbidden place. Scram,” Wuma Hanshuang said.","She didn’t show him respect just because the identity he assumed was a Netherworld General. It was doubtful whether she even viewed him as a human.","“What’s she acting so arrogantly for? I’ll head in and obliterate her!” Eggy was displeased that someone was speaking to Chu Feng in such a manner.","“It’s fine. She’s reprimanding the Netherworld Sect’s Liu Kuangkuo and not me, Chu Feng.” Unfazed, Chu Feng turned around and left.","“What you said makes sense.” Eggy’s anger subsided considerably.","“Hahaha! Old Liu, you got scolded, didn’t you? Someone of your age should conduct himself more maturely!” a voice transmission was relayed to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng soon identified the source of the voice transmission. It was from another old Netherworld General standing not too far away, with a bamboo veil concealing his face.","“Liu Kuangkuo, someone has just spoken to me. Tell me your relationship with him, or else I’ll inflict the Punishment Sword on you,” Chu Feng questioned Liu Kuangkuo before imitating the voice he had just heard.","Liu Kuangkuo quickly identified the other party’s identity through his voice.","It was a Netherworld General who went by the family name of ‘Sun’. They were at the same cultivation level and were old acquaintances.","The old Netherworld General walked up to Chu Feng and asked, “What’s wrong, Brother Liu? Why are you ignoring me? Are you unhappy at being berated by Lord Wuma?”","“No, I wouldn’t dare to show any displeasure toward Lord Wuma,” Chu Feng quickly replied.","“That’s good. What brings you here?” the old Netherworld General asked.","“I was in the vicinity for a mission, so I thought I’d drop by to take a look at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission.","“Keep your distance. Don’t even think about entering it. That remnant is important to us. Lord Wuma will not permit anyone to enter it,” the old Netherworld General said.","Chu Feng was troubled. He had observed the remnant and confirmed that it only had one entrance. There was nothing he could do if the Netherworld Sect forbade anyone from entering its premises.","He was not confident of sneaking in under Wuma Hanshuang’s watch.","Just then, Chu Feng noticed a woman strutting out from the remnant.","“Old Sun, why can that woman enter the remnant?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s Lord Wuma’s new disciple. She’s extremely powerful despite her young age. It hasn’t been long since she joined our Netherworld Sect, but her position already far surpasses ours,” the old Netherworld General replied.","“I see.” Chu Feng nodded.","Just then, he noticed the woman looking in their direction.","“I told you to steer clear. Didn’t you hear me?” that woman said. Her voice was cold and impassive, similar to Wuma Hanshuang’s.","“We’ll leave right now!”","Intimidated, the old Netherworld General bowed deeply to the woman. Chu Feng did the same as well and was about to leave when he heard the woman’s voice once more, but this time, she spoke to him via voice transmission.","His words left him with goosebumps and chills.","“Audacious, Chu Feng. How dare you come here?”"]},{"number":6478,"title":"Chapter 6478: Chapter 6476: Dream On","paragraphs":["Chapter 6476: Dream On","Eggy, who had been sitting idly in Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space, leaped to her feet and prepared for battle. Things had gone awry. The other party knew Chu Feng’s identity.","“Leave this place and head westward. I’ll look for you later,” the woman sent another voice transmission over before leaving the place.","“What’s going on, Chu Feng? Do you know her?” Eggy asked.","“I don’t recognize that voice, but that person might have altered her voice. Regardless, let’s leave this place first.”","Chu Feng knew he would be in danger if his identity was exposed here, but since the other party didn’t expose him on the spot, there might be room for negotiation. He was curious to know what the other party was up to.","So, Chu Feng shook off the old Netherworld General, left the Netherworld Sect’s base, and headed westward as the woman had told him to.","“Chu Feng, who do you think it is?” Eggy asked.","“I have someone in mind, but I can’t confirm it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Who?”","Just then, Chu Feng felt a surge of killing intent coming from behind. It was from a rank nine True God level cultivator.","Without any hesitation, he activated his Lightning Mark, Lightning Armor, and Lightning Wings, raising his cultivation to rank nine True God level as well.","The killing intent finally reached him.","Chu Feng manifested a formation sword and held it horizontally before him with a single hand. There was nothing ahead of him initially, but as his sword got into position, the fabrics of space suddenly tore, and a God Armament gushed out and hacked on his formation sword.","This attack left a mark on the formation sword, and Chu Feng was sent skidding into the distance. The formation sword he manifested was not weak by any means, but it was lacking when faced against a comparable cultivator wielding a God Armament.","Chu Feng was aware of this. He had chosen not to draw his God Armament because he wasn’t planning on engaging the other party in a fight. He just wanted to know that woman’s identity.","“Who are you?” Chu Feng asked.","The attacker was none other than the woman who had sent a voice transmission to him earlier.","“Heh...” the woman sneered.","Her aura changed once more. She was still at rank nine True God level, but she gained heaven-defying battle power of one cultivation rank.","In response, Chu Feng activated his Lightning Aura to match the woman’s cultivation.","The woman wrapped her hands around her God Armament saber and charged at Chu Feng. She didn’t utilize any martial skills, but her attacks were aimed at Chu Feng’s vitals.","Chu Feng deflected her attacks with his formation sword.","The woman had a slender and short stature—she wasn’t even half as tall as her God Armament saber. However, her attacks were ferocious, and her fighting prowess was formidable.","“You still aren’t getting serious. You must be looking down on me,” the woman scoffed.","Chu Feng could have counterattacked, but he maintained his defensive posture because he wasn’t serious about this fight. This angered her.","“Who are you?” Chu Feng asked once more.","“We’ll talk once you defeat me.”","The woman wrapped her martial power around her God Armament saber, further raising the prowess of her attacks. She focused her attacks not on Chu Feng but his formation sword in hopes of shattering it.","But Chu Feng saw through her intent and retreated instead of facing her attack head on.","The woman immediately gave chase.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng suddenly hurled his formation sword at the woman like a dart.","The woman instinctively slashed her saber, slicing the formation sword apart.","But what awaited her behind the sliced formation sword was another sword thrusting toward her at an incredible speed.","“You’re still underestimating me?”","The woman immediately halted her advancement and retreated. That bought her enough time to deflect Chu Feng’s incoming attack with her God Armament saber.","But the next moment, she widened her eyes in shock.","Chu Feng’s sword shattered her God Armament saber and arrived before her neck. He was brandishing the Lightning Flame Sword, which was far superior to her God Armament saber.","But Chu Feng didn’t push on.","The woman was stunned. She eyed her shattered God Armament saber and angrily exclaimed, “You bastard Chu Feng! You have to compensate me for my God Armament!”","Chu Feng wasn’t surprised by her reaction. He stowed away his sword and dispelled the lightning around him.","“I knew it was you,” Chu Feng replied.","“Oh? How did you know?”","The woman took off her veiled bamboo hat, revealing her beautiful face.","“Ah, it’s that lass, Wen Xue.” Eggy breathed a sigh of relief.","Chu Feng had first met Wen Xue in the Purple Star Hall.","Back then, she was a demonic cultivation treasure that wielded special powers. She had infiltrated Chu Feng’s dantian in an attempt to devour his bloodline, only to be cornered by his bloodline. In the end, she had to leave her Life Soul in his body to escape.","In a stroke of coincidence, the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster took her in as her disciple and named her Wen Xue.","Wen Xue was not a human.","She had existed for countless years now, but in her words, she had been granted a new lease of life. She was also a junior, one who was much younger than Chu Feng and Zi Ling.","She wielded special powers, too. Her energy carried incredible recovery potency.","Back when several Ancient Era’s races joined forces to attack the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, Zi Ling was forced to break out of her closed-door cultivation to defend it. That nearly resulted in her death. It was thanks to Wen Xue’s help that Zi Ling survived the ordeal.","Later, Chu Feng had a psyche battle with Jie Tianran in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city and became greatly weakened. Wen Xue intervened and helped him to swiftly recover, but she had to pay a heavy price for that.","Due to that, Chu Feng owed her a favor.","When Chu Feng and Zi Ling left the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect to compete for the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city’s key fragments, Wen Xue insisted on tagging along. However, when they arrived at the Immortal Sea Galaxy, she found a chance to slip away.","Chu Feng would have never expected Wen Xue to have joined the Netherworld Sect.","“How did you know it’s me, Junior Chu Feng?” Wen Xue asked in surprise.","“I’m confident in my disguise. I’m guessing you left something in me back when you treated me back then, and that was how you recognized me,” Chu Feng said.","The woman had the means to identify him, was willing to join the Netherworld Sect, but harbored enough goodwill toward him as to not rat him out... Of the people Chu Feng knew, the only person who fit the criteria other than Song Yun was Wen Xue.","“You talk as if I had been scheming against you. I had to fuse my bloodline power into you to treat you back then. That’s why I can sense you whenever you’re within a certain radius of me. How can you shatter the God Armament I obtained with great difficulty if you knew it was me? I don’t care. You have to compensate me!” Wen Xue looked at Chu Feng, aggrieved.","“Fine, I’ll compensate you.”","Chu Feng casually took out a God Armament saber and handed it to Wen Xue. There was no need for him to hesitate, as he had plenty of God Armaments with him. He was very generous here, giving her a ‘True’ character God Armament.","But Wen Xue pointed at Chu Feng’s Lightning Flame Sword and said, “I want this one.”","“Dream on,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6479,"title":"Chapter 6479: Chapter 6477: Your Senior Isn’t Just Anyone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6477: Your Senior Isn’t Just Anyone","“You’re so stingy, Junior Chu Feng. Have you forgotten that you owe me a favor?”","Wen Xue pouted as if she had been wronged. She looked innocent like a young lady oblivious to the ways of the world, but her eyes, which were nowhere as clear as Little Fishy’s, gleamed with slyness.","“I’ll return the favor, but I can’t give you this sword. You can’t control it anyway,” Chu Feng replied.","“Fine.” Wen Xue took the God Armament saber from Chu Feng, though her eyes remained on his Lightning Flame Sword. “Isn’t your sword a God Armament, too? How can it cut through my God Armament saber just like that?”","Chu Feng chuckled. “I can only say there’s a disparity between God Armaments.”","He had many God Armaments in his inventory, including invaluable ‘True’ character God Armaments, but the Lightning Flame Sword was the only ‘Heaven’ character God Armament he had.","Having wielded the Lightning Flame Sword, he could say with certainty that it wielded prowess far surpassing that of other God Armaments. That was also why he had made that earlier slash.","“How did you end up in the Netherworld Sect?” Chu Feng asked.","“I realized that the Netherworld Embryo is beneficial to my cultivation, so I joined the Netherworld Sect to get one. I ended up triggering the guidance of the Divine Vat and caught the eye of Wuma Hanshuang. She insisted on taking me in as her disciple,” Wen Xue said.","“Do you identify as a Netherworld Sectmember or a Hidden Dragon Martial Sectmember now?” Chu Feng asked.","“I don’t think they are mutually exclusive?” Wen Xue asked.","Chu Feng sighed, though he knew this was Wen Xue’s personality. “You have made great advancements in your cultivation.”","He could sense that Wen Xue’s base cultivation was rank seven True God level, which was higher than his.","“Shouldn’t you know me better? I’m not a real junior. Do you think my countless years of accumulation would have been in vain? I would have to be inept to grow slowly. I’m more surprised with you, Junior Chu Feng. Were you an old monster as well? How did you grow this quickly? This doesn’t make sense,” Wen Xue said.","“All right, let’s stop heaping compliments on each other. Since you’re a Netherworld Sectmember, senior, I’d like to request your help,” Chu Feng said.","“You wish to enter the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant, right? You already owe me a favor, but you still want to take advantage of me? Junior Chu Feng, I didn’t take you to be such a person.” Wen Xue crossed her arms and shook her head.","“Please help me, senior. I know your heart is still with the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect even though you joined the Netherworld Sect, right? You can trust me to jump to your rescue if you’re ever in need of help in the future,” Chu Feng said.","“There’s no need to wait for the future. You can do it right now,” Wen Xue stated.","“I’m serious when I said you can’t control this sword. You can give it a try if you doubt my words, but you’ll suffer a backlash.”","“I’m not so callous as to extort my junior’s weapon. You can help me with something else.”","“What is it?”","“The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant.”","“Oh?”","Wen Xue shared with Chu Feng what she was after.","Wen Xue was no ordinary entity; she was a natural oddity that cultivated into a human. Naturally, she wielded powers that other humans didn’t have.","She sensed that a demonic entity was sealed inside the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant, and this demonic entity was beneficial to the nurturing of her bloodline.","Since the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect had left that remnant behind to pass down its legacy to the later generations, it was unlikely that they would place a demonic entity there to ambush the successor of their legacy. It was more likely that the demonic entity was placed there as a reward for clearing the remnant.","“Fine. Take me into the remnant. If I obtain the demonic entity and can control it, I’ll give it to you,” Chu Feng declared.","“We’ll enter the remnant together,” Wen Xue said.","“Together? I thought the Netherworld Sect forbade anyone from entering it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Indeed. The Netherworld Sect plans to hand this remnant to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.” Wen Xue proceeded to tell Chu Feng about the Netherworld Sect’s intention to work with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Chu Feng wasn’t surprised. The Netherworld Sect, as a cultivator sect, had no reason to be interested in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant. It made more sense for them to have claimed the remnant as leverage to negotiate a partnership with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","But what Wen Xue revealed next surprised Chu Feng. She told him what the Netherworld Sect needed the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s help for.","The Netherworld Sect coveted an unknown power but wasn’t confident of obtaining it, so they sought the help of powerful world spiritists. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was the perfect choice for that.","But that, in itself, was not enough to surprise Chu Feng. What surprised him was where the unknown power was located—the Undying Starfield.","“You’re saying the unknown power is at the Undying Starfield? The Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Undying Starfield?”","Chu Feng was familiar with the Undying Starfield.","He, together with the Mystic Cave Saints, had ventured into the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s tomb, encountered the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s fragmented soul, obtained his acknowledgment and the Monstrous Slayer Sword.","However, the Great Monstrous Slayer didn’t leave his true legacy at the tomb but the Undying Starfield’s Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","And the key to opening the treasure was the Monstrous Slayer Sword.","Before the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s soul dissipated, he reminded Chu Feng that he had to reach Martial Exalted level before heading to the Flowersea Ordinary Realm to unlock his tombstone.","When Chu Feng finally reached the required cultivation level and made his way to the Flowersea Ordinary Realm to claim the legacy, he discovered that the entire Undying Starfield had vanished.","“Yes, it’s the Holy Light Galaxy’s Undying Starfield. No no no, I mean the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Undying Starfield,” Wen Xue replied.","“Why did they move the Undying Starfield to the Bloodline Galaxy? That should be a difficult feat even for the Netherworld Sect, right?” Chu Feng asked.","It was an inconceivable feat, even to the current him. The Netherworld Sect must have paid a hefty price to pull it off. There must be a reason they had gone to this extent for it.","“You’re right, but the Netherworld Sect has a treasure to accomplish that. They had to do it to nourish the Undying Starfield with the Bloodline Galaxy’s energy,” Wen Xue replied.","“So, their goal is only that unknown power. Did they find anything else in the Undying Starfield?” Chu Feng was referring to the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s tomb.","“I haven’t heard anything about that. Most treasures in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy have been claimed in the earlier years of the present era. What valuable items can there be in the Undying Starfield?” The sharp-witted Wen Xue knew right away what Chu Feng was asking.","Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief.","He had suspected that the Netherworld Sect was behind the Undying Starfield’s disappearance, but back then, he thought they were after the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s tomb. From the looks of it now, they were after something else. This hinted that the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s tomb might still be intact in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","“Are you able to enter the Undying Starfield?” Chu Feng asked.","“Do you think they will allow anyone to enter the Undying Starfield?” Wen Xue asked.","“That’s true.” Chu Feng nodded with a smile.","The Netherworld Sect had assigned a Netherworld Marshall to guard the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant when it was merely a bargaining chip. Their security for the Undying Starfield would only be tighter than this.","But then Wen Xue added, “But I am not just anyone. I can enter the Undying Starfield.”"]},{"number":6480,"title":"Chapter 6480: Chapter 6478: Senior’s Treasure","paragraphs":["Chapter 6478: Senior’s Treasure","“Can you take me there, senior?” Chu Feng asked.","“Why do you want to go there? To wreak havoc? Do you harbor a huge grudge against the Netherworld Sect?” Wen Xue asked.","“I have my plans.”","“I’ll consider it based on your performance. Come in here first.”","Wen Xue grabbed her robe and pulled it down, revealing her fair shoulder and collarbone.","Chu Feng felt his blood rush. He had known she was beautiful, but he didn’t expect her to have such a good figure.","“Hoh, she has some substance.” Eggy stared at Wen Xue more intently than Chu Feng.","Chu Feng waved his hand and said, “Senior, I only offer my skills, not my body.”","“What nonsense are you spouting? I’m telling you to come in.”","Wen Xue formed a hand seal, and a spirit formation gate appeared beneath her collar bone. She had an innate formation realm inside her body!","“Senior, can’t you put the entrance in a more decent place?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s safer this way because of the proximity to my bloodline. Cut the crap. Are you coming in or not?” Wen Xue urged.","“Chu Feng, could this be a trap?” Eggy was worried.","She found Wen Xue unreliable, even though she had saved Zi Ling and Chu Feng before.","Just then, the Divine Deer interjected, “While that formation realm is fused with her bloodline, I can still take you out of there if needed. You don’t have to worry.”","She had spoken up to ease Chu Feng’s worries, knowing that Wen Xue was a special entity.","“All right.”","Chu Feng did harbor some reservations, but he was planning to trust Wen Xue. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have reached out to Wen Xue in the first place. Nevertheless, it was still best to have a backup plan in the worst-case scenario.","Chu Feng entered the formation realm.","It wasn’t big, but he could communicate freely with Wen Xue. She had also left the gate open, allowing him to leave whenever he wanted. This was done to dispel his worry.","“Junior, stay in there for the time being,” Wen Xue said.","She tidied up her robe, wore her veiled bamboo hat, and made her way to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant.","“Senior, how do we enter the remnant?” Chu Feng asked.","“We’ll enter it straight,” Wen Xue replied.","“Enter it straight?” Chu Feng was taken aback.","The Netherworld Sect forbade others from entering the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant because they planned to give it to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion for their alliance.","“Didn’t I tell you I’m not just anyone?” Wen Xue replied with a smile.","“Amazing.” Chu Feng shot her a thumbs-up.","While they were chatting, Wen Xue arrived at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant and entered it straight.","The corridor beyond its entrance felt awfully eerie, unlike the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s usual style.","Soon, a figure appeared in the corridor.","A middle-aged woman sat on the ground, cultivating. She had placed her veiled bamboo hat beside her, revealing her looks. She looked beautiful, but she had a sharp glare that made it known that she was not to be trifled with.","She must be Netherworld Marshall Wuma Hanshuang.","“Master, I’m back.” Wen Xue walked up to Wuma Hanshuang and bowed to her.","“Are you still going to enter?” Wuma Hanshuang asked, but her eyes remained closed and she continued to cultivate.","“Master, I’d like to continue trying,” Wen Xue replied.","“Lord Baili has sent word that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master has agreed to work with our Netherworld Sect. The two of them are currently making their way over.”","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master is coming? Then I shan’t enter lest I cause master trouble,” Wen Xue said.","There was a brief silence before Wuma Hanshuang said, “You can give it one last try. You should know what to say if you fail to leave in time and encounter the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, right?”","“I understand. I’ll say that I’m scouting the path for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master,” Wen Xue replied.","“Say that you did it under my order,” Wuma Hanshuang replied.","“Thank you, master.” Wen Xue bowed gratefully.","Wuma Hanshuang was offering to take responsibility for Wen Xue’s action to protect her.","“Go ahead and enter the remnant. Remember, you can take what you need, but don’t touch the legacy,” Wuma Hanshuang reminded.","“I understand,” Wen Xue replied.","She entered the corridor.","It was like a labyrinth, with many forks in the road, but Wen Xue navigated it with ease. Clearly, she had been here many times before.","“Does Wuma Hanshuang know what you’re after?” Chu Feng asked.","“She does. I told her what I wanted. But she doesn’t know that I’m bringing you in. You’d be in trouble if she ever finds out,” Wen Xue replied.","“That Wuma Hanshuang treats you very well, but won’t you be in trouble if I obtain the legacy?” Chu Feng asked.","“Obviously. I’d be implicated. Do you know who Lord Baili is? He is Baili Xukong, the leader of the Netherworld Sect’s new faction. Even Wuma Hanshuang is subservient to him despite being a Netherworld Marshall.","“But more importantly, Baili Xukong is Baili Zilin’s father. He won’t let you off if he learns that you’re here, not to mention that he’s with Jie Tianran. Naturally, I’ll be dragged into the mess, too. Wuma Hanshuang won’t protect me if she learns about this. I’ll have to flee with you from the Netherworld Sect.","“Do you finally understand how big a sacrifice I am making here?” Wen Xue said.","“I owe you a big one. I’ll do my best to help you obtain what you want,” Chu Feng replied. “Senior, we won’t be able to go to the Undying Starfield if you get exposed, right?”","“Junior Chu Feng, are you still thinking of going to the Undying Starfield? What a greedy one you are. You don’t have to worry. I have my way of bringing you there,” Wen Xue replied.","“You’re the best, senior.” Chu Feng smiled.","Wen Xue initially navigated the labyrinth with ease as if she were merely taking a stroll in her own backyard. She also overcame the obstacles along the way with ease. But her footsteps soon came to a halt.","This must be where she had gotten stuck.","Chu Feng thought it was finally time for him to make a move, but Wen Xue didn’t call for him. Instead, she took out a red compass with a flick of her wrist.","The red compass emanated the Ancient Era’s aura. Its surface was covered in noses that twitched as if it was sniffing for something, and it looked sinister and disgusting.","Wen Xue formed a hand seal and tapped the compass, prompting the noses to emanate auras that drifted eastward. She followed the auras and traveled eastward as well.","“Senior, where did you obtain this treasure from?” Chu Feng asked.","The compass resembled his Celestial Master’s Horsetail Whisk.","The Celestial Master’s Horsetail Whisk was a useful tool that had saved him many times in the past, but it was not very useful to him currently. In fact, it was inferior to his Heaven's Eyes now. Needless to say, it was also weaker than Wen Xue’s compass.","And the Celestial Master’s Horsetail Whisk was a sect-protection treasure of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect. Wen Xue’s compass must have quite an astounding background.","“I’d have lived for so many years in vain if I didn’t at least accumulate some fortune. Why? Do you want it?” Wen Xue asked.","“Sure, give it to me,” Chu Feng replied.","“Dream on. I won’t even trade it for that God Armament sword of yours,” Wen Xue scoffed."]},{"number":6481,"title":"Chapter 6481: Chapter 6479: Filled With Gu","paragraphs":["Chapter 6479: Filled With Gu","Despite Wen Xue’s formidable compass, she soon met a bottleneck. What stood before them was no longer a fork in the road but a spirit formation gate.","The spirit formation gate was covered in runes that appeared to be hints.","Sensing something amiss, Wen Xue stowed away her compass and called for Chu Feng, “Junior Chu Feng, you should come out and take a look.”","“Senior, you’ll have to lower your clothes a little.”","While Wen Xue had left the entrance to her body’s formation realm open, it was located under her clothes. Chu Feng could see past her clothes, but he couldn't travel through them when leaving her formation realm.","Wen Xue knew what Chu Feng was worried about, but she didn’t do as she was told. Instead, she remarked with a grin, “What are you afraid of? Getting stuck in my clothes?”","“That’s what I’m afraid of,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’ll tell Zi Ling if you dare take advantage of me.”","“That only makes me more scared.”","“Heh, I’m teasing you! Do I look like such a person? Feel free to dive right into my robes. I promise I won’t tell on you to Zi Ling.” Wen Xue laughed mischievously.","“Senior, stop messing around. We should get to business,” Chu Feng replied.","“Tsk, what a boring person you are. Forget it! You can come out now.”","Wen Xue tugged her robe downward.","Only then did Chu Feng dare to slip out of Wen Xue’s formation realm.","Wen Xue quickly tidied up her robe. There was no need for Chu Feng to hide inside her anymore now that they were inside the remnant.","“Senior, the formation realm inside your body is useful, but isn’t its entrance awfully inconvenient?” Chu Feng asked.","“What’s inconvenient about it? Why are you acting demure when I’m not even embarrassed? You’re the one taking advantage of me here,” Wen Xue scoffed.","“I’m no gentleman. I might lose control of myself at this rate.”","“Oh no! My talented junior, who is destined for greatness, wants to take advantage of me? I have no choice but to submit,” Wen Xue said flirtatiously. Her seductive demeanor contrasted with her youthful features, but that only made her more alluring.","As expected of an old demon who had been around for a long time. Playing innocent might be tough for her, but she can flirt with ease.","“I apologize. I shouldn’t have cracked such a joke with you.” Chu Feng had wanted to tease Wen Xue, since the latter had also been teasing him, but it would appear that he had messed with the wrong person.","“Who’s joking with you? I’m being serious here. Junior Chu Feng, won’t you consider me?”","Wen Xue stepped up to Chu Feng, allowing her chest to press against Chu Feng’s. It looked almost as if they were going to kiss the next second.","Chu Feng couldn’t tell if she was joking or being serious.","“Look at how arrogant she is! Chu Feng, screw her!” Eggy exclaimed.","She was the type to pour fuel on fire, but Chu Feng dared not push any further. He hurriedly took a step back to distance himself from her before turning his gaze to the spirit formation gate.","“Let’s focus on the main task at hand.”","Chu Feng activated his Heaven’s Eyes and soon deciphered some details. “Beyond this spirit formation gate is a formation. If we fail to breach the formation, we’ll lose our qualification to venture deeper into the remnant. Simply said, our journey will end here.”","“Got it.”","Wen Xue grabbed Chu Feng and dragged him into the spirit formation gate before he could utter a word.","They were transported into a space shrouded in fog. At the same time, the spirit formation gate vanished.","Chu Feng turned to Wen Xue and remarked helplessly, “Senior, shouldn’t you at least ask for my opinion before dragging me in here?”","“Junior, aren’t you here for the legacy? You only have two options—succeed or fail. If you can’t decipher this formation, we won’t be able to venture deeper into the remnant. If so, we can turn around and leave right away; there’s no point wasting time here. There’s no point in hesitating,” Wen Xue replied.","“I’m not hesitating. I was still studying the spirit formation gate to see if there were further clues regarding the deciphering of the formation,” Chu Feng replied with a sigh.","Wen Xue widened her eyes. “Why didn’t you say so earlier!”","“You didn’t give me a chance to speak up.”","“What do we do now? The spirit formation gate has vanished. I don’t think we can turn back, right?” Wen Xue lowered her head in shame, knowing she had acted hastily.","“It’s fine. We’re already in here anyway.”","Chu Feng remained calm. He lamented not being able to uncover more clues beforehand, but that didn’t mean he was helpless before the formation.","Clang!","Clang!","...","Metallic clangs echoed, and the fog dissipated, revealing their surroundings.","They were in a metal palace made out of countless parts. The walls were installed with convoluted mechanisms that seemed to contain a secret. Chu Feng and Wen Xue scanned their surroundings before looking forward, where a gigantic metal door stood.","The door was so huge that it covered half the wall, but it was covered in bugs.","The bugs were around the size of a fingernail, but there were countless of them scuttling around. Unnerving, colorful bumps grew out of their bodies.","“Ugh, disgusting! Look at my goosebumps!” Wen Xue cried out before hiding behind Chu Feng. There were still things that frightened her despite her old age, though she looked adorable.","“Senior, is this what you’re looking for? I’ll catch them for you,” Chu Feng pointed at the bugs as he asked.","“Of course not! Those are clearly gu bugs!” Wen Xue frowned.","Chu Feng revealed a mischievous smile. There was no way he couldn’t recognize those bugs when Wen Xue could do so.","Wen Xue noticed his smile and gritted her teeth. “You bastard. You knew I’m afraid of those bugs, but you intentionally asked that question to scare me!”","She angrily pinched Chu Feng’s arm without holding back at all. Chu Feng winced in pain.","“Stop stop stop, senior. I was wrong.”","“Hmph.” Wen Xue turned her gaze back to the gu bugs. “Looks like we’ll have to overcome those gus to advance, but why are there so many of them? Junior Chu Feng, have you found a way to decipher the formation yet?”","She eyed the metallic mechanisms, deducing that the solution lay in there.","Chu Feng replied, “Don’t bother studying those mechanisms. They don’t work.”"]},{"number":6482,"title":"Chapter 6482: Chapter 6480: Shangguan Fengquan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6480: Shangguan Fengquan","“Then what should we be focusing on?” Wen Xue was confused.","“That’s a feint. We have to let the gus enter our bodies,” Chu Feng replied.","“Huh? We have to let those disgusting bugs enter our bodies?” Wen Xue stared at the countless gus crawling on the metal door in fear.","“That’s right.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Won’t we be controlled by the gus?”","“It’s just a trial. It won’t control us for real.”","“How do you know?” Wen Xue frowned. She couldn’t accept the situation, especially since she could tell how dangerous the gus were.","“That’s what I have discerned.”","“So, we won’t be able to advance if we don’t allow the gus to enter our bodies? What about the formation then?”","“That’s why I said it’s a feint. It looks as if the key to overcoming this formation lies in the walls, but there’s no need to decipher the formation here. The key is to take in the gus.”","“How do you know?”","“I can tell from the gus. It may look like they are randomly clustered, but the thickness of their stack and the trajectory of their movements are all clues.”","“Are you sure?” Wen Xue remained skeptical.","“You can wait for me out here if you can’t accept the solution. I can venture into the remnant alone. If the monstrous entity you mentioned truly exists, I’ll try my best to capture it for you,” Chu Feng replied.","“That won’t do. I’ll go in with you. So, how do we take in the gus?” Wen Xue asked.","Chu Feng remotely grabbed a gu and presented it to Wen Xue. “Stretch your hand forth and allow it to enter your body. Remember, you have to accept it. You mustn’t resist it.”","“Eeee~” Wen Xue’s face was dripping with contempt, but she still stretched her fair hand forth.","Chu Feng placed the gu on Wen Xue’s palm. The gu morphed into a golden light and seeped inside her palm.","Wen Xue quickly got into a relaxed state, loosening even her frown. She was not some immature brat who couldn’t control her feelings; no matter how much she despised the gu, she still heeded Chu Feng’s instruction and allowed the gu into her without any resistance.","Spirit power manifested around Wen Xue and devoured her. She must have cleared the trial and was teleported out.","Chu Feng was not surprised. While he didn’t like to give guarantees, he was confident in his judgment.","He reached out and placed a gu on his palm. Warmth surged through his body. His consciousness plunged into darkness, but he still saw specks of light as if he were in a dark forest filled with fireflies.","A woman sat dignified on the ground not too far away, facing away from him. She wore simple garments. Her hair was mostly white from old age, but there were also strands of other colors as well—seven colors, to be exact. There was a peculiar beauty to it.","Before Chu Feng could utter a word, the old woman spoke, “You took in the gus fast. You must have outstanding discernment. But if you wish to obtain the legacy here, you have to truly grasp the meaning behind this world.”","The old woman picked up a burning wood and drew a word in mid-air using its flame.","Plunder.","Chu Feng felt intense heat gushing at him as if this character harnessed extraordinary power, but the ‘Plunder’ character only lasted for an instant.","The old woman proceeded to write another character out of fire.","Nurture .","This character felt gentle, unlike the previous ‘Plunder’, but it also only lasted an instant.","Then, Chu Feng’s consciousness returned to his body.","He was no longer in the metal palace but in a stone realm. With a quick glance, he saw countless caverns, each appearing to contain something extraordinary.","“Amazing! You were right, Junior Chu Feng! We advanced from the metal palace once we let those gus enter our bodies. Not anyone can get here. We’re incredible!” Wen Xue exclaimed as she made her way up to Chu Feng, looking at him with respect.","“Chu Feng, what do those two characters mean?” Eggy asked.","She shared sight and hearing with Chu Feng, though there were also remnants that Eggy couldn’t tap into Chu Feng’s senses. It depended on whether the remnant’s owner allowed others to see what Chu Feng could.","And she saw the place Chu Feng’s consciousness was transported to earlier.","“I’m not sure. I only noticed her writing ‘Nurture’ more forcefully than ‘Plunder’,” Chu Feng replied.","“There’s something special about that old woman. That should be an important clue, right?” Eggy asked.","“It should be.” Chu Feng nodded in agreement.","The old woman was a formation entity, devoid of sentience, but even so, Chu Feng could tell that she was no ordinary person, possibly a formidable figure from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect.","“Junior Chu Feng, did you see that old woman in that forest earlier?” Wen Xue asked.","“Mmhm. Senior, did you see her, too?” Chu Feng asked.","“I was evicted before I could utter a word. Did she speak to you?”","“She did.” Chu Feng told Wen Xue about the two characters the old woman left him.","“Just two characters? She didn’t leave you with a legacy or something?” Wen Xue asked.","“I’m afraid not.” Chu Feng shook his head.","“What a pity.” Wen Xue sighed in regret. “Junior Chu Feng, do you know who she is?”","“Senior, you know her?”","“She is Shangguan Fengquan, the sect master of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect before they left for the Ninth Galaxy. She was one of the strongest experts in the earlier years of the present era.”","“That elder was the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s sectmaster?” Chu Feng was not too surprised by that news, since that old woman felt extremely strong to him.","“That’s right. Isn’t it a pity to meet such an entity but not receive her legacy?” Wen Xue remarked.","“She was just a formation entity,” Chu Feng replied.","“Who says a formation entity can’t leave a legacy behind? This remnant itself is a formation, too!” Wen Xue exclaimed.","Chu Feng couldn’t retort against that. Wen Xue’s words made perfect sense.","“Forget it. Let’s focus on the task at hand. Junior Chu Feng, I can sense what I want in there,” Wen Xue said as she darted toward one of the caverns.","But Chu Feng grabbed her hand and stopped her. “Senior, you’ll die if you enter there now.”"]},{"number":6483,"title":"Chapter 6483: Chapter 6481: My Grandfather Is Here","paragraphs":["Chapter 6481: My Grandfather Is Here","“What do you mean?” Wen Xue was perplexed.","“You shouldn’t let your guard down just because we have come this far. You mustn’t enter the caverns with your physical body; you can only do so with your consciousness,” Chu Feng said.","“How do we do that? Cultivators of our level can’t actively project our consciousness from our body yet,” Wen Xue replied.","“You’re right, but there’s a formation here that can aid us in achieving that,” Chu Feng replied.","“Formation? Where? I don’t see it.”","“It’s well-concealed. I’ll need some time to find it as well. Senior, why don’t you cultivate first? I’ll teach you the method once I obtain it,” Chu Feng replied.","He activated Heaven’s Eyes and began surveying the surroundings.","Wen Xue took out the compass covered in noses, but the compass merely pointed at a cavern without providing any clues. She took out another treasure to enhance her observation, but she was still unable to discern anything.","She looked at Chu Feng. The latter was studying their surroundings earnestly while forming hand seals now and then. He didn’t seem to be lying to her.","“Junior, I can’t discern anything at all. I’ll leave it to you.”","Left with no choice, Wen Xue sat down and began cultivating. She didn’t expect Chu Feng’s observation to take days.","...","“Haaaa~” Wen Xue yawned loudly inside the stone realm while stretching her back. “Junior, is it really that tough? It has already been days!”","“I’m almost done. You just have to wait a bit longer,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’m not in a rush, but that trashy grandfather of yours is on his way here, right? He isn’t a pushover. We won’t be a match for him if he gets here,” Wen Xue said.","“Don’t worry, senior. There are multiple paths in the remnant, and each path promises different benefits. Jie Tianran will not take the same path as us,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is that so? Hold on! Doesn’t that mean that you’re missing out on better rewards by following my path?”","It suddenly dawned on Wen Xue that Chu Feng had uncovered clues along the way while following her, but he chose to follow her because what she wanted was on this path, even if it meant missing out on better rewards.","“Our path is the best path,” Chu Feng replied.","“You have a glib tongue,” Wen Xue said with a smile. She felt a surge of warmth in her heart.","Chu Feng didn’t criticize her or make any remarks to stoke her guilt. He didn’t hold a grudge against her despite being at a disadvantage. His tenderness made her happy.","Chu Feng was right. The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant had many correct paths.","Aside from the stone realm where they were, there was also a stiflingly dark underground realm. This underground realm was made from dark stones, and there were many caverns in there as well. In fact, the number of caverns in the underground realm matched that of the stone realm.","A person was in the underground realm—it was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, Jie Tianran. He had been here for ten hours now.","“I get it now.”","Jie Tianran was alone here, so his words were naturally intended for the entity inside him.","“What did you decipher?” the voice inside his body asked.","“We don’t have to project our consciousness into the cavern. Most caverns are dead ends; entering them results in immediate disqualification. There are only four correct paths, and we have to enter them in the correct sequence,” Jie Tianran replied.","“The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect is just a newborn power founded in the earlier years of this era, yet they dabble in such convoluted bullshit, thinking it elevates their stature. They must not have known that such means are viewed in contempt in our era.","“If they want to pass their legacy down, they can just test the challenger. There’s no need to make things so complicated,” the voice inside his voice scoffed.","Jie Tianran formed a hand seal. Countless glowing runes surfaced from the surrounding stone walls and gathered around him—he was invoking the underground realm’s formation.","He had spent ten hours figuring out how to channel the underground realm’s formation to draw out his consciousness. As the formation activated, his consciousness began pulling away from his body.","It was a success.","But Jie Tianran didn’t head for the cavern right away. Instead, he dispelled the formation, and his consciousness returned to his body.","“The formation works. Let’s go together,” Jie Tianran said. He conjured a formation blueprint with a wave of his sleeves.","“Do you need me to accompany you?” the voice in his body asked.","“I feel more confident with you around.”","“All right.”","The space around Jie Tianran warped. A black world spiritist cloak flew out of his body. This world spiritist cloak was puffed up as if someone were wearing it, but there were no feet beneath the cloak. However, a pair of old eyes gleamed beneath its hood as if a ghost had possessed it.","“Let’s begin,” a voice echoed from the cloak. It was the same voice as the entity inside Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran and the entity formed hand seals together. The runes surfaced, but this time, they shrouded not just Jie Tianran but that entity as well. Their consciousness drew away from their bodies and headed toward one of the caverns.","Meanwhile, in the stone realm, there was also a formation blueprint floating in the sky. Runes surfaced from the stone walls and shrouded Chu Feng and Wen Xue.","“Woah! Junior Chu Feng, you found a way to draw our consciousness out from our bodies! You’re amazing!” Wen Xue exclaimed in awe. She was only able to draw her consciousness out thanks to the formation blueprint Chu Feng had provided her.","“Let’s get going, senior.” Chu Feng made his way to one of the caverns.","“That’s wrong, junior. It’s that cavern.” Wen Xue pointed to another cavern.","“Senior, we have to follow the sequence,” Chu Feng said.","“Is that so?” Wen Xue murmured before following Chu Feng. She had made up her mind not to doubt Chu Feng’s judgment anymore.","In the meantime, Jie Tianran and the entity entered a barren formation realm. Their consciousness manifested as complete bodies in this realm, though their bodies were transparent like a soul.","Jie Tianran examined the sky, where countless runes reminiscent of birds swiftly darted by. Within these runes contained clues.","“Take it easy. No one is here to compete with you,” the entity said lackadaisically.","Weng!","Two figures suddenly appeared next to them. Jie Tianran and the entity were taken aback."]},{"number":6484,"title":"Chapter 6484: Chapter 6482: Wen Xue Cusses Out Jie Tianran","paragraphs":["Chapter 6482: Wen Xue Cusses Out Jie Tianran","The two figures were none other than Chu Feng and Wen Xue.","Chu Feng and Wen Xue were taken aback to see Jie Tianran and the entity beside him, too. Wen Xue even pointed at Jie Tianran and exclaimed aloud, “Holy shit! Junior Chu Feng, isn’t that your loser grandfather?”","She quickly realized what was going on and turned tail to flee, but her footsteps were shockingly slow despite her running with all her might.","Jie Tianran’s killing intent flared. His hand shot forth for not Wen Xue but Chu Feng’s neck.","Chu Feng stood nonchalantly in the face of Jie Tianran’s assault. It was not that he couldn’t avoid the attack, but he couldn’t be bothered to.","As he had expected, Jie Tianran’s hand passed right through his neck without hurting him.","Jie Tianran was stunned.","Chu Feng calmly spoke up, “I can’t believe a person like you is the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master. This place can only be accessed by one’s consciousness; you can’t bring your cultivation in here.”","His eyes were filled with disdain.","“Oh right. It’s my consciousness that’s in here. No wonder I run so slowly.” Wen Xue stopped escaping, but she didn’t return either, choosing to maintain her distance. She wasn’t sure if Jie Tianran had other means up his sleeves.","“Hahaha! Jie Tianran, your anger must have gotten to you! To think you aren’t as calm as your grandson!” The entity beside Jie Tianran burst into laughter.","Chu Feng eyed the spectral-like entity. This entity must be even more troublesome than Jie Tianran, or else he wouldn’t have dared speak to Jie Tianran in such a manner.","Jie Tianran did have other means up his sleeves.","“You bastard, Chu Feng. You just keep appearing everywhere I go,” Jie Tianran sneered.","“Is there anything wrong with a weak junior like me entering remnants to advance my cultivation?","“Rather, I should be the one asking: Jie Tianran, do you have no sense of shame? Don’t you find it embarrassing how, on the one hand, you claim that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is the strongest world spiritist power, but on the other hand, you are so desperate to obtain the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy?","“Above all, you, despite being the Mansion Master, have to bow down to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s rules and undergo their trials. I guess the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is still nowhere near on par with the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect,” Chu Feng said.","Jie Tianran’s cheeks twitched.","No one had ever dared to speak to him like that. His anger flared as he couldn’t stand anyone making light of him, but he didn’t make a move or lose his temper.","He knew he couldn’t do anything about Chu Feng in here. The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect must have designed this trial in this way to ensure fair competition.","“Chu Feng, I might not be able to do anything about you here, but do you think you and that insider you have in the Netherworld Sect can escape scot-free now that I have found you?” Jie Tianran eyed Wen Xue menacingly.","“It’s a misunderstanding! Chu Feng forced me to bring him in here. I am a victim!” Wen Xue frantically waved her hand as she tried to explain herself. But her face suddenly stiffened as she recalled what she said earlier, and she smacked her forehead. “Gah! I scolded him earlier!”","Knowing there was no way to turn back time, Wen Xue raised her head, her earlier innocence giving way to savagery. “You old thing! Yes, I am helping Chu Feng out. What about it? I dare you to beat me to death!","“Come on, make your move! You despicable, underhanded, ugly, sly, shameless, old beast! I have lived for many years, but I have never seen anyone as disgusting as you!","“You claim that you only turned against your daughter because she sullied your bloodline. Please! You were merely angry because you couldn’t control her anymore.","“You said that Chu Feng’s father is a good-for-nothing, but you would have known otherwise if you looked into the Ancestral Martial Starfield. Chu Feng’s father is a true prodigy; he only grew slower due to the scarce resources there. That much should be obvious just by looking at Chu Feng’s overwhelmingly powerful Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. A good-for-nothing couldn’t have had such a formidable son.","“You refuse to acknowledge Chu Feng and his father because you’re angry that you failed to control Lord Jie Ranqing, so you directed your anger toward Chu Feng. You’re so shameless that you would attempt to plunder your own grandson’s bloodline. I’ve never seen someone as shameless as you.","“You only became the Mansion Master because you were unscrupulous enough to backstab everyone around you to acquire a bit of power. Do you think your people truly respect you? No, they are just afraid of you. Who knows how much they despise you on the inside?","“No one sane would respect a scum like you!” Wen Xue pointed at Jie Tianran and cussed him out at a rapid pace, leaving no room for the latter to argue back.","Chu Feng could hear Jie Tianran gnashing his teeth. The latter’s killing intent was palpable even though they were mere consciousness here.","All of a sudden, everyone raised their heads. The runes reminiscent of birds were buzzing loudly in the sky.","What they had to do now was to acquire the benefits hidden here, and the runes were the clue. They might have lost their cultivation, but they retained their observation prowess. Neither Chu Feng nor Jie Tianran wanted to lose out, so they began observing the runes intently.","Wen Xue tried observing the runes as well, but she gave up shortly after and sat on the ground. She felt helpless. She sensed that something was hidden in the runes, but she couldn’t decipher it.","Soon, Jie Tianran began forming hand seals. A red aura emanated from his body.","Almost at the same time, Chu Feng also formed hand seals, but he emanated a green aura instead.","“Activate!” the two yelled at the same time.","The runes plummeted from the sky and fused into their bodies; Chu Feng took in the green runes, whereas Jie Tianran took in the red runes.","Moments later, the runes transformed into living entities.","Little green saplings sprouted on the desert over on Chu Feng’s side.","A red, translucent egg manifested on Jie Tianran’s side. A ferocious beast could be vaguely seen inside the egg."]},{"number":6485,"title":"Chapter 6485: Chapter 6483: Nurture and Plunder","paragraphs":["Chapter 6483: Nurture and Plunder","“What’s that, Junior Chu Feng? Why is your aura different from that of your loser grandfather?”","Wen Xue was reluctant to ask this question because they couldn’t do voice transmission here, but she was burning with curiosity.","She could tell that Chu Feng and Jie Tianran had grasped the formation from the runes above, but she couldn’t understand why the results were different. Furthermore, Jie Tianran’s egg felt more imposing than Chu Feng’s sprout.","“We have to accrue energy here to open the spirit formation gate to leave this place. There are two ways to accrue energy. One is through nurturing plants that innately harness the energy, and the other is to plunder energy from the surroundings. We can only choose one of the two.”","Chu Feng didn’t bother to be discreet, knowing Jie Tianran must have deciphered the rules, too.","“I see. That’s what ‘nurture’ and ‘plunder’ mean,” the entity beside Jie Tianran remarked. He turned to Chu Feng and asked, “You must have met that person as well, didn’t you?”","“Who are you talking about?” Chu Feng feigned ignorance.","“There’s no need to put on an act. Who else can I possibly be talking about other than the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s sectmaster, Shangguan Fengquan? You can’t have reached this place without meeting her,” the entity asked.","“So what if I met her?” Chu Feng asked.","From that, he understood that Jie Tianran had met Shangguan Fengquan as well.","“Did you choose ‘nurture’ because Shangguan Fengquan wrote the word with more force? If so, I should let you know that you have chosen wrong,” the entity said.","Chu Feng scoffed, “Yet another fellow who is full of himself. You don’t look like someone from the present era. Your years must be numbered now?”","“Indeed, I’m nearing the limit of my lifespan. A brat like you would be perfect for extending my lifespan. Today could be the day,” the entity laughed eerily.","“We’ll see if you have the ability to pull that off,” Chu Feng replied as he continued forming hand seals.","His sprout swiftly grew into a towering tree over a thousand meters tall.","On the other side, Jie Tianran’s egg hatched into a red monstrous beast, and it grew to over three hundred meters tall. It was smaller than Chu Feng’s massive tree, but it exuded greater power.","But there was a fundamental difference between the two.","The energy emanated by Chu Feng’s tree became increasingly concentrated as it matured, whereas the red monstrous beast didn’t wield such a power.","Instead, the red monstrous beast opened its mouth wide and devoured the surrounding energy. The amount of energy it devoured was nowhere close to the amount harnessed by Chu Feng’s tree, but it allowed the red monstrous beast to evolve.","The red monstrous beast started with a single mouth, but as it devoured more energy, three more mouths grew on the back of its head. Eventually, its eyes, nose, and ears disappeared in favor of growing more mouths.","Despite its increasingly hideous appearance, it was becoming more powerful.","Chu Feng’s massive tree soon grew to over ten thousand meters tall. Its leaves glowed, and its branches swayed ever so slightly. Its presence changed the surrounding air as if a divine tree.","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran’s red monstrous beast grew to over a thousand meters tall. The energy it harnessed was still weaker than Chu Feng’s massive tree, but it was starting to get close.","But there was only so much energy in this realm. The energy available for the red monstrous beast to devour grew less and less.","Boom!","An explosion could be heard, and the realm began to collapse in on them.","Wen Xue turned to Jie Tianran and roared, “Stop absorbing your energy! Your hideous monster is absorbing the very foundation of this realm!”","Weng!","A spatial rift suddenly appeared. It was a spirit formation gate.","“It looks like we have cleared the test,” Wen Xue said in delight.","Even though the realm was collapsing on them, they could leave before it reached them. They might have chosen different methods, but Chu Feng had clearly obtained more energy. Even if they left now, they would still wield the advantage.","Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and the massive tree began to miniaturize. He planned to take the massive tree out of here, for he sensed that the tree’s energy would play a role later on.","Jie Tianran flitted toward the spirit formation gate, and the hideous red monstrous beast followed him like a pet. Just as he was about to enter the spirit formation gate, he suddenly stopped, turned around, and formed a hand seal.","Whoosh!","The red monstrous beast transformed into a massive mouth and exerted a strong suction force, directed at Chu Feng’s massive tree.","Huuuuuu!","Chu Feng’s massive tree began losing its energy to the red monstrous beast.","“You despicable bastard, Jie Tianran! You’re going too far!” Wen Xue roared in anger.","Chu Feng frowned. He hurriedly formed a hand seal to stop the red monstrous beast. It worked, but its effectiveness was limited.","The entity beside Jie Tianran sneered, “Chu Feng, do you think Jie Tianran and I can’t tell that we can obtain more energy from ‘nurture’? But this trial is more than just a test; it’s a reflection of the world of cultivation.","“Those who stay in their places are sheep destined for the slaughterhouse. Only those who are tenacious enough to plunder from others can reach the top of the world of cultivation. If one has to choose between ‘nurture’ and ‘plunder’, the answer has to be ‘plunder’.","“And we were right. This red monstrous beast can evolve after plundering energy. Do you understand it now? You thought you had claimed the initiative, but you are merely paving the path for us.”","By this point, the red monstrous beast’s energy had surpassed that of Chu Feng’s massive tree."]},{"number":6486,"title":"Chapter 6486: Chapter 6484: We’ll Go Down Together","paragraphs":["Chapter 6484: We’ll Go Down Together","“If a fight is what you want, a fight is what you’ll get,” Chu Feng replied.","He changed his hand seal. The lush tree that had been compressed to less than a hundred meters tall suddenly reverted to its ten-thousand-meter-tall stature. Its branches shot out like serpents to seal the spirit formation gate.","“You have such means?” Wen Xue was amazed.","“Heh...” Jie Tianran scoffed.","The red monstrous beast opened its mouth wide to devour the branches sealing the spirit formation gate, but its teeth passed right through the branches. Somehow, the two entities were unable to make contact!","Jie Tianran’s smile stiffened. He tried to touch the branches with his hand—it felt solid. His face further darkened.","The red monstrous beast couldn’t destroy the tree, and his consciousness couldn’t leave the realm unless the tree was destroyed. Time was not on his side, as the realm was collapsing on them. Who knew what would happen if their consciousness remained in the collapsing realm?","Chu Feng was planning to bring them down with him!","“Chu Feng, you must be desperate. Do you think I’d fear you?” Jie Tianran glared at Chu Feng.","“Return my energy to me. Otherwise, none of us is getting out of here,” Chu Feng replied.","“So be it. Let me see what will happen once this realm collapses!” Jie Tianran scoffed.","The realm was collapsing so quickly that even Wen Xue panicked. It was unlikely they would escape unscathed if their consciousness were to be caught in this destruction.","Wen Xue made her way to Chu Feng’s side, grabbed his sleeves, and said, “Forget it, Junior Chu Feng. Let’s not stoop down to their level. We can always turn the tables on them as long as we continue living. It won’t be worthwhile to give our lives away for those two old things.”","But Chu Feng quietly stared at Jie Tianran, determined to pit his guts against the latter.","“Junior Chu Feng, why are you so stubborn? Those two already have a foot in the grave, but we’re still young. It isn’t worth it!” Wen Xue panicked.","But Chu Feng remained firm.","Jie Tianran coldly looked at Chu Feng. He also seemed determined to wait it out to the end.","The previously boundless realm had been reduced to a pitch black void, and the collapse was already on the verge of reaching them.","“Jie Tianran, return the energy to him. There’s no need to go this far against a mere child,” the entity succumbed first and issued an order to Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran finally formed a hand seal, and the red monstrous beast opened its mouth and returned the mysterious energy it had devoured from Chu Feng’s tree.","In response, Chu Feng formed a hand seal and compressed the tree. At the same time, the branches blocking the spirit formation gate retracted back to the tree.","Jie Tianran glared at Chu Feng before stepping into the spirit formation gate.","The entity looked at Chu Feng and remarked, “Chu Feng, the truly strong will not pit their lives against others. You won’t be this lucky the next time we meet.”","“Old thing, the next time we meet, I’ll rip off your hood and expose that hideous face that you dare not show others,” Wen Xue scoffed.","“Hmph!” The entity harrumphed before leaving via the spirit formation gate.","Wen Xue was so anxious that she rushed to the spirit formation gate, but she stopped at the entrance and urged Chu Feng to hurry.","“The tree’s roots are too deeply lodged in the ground. I need to compress it further before I can take it with me.” Chu Feng revealed the reason he was still staying put.","“Hurry up, Junior Chu Feng,” Wen Xue urged.","“Don’t worry, I’ll make it in time.” Chu Feng was calm in contrast.","His calculation was on the dot. Before the destruction could engulf him, he reduced the tree to the size of a sapling, picked it up, and stepped through the spirit formation gate with Wen Xue.","They returned to the stone realm. Wen Xue looked at the sapling sitting on Chu Feng’s palm. The tree was still emanating a green light, and it commanded the same imposing aura despite its smaller size.","“You really brought it out. Is there a use for it later?” Wen Xue asked.","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded.","“That grandfather of yours is a loser, but Junior Chu Feng, you’re too obstinate. We nearly lost our lives there,” Wen Xue said grudgingly.","“I was just intimidating them into submission. I wouldn’t have done that if he truly had the guts to hold it till the very end. Why would I give my life away in vain?”","“Are you sure about that?” Wen Xue narrowed her eyes in skepticism. She thought that Chu Feng was serious about it.","“Of course. I wouldn’t put your life at risk, senior.”","“Oh? You care that much about me?” Wen Xue further narrowed her eyes in skepticism.","“Senior, shouldn’t you at least trust me that much?” Chu Feng asked with a smile.","“Fine. Which cavern do we enter next?” Wen Xue asked.","“That one.”","Chu Feng led Wen Xue toward another cavern.","As soon as Chu Feng entered the cavern, a surge of spirit power tugged his consciousness into a blank space. In that blank space, Chu Feng saw another figure—his physical body. It stood in the same pose as it did in the stone realm, and he could clearly feel its bloodline power.","“Oh? I can choose a bloodline power to take with me?”","Chu Feng’s consciousness walked up to his physical body and reached into it. Two powerful bloodline powers stirred inside his physical body.","Clearly, the next trial required him to channel his bloodline power to accomplish a task.","Chu Feng’s first thought was to take the Ruler’s Bloodline with him, considering that this was a world spiritist trial. But he quickly noticed something that made his eyes light up.","“I see.” Chu Feng spent a moment in thought before making an unbelievable choice.","He reached for his Heavenly Lightning Bloodline, but instead of taking it right away, he closed his eyes as if trying to sense something. He stayed in this state for a while before finally taking the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline into his consciousness.","His surroundings morphed.","He was transported to an island surrounded by gigantic waves.","“Junior Chu Feng, what took you so long?” Wen Xue rushed to his side and exclaimed.","She was panicking because Jie Tianran and that entity were on this island, too."]},{"number":6487,"title":"Chapter 6487: Chapter 6485: I’ll Play With You","paragraphs":["Chapter 6485: I’ll Play With You","Massive waves roared as they crashed down on the island, resembling ferocious beasts encircling their prey.","Jie Tianran stood by the corner of the island, channeling the red monstrous beast to maneuver within the devastating waves.","Iridescent lights resembling rainbows flowed within the water—they were all large schools of fish, which came in all colors. They looked mesmerizing.","The red monstrous beast was busy catching fish. There were so many fish that the red monstrous beast could devour an entire patch of them just by opening its mouth, but most fish simply passed through the red monstrous beast’s mouth and stomach.","Only one type of fish could be trapped inside the red monstrous beast’s belly—a golden, translucent fish that was only the length of a finger. There were very few of these fish, and they swam extremely fast. They were harder to capture compared to the other fish.","It had been some time since Jie Tianran arrived here, but the red monstrous beast only had thirty golden fish in its belly. The golden fish was being broken down and assimilated by the red monstrous beast, but the process was extremely slow.","“What do we do, Junior Chu Feng? Your loser grandfather is using his red monstrous beast to catch and assimilate golden fish. Those golden fish must be important here. Can your tree catch fish, too?” Wen Xue was worried.","“Of course it can.”","Chu Feng put the sapling down and formed a hand seal. The sapling swiftly grew to over ten thousand meters in height. The tree branches extended into the sea before weaving together into a net. The net was placed in the vicinity of the red monstrous beast.","The red monstrous beast’s forceful movements sent the fish scattering into the surroundings. Many fish naturally swam into Chu Feng’s net, but most simply passed through it. The golden fish are the only ones caught by the net.","It didn’t take long for the net to catch several golden fish.","“Well done, Junior Chu Feng!” Wen Xue was overjoyed.","At this rate, Chu Feng could capture far more fish than Jie Tianran thanks to the wider range of his net.","“Hmph!” Jie Tianran scoffed.","Wen Xue shouted to Jie Tianran,” Too slow, old pervert. Get your little pet to swim faster! Are your reactions slowing down because age has caught up with you? You won’t catch as many fish as my Junior Chu Feng at this rate. You sure are useless. You should stop being a waste of space and just drop dead.”","Jie Tianran’s face darkened. He was so used to being fawned on by others that he couldn’t accept being insulted in such a crude manner. However, he didn’t bother arguing with Wen Xue. He focused on channeling the red monstrous beast to continue catching golden fish.","But as big as his red monstrous beast’s mouth was, it was still nowhere as wide as Chu Feng’s net. Soon, there were more fish in Chu Feng’s net than in the red monstrous beast’s belly.","By the time six hours had passed, Chu Feng’s tree had caught twice as many golden fish as the red monstrous beast.","Just then, a massive spatial rift appeared in the middle of the island. A spirit formation gate was manifesting.","“It’s finally over. It looks like we have caught the required number of golden fish.” Wen Xue looked at the spirit formation gate with gleeful eyes.","GWAH!","The red monstrous beast suddenly spat out all the golden fish in its mouth with a roar.","“What’s that old pervert up to? Is he giving up?” Wen Xue was perplexed, but she had a feeling Jie Tianran was scheming something.","Jie Tianran changed his hand seal. The red monstrous beast emanated an iridescent aura identical to that of the schools of fish. At the same time, the manifestation speed of the spirit formation gate suddenly accelerated.","“Something is amiss. Junior Chu Feng, what’s going on?” Wen Xue looked at Chu Feng in bewilderment.","GWAR!","The red monstrous beast opened its mouth wide and devoured a large patch of fish. This time, even the fish of other colors couldn’t escape from the red monstrous beast’s mouth and belly.","Jie Tianran looked at Chu Feng in contempt and scorn.","The entity beside Jie Tianran scoffed, “Chu Feng, you might be talented, but you’re too young. You couldn’t tell that the golden fish are the most useless ones here. It is the other fish that harness true power. Jie Tianran released the other fish to make you think that catching the golden fish is the key to clearing this test. You thought you were getting ahead of us, but you were squandering your energy on a useless endeavor.”","“No, that’s impossible!” Wen Xue exclaimed. “The other fish pass right through the red monstrous beast. How can the red monstrous beast siphon energy from them? What did you do?”","“Hah! Lass, who told you that you have to capture the fish to siphon their energy?” the entity sneered.","Wen Xue widened her eyes in realization.","It might look like the other fish had safely passed through the red monstrous beast’s belly, but the truth was that the red monstrous beast had already devoured their energies.","That must have been the reason the red monstrous beast wasn’t moving particularly fast. It was busy siphoning energy from other fish.","“You shameless old bastards. Aren’t you embarrassed to be resorting to underhanded tricks against a junior?” Wen Xue roared.","Chu Feng suddenly interjected, “There are fools here, but it isn’t me.”","Chu Feng retracted his net and released the golden fish he had captured back into the water. He changed his hand seal, and the tree also emanated an iridescent aura. Its aura was even stronger than what the red monstrous beast released.","“I’m merely playing with you. Do you think I can’t tell as much?” Chu Feng sneered."]},{"number":6488,"title":"Chapter 6488: Chapter 6486: Combat Experience","paragraphs":["Chapter 6486: Combat Experience","“As expected of Junior Chu Feng!” Wen Xue was overjoyed.","But then, the entity accompanying Jie Tianran laughed. “Hahaha... Jie Tianran, it looks like we really can’t underestimate this grandson of yours!”","Wen Xue’s face turned grim. The other party must be confident if he could laugh in this situation. This didn’t bode well for them.","Jie Tianran sneered, “I shan’t hold back either.”","Jie Tianran released a golden aura from his body and fused it into the red monstrous beast. That golden aura was Jie Tianran’s world spiritist bloodline. The red monstrous beast’s aura immediately flared as if having undergone a metamorphosis.","But Jie Tianran didn’t order the red monstrous beast to attack Chu Feng right away. “Chu Feng, let me see what your Ruler’s Bloodline is capable of.”","He deduced that since he could bring his bloodline power in here, the same must be true for Chu Feng.","“You want to clash with my bloodline? I’ll grant your wish.”","Chu Feng formed a hand seal and unleashed nine-colored lightning from his body.","“The Heavenly Lightning Bloodline?”","Both Jie Tianran and the entity beside him were stunned.","“Junior Chu Feng, why...”","Even Wen Xue was perplexed.","“Hahahaha...” A moment later, the entity beside Jie Tianran burst into laughter. “You, who possess the strongest Ruler’s Bloodline, chose to bring a cultivator’s bloodline to a world spiritist trial? Jie Tianran, this grandson of yours truly thinks lowly of you!”","Jie Tianran’s face darkened. He also thought that Chu Feng was making light of him. With a cold harrumph, he changed his hand seal.","GRAR!","With a deafening roar, the red monstrous beast opened its mouth and unleashed a red beam of light at Chu Feng.","“Junior Chu Feng, you mustn’t let your guard down,” Wen Xue anxiously reminded.","The red monstrous beast couldn’t hurt Chu Feng or his tree earlier, but things could be different now that Jie Tianran had infused his bloodline power into the red monstrous beast. It was likely capable of hurting Chu Feng now, or else Jie Tianran wouldn’t have launched this attack.","This attack was unlikely to hurt them, since only their consciousness had been transported into this realm, but being defeated here likely spelled elimination.","But Wen Xue’s worry was unfounded.","Tzlala!","Chu Feng infused his nine-colored lightning into his tree. Its branches began extending like lightning rods.","“Hmph!” Jie Tianran sneered.","Chu Feng’s nine-colored lightning was formidable, and so was the tree he had nurtured. However, the tree was made out of spirit power, whereas the nine-colored lightning was the manifestation of a cultivator's bloodline. They were incompatible with each other.","Even though the tree had undergone a metamorphosis after being infused with Chu Feng’s Heavenly Lightning Bloodline, becoming capable of unleashing attacks, its fighting prowess was inferior to that of the red monstrous beast. Even if it could stop the red monstrous beast’s attack, it would sustain significant damage in the process.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","The lightning branches suddenly coiled together to form something that resembled a massive lightning sword. The sword swung downward, slicing the red beam of light into two.","“This...” Jie Tianran was stunned.","The lightning sword’s attack didn’t stop there. It continued extending toward Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran changed his hand seal, causing the red monstrous beast’s aura to flare more fervently than before. The red monstrous beast swiped its claws against the approaching lightning sword.","BAM!","The sharp claws collided with the lightning sword, striking it off its trajectory.","But the lightning sword suddenly became soft, transforming into a gigantic lightning whip that lashed at Jie Tianran.","The red monstrous beast retreated to Jie Tianran’s side to block the lightning whip.","The lightning whip was shockingly nimble, and its movements were unpredictable. The red monstrous beast managed to block the lightning whip’s lashes, but it was unable to launch a counterattack.","“Well done, Junior Chu Feng!” Wen Xue cheered.","Even though Chu Feng’s attacks had failed to hurt Jie Tianran, he had managed to claim the upper hand in this clash and force the latter into a defensive position.","In truth, the tree was weaker than the red monstrous beast; this was evident from how the red monstrous beast withstood the lightning whip’s relentless aggression. What made the difference here was Chu Feng’s combat tactics.","Chu Feng’s moves were layered. Every attack he dished out contained a trap, and they strung together to form a bottomless pitfall that Jie Tianran simply couldn’t climb out of.","This was the combat sense honed by cultivators.","Jie Tianran was a powerful world spiritist, and he had been through many battles as well. However, his combat style was centered around combining formations together in intricate ways to throw his opponent off the loop.","Unfortunately, he could only control the red monstrous beast here, which turned this battle into a straightforward, close-quarter combat.","Such a simple duel format was to Chu Feng’s advantage.","The entity beside Jie Tianran realized that as well, and the smile on his face faded. It was humiliating for a veteran who had lived for tens of thousands of years to be suppressed by a junior in combat.","Boom!","Roaring sounds echoed in the distance. The spirit formation gate had fully opened.","The ocean realm began crumbling like the previous desert realm.","“Stop wasting time, Jie Tianran,” the entity said, knowing that Jie Tianran wouldn’t be able to defeat Chu Feng here.","“Fine, Chu Feng. I’ll let you prance around for a while longer. It won’t make a difference anyway. You can’t defeat me.”","The red monstrous beast opened its mouth and exerted a bizarre suction force. This time, it siphoned energy from not just the tree but the surroundings as well. While Jie Tianran couldn’t defeat Chu Feng, he could still devour his tree’s energy.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal. Several branches extended from the tree to seal off the spirit formation gate.","“You could have told me straight if you didn't want to leave.”","It was the same trick Chu Feng had used against Jie Tianran in the desert realm to force him to spit out the energy he had siphoned away.","“Aren’t you going to make a move? We won’t be able to leave at this rate,” Jie Tianran asked the entity beside him.","“Kikiki... Chu Feng, do you think the same trick would work twice against us?” The entity laughed gleefully as he formed a hand seal.","Boom!","A green aura gushed out from the entity’s body and fused into the red monstrous beast, causing the red monstrous beast to transform once more. Its aura felt more sinister than ever.","Above all, it had grown far stronger than before. With a single swipe, it tore through Chu Feng’s lightning branch."]},{"number":6489,"title":"Chapter 6489: Chapter 6487: Senior, Why Didn’t You Help Me?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6487: Senior, Why Didn’t You Help Me?","“This isn’t good!” Wen Xue’s eyes narrowed.","She didn’t think the red monstrous beast could grow even stronger. At this rate, she had to worry about whether she and Chu Feng could even safely leave the ocean realm or not.","Tzzzz!","Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and more lightning branches surged at the red monstrous beast. This time, the lightning branches encircled the red monstrous beast and attacked it from different angles.","The red monstrous beast would shred the lightning branches as soon as it came within range, but the lightning branches simply regrew infinitely and continued their assault.","“Junior Chu Feng, you...” Wen Xue looked at Chu Feng with complicated eyes.","The tree could only regrow its branches so quickly thanks to Chu Feng channeling it, but that also resulted in the weakening of Chu Feng’s consciousness.","Wen Xue felt helpless. She couldn’t tell Chu Feng to stop fighting, or else the red monstrous beast would simply crush them. Their only option was to go all out.","“You’re still struggling?” Jie Tianran sneered, knowing that Chu Feng wouldn’t last long at this rate. The latter was merely stalling for time.","It was unlikely that Chu Feng would sustain any tangible damage if his consciousness dissipated here, but that ought to spell his disqualification from this trial. Even if he could enter the cavern once more, his progress was bound to be a step slower.","Soon, Jie Tianran’s smile faded. He realized that he had underestimated Chu Feng.","Despite Chu Feng’s consciousness flickering unstably, it refused to extinguish.","While he was still holding on, the ocean realm continued to collapse. Seeing that, Jie Tianran and the entity beside him got on top of the red monstrous beast and made their way toward the spirit formation gate. They had decided to leave instead of holding their ground.","But Chu Feng was prepared for that as well.","More branches extended from the tree. Some blocked Jie Tianran’s path, whereas the others reinforced the seal on the spirit formation gate.","The red monstrous beast furiously shredded the tree branches, but more tree branches grew out to block the path. The red monstrous beast was destroying the tree branches faster than they could regrow, so it was only a matter of time before the seal was breached, but the problem was that the ocean realm was collapsing too quickly.","Time was not on Jie Tianran’s side.","“Forget it, Jie Tianran. Return the energy to him. We can deal with him in the subsequent caverns,” the entity advised.","“That brat might think I’m afraid of him if I keep conceding. I’ll start this trial from scratch if necessary. Worse comes to worst, I’ll give up on this legacy. It’s not like I’m lacking in legacies.”","But Jie Tianran took a tough stance this time. He ignored the entity’s order and was determined to push this to the very end.","“Forget it, Junior Chu Feng. That loser grandfather of yours isn’t a human. He’s a mad dog. There’s no point pitting it out with him. You won’t bite a dog just because a dog bites you, right? Don’t forget our goal here. Let him go. It’s just a small setback,” Wen Xue advised.","Chu Feng didn’t answer, but his unyielding expression said it all.","Left with no choice, Wen Xue could only coerce Chu Feng into giving in, “Junior Chu Feng, can’t you do it for me? You owe me a favor, remember? You know I want the item in here. Are you not going to repay my favor anymore?”","That worked like a charm. Chu Feng hesitated before retracting the tree branches sealing the spirit formation gate.","“Hmph...” Jie Tianran snorted. He finally managed to get back at Chu Feng after being humiliated in the desert realm. With a triumphant smirk, he rode the red monstrous beast out of the ocean realm.","Chu Feng also left the ocean realm with Wen Xue. He had gained greater control over the tree, allowing him to shrink it much faster than before.","The two of them returned to the stone realm.","“Not bad, Junior Chu Feng. At least you do have some respect for me.” Wen Xue nodded in satisfaction.","Chu Feng had intended to pit it out with his grandfather earlier. He had only given in because of Wen Xue.","“That goes without saying, but senior... Even Jie Tianran had the aid of that old monster, so why did you just watch the commotion and not lend a helping hand?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’d love to help you, junior, but there’s nothing I can do.” Wen Xue looked indignant.","“Didn’t you bring a bloodline power in?”","“I did, but I couldn’t use it.”","“Really?”","“Of course! I wouldn’t lie to you.”","“All right. Let’s continue.” Chu Feng remained motivated, even though he had conceded because of Wen Xue.","“Which one do we go next?” Wen Xue asked.","Chu Feng had previously told her that they needed to enter four caverns in the right order, but there were so many caverns in this stone realm that she had no idea which one to enter. They would have to start from scratch if they entered the wrong one.","“We’re entering the one you want to enter the most,” Chu Feng replied.","“Finally!”","Wen Xue was overjoyed since the item was finally within reach. She entered the cavern first, and Chu Feng followed closely behind.","The two of them were transported into a lush forest realm.","Even the shortest tree here was at least fifty meters tall. The taller ones could easily reach thousands of meters in height. The contrast in height made Chu Feng and Wen Xue look like ants, and it didn’t help that they were currently just conscious beings without their cultivation.","This forest realm was larger than the previous two realms. There were creatures residing in this forest, and bugs could be heard buzzing in the surroundings. The buzzes were so loud that they resembled roars of ferocious beasts.","Both Jie Tianran and the entity accompanying him were nowhere to be seen, but it was certain that they were already here. Jie Tianran understood the importance of claiming the initiative, so he would have entered right away.","Chances were that they were simply transported to a different place.","“Junior Chu Feng, I can feel it. Quick, come with me,” Wen Xue said as she sprinted off in a direction. She had a wide grin that reflected her excitement.","Chu Feng was curious what the item she coveted was."]},{"number":6490,"title":"Chapter 6490: Chapter 6488: Lotus Gu","paragraphs":["Chapter 6488: Lotus Gu","The forest was practically a labyrinth, but fortunately, Wen Xue could sense the location of the item she sought. Their only complaint was that their traveling speed was much slower as they had lost their cultivation.","They took ages to travel a distance that would have only taken them an instant before.","While sprinting ahead, Wen Xue suddenly tugged Chu Feng’s sleeve and asked, “Junior Chu Feng, don’t you think this is not too bad?”","“What do you mean?”","“I’m talking about temporarily losing our cultivation and becoming weak. Doesn’t that make you cherish your cultivation even more?” Wen Xue asked.","“I have always cherished my cultivation,” Chu Feng replied.","Wen Xue sighed. “You’re a weird one, Junior Chu Feng.”","“How so?” Chu Feng asked.","“Sometimes, I find you interesting. Other times, you just render me speechless.”","“I don’t like to engage in idle chatter while at work.”","“Got it. I’ll shut up.”","Chu Feng smiled. Despite having known Wen Xue for some time, he still lacked understanding about her. This encounter did give him a better grasp of her personality. She had an old soul in her junior body. While she often acted innocent, she did have an adorable personality.","Just like that, Wen Xue sprinted across the forest with Chu Feng for two whole hours before the scenery before them brightened up.","A lake appeared before their eyes.","A glowing white lotus that was over a thousand meters tall floated in the middle of the lake. It resembled a beautiful artwork, and there was no doubt that it was something extraordinary. Its petals were transparent, revealing a beautiful meter long bug sleeping inside.","The lotus was transparent, so a meter-long bug could be seen inside.","“That’s the one, Junior Chu Feng! That’s the thing I’m looking for. Can you acquire it for me?” Wen Xue tugged Chu Feng’s sleeve as she pointed at the lotus. She looked like a child who had just seen something she fancied.","In truth, she could sense danger lurking in the lotus.","“Senior, do you want the bug or the lotus?” Chu Feng asked.","“The lotus,” Wen Xue replied.","“Actually, the mission in this realm is to collect a gu. The bug inside that lotus is an excellent gu. Since you want the lotus, I’ll take that gu,” Chu Feng said.","“Do you have a solution?” Wen Xue’s eyes lit up.","“Of course. Watch me.”","Chu Feng placed the tree down, and the tree swiftly grew to its full glory. Its branches crackled with lightning as it abruptly stretched outward to attack the lotus.","Weng!","As the lightning branches drew close, the lotus suddenly conjured a brilliant light sphere around it that vaporized everything within range.","But Chu Feng was already prepared for that. He used the tree’s endless regeneration to launch a ceaseless stream of attacks against the lotus.","“Junior Chu Feng, are you all right?” Wen Xue was worried, knowing that this fighting style would place a burden on Chu Feng’s consciousness.","“Don’t worry, I can hold on,” Chu Feng replied with a confident smile.","The light sphere steadily weakened under the relentless assault of the lightning branches, till it completely dissipated four hours later.","Chu Feng retracted the lightning branches, but his attack wasn’t over yet. The tree released a stream of hypnotic energy against the lotus, and the lotus began to diminish in size.","“Junior Chu Feng, what are you doing now?” Wen Xue asked out of curiosity.","“The lotus still retains its offensive prowess even though it is no longer protected by that light sphere, but based on what I have observed, its offensive ability declines as it shrinks. My tree happens to have a power that curbs it. I can hypnotize it and make it diminish in size,” Chu Feng replied.","“You’re so reliable, Junior Chu Feng! No wonder Zi Ling is devoted to you, even though she’s so beautiful. I’d want a man like you, too!” Wen Xue complimented Chu Feng.","“You can withhold your compliments for later. Nothing is for certain until we obtain the lotus and the gu,” Chu Feng replied.","“Nothing will go wrong with you around.” Wen Xue completely trusted Chu Feng.","Six hours later, the lotus became less than a meter tall, and the gu had shrunk so much that it couldn’t be seen unless one paid close attention.","Chu Feng stopped the stream of hypnotic energy.","It was time to harvest the lotus.","“Chu Feng, I’ll be taking the gu you picked with great care,” Jie Tianran’s voice suddenly echoed from above.","The space above them suddenly warped, and the red monstrous beast appeared out of thin air. Jie Tianran and the entity were riding on it.","“Jie Tianran?” Chu Feng and Wen Xue’s faces darkened.","It would appear that Jie Tianran had been here all along, but how did they conceal themselves? Did they acquire new powers here?","But this wasn’t the time to be thinking about that, for the red monstrous beast was about to devour the lotus whole!","“Screw you, Jie Tianran!”","A brilliant burst of white light enveloped the lotus. It was from Wen Xue.","“Senior, didn’t you fail to obtain a bloodline power?” Chu Feng asked.","“Cut the crap and help me snatch the lotus over!” Wen Xue exclaimed. She was so anxious that she infused her bloodline power into Chu Feng’s tree as well, greatly raising its fighting prowess.","Chu Feng immediately channeled the tree to attack Jie Tianran and the red monstrous beast.","But for some reason, the red monstrous beast had grown stronger. Even with the infusion of Wen Xue’s bloodline power, the tree was still only barely a match for the red monstrous beast.","But as time passed, Chu Feng’s consciousness weakened, and Wen Xue’s expression distorted in pain. It would appear that using her bloodline power took a toll on Wen Xue.","“Lass, you care a lot about this lotus. It must be your agenda for entering this remnant. That’s more reason for me to take this lotus.” Jie Tianran was vindictive. He had been wanting to get back at Wen Xue for insulting him, and this was his chance.","Wen Xue formed a hand seal, and the white light reappeared stronger than ever. However, her consciousness flickered, and it looked like she would disintegrate at any moment. Nevertheless, her eyes hardened with determination. She would fight Jie Tianran to the bitter end for the lotus.","“Forget it, senior. Let’s not stoop down to their level. We can always turn the tables on them as long as we continue living. It won’t be worthwhile to give our lives away for those two old things,” Chu Feng said.","“That won’t do! How dare they steal my things?!” Wen Xue clenched her teeth in anger, but her consciousness grew even more unstable.","“Forget it, senior. Jie Tianran is a mad dog. There’s no point pitting it out with him. You won’t bite a dog just because a dog bites you, right?” Chu Feng added.","“Hold on. You...” It belatedly struck Wen Xue that Chu Feng was using her words against her."]},{"number":6491,"title":"Chapter 6491: Chapter 6489: The Fight For the Lotus","paragraphs":["Chapter 6489: The Fight For the Lotus","Wen Xue didn’t lose her temper despite the realization that Chu Feng was teasing her. Instead, she looked at him with pleading eyes. “Help me, Junior Chu Feng. Your senior really needs it.”","“Senior, why are you so obstinate?” Chu Feng revealed a mischievous smile, making it obvious that he was indeed teasing Wen Xue.","Wen Xue rolled her eyes, but she quickly reverted to her pleading appearance. She even clasped her hands together and said, “Junior, I’m begging you. I’m desperate.”","She looked extremely sincere.","Before Chu Feng could reply, the entity beside Jie Tianran scoffed, “You’re begging him? Can’t you tell that your junior is cornered as well? Jie Tianran, stop playing around. It’s time to put an end to this farce. ”","“My thoughts exactly,” Jie Tianran replied.","Boom!","The red monstrous beast suddenly became two times larger, and its strength grew proportionately as well.","It was spirit power! It was weak, but there was no doubt it was Jie Tianran’s doing. He had somehow managed to manifest psyche here, and through it, he conjured this bit of spirit power.","“How is that possible? Has he been hiding that all along?” Wen Xue’s face crumbled in despair. She had already given it her all. She felt indignant, but there was nothing she could do.","“Senior, you can retract your energy now,” Chu Feng said.","“All right,” Wen Xue replied weakly. She resigned herself to fate and stopped channeling her bloodline power. It was meaningless to prolong the fight when the situation was hopeless.","Weng!","Chu Feng’s tree suddenly grew even brighter.","Wen Xue was taken aback. How could the tree grow brighter when she had retracted her bloodline power from it? She turned to Chu Feng, and what she saw brought frenzied joy back to her face.","Somehow, Chu Feng was emanating psyche, and his psyche was stronger than Jie Tianran’s. With that, he reinforced his tree to the point where it could oppose the combined prowess of Jie Tianran and the entity.","“Junior Chu Feng, you were hiding such a means? Let me help you!” Wen Xue exclaimed.","But Chu Feng stopped her. “Take a rest, senior. I’ll handle them.”","He turned to Jie Tianran and said, “Old thing, do you think you’re the only one who obtained psyche? I obtained more than you.”","More lightning branches surged toward the red monstrous beast, raining torrential attacks on it.","“Jie Tianran, your grandson isn’t easy to deal with,” the entity remarked.","Jie Tianran didn’t say a word, but his face was livid. He began going all out, which caused his consciousness to weaken.","“Very well. Let’s see whose consciousness is stronger.”","Chu Feng further raised his power output, causing his consciousness to become so weak that a stronger wind might dissipate it. Yet, he held firm despite the furious winds raging all around.","Just then, Wen Xue’s bloodline power enveloped the tree.","“Go, junior! Screw them over!” she roared.","“You two seem to think I don’t exist.”","With Wen Xue rejoining the fray, the entity beside Jie Tianran also began going all out.","Both the red monstrous beast and the green tree had grown many times stronger than before, yet they remained almost equally matched. There was no clear victor between them.","Weng!","Moments later, a spirit formation gate appeared not too far away from them.","“Oh no,” Wen Xue murmured.","Her guess was on the mark. Shortly after the spirit formation gate appeared, the forest realm began crumbling apart.","“What the hell! We haven’t obtained a gu yet. Why did this realm start crumbling on its own?” Wen Xue angrily stomped her feet.","“There might have been a time limit before the realm collapses,” Chu Feng replied.","“Damn it.” Wen Xue was anxious.","“Looks like you won’t get what you want,” Jie Tianran snickered.","“Old thing, you insist on getting in my way, huh? Two can play the game.” Wen Xue glared at Jie Tianran.","“What can you do?” Jie Tianran revealed a revolting smile.","Just like that, the stalemate persisted. Neither side could defeat the other, so no one could claim the lotus or the gu.","Meanwhile, the realm continued collapsing toward them. Despite the realm’s massive size, it didn’t take long for the collapse to be right before them.","“Forget it, I’ll let you have it,” Jie Tianran said.","Much to Wen Xue’s astonishment, he halted his attack and rode the red monstrous beast away. It confused her why he would give up at this juncture, but she still looked at Chu Feng and said, “Junior.”","Chu Feng understood her intent. He nodded. “Go take it.”","Wen Xue ran up to the lotus and grabbed it.","Wu!","Her expression distorted the moment she grabbed the lotus. It was the lotus. It was attacking her even though it had shrunk to less than a meter tall. Fortunately, the pain was not beyond what she could bear. She gritted her teeth and pulled the lotus out.","She was about to turn to Chu Feng to brag about her success when her face suddenly stiffened.","A tiny surge of teleportation energy appeared from within the lotus, and it enveloped the gu. Then, the gu vanished before reappearing in Jie Tianran’s grasp.","It was a formation!","Jie Tianran had secretly constructed this teleportation formation while fighting against Chu Feng. He had pretended to give up earlier so that he could retrieve the gu in such a manner.","“Chu Feng, you’re still too young. It’s a good thing that there is still time. I hope you find a gu that is to your liking,” Jie Tianran scoffed before he entered the spirit formation gate with the red monstrous beast.","“That bastard! He’s too much. I’ll obliterate his Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Wen Xue cursed. She then turned to Chu Feng with an apologetic look. “I’m sorry, junior. It’s all because of me...”","She knew there was no time to find a new gu. If not to fight for her lotus, Chu Feng could have found another gu that was to his liking.","But Chu Feng smiled as if unfazed by the turn of events. “Don’t worry. There might be another way out.”","He compressed the tree until it fit on his palm before walking up to Wen Xue."]},{"number":6492,"title":"Chapter 6492: Chapter 6490: Certain Defeat?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6490: Certain Defeat?","Wen Xue looked at the lotus in her hand before looking at Chu Feng. Her guilt deepened. “Junior, there’s still time. Take the lotus out for me. I’ll help you find a gu.”","Chu Feng reached out and grabbed Wen Xue’s wrist. “You won’t make it in time. Besides, you don’t know how to control the gu.”","With that, he forcefully dragged Wen Xue back into the stone realm.","Since the dust had settled, Wen Xue decided to stop harping on it. “Junior Chu Feng, I’ll consider you to have repaid half the debt you owe to me.”","“Only half?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course. I’ll admit that you are loyal, not hesitating to help me even if it means losing this remnant’s legacy. However, you owe me a debt of life. As much as I’m grateful to you, we need to distinguish between feelings and the objective truth, right?”","“Fine.” Chu Feng had to concede that Wen Xue was right.","“What do we do now? Do we leave? Or do you truly have another way out?” Wen Xue asked.","Failing to capture a gu in the forest remnant could result in massive repercussions going forth. Under normal circumstances, they should have given up at this point.","“There might still be a chance, but I’m not sure about it. Let me give it a try. But senior, you should stop holding back when I need your help,” Chu Feng said.","“What are you saying? It should go without saying that I’ll help you. I just wanted to preserve a hand just now as I haven’t gotten what I wanted yet. I’ll put my life on the line if you need it. The worst that can happen is the shattering of my consciousness anyway,” Wen Xue replied as she stowed the lotus into her Cosmos Sack.","Seeing Wen Xue’s careful movements, Chu Feng asked, “This lotus is far more valuable than it appears.”","“Not at all. It’s just useful to me,” Wen Xue replied.","Chu Feng simply smiled in response. He was confident in his observation. The lotus was an invaluable treasure, but this also showed how formidable the gu inside it was.","“Lead the way, junior.” Wen Xue was prepared for the final battle.","“Let’s go.”","Chu Feng led Wen Xue toward one of the caverns.","This was their final stop. The previous three caverns were merely building up to this moment. This was where the victor would be decided.","As soon as they passed through the spirit formation gate, they felt a breeze tickling their faces.","Taking a quick look around, they were in a vast grassland. Even the slightest wind stirred ripples on the grassland. The grassland was filled with not just grass but insect eggs as well, and these weren’t just any insect eggs.","The atmosphere felt heavy.","The sky was covered in gray clouds. The surroundings would have been completely black if not for cracks of light shining through the clouds. Nevertheless, it still felt stifling.","“Are those gus? Do we need to be cautious of them?” Wen Xue asked while directing wary glances at the eggs.","“They are gus, but they are low quality ones,” Chu Feng replied.","“How do they compare to the gu obtained by your loser grandfather?”","“The difference is like heaven and earth.”","“Haa...” Wen Xue sighed. “Let’s search the area. Since there are gus here, we might find higher quality ones that would be useful to you.”","“Don’t bother. I can sense it. While this realm is far larger than the forest realm, everything in here is identical, be it the grass or the gus. There won’t be any stronger gus here,” Chu Feng said as he planted the tree. “But we can compensate quality with quantity.","The tree grew to over ten thousand meters tall, and its branches extended outward to envelop the world. The tree released its own energy, as well as the energy it had obtained from the fish, and scattered it like a mist.","It was a beautiful sight.","The grass remained the same as ever, but the gus began devouring the energy.","“Junior, is the legacy related to gus?” Wen Xue asked.","“Indeed. The stronger the gu nurtured, the more likely one will obtain the legacy. It’s even possible that the legacy itself is the gu nurtured,” Chu Feng replied.","Wen Xue pursed her lips as guilt gripped her once more. She could now sense how strong the gus were after they began devouring energy from Chu Feng’s tree.","Chu Feng had been downplaying the severity of the situation. It was not just a world of a difference; it felt like they were completely different entities, like mud before gold. There was no comparing the two.","“Junior Chu Feng, is there anything I can help you with?” Wen Xue asked.","“Not yet. I can do this myself,” Chu Feng replied.","As time passed, the eggs began to emanate faint lights.","By the sixth hour, the eggs were glowing brightly. They had evolved from normal eggs into something extraordinary.","“Woah. We might just stand a chance.”","Hope glimmered in Wen Xue’s eyes. These gus were still nowhere close to the level of Jie Tianran’s gu, but at least they weren’t mud anymore. They had reached the level of impure silver now.","If these gus evolved further, they might stand a chance with their numerical advantage.","Weng!","A brilliant light pillar suddenly gushed into the sky, illuminating the entire realm. From it, an unimaginably huge bug emerged. It was the gu inside the lotus, but it wasn’t the gu’s real body but an avatar.","It was a phenomenon!","“Junior, I’d like to retract my earlier statement. Your loser grandfather might be a loser, but he has nurtured quite the formidable gu. Can your gus fight against that?” Wen Xue asked with a tight frown.","She saw no hope for Chu Feng."]},{"number":6493,"title":"Chapter 6493: Chapter 6491: Stepping Stone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6491: Stepping Stone","“I’ll show you,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He formed a hand seal.","A powerful surge of energy gushed out from the tree, but this was unlike any of the energies it had emitted before—it was the tree’s life force. Unsurprisingly, the tree swiftly withered.","The gus ravenously devoured the life force before breaking free of their cocoons and metamorphosing into seven-colored butterflies. Their bodies grew till they were over three meters tall.","There were so many of them around that they filled up the surroundings like an army.","“Woah! Junior Chu Feng, were you withholding a hand, too?” Wen Xue exclaimed in surprise.","These seven-colored butterflies definitely stood a chance against Jie Tianran’s gu, even when considering the earlier phenomenon.","“Not at all. These gus would only metamorphose after taking in the tree’s life force,” Chu Feng replied.","“What do we do next? Should we pick a fight with your grandfather?” Wen Xue was raring to go now that they had an army of butterflies.","Just then, the clouds covering the sky scattered.","A humongous tower that stood taller than the mountains could be seen in the sky. The tower was imbued with spirit power, which was why Chu Feng and the others to see it clearly despite having lost their cultivation in here.","There was a key fragment on top of the tower.","“It looks like we’re due for a fight.”","Chu Feng and Wen Xue climbed onto the back of a seven-colored butterfly each before leading the butterfly army toward the tower.","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran and the entity were also making their way toward the tower. Thanks to their proximity, they were the first to arrive at the tower.","A humongous gu that was over ten thousand meters in length stood outside the tower. It was still shaped like a bug, but its physique had grown more slender, making it resemble a dragon instead.","It had devoured the red monstrous beast to manifest red aura armor, which gave it a domineering appearance.","Jie Tianran and the entity rode on the gu’s head.","Jie Tianran’s complexion looked awful, and his body had become extremely faint. He must have paid a hefty price to strengthen the gu. His eyes were closed, and he was channeling his spirit power to heal up.","“Jie Tianran, there’s something off here. Did your grandson not give up?” the entity asked.","There was a barrier around the tower that prevented them from accessing it.","Jie Tianran opened his eyes and examined the barrier, but he couldn’t decipher it. That made him uneasy. His wealth of experience told him that the entity was right. Chances were that there was another competitor in this realm.","Jie Tianran and the entity suddenly looked in the same direction at the same time, where they saw a huge army of seven-colored butterflies rushing toward them.","“He’s a persistent one. Very well.” Jie Tianran channeled his gu to head toward Chu Feng.","Chu Feng was already prepared for that. He raised his finger and pointed it forth. The other butterflies, except for the ones he and Wen Xue were riding on, swiftly gathered together to form a butterfly spear to impale the gu.","Each butterfly was merely three meters long, but there were so many of them that the spear they formed was much larger than the gu.","Even so, the gu still wielded the advantage. It was evidently far superior in terms of speed and strength. In a direct confrontation, the butterfly army was no match for the gu.","But Chu Feng had anticipated that.","Just as both sides were about to clash, the butterfly army suddenly scattered before encircling the gu while keeping a safe distance away.","But the gu was simply too fast.","Whoosh!","The gu swung its tail, crushing an entire row of butterflies into dust.","Meanwhile, the remaining butterflies morphed into seven-colored lights and attacked the gu. It was an effective attack as not even the gu’s red aura armor could stop it. This onslaught greatly reduced the gu’s speed and strength while keeping it in place, leaving it with no chance to dish out a second attack.","“Get those two old things as well, junior! Teach them a lesson they’ll never forget!” Wen Xue excitedly urged Chu Feng to attack Jie Tianran and the entity as well.","“This attack only works on the gu,” Chu Feng replied.","“Jie Tianran, your gu isn’t as useful as it appears. It can’t even match the butterflies your grandson pulled out of nowhere,” the entity scoffed, though he didn’t panic. He continued observing the butterflies to find their weakness.","When his gaze happened to cross the tower, his eyes suddenly narrowed.","“Jie Tianran, we can’t drag things out any longer. Look.” The entity pointed to the tower.","Jie Tianran looked over.","An incense stick had appeared above the tower. Two characters swiftly revolved around the incense stick as if battling each other—’Nurture’ and ‘Plunder’. These two words harnessed spirit power.","Beneath the incense stick was a destruction formation.","As a world spiritist, Jie Tianran understood the significance of the incense stick. He had to defeat Chu Feng before the incense stick burned out, or else the destruction formation would be activated, and they would both fail the trial.","To his dismay, the incense stick was burning down extremely quickly.","“Help me!” Jie Tianran roared. His consciousness further weakened as he put everything into channeling the gu.","The entity formed a hand seal and released a green aura, which was noticeably stronger than before. He infused the green aura into the gu, making it stronger than ever.","Even so, the gu still remained suppressed by the butterflies’ seven-colored lights.","“Damn it.” Jie Tianran gritted his teeth as he glared at Chu Feng. He was already going all out; he had no hidden cards to pull anymore.","Just then, the gu suddenly emanated a brilliant light, and its massive body began to shrink. Eventually, it morphed into a ten-meter-wide cocoon.","A bizarre surge of energy rippled from the cocoon.","As soon as the butterflies were touched by the energy, they were reduced to seven-colored auras before being absorbed into the cocoon. In the blink of an eye, the only butterflies left in the vicinity were the ones Chu Feng and Wen Xue were riding on.","Just then, the cocoon was ripped open from within. A three-meter-tall humanoid monster emerged from within. It had three pairs of wings, and it was shrouded in a seven-colored light.","“Oh no.” Wen Xue’s face turned pale.","Even Chu Feng frowned.","Jie Tianran’s gu had metamorphosed into the humanoid monster, and it commanded an aura far stronger than the earlier gu and the butterfly army.","“Hahahaha!” The entity burst into laughter. “Chu Feng, you are indeed a filial grandson. If not for the butterflies you have gathered, Jie Tianran’s gu couldn’t have metamorphosed. You have achieved nothing other than being a stepping stone for him.”","Jie Tianran also looked at Chu Feng with a gleeful smile.","At the same time, the character ‘Plunder’ transformed into a wisp of smoke, fused with the incense stick, and the two disappeared. Following that, the barrier sealing the tower vanished.","The key fragment located at the top of the tower flew down.","But what happened next erased the smiles from Jie Tianran’s and the entity’s face. The key fragment flew not toward Jie Tianran but Chu Feng.","“It looks like I’m not the stepping stone.” Chu Feng’s frown slowly faded as he revealed a provocative smile.","“Chu Feng, I’ll murder you,” Jie Tianran spat as he ordered the gu to attack Chu Feng.","The gu turned around and grabbed Jie Tianran’s and the entity’s necks.","Wen Xue was dumbstruck.","Jie Tianran and the entity couldn’t believe their eyes."]},{"number":6494,"title":"Chapter 6494: Chapter 6492: Hundred Methods of Gu Control","paragraphs":["Chapter 6492: Hundred Methods of Gu Control","“You conceited old thing. Why don’t you tell me now if nurture or plunder is more important?” Chu Feng looked at the entity beside Jie Tianran.","The entity didn’t answer, but his animosity could be felt from the intensity of his glare. He was livid, but he had already outgrown throwing tantrums. Instead, he burst into laughter.","“Kikiki... Jie Tianran, you worked so hard only to become your grandson’s stepping stone. You didn’t notice that your grandson has tampered with the gu. I have imparted the Immemorial Gu Art to you in vain.”","Jie Tianran replied, “There’s nothing wrong with the gu. It’s the energy nourishing the gu.”","He turned to Chu Feng and said, “You intentionally allowed my red monstrous beast to siphon your tree’s energy. You tampered with that energy with a gu control skill.”","“You’re smarter than the other old thing.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Junior Chu Feng, did you do that on purpose? I was fooled by your acting!” Wen Xue widened her eyes in astonishment.","“You helped me well.” Chu Feng smiled.","“Of course. We have a telepathic connection.”","Wen Xue scratched her head in embarrassment. She hadn’t known that Chu Feng was acting and thought he was truly angry and wanted to pit his life against them. She was earnestly trying to dissuade him from doing so.","That, in turn, made Chu Feng’s act more realistic.","“Even the earlier attack from the butterfly army on purpose. You intentionally induced the metamorphosis of my gu. It’s also not by coincidence that your consciousness didn’t dissipate. You have acquired some kind of means here. I’m curious to know you pulled it off,” Jie Tianran asked.","Instead of answering the question, Chu Feng unleashed his psyche, but this time, it was far stronger than what he had previously revealed.","“Psyche? Was it when you picked your bloodline?” Jie Tianran asked.","“That’s right. Picking a world spiritist bloodline does grant you some psyche, but picking a cultivator bloodline grants you even more psyche,” Chu Feng replied.","“I didn’t think that there was such a dynamic at play. I was careless. But you acquired your gu control skills from this remnant, right? You must have received the remnant’s support, or else you couldn’t have slipped your gu control skill into your tree’s energy without me noticing,” Jie Tianran asked.","Chu Feng was astounded.","Jie Tianran might have been a poor excuse of a human being, but there was no denying that he was a highly talented world spiritist. His conjectures were all on the mark!","Chu Feng’s gu control skill was indeed acquired from the remnant, or more specifically, the stone realm. While deciphering the method to draw his consciousness from his body, he also discovered the gu control skill as well. That was why he had spent such a long time there.","The gu control skill was created by Qin Jiu, and its name was the Hundred Methods of Gu Control. The bulk of its content was about lifting gus, but there were also details about creating and planting gus.","Chu Feng figured that the Hundred Methods of Gu Control was the true legacy of this remnant, and that only those who discovered it would have a chance to obtain it in its entirety. Those who failed to notice it, even if they fulfilled all the criteria, would only obtain the key fragment.","That was also why it took Chu Feng so long to decipher the content in the stone realm, so much so that Jie Tianran overtook him and entered a cavern first.","“Looks like I’m right,” Jie Tianran sneered at Chu Feng’s lack of response.","“Does it matter? You still lost,” Wen Xue scoffed.","Jie Tianran ignored Wen Xue and continued addressing Chu Feng, “Chu Feng, you might have outdone me today, but that’s only because you were protected by the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. You won’t be as lucky once we’re out of here.”","Right after those words were uttered, Jie Tianran’s face stiffened.","The tower collapsed into a swirl of spirit power before manifesting into a spirit formation gate.","As soon as the spirit formation gate appeared, the realm began collapsing from the far distance.","The trial was over.","Chu Feng and Wen Xue could simply enter the spirit formation gate and leave, but Jie Tianran and the entity beside him wouldn’t be able to do the same. Ironically, they were held in place by the gu they had painstakingly nurtured.","“You loser old thing! Still trying to intimidate us? You should worry about yourself first! Let’s see how you cope with this!” Wen Xue spat gloatingly.","“No one knows what the future holds in store, but there is one thing I know for certain. It’s only a matter of time before I surpass you, and that day isn’t that far away,” Chu Feng declared.","“Hahaha... Hahahahaha....” Jie Tianran laughed for a long time before he turned to Chu Feng. Despite having his neck clutched by the humanoid gu, his eyes still reflected an unnerving glint. “Do you know what my current cultivation level is?”","“It matters not. You’ll soon be trampled beneath my feet,” Chu Feng replied with a smile. He remained confident and composed despite Jie Tianran’s threat.","“Very well. I hope that you’ll still have that smile the next time we meet.”","Jie Tianran and the entity’s consciousness began to shatter. They were intentionally pushing themselves beyond their limits to leave this place.","“I didn’t expect those two losers to have such a trick up their sleeves,” Wen Xue remarked with a sigh.","Chu Feng’s face darkened. He grabbed Wen Xue and dashed out of the spirit formation gate.","“Why are you in such a rush, junior? Are there other benefits to claim?” Wen Xue was confused.","“Jie Tianran won’t let things rest easily. He’ll try to seal our paths of escape,” Chu Feng replied.","Wen Xue widened her eyes. “What about the gu? Aren’t you going to bring it with you?”","The gu looked powerful. It would be a pity if they couldn’t take it out with them.","“It’s designed specifically for this trial. It’s impossible to take it out. Even if I find a way to do so, it’ll be severely weakened once it is taken out of this remnant.”","Chu Feng and Wen Xue left the spirit formation gate, and their consciousness returned to their bodies. At the same time, the key fragment also entered Chu Feng’s body.","A spirit formation gate manifested before Chu Feng and Wen Xue."]},{"number":6495,"title":"Chapter 6495: Chapter 6493: Obstruction","paragraphs":["Chapter 6493: Obstruction","This spirit formation gate swirled with powerful teleportation energy.","Chu Feng and Wen Xue quickly entered it and were transported into a teleportation passageway. As someone who frequented remnants, Chu Feng understood that this was a measure to protect the victor of the remnant.","They were going to be transported to somewhere safe.","Wen Xue dropped on her bum and lazily stretched her back. Then, she looked at Chu Feng and asked, “Junior, is it over just like that? Is that key fragment the legacy?”","“The key fragment is not the legacy. It’s just a tool to open the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. However, I did benefit from this trip,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s good to hear.” Wen Xue breathed a sigh of relief. Seconds later, her eyes lit up. “Eh? You benefited from this trip? When? How?”","“It was when I was learning to remove my consciousness from my body,” Chu Feng replied.","“No wonder it took you so long! You were secretly learning something good!” Wen Xue stretched her hand forth demandingly. “Shouldn’t I get a share of the reward, too?”","“It’s the Hundred Methods of Gu Control. You want to learn it?”","“I do. Gu control skills are highly compatible with me.”","“All right. I’ll teach you once we’re out.”","“Great!” Wen Xue nodded. “Junior, you’re the world spiritist here. Will this teleportation formation just transport us out of the remnant, or out of this realm?”","“It should transport us to another realm.”","“That’s good to hear. That loser grandfather of yours will get in our way otherwise.”","Boom!","Explosions could suddenly be heard outside, and the teleportation passageway shook. Following that, the movement speed within the teleportation passageway began to decelerate rapidly.","“Is that your grandfather’s doing?” Wen Xue asked.","“It should be.”","“Damn it. I must have jinxed it.” Wen Xue covered her mouth.","...","Jie Tianran was already outside the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant.","He raised his palm against the sky and unleashed a gush of spirit power, which swiftly enveloped the realm. Under his spirit power, a hidden teleportation passageway was vaguely revealed.","“Found you, Chu Feng,” Jie Tianran murmured with a smirk as he unleashed even more spirit power to reinforce his sealing formation.","The sealing formation cut into the teleportation passageway like a sharp knife, causing teleportation energy to spurt out from within. At the same time, the teleportation passageway grew increasingly visibly.","Just then, a surge of spirit power flowed from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant toward the teleportation passageway. This reinforced the teleportation passageway, allowing it to resume its function and breach the sealing formation.","“Hmph.” Jie Tianran harrumphed.","He took out a golden talisman paper, which turned into a golden aura and rushed into the sky. The golden aura transformed into hundreds of millions of formation soldiers dressed in golden armor and armed with spears.","These hundreds of millions of formation soldiers plunged their spears into the teleportation passageway. They shattered upon striking the teleportation passageway, but their efforts slowed down the teleportation passageway once more.","“Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, you mentioned Chu Feng. Is he here, too?” Baili Xukong rose to the sky and stood beside Jie Tianran.","“It’s not just Chu Feng. He’s with your Netherworld Sect’s Wen Xue,” Jie Tianran scoffed.","“Wen Xue?” Baili Xukong’s eyes narrowed. He glanced at Wuma Hanshuang, who was stationed at the entrance of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant. He knew that Wen Xue was Wuma Hanshuang’s disciple.","Wuma Hanshuang’s face turned pale. She realized that she was in huge trouble.","“Mansion Master, what’s going on?” Baili Xukong asked.","“What’s going on? Can’t you tell? Chu Feng and Wen Xue have obtained the remnant’s legacy and are currently being escorted out the remnant. Those two address each other as senior and junior. Is Chu Feng a member of your Netherworld Sect, too?” Jie Tianran coldly asked.","“It’s a misunderstanding, Mansion Master. Chu Feng is not a Netherworld Sectmember. I didn’t expect him to have an insider in our sect. Don’t worry, I’ll give you a satisfactory explanation for this matter,” Baili Xukong replied.","He raised his palm and manifested a massive martial power hand to grab the teleportation passageway.","In the teleportation passageway, Chu Feng and Wen Xue could feel Jie Tianran’s spirit power and Baili Xukong’s martial power spilling into the teleportation passageway. Those two were so strong that the teleportation passageway would collapse at this rate.","“We’re doomed. Even the experts of the Netherworld Sect have made a move.” Wen Xue panicked. She turned to Chu Feng, but the latter was relaxed.","“Why aren’t you worried, Junior Chu Feng? Do you have more tricks up your sleeves?” Wen Xue asked.","Chu Feng calmly replied, “Don’t worry, senior. No one can stop us from leaving this place today.”","“How are you so certain?” Wen Xue asked.","Boom!","A black aura gushed out from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant and morphed into a black vortex. The black vortex was so powerful that it devoured Jie Tianran’s sealing formation and Baili Xukong’s martial power hand.","In response, Jie Tianran took out three golden talisman papers.","The three golden talisman papers morphed into powerful golden pythons, which lunged at the black vortex. Yet, the golden pythons were simply devoured by the black vortex; they stood no chance against it whatsoever!!!","“Forget it, Jie Tianran. You don’t stand a chance against that remnant’s spirit power,” the entity inside Jie Tianran said.","Jie Tianran could already tell as much.","“The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect... Just what kind of legacy did they obtain back then?” Jie Tianran narrowed his eyes in indignation.","“What happened? Isn’t Wen Xue with you? How did she slip into the remnant?” Baili Xukong roared at Wuma Hanshuang.","He had aided Jie Tianran in apprehending Chu Feng, thinking that everything could be smoothened over as long as they caught Chu Feng. Unfortunately, Chu Feng and Wen Xue slipped away.","Since that was the case, Wuma Hanshuang would have to take full responsibility for this matter.","“Lord Baili, I have made a misjudgment. Wen Xue possesses a special power; I thought she could scout the way for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master. I didn’t expect Wen Xue to slip Chu Feng in,” Wuma Hanshuang explained.","“Hmph...” Jie Tianran scoffed from the sky. “Do you think I’d need someone to scout the way for me?”","Wuma Hanshuang could tell from Jie Tianran’s tone that he wouldn’t let things slip just like that, so she kneeled to Baili Xukong and said, “Milord, I have erred. Please punish me.”","“You deserve to die.”","A gush of spirit power carrying overwhelming killing intent descended from the sky. Jie Tianran was planning to kill Wuma Hanshuang.","Boom!","The spirit power dissipated before it could strike Wuma Hanshuang. Baili Xukong had stopped him.","“Mansion Master, she might have erred, but I don’t think she deserves death.” Baili Xukong looked at Jie Tianran with a displeased frown."]},{"number":6496,"title":"Chapter 6496: Chapter 6494: Explanation to the Netherworld Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6494: Explanation to the Netherworld Sect","Jie Tianran coldly formed a hand seal, and a massive face reminiscent of a demon manifested in the sky.","Shoosh!","Jie Tianran pointed his finger downward. The massive face opened its gaping mouth and descended to devour everything beneath.","All Netherworld Sectmembers were horrified, thinking that this was the end of them. Even the rank four Heavenly God Wuma Hanshuang revealed a look of despair. That power that surpassed rank five Heavenly God level. It could easily destroy the entire realm.","Yet, Baili Xukong remained unfazed. He unleashed his martial power, which manifested in the form of a black aura. A pair of brilliant eyes shone amid the black aura reminiscent of the sun.","If Jie Tianran’s attack resembled a demon descending upon the world, Baili Xukong’s counterattack was reminiscent of a demon escaping from hell.","Boom!","The spirit power clashed with the martial power, unleashing terrifying shockwaves that split the world into two. However, neither was able to defeat the other.","The earth shattered, and space ripped apart.","Everyone in the realm felt the threat of death. At this rate, the realm would collapse before a victor could emerge between the two fighters.","Fortunately, the battle didn’t continue.","Jie Tianran was the first to step back and dispel his formation. Baili Xukong followed suit and dispelled his martial power.","Even though the battle had stopped, the collapsed earth didn’t regenerate, and space remained fragmented.","“Baili Xukong, is this the explanation you have to offer me?” Jie Tianran coldly eyed Baili Xukong.","“I’ll personally punish my subordinates for their mistakes. You need not trouble yourself on that, Mansion Master. I’ll admit as much that Chu Feng’s appearance here is our slip up, but what’s done is done. Killing Wuma Hanshuang will not bring back the legacy.","“Regardless, our Netherworld Sect is sincere about working with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. We won’t let you make a wasted trip here.”","Baili Xukong took out the Demonslayer Saber and tossed it to Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran stopped the Demonslayer Saber in mid air before it could reach him. Instead of grabbing the Demonslayer Saber, he asked, “Baili Xukong, what do you mean by this?”","“This is our Netherworld Sect’s explanation to you, Mansion Master,” Baili Xukong replied.","“You won’t be a match for me once this saber is in my hand. Yet, you still plan to hand it over to me just like that?”","“I know what it means for you to acquire the Demonslayer Saber, but this represents our sincerity, whether the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is willing to work with us or not.”","“Very well. You have changed my impression of the Netherworld Sect today.”","Jie Tianran grabbed the Demonslayer Saber.","The world immediately trembled. Even Jie Tianran’s arm was shaking ever so slightly under the Demonslayer Saber’s rejection.","But Jie Tianran merely smirked. He channeled his overwhelming spirit power into the Demonslayer Saber, suppressing both the trembling and the Demonslayer Saber.","He tried swinging the Demonslayer Saber, and despite not inflicting any damage whatsoever, his face beamed with joy. “What an incredible saber!”","Only he understood how strong he had become with the Demonslayer Saber.","Jie Tianran stowed the Demonslayer Saber in his palm before he turned to Baili Xukong and said, “Baili Xukong, I accept your Netherworld Sect’s sincerity. However, I have another matter to attend to. Send me the location. I’ll send our experts over first. They’ll follow your orders.”","“I’ll be troubling you, Mansion Master.” Baili Xukong clasped his fist. He made his way up to Jie Tianran and handed a scroll over. That was where the Undying Starfield was hidden.","“May we have a pleasant partnership, Baili Xukong,” Jie Tianran said before leaving.","He swiftly slipped into a teleportation passageway, but his movement speed far surpassed that of ordinary teleportation formations. His destination was not the Seven Realms Galaxy but the Totem Galaxy.","“What is your current plan, Jie Tianran?” the entity inside Jie Tianran asked.","“I was too busy preparing for God’s Era to deal with Chu Feng, but it’s about time to let him know who calls the shots in the world of cultivation. It’s one thing if I give up on the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy on my volition, but if I covet it, it will be mine,” Jie Tianran spoke with a mix of confidence and anger.","He was displeased at being outdone by Chu Feng.","“That grandson of yours is a dangerous one. It’s a matter of time before he surpasses you if he continues growing at that rate,” the entity remarked.","“Even if he’s lucky enough to escape my clutches, once I enter the Ninth Galaxy, my suppressed talent will be unleashed. The cultivation that the world of cultivation owes me will finally be returned to me. That is the fruits from my many years of accumulation. Juniors like him won’t enjoy the same benefit. There’s no way he can surpass me anytime soon,” Jie Tianran scoffed.","“You possess decent talent, just that it has been suppressed by the world of cultivation. The present juniors are already growing extremely fast; they won’t receive any compensation when they enter the Ninth Galaxy. From that point of view, it’s impossible for the current generation of juniors to catch up with you in the Ninth Galaxy.","“But Jie Tianran, that only applies to normal people. Your grandson is not a normal person. I have faced many opponents in my many years of existence, but few are as troublesome as your grandson. And all of them went on to achieve great things in the world of cultivation.”","Jie Tianran laughed upon hearing the entity’s words. “I’d have never expected you to put yourself down for others.”","“I’m not putting myself down for others, Jie Tianran. Your grandson is indeed a rare talent. His aptitude, mindset, and wits are all comparable to a top expert. He has already surpassed your daughter, Jie Ranqing. It’s time for you to face facts and dispel your prejudice.","“Why don’t you make use of him instead of destroying him? There are many ways to tap into his power. You don’t necessarily have to plunder his bloodline power. If you ask me, Chu Feng is much more useful than Jie Tian,” the entity said.","Jie Tianran didn’t reply. No one could tell what he was thinking beneath his contemplative eyes."]},{"number":6497,"title":"Chapter 6497: Chapter 6495: The Mysterious Wen Xue","paragraphs":["Chapter 6495: The Mysterious Wen Xue","“The Netherworld Sect’s Baili Xukong is no pushover. He didn’t hesitate to hand the Demonslayer Saber to you, even after crossing blows with you. He might have more tricks hidden up his sleeves. The Netherworld Sect is stronger than we expected.","“They approached us seeking a partnership, but who knows what they are truly after? You need to tread carefully around them,” the entity said.","“The Netherworld Sect? They want to exploit me, but they’ll serve as my stepping stones.” Jie Tianran chuckled.","His confident laughter showed that he had everything under control.","...","Meanwhile, Baili Xukong entered a palace.","Wuma Hanshuang followed him. Despite being a Netherworld Marshall and a rank four Heavenly God, she looked as meek as a child who had committed a mistake. Her head was lowered in shame, and she dared not to utter a word.","“Sit down.” Baili Xukong took a seat before turning to Wuma Hanshuang.","But Wuma Hanshuang dared not take a seat. She kneeled before Baili Xukong and said, “Lord Baili, I have made a grievous mistake that cost our sect the Demonslayer Saber. Please punish me.”","“Punish? What’s the use of punishing you? Will that bring back the remnant’s legacy, or will it help us capture Wen Xue and Chu Feng?” Baili Xukong asked.","Wuma Hanshuang was stumped.","“You have made a grievous mistake, but it isn’t severe enough to deserve death. Besides, punishing you brings no benefit to our Netherworld Sect. It’d be merely to appease Jie Tianran, but I have already given him the Demonslayer Saber. There’s no need to do anything more for him,” Baili Xukong said.","“Lord Baili, you...” Wuma Hanshuang looked at Baili Xukong with tears in her eyes.","She had known what kind of person Baili Xukong was beforehand and was thus not surprised by his decision, but she was still moved by how he had given away something this valuable to protect her.","That was also the reason they were so loyal to Baili Xukong. While the latter had his vicious side, he was also extremely protective of his people.","“Stand up. Some things are beyond your control, though I didn’t expect there to be so many traitors in our Netherworld Sect. First, Song Yun, and now, Wen Xue. Losing them is a huge loss to our Netherworld Sect,” Baili Xukong said.","“I don’t know about Song Yun, but supposing Jie Tianran wasn’t lying, Wen Xue has close ties with Chu Feng. She could have had a bright future in our sect. I wonder what sorcery Chu Feng has cast on her to make her turn her back on us.” Wuma Hanshuang was confused.","“They might have joined our Netherworld Sect with ulterior motives in the first place. Forget it, I shan’t think so much into it. There’s no point retaining those whose hearts aren’t with us. It’s a blessing in disguise to have them reveal their true colors earlier rather than later. I’ll leave you to deal with Wen Xue. You should know what to do, right?” Baili Xukong asked.","“I’ll dispatch my aides to track down Wen Xue secretly. My subordinates will maintain absolute silence about this matter, even if others question them about it,” Wuma Hanshuang replied.","“Good. Our new faction is using Song Yun’s betrayal to curb the conservative faction. If they learn that Wen Xue has colluded with Chu Feng, we will lose our edge over them,” Baili Xukong replied.","“Even if Wen Xue betrayed us, her crime is nothing compared to Song Yun’s. She didn’t hurt anyone from the Netherworld Sect,” Wuma Hanshuang replied.","“That’s true. Song Yun’s crimes are unpardonable. That said, we cannot be lenient on those who dare betray our Netherworld Sect. If we do capture Wen Xue, you mustn’t go easy on her just because she’s talented,” Baili Xukong instructed.","“Rest assured, milord. I’ll sentence her to death if I capture her,” Wuma Hanshuang replied.","“All right. I’m going to meet those six fellows in the neutral faction. If I can convince them to support our new faction, we’ll become the ones calling the shots in the Netherworld Sect,” Baili Xukong replied.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng and Wen Xue had been transported to another realm.","“Junior Chu Feng, you’re amazing! No wonder you were so calm. Did you know from the start that your loser grandfather can’t stop the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s formation?” Wen Xue asked.","“Of course. Jie Tianran wouldn’t have been bound by the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s restrictions in the first place if he were that powerful,” Chu Feng replied.","“That makes sense, but you can never know for sure. Brother Chu Feng, are you just reckless, or are you that confident in your decision? I can’t believe you aren’t afraid at all.” Wen Xue eyed Chu Feng from head to toe, curious to know the truth.","Chu Feng conjured a scroll with his spirit power and handed it to Wen Xue. “Senior, this is the Hundred Methods of Gu Control I have learned from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. It is a highly complicated skill, so I’m afraid my grasp of it is incomplete. I have summarized the key points of what I have learned in this scroll. Senior, with your talent, you should be able to benefit from it if you study it.”","“Thank you, junior.” Wen Xue excitedly unfurled the scroll, only for her face to scrunch up a second later. She glared at Chu Feng grudgingly, “Junior, do you take me to be a fool? Are you sure you summarized the skill for me?”","Chu Feng smiled. “Senior, I wouldn’t have spent so long deciphering it if it’s that simple to grasp. If you doubt my words, I can show you the original copy.”","“Sure. Show it to me,” Wen Xue said.","“Come.” Chu Feng placed his finger on Wen Xue’s forehead.","A surge of energy containing the original Hundred Methods of Gu Control flowed into Wen Xue’s mind.","“Ugh~~” Wen Xue hurriedly took a step back before staring at Chu Feng in utter disbelief. “Junior Chu Feng, you are a monster! Can that thing be considered a legacy? I think you’re the only one in the world who can decipher that!”","It was only after seeing the original copy that Wen Xue learned to appreciate the summarized version.","The summarized scroll contained confusing parts, but she still understood most of it. If she earnestly studied it, there was a good chance she could achieve a decent level of mastery in it.","But there was no chance of her understanding the original copy.","“It’s pretty summarized, isn’t it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, it’s very summarized. Our Junior Chu Feng is the best.” Wen Xue shot a thumbs up at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng responded with a grin. This encounter deepened his belief that Wen Xue was a decent person.","“Senior, you can’t return to the Netherworld Sect now. What are your plans? Do you intend to return to the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect? Or do you want to travel with me?” Chu Feng asked.","Despite his question, he didn’t think Wen Xue would travel with him. He had a feeling that Wen Xue had her own unique path to walk, similar to Song Yun.","“Do you still wish to visit the Undying Starfield?” Wen Xue asked.","“Of course, but I don’t think that’s possible anymore now that you have been exposed,” Chu Feng replied.","“I have my ways. You wait here,” Wen Xue said.","“How long will you be gone for?”","“I might need quite some time.”","“Actually, I have other matters to attend to. Why don’t we settle our respective businesses first and gather here once we’re done?” Chu Feng proposed.","“Sounds good.”","Thus, Chu Feng and Wen Xue parted ways.","Chu Feng made his way to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy via the Nine Heavens Secret Domain. The agenda of his trip was to obtain the legacy of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. Now that he had collected three key fragments, he wanted to see if it was sufficient to unlock the main city.","Little did Chu Feng know that Wen Xue had returned to the realm where they had just escaped from, the realm where the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant was located!"]},{"number":6498,"title":"Chapter 6498: Chapter 6496: The Netherworld Sect’s Traitor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6496: The Netherworld Sect’s Traitor","As soon as Baili Xukong left, Wuma Hanshuang summoned her aides and tasked them to capture Wen Xue. She even spent some time devising a plan to ensure they would succeed in apprehending Wen Xue.","The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy had been claimed, so there was no point in protecting it anymore. So, Wuma Hanshuang returned to her private territory.","She was exhausted. She had truly harbored high expectations of Wen Xue; she didn’t think things would end up like that. She trudged toward her palace and opened its doors, only to find someone awaiting her inside.","Her eyes narrowed in astonishment.","It was Wen Xue.","Wuma Hanshuang thought she was seeing things. Didn’t Wen Xue escape? What is she doing here?","Wen Xue bowed to her and greeted, “Master.”","Shoosh!","Wuma Hanshuang flitted up to Wen Xue and lifted her with a single hand. She glared at Wen Xue with eyes filled with anger and killing intent. “How dare you return?!”","But when she saw Wen Xue’s face twisted in agony, she loosened her grip a little. She couldn’t help but wonder if there was another side to the story, or else Wen Xue wouldn’t have been so bold as to return and confront her.","It would be unwise to trust Jie Tianran’s one-sided words.","“What happened, Wen Xue? Why did Jie Tianran claim that you have colluded with Chu Feng to steal the legacy?” Wuma Hanshuang questioned.","“Master, Jie Tianran’s words can’t be trusted. That isn’t true at all!” Wen Xue exclaimed indignantly.","Wuma Hanshuang released Wen Xue and spat with clenched jaws, “I knew it! Jie Tianran can’t be trusted!”","Wen Xue continued, “Even though Chu Feng shared a portion of the legacy with me, I didn’t help him steal it at all. He did everything by himself. That Jie Tianran is such a liar!”","Wuma Hanshuang froze in place. She couldn’t believe her ears. “What are you saying?”","“I didn’t collude with Chu Feng to steal the legacy. He did it all by himself,” Wen Xue replied.","“But you were working with him?” Wuma Hanshuang asked.","“I was, but I didn’t have to do a thing at all.”","Pu!","Wuma Hanshuang’s palm impaled Wen Xue’s body, and fresh blood splattered. The fury in her eyes blazed even more fervently than before. It had become apparent to her that Wen Xue was toying with her.","“Wen Xue, I treated you well. Why did you betray me?” Wuma Hanshuang spat.","“You have indeed treated me well, master, but my ties with Chu Feng go even deeper than that. It’s only right for me to help him. There was also something I coveted in the remnant, and I couldn’t have obtained it without his help,” Wen Xue replied with unnerving composure even though her body had been impaled and she was bleeding profusely.","But Wuma Hanshuang was too caught up in her anger to notice that. “So, you were using me and the Netherworld Sect right from the start?”","“Isn’t that how all relationships work? Master, why did you choose me, of all people, as your disciple? Would you have still chosen me if I lacked talent?” Wen Xue asked.","“Yes, I chose you because of your outstanding talent, but I have never let you down!”","“And that’s why I returned to look for you.”","Those words made Wuma Hanshuang lurch.","Indeed. Why did Wen Xue return to look for me when she has already gotten away?","She thought that Wen Xue had returned to redress her grievances, but instead, the latter confessed that she had been colluding with Chu Feng. So, what could Wen Xue’s agenda be? Was it just to make a fool of her?","But that was courting death!","“What are you up to?” Wuma Hanshuang asked.","“I need your help, master. My junior, Chu Feng, wishes to enter the Undying Starfield. Please lead the way for us,” Wen Xue said.","Wuma Hanshuang’s eyes blazed with murderous intent. “You want me to betray the Netherworld Sect, too?”","She clenched the hand impaling Wen Xue’s abdomen, causing the latter’s face to twist in pain.","But Wen Xue suddenly raised her head and revealed an eerie smile. “Master, are you trying to kill me?”","“You have betrayed me and the Netherworld Sect. Don’t you think you deserve to die?” Wuma Hanshuang roared through gritted teeth.","She didn’t consider Wen Xue as her disciple anymore; the latter was just an enemy. Her trust in Wen Xue had only put her and Baili Xukong into trouble.","“Go ahead and make your move, master. But be warned that if you kill me, our master-disciple ties will end right here,” Wen Xue replied.","“Master-disciple ties? How dare you say that to me?”","Pu!","Wuma Hanshuang’s martial power raged.","Wen Xue’s blood and flesh bits splattered all over the walls, the ground, and the ceiling.","Wuma Hanshuang breathed raggedly. Her anger remained unquelled despite having eliminated Wen Xue. She couldn’t understand why Wen Xue had returned to die despite having escaped.","“Master, you shouldn’t blame me for not reminiscing about our old ties then,” Wen Xue’s voice echoed.","Wuma Hanshuang was appalled. She should have destroyed Wen Xue, both body and soul!","The palace suddenly vanished.","Wuma Hanshuang found herself transported into a void.","A light appeared in the distance, and it swiftly approached Wuma Hanshuang. It was so huge that it was even larger than ordinary realms, almost resembling a sun. However, it was not a ball of fire but a sphere of pure white light.","But the white light was filled with countless gigantic lightning beasts. Unlike Chu Feng’s nine-colored lightning beasts, these were completely white.","The light sphere abruptly shrank, turning into the size of an apple in the blink of an eye before falling into the hand of a woman.","This woman had white hair, wore a white dress, and had an abnormally white and smooth complexion.","“Wen Xue?” Wuma Hanshuang called out in surprise.","This woman was taller and more mature than Wen Xue, but her facial features still bore striking resemblance to Wen Xue.","“It’s me, master,” the woman replied with a slightly different voice, though her smile was identical to Wen Xue’s.","Boom!","A powerful burst of martial power gushed at Wen Xue, but it dissipated before it could strike her.","Clang!","A God Armament saber descended from the sky to slice Wen Xue apart, but it stopped short of striking her. It was as if an invisible wall stood between the two of them.","“Who are you?” Wuma Hanshuang asked.","By now, it couldn’t have been more apparent that Wen Xue was stronger than her. Wen Xue had blocked all her attacks using her oppressive might.","On top of that, Wen Xue was emanating an extremely old aura that could usually only be found on old monsters. She was no longer a junior.","“Who am I? I am your beloved disciple, master,” Wen Xue replied with an eerie smile.","She opened her palm, revealing a sinister bug. Before Wuma Hanshuang could react, she plunged that palm into Wuma Hanshuang’s dantian.","Wuma Hanshuang’s face distorted in agony as if fighting against something.","Wen Xue tenderly stroked Wuma Hanshuang’s head, saying, “Don’t bother struggling, master. You’re doomed to become the Netherworld Sect’s traitor.”","Her smile grew increasingly twisted."]},{"number":6499,"title":"Chapter 6499: Chapter 6497: The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s Sectmaster Appears","paragraphs":["Chapter 6497: The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s Sectmaster Appears","The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city was under the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s control. It was sealed off by a humongous barrier, which showed how highly the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion regarded it.","But Chu Feng felt a response from his key fragments. They were linked to an even more powerful formation hidden here—the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s formation.","“Did the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion construct this barrier to guard against me? Unfortunately, you have miscalculated.” Chu Feng looked at his key fragments and smiled in glee.","This saved him a lot of trouble.","“What’s the matter, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","“With these key fragments, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion can’t hope to stop me.”","Chu Feng tightly grasped his key fragments. Teleportation energy enveloped him, and he was transported into a vast city.","He rose into the air to take a look. The city was so huge that he couldn’t see the ends of it, except for the massive gate and the city walls behind him. Despite his current cultivation level, he felt insignificant here.","“Chu Feng, did you succeed?” Eggy exclaimed.","Chu Feng had entered the main city with not just his consciousness but his physical body.","The exquisite constructions around had been painstakingly constructed by world spiritists. Without a doubt, this had to be the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","Chu Feng attempted to fly ahead, but he was soon enveloped by teleportation energy and transported back to his original position.","“Looks like it wasn’t a success,” Chu Feng replied.","He was trapped in this area, evident by how he was automatically teleported back to his original position when he stepped out of a demarcated area.","“Why are you here, Chu Feng? You have yet to collect all the key fragments,” an old man’s voice echoed from behind.","Chu Feng turned around and saw a two-meter-tall man wearing a snowy robe and holding onto a white jade walking cane floating in mid-air.","“Junior pays respect to Elder Sikong.” Chu Feng hurriedly bowed.","This man was Sikong Changsheng, an expert of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. He wasn’t just a formation entity but a living being. Chu Feng had met him when he acquired his first key fragment.","“State the reason you’re here,” Sikong Changsheng said coldly.","His attitude was much more formal compared to the first conversation they had.","Chu Feng opened his palm and revealed three key fragments. “Elder, all the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnants have been breached, but the other two key fragments have fallen into someone else’s hand. I have only managed to obtain three.”","“You want to ask if you can obtain our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy with just three key fragments?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","“That’s right,” Chu Feng replied.","“Impossible. You have to collect all five key fragments and forge the complete key to obtain the legacy here. Otherwise, you aren’t qualified,” Sikong Changsheng replied.","“Elder, I’m afraid that I’m unable to obtain the other two keys any time soon, and the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy might never be claimed. I’ll have to enter the Ninth Galaxy, and if I do so with the key fragments, others won’t have a chance to enter the main city.","“The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect left its legacy here for those in need of it. It’s the same thing whether you give it to someone else or me. Why don’t you make an exception and give it to me instead?” Chu Feng asked.","“You want me to make an exception? Give me a reason why I should do so,” Sikong Changsheng asked.","“Well...” Chu Feng thought hard but couldn’t think of a reason. Bragging about his talent here wouldn’t work, since Sikong Changsheng already knew about his talents. In the end, he said, “We came from the same place.”","Sikong Changsheng shook his head, not saying a word.","“Elder, is there no way around it?” Chu Feng asked once more.","“There’s no way around it,” Sikong Changsheng replied.","“Thank you for your guidance, elder. I’ll be taking my leave.” Chu Feng bowed before turning around to leave.","“Who says there’s no way around it?” an old woman’s voice echoed.","“Who is it?” Sikong Changsheng eyed his surroundings warily.","He had made a special exception to permit Chu Feng’s entry; no one else should be able to enter this place. Yet, he couldn’t find anyone despite searching the area.","“Sikong Changsheng, you can’t even recognize my voice?” the old woman’s voice echoed once more.","Space distorted, and a translucent soul entity appeared in mid-air.","It was an old woman with white hair that ended with a rainbow tip. Despite her old age, her skin remained as smooth as jade. She was beautiful and dignified. She must have been gorgeous in her younger years.","A seven-colored gemstone was embedded in her forehead. It was the sheer power of the gemstone that kept her soul from dissipating.","Sikong Changsheng was momentarily stunned to see the old woman before hurriedly falling to his knees and greeting, “Sikong Changsheng pays respect to Lord Sectmaster!”","Chu Feng hurriedly did the same as well. “Junior Chu Feng pays respect to elder.”","This was the same old woman who had provided Chu Feng with the clue of ‘Nurture’ and ‘Plunder’ in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant. Wen Xue had said that she was the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s sectmaster, Shangguan Fengquan.","The person whom Chu Feng had met in the remnant was a formation entity, but this soul was the real deal. It might not be Shangguang Fengquan’s main body, but it had the consciousness of the main body.","“Time is truly harsh. You were just a junior in our sect back then, but you have grown so old.” Shangguan Fengquan drifted over and raised her palm.","Sikong Changsheng understood her gesture and stood up. “I didn’t expect to be able to meet Lord Sectmaster again. How have you been, Lord Sectmaster?”","His voice was quivering in excitement, and his eyes brimmed with tears.","Shangguan Fengquan was already at the limit of her lifespan when she left back then. Even though the Shangguan Fengquan before him was not the main body, the fact that she could control this soul entity meant that she was still alive.","“I’m doing well,” Shangguan Fengquan replied with a smile. “Is the Dragon Imprisonment Orb still here?”","“Yes, it’s still here.” Sikong Changsheng hurriedly took out an orb.","The orb was oval in shape, and it was around the size of a watermelon. It was enveloped in a formidable layer of spirit power, emanating the Ancient Era’s aura.","Shangguan Fengquan took the Dragon Imprisonment Orb before turning to Chu Feng. “Chu Feng, I can grant you an opportunity, but it’s up to you whether you want to take it or not.”","“I’ll take it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Don’t be so quick to answer me. Sealed within this orb is the fragmented consciousness of a true dragon. Fragmented as it is, it harnesses incredible power. Even I am unable to do anything about it as long as it’s in the vicinity of its lair. If you can lure it out of its lair, I’ll be able to subdue it. Your mission is to lure the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness out of its lair.","“There is a real risk of being killed by the true dragon. Even so, are you still willing to take on this mission?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","“Yes, I’m willing to take on this mission,” Chu Feng replied.","Shangguan Fengquan narrowed her eyes. “It seems like you truly don’t fear death.”","“I fear death, but there’s something I have to do.”","“Fine. Follow me,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","Chu Feng’s surroundings morphed. He was transported out of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect to a lush plain. In the distance was a mountain emanating a powerful aura that warped even the surroundings.","That had to be the dragon lair.","Beside Chu Feng were Shangguan Fengquan and Sikong Changsheng."]},{"number":6500,"title":"Chapter 6500: Chapter 6498: Shangguan Fengquan’s Goal","paragraphs":["Chapter 6498: Shangguan Fengquan’s Goal","“The true dragon will notice me if I get too close to its lair. You’ll have to head there by yourself,” Shangguan Fengquan replied.","“Elder, how do I lure the true dragon out?” Chu Feng asked.","“You’ll have to figure a way out yourself. I wouldn’t have to seek your help if I knew. However, you should know that no one has ever succeeded in this feat,” Shangguan Fengquan warned.","“Please wait here, elder,” Chu Feng said before he began flying toward the dragon lair.","Sikong Changsheng suddenly interjected, “Chu Feng, you ought to think things through. This true dragon’s fragmented consciousness is extremely cunning and vicious. Countless have died in its hands, and most of them were stronger than you.”","“I’ll be careful,” Chu Feng replied. He began making his way toward the dragon lair while constructing a concealment formation.","“What’s wrong? You find it a waste of his talents?” Shangguan Fengquan smiled, but her eyes were as sharp as daggers.","“My apologies, Lord Sectmaster. Chu Feng is indeed a rare talent. I fear that the odds aren’t in his favor.” Sikong Changsheng bowed deeply, not daring to conceal his thoughts.","“Do you have alcohol?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","“Lord Sectmaster, I don’t have alcohol as I don’t drink, but I do have some Dragon Spring,” Sikong Changsheng said as he took out a gourd.","“The Dragon Breath Clan’s Dragon Spring?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","“Yes. It’s a more refined version.”","“I’ll have a taste.”","Shangguan Fengquan uncorked the gourd and poured its contents into her mouth. She sputtered a second later and spat it all out.","“It tastes as horrendous as ever.” She tossed the gourd back to Sikong Changsheng. “I left behind a treasure that is connected to my main body, but I have refrained from activating it thus far because it will only last at most twenty days after it is activated. Once its energy dissipates, I’ll lose all connection with this part of the world of cultivation.”","Sikong Changsheng widened his eyes in astonishment. He didn’t know Shangguan Fengquan had left such a means behind. He had thought that Shangguan Fengquan was dead, which was why he was moved to tears when he saw her.","“Lord Sectmaster, did you activate that treasure for Chu Feng?”","Shangguan Fengquan didn’t answer the question directly. “Since the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion entered the Ninth Galaxy, they have been recruiting talents and growing swiftly. They have secured a place for themselves in the Ninth Galaxy, though they have been overshadowed by our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. However, there has been a change recently.”","“What is it?” Sikong Changsheng was worried.","“A powerful helper has joined the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Her existence threatens the standing of our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. I wanted to recruit her, but I couldn’t stop her from joining the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.”","Sikong Changsheng blurted out the first name that came to his mind, “Jie Ranqing?”","The top experts of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect had entered the Ninth Galaxy in the earlier years of the present era. The only person he could think of who wielded the ability to tip the balance was Jie Ranqing.","And he had witnessed with his own eyes how Jie Tianran duped Jie Ranqing into entering the Ninth Galaxy.","Shangguan Fengquan looked at Sikong Changsheng and asked, “What made you think so?”","“Jie Ranqing is incredibly talented, and she’s from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Sikong Changsheng replied.","“Why can’t it be another talent nurtured by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in the Ninth Galaxy, or that a formidable world spiritist had joined the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","“I should have thought more deeply into it.” Sikong Changsheng lowered his head in shame, thinking that his conjecture was off the mark.","But Shangguan Fengquan smiled. “You’re right. It is Chu Feng’s mother.”","“Is it really Jie Ranqing?” Sikong Changsheng had a complicated look on his face. He had a high opinion of Jie Ranqing, but he would have never thought she would become a hindrance to their Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect.","“I saw something more terrifying when Chu Feng was breaching our remnant. He wields even greater potential than his mother. He’ll eventually enter the Ninth Galaxy. While he has a grudge against his grandfather, that is mainly personal. If his mother asks him to join the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, do you think that he’ll turn her down?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","Sikong Changsheng’s face turned grim. While he had a high opinion of Chu Feng, he had a clear idea where his loyalties lay. If Chu Feng’s existence was going to threaten the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, he wouldn’t plead for Chu Feng’s mercy.","It might be underhanded, but this was all for the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect.","“We mustn’t let Chu Feng join the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Shangguan Fengquan declared as she looked at the dragon lair.","...","Chu Feng was oblivious to Shangguan Fengquan’s thoughts, and he didn’t hear their conversation either. His mind was focused on completing the mission at hand and obtaining the legacy.","But he could sense tremendous danger from the entity inside the dragon lair.","So, he channeled all his power into constructing a concealment formation. At the same time, he used the Divine Deer’s Divine Concealment to obscure his aura.","“Chu Feng, why don’t we just give up on this?” Eggy asked.","She, too, could tell how dangerous the dragon lair was.","Chu Feng turned to the Divine Deer and asked, “Elder, can you use your power here?”","“Yes, I can,” the Divine Deer replied.","Chu Feng sent a voice transmission to reply to Eggy, “Eggy, Elder Divine Deer says that she can take me away from the dragon lair if things get too dangerous. I’ll just give it a try first.”","“All right. Go ahead.” Eggy was merely worried about Chu Feng. Since the latter had a way out, there was no reason for her to continue dissuading him. So, she asked, “What is your plan?”","“Someone else would have long succeeded if it were possible to lure it out of its lair from the outside. I think I’ll have to enter the lair to take a closer look. Don’t worry, Eggy. I’ll give up if it proves to be impossible.”","Chu Feng would prefer not to tap into the Divine Deer’s power if possible, since it would be better to reserve this hand for times of danger.","Chu Feng finally arrived before the dragon lair. As soon as he stepped in, he was confronted by an overwhelming aura.","“This feeling...”","Chu Feng frowned. This aura far surpassed that of any expert he had faced; it transcended Heavenly God.","“Is this for real? Even the fragmented consciousness of a true dragon is this powerful?” Eggy was shocked as well.","“It’s not just the true dragon but the lair as well. This lair appears to be enriching the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness,” Chu Feng replied."]}]);
